        "summary": "All 17 feedback items (Quick-1 through Quick-5 and A through L) have been grounded in specific file and line evidence. The five quick UX fixes are: (1) canvas nodes missing rdfs:label in the React Flow data bag, (2) edges missing markerEnd for directional arrows, (3) Inspector Subject/Object rows showing raw IRIs without label resolution, (4) the outputs panel fixed at 180px vs the requested ~75px, and (5) the Add-Literal dialog appearing top-left due to the global CSS margin:0 reset overriding the native <dialog> element's UA margin:auto centering. All five are confirmed CSS or small-edit fixes with no hidden state-propagation complexity. Among the 12 spec-level items: Item A (Save semantics) is genuinely large\u00e2\u20ac\u201dFR-U003 as written and implemented is 'download as file,' not IndexedDB; the persistent-storage path is Phase 5 gated on OED-302. Item E (Mermaid export) is not 'a small UI wrapper'\u00e2\u20ac\u201dsrc/emit/mermaid.ts does not exist; ft-112 is about test coverage for existing emitters, not the missing implementation. Item H (domain/range) is explicitly deferred in SPEC \u00c2\u00a77.5 with no schema fields in \u00c2\u00a75.7\u00e2\u20ac\u201da full spec amendment is required. Item I (functional property) is explicitly out of scope in SPEC \u00c2\u00a77.6\u00e2\u20ac\u201drequires a new term-vocabulary extension and new validation warning. Item K (Turtle prefix) is trivially fixable: the N3.js Writer at turtle.ts:258 receives no prefixes argument; PREFIX_MAP already exists but is used only for IRI expansion. Items B, C, D, F, G, L range from trivial to small; each has a clear SPEC-grounding. Items J (rdfs:label collision) and L (class assignment at creation) are independent of Item H and can be implemented without the domain/range schema change. Cross-dependencies are minor: B and L could share a creation-time dialog pattern; H and I are complementary but each independently useful.",
