        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM (urn:fnsr:task:261-recon-feedback) and covers all 17 items with specific file/line evidence. The proposed document reconciles faithfully with reconnaissance on all 17 items. Specific verification passes: (1) Effort calibration \u00e2\u20ac\u201d all 17 items match recon estimates exactly (trivial/small/moderate/large). (2) Accept-ready set (Quick-1\u00e2\u20ac\u201c5, C, D, K) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d all confirmed as non-spec-amendment fixes in recon; no large-effort item is labeled Accept without qualification. (3) Spec amendments correctly flagged \u00e2\u20ac\u201d B, G, J, L require FR/spec changes per recon; H and I cite explicit SPEC \u00c2\u00a77.5 and \u00c2\u00a77.6 deferral/out-of-scope language; F correctly notes the drag path is already within FR-U011 scope (no new FR). (4) Operator decision items A and E correctly forwarded as sequencing calls beyond developer authority (A: OED-302 dependency; E: Phase 3 vs Phase 4 scope call). (5) K correctly placed as Accept with K1/K2 strategy queued in the operator decision table \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the duplicate-@prefix question is surfaced. (6) Item G delete-instance cascade question (kernel vs UI layer) correctly gated before dev chain. Two minor quality gaps noted but non-blocking: (a) Item F's 'Amend' classification in the document overstates the spec change required \u00e2\u20ac\u201d recon confirms no new FR is needed; what F actually gates on is an IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN status confirmation, not a spec text amendment. The developer's rationale text is accurate but the per-item 'Recommendation: Amend' header conflates spec-text-amendment with operator-action-gate. (b) The J\u00e2\u2020\u2019L cross-dependency is not surfaced \u00e2\u20ac\u201d both J (buildNewDocument() starter-term initialization) and L (creation-time class assignment) touch the new-project initialization path and could share a combined design pass, but the document connects B+L without noting J's initialization-path overlap with L. Neither gap alters the correctness of any per-item recommendation. The document is self-consistent, grounded in reconnaissance, and does not conflict with frozen contracts, SPEC text, or existing ADRs. The canonical-doc ADR-citation CPS check is not triggered (demo/ is not a canonical path; no ADR-NNN citations in the proposed content). Ruling: ratified.",
