        "rationale": "Reconnaissance task 265 explicitly enumerated two and only two user-facing touchpoints for Item C (FEEDBACK-RESPONSE.md Item C scope): (1) ProjectSettingsDialog.tsx:100 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the form label rendering 'Subject IRIs (<code>iao:isAbout</code>)' [F11]; and (2) App.tsx:305 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the banner action button rendering 'Add subject IRI' for the missing-anchor state [F12]. The developer's proposed changes address touchpoint 1 via C9 (replacing the form label with 'Subject of the graph') but do not include any change for touchpoint 2. After applying C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC10 to the current codebase, App.tsx:305 will still render {isAboutState === \"missing\" ? \"Add subject IRI\" : \"Set real subject\"} \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the missing-state button text is unchanged. FEEDBACK-RESPONSE.md Item C states explicitly: 'any locations where \"iao:isAbout\" or \"Add subject IRI\" appear as primary user-facing labels (including App.tsx line 305 button text), replace with \"Subject\" or \"What is this graph about?\" as context warrants.' Reconnaissance F12 confirms: 'App.tsx line 305 renders \"Add subject IRI\" as the action button text in the anchor banner when isAboutState === \"missing\"; this is the only other user-facing label singled out by FEEDBACK-RESPONSE.md Item C.' The ratification check criterion 'Item C: ALL user-facing iao:isAbout references replaced (no missed touchpoint)' is not satisfied because FEEDBACK-RESPONSE.md treats \"Add subject IRI\" as an Item C target (alongside the literal iao:isAbout mention) and the reconnaissance's explicit two-touchpoint enumeration (F11, F12) is the authoritative scope. All other proposed changes are technically sound and well-grounded in reconnaissance evidence: @xyflow/react ^12.0.0 confirmed in package.json (C1 MarkerType import valid); before-snippet accuracy verified for C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC10 against actual file content; EcmInstance interface extension (C2) does not alter the isEcmInstance type guard predicate set; iriTail helper (C4) is a pure string function with no non-deterministic API calls and operates exclusively in the UI layer; label resolution (C5) mirrors the Inspector.tsx pattern (F4); CSS max-height (C7) and margin:auto (C8) correct the exact conditions identified in F7, F9, F10; banner text (C10) removes MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR and LEGACY_REALIST_ANCHOR_PLACEHOLDER from the rendered span while leaving the validation codes intact in code comments and kernel contracts per Item D's constraint; no Playwright tests assert the missing-state button text specifically (AC4 asserts 'Set real subject' for the legacy state only, via data-testid selector; the missing-state path uses no text assertion). The denial is narrow: one additional changes[] entry for App.tsx:305 is all that is needed. The operator should direct the developer to add a change replacing {isAboutState === \"missing\" ? \"Add subject IRI\" : \"Set real subject\"} \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the missing-branch text \u00e2\u20ac\u201d with appropriate plain language (e.g., 'Add subject' or 'Set subject') while preserving 'Set real subject' for the legacy branch (the legacy-branch text is not an Item C target and is tested by isabout-ui.spec.ts AC4 line 125).",
