      "@id": "urn:fnsr:task:270-recon-inspector-labels",
      "agent": "reconnaissance",
      "status": "done",
      "attempts": 1,
      "outputs": {
        "findings": [
          {
            "id": "F1",
            "claim": "In Inspector.tsx relation-mode JSX, the Subject row renders the raw IRI string via bare `{rel[\"ecm:subjectIri\"]}` with no label resolution or wrapper.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/ui/Inspector.tsx",
                "lines": "527-539",
                "excerpt": "<p\n  style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", wordBreak: \"break-all\", marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}\n  data-testid=\"gw-inspector-subject\"\n>\n  {rel[\"ecm:subjectIri\"]}\n</p>"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F2",
            "claim": "In Inspector.tsx relation-mode JSX, the Object row renders the raw IRI string via bare `{rel[\"ecm:objectIri\"]}` with no label resolution or wrapper.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/ui/Inspector.tsx",
                "lines": "558-570",
                "excerpt": "<p\n  style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", wordBreak: \"break-all\", marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}\n  data-testid=\"gw-inspector-object\"\n>\n  {rel[\"ecm:objectIri\"]}\n</p>"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F3",
            "claim": "Inspector.tsx already contains a private `resolveRelationNarration()` function that builds an `instanceLabel` map by iterating `project[\"ecm:instances\"]` and reading `rdfs:label`; this map is constructed but consumed only for the narration row, never applied to the Subject/Object display rows.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/ui/Inspector.tsx",
                "lines": "82-129",
                "excerpt": "function resolveRelationNarration(rel: EcmRelation, project: Record<string, unknown>): string {\n  const instanceLabel = new Map<string, string>();\n  ...\n  for (const item of instances as unknown[]) {\n    ...\n    instanceLabel.set(id, typeof inst[\"rdfs:label\"] === \"string\" ? inst[\"rdfs:label\"] : id);\n  }\n  ...\n  const subjectLabel = instanceLabel.get(sIri) ?? sIri;\n  const objectLabel  = instanceLabel.get(oIri) ?? oIri;\n}"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F4",
            "claim": "Inspector.tsx has a module-private `iriTail` function at lines 70-75 that splits on the last `#` or `/`; it is not exported and not accessible from other modules.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/ui/Inspector.tsx",
                "lines": "70-75",
                "excerpt": "function iriTail(iri: string): string {\n  const hash = iri.lastIndexOf(\"#\");\n  const slash = iri.lastIndexOf(\"/\");\n  const idx = Math.max(hash, slash);\n  return idx >= 0 ? iri.slice(idx + 1) : iri;\n}"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F5",
            "claim": "CanvasView.tsx has a separate module-private `iriTail` at lines 108-111 with a different implementation that splits on `/[-#/:]/.filter(s => s.length > 0)` and returns the last non-empty segment; it is not exported.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/ui/CanvasView.tsx",
                "lines": "107-111",
                "excerpt": "/** Returns the last non-empty segment of an IRI, split on /, #, :, or -. */\nfunction iriTail(iri: string): string {\n  const parts = iri.split(/[-#/:]/).filter((s) => s.length > 0);\n  return parts[parts.length - 1] ?? iri;\n}"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F6",
            "claim": "The two `iriTail` implementations (Inspector.tsx vs CanvasView.tsx) differ in their splitting regex: Inspector splits only on the last `#` or `/`; CanvasView additionally splits on `:` and `-`. These are not the same function.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/ui/Inspector.tsx",
                "lines": "70-75",
                "excerpt": "const hash = iri.lastIndexOf(\"#\"); const slash = iri.lastIndexOf(\"/\");"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/ui/CanvasView.tsx",
                "lines": "108-111",
                "excerpt": "const parts = iri.split(/[-#/:]/).filter((s) => s.length > 0);"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F7",
            "claim": "Neither `iriTail` function is exported from its module; there is no shared utility file containing a common `iriTail` in the `src/` tree that either module imports.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/ui/Inspector.tsx",
                "lines": "1-4",
                "excerpt": "import { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { AddLiteralDialog } from \"./AddLiteralDialog.js\";\nimport { narrateTriple } from \"../emit/triple-narration.js\";"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/ui/CanvasView.tsx",
                "lines": "1-12",
                "excerpt": "import { useMemo, useCallback, type MouseEvent as ReactMouseEvent } from \"react\";\nimport { ReactFlow, ReactFlowProvider, Background, Controls, useReactFlow, MarkerType, ... } from \"@xyflow/react\";"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F8",
            "claim": "FEEDBACK-RESPONSE.md Quick-3 specifies the desired display format for Subject and Object rows as: `label (IRI)` or `label` with IRI as title/tooltip, falling back to raw IRI when no label exists.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "demo/FEEDBACK-RESPONSE.md",
                "lines": "65-68",
                "excerpt": "Proposed resolution: In `src/ui/Inspector.tsx`, extract the `instanceLabel` construction from `resolveRelationNarration()` into a shared helper (e.g., `buildInstanceLabelMap(project)`). Apply it in the relation-mode Subject and Object rows: render `label (IRI)` or just `label` with IRI as title/tooltip, falling back to the raw IRI when no label exists."
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F9",
            "claim": "Playwright test AC3 in relation-crud.spec.ts asserts that `data-testid=\"gw-inspector-subject\"` has exact text equal to the raw UUID IRI `\"urn:uuid:c3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001\"` and `data-testid=\"gw-inspector-object\"` has text `\"urn:uuid:c3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002\"`, and after Reverse, asserts those values are swapped.",
