        "summary": "Inspector.tsx relation-mode renders both Subject (line 538, `data-testid=\"gw-inspector-subject\"`) and Object (line 569, `data-testid=\"gw-inspector-object\"`) as bare `{rel[\"ecm:subjectIri\"]}` / `{rel[\"ecm:objectIri\"]}` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d no label resolution. The label-resolution logic needed for Quick-3 already exists within the same file in `resolveRelationNarration()` (lines 82\u00e2\u20ac\u201c129), which builds an `instanceLabel` map from `project[\"ecm:instances\"]` reading `rdfs:label`; however that map is private to the narration function and not a standalone helper. Two distinct `iriTail` implementations exist \u00e2\u20ac\u201d one in Inspector.tsx (lines 70\u00e2\u20ac\u201c75, splits on last `#`/`/`) and one in CanvasView.tsx (lines 108\u00e2\u20ac\u201c111, additionally splits on `:` and `-`) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d both are module-private with no shared utility extraction. FEEDBACK-RESPONSE.md \u00c2\u00a7Quick-3 (line 66) specifies the target display format as `label (IRI)` or `label` with IRI as tooltip/title. Critically, Playwright AC3 (`relation-crud.spec.ts` lines 241\u00e2\u20ac\u201c256) asserts `toHaveText(rawUUID)` on both `gw-inspector-subject` and `gw-inspector-object`; the fixture used (`canvas-3i-2r-with-ops.jsonld`) carries no `rdfs:label` on any instance, meaning any format change beyond a pure IRI-string passthrough \u00e2\u20ac\u201d including wrapping as `label (IRI)`, using `iriTail()` as fallback, or adding tooltip markup \u00e2\u20ac\u201d will break these assertions.",
