          "triple-preview.spec.ts AC1 is fragile: it asserts toContainText(SUBJECT_IRI) specifically because the fixture has no rdfs:label. If a future chain adds rdfs:label to canvas-3i-2r-with-ops.jsonld to exercise the label-resolution path in relation-crud AC3, triple-preview AC1 will break. Recommend the operator either (a) keep the two tests intentionally un-labeled (test iriTail path) or (b) create a separate labeled fixture for the label-resolution AC3 test and leave the existing fixture unchanged.",
          "The secondary IRI span in Subject/Object rows uses inline style `color: #64748b` consistent with other muted labels in Inspector. If a design system token or CSS class is introduced in a future chain, this inline style is the first candidate for extraction.",
          "iriTail behavior difference: Inspector's original iriTail (last `#` or `/`) produced `c3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001` for UUID URNs; the new shared iriTail (splits on `-` too) produces `000000000001`. This affects the no-label fallback displayed in the Subject/Object rows. All existing call-sites that pass term IRIs (e.g., `https://example.org/ontology/HasRole`) are unaffected because the last segment is the same under both algorithms. Operator should confirm the shorter UUID tail (`000000000001`) is acceptable as the no-label fallback display."
        ],
        "summary": "9 changes across 4 files implement Quick-3 (Inspector Subject/Object plain-language labels). New shared module src/ui/label-resolution.ts exports iriTail (CanvasView's algorithm, made canonical), buildInstanceLabelMap (extracted from resolveRelationNarration), and resolveInstanceDisplay (returns { label, iriTail, displayLabel }). Inspector.tsx imports from this module, drops its private iriTail, refactors resolveRelationNarration to delegate instance-label map construction to buildInstanceLabelMap, and updates the Subject/Object JSX rows to show displayLabel as primary text with a muted secondary span for the full IRI. CanvasView.tsx drops its private iriTail and imports from the shared module, resolving the two-implementation drift flagged in reconnaissance F6. Playwright AC3 is updated from toHaveText(rawUUID) to toContainText(iriTail-segment) to match the new visible content; the post-Reverse data-model assertions are unchanged.",
