        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposed change adds new UX behavior (label-resolved Subject/Object rows in the Inspector relation panel), introduces a new shared module, refactors an existing function, and updates Playwright acceptance tests \u00e2\u20ac\u201d none of these are typo, formatting, or terminology-tightening corrections.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM (task 270). All twelve recon findings are addressed: F1/F2 (bare IRI rendering) \u00e2\u2020\u2019 C5/C6; F3 (label-resolution logic confined to narration function) \u00e2\u2020\u2019 C1/C3 extract buildInstanceLabelMap; F4 (private iriTail in Inspector) \u00e2\u2020\u2019 removed by C3, imported by C2; F5/F6/F7 (duplicate divergent iriTail, no shared utility) \u00e2\u2020\u2019 resolved by C1 canonical shared module; F8 (Quick-3 format) \u00e2\u2020\u2019 implemented via displayLabel + conditional secondary IRI span; F9 (AC3 toHaveText raw UUID) \u00e2\u2020\u2019 updated by C9; F10/F11/F12 (fixture has no rdfs:label, format change breaks AC3, only one spec file affected) \u00e2\u2020\u2019 C9 accounts for no-label fallback path and confines changes to relation-crud.spec.ts.\n\nQuick-3 coverage: BOTH subject (C5) and object (C6) rows receive label-resolved display. \u00e2\u0153\u201c\n\nHelper extraction: C1 (src/ui/label-resolution.ts) is declared as 'Pure functions -- no React imports; no side effects'; exports iriTail, buildInstanceLabelMap, resolveInstanceDisplay, and InstanceDisplayInfo. No React import, no I/O. \u00e2\u0153\u201c\n\nPlaywright tests: C9 correctly migrates AC3 from toHaveText(rawUUID) to toContainText(iriTail-segment). The fixture carries no rdfs:label, so the fallback is iriTail. iriTail('urn:uuid:c3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001') under the CanvasView regex yields '000000000001'; the element now contains primary ('000000000001') and secondary (full IRI) spans; toContainText('000000000001') passes. Post-Reverse data-model assertions (originalSubject/originalObject on ecm:subjectIri/ecm:objectIri fields in the downloaded JSON) are unchanged. triple-preview.spec.ts AC1 uses toContainText(SUBJECT_IRI) on gw-triple-narration, which is produced by resolveRelationNarration; the refactored function still falls back to the IRI when no rdfs:label is present (buildInstanceLabelMap stores id as fallback), so AC1 is unaffected. \u00e2\u0153\u201c\n\nLayer boundaries: src/ui/label-resolution.ts is a UI-layer utility with no imports from src/adapters/ or src/composition/; no kernel imports; no layer-0 contamination. \u00e2\u0153\u201c\n\nThree advisory-level concerns (non-blocking): (1) C4 calls resolveInstanceDisplay twice per render, each invoking buildInstanceLabelMap, which scans all instances \u00e2\u20ac\u201d minor redundancy for typical project sizes. (2) C9's toContainText('000000000001') cannot distinguish iriTail display from a regression to raw-IRI display (since the UUID IRI contains '000000000001' as a substring); developer's recommended fix is a labeled-fixture AC3 test for the label-resolution path. (3) Replacing Inspector's private iriTail (splits on last '#'/'/' only) with the shared iriTail (additionally splits on ':' and '-') silently changes the fallback label for hyphenated IRI paths in getObjectPropertyOptions/getDatatypePropertyOptions; this is low-impact for typical HTTP-scheme term IRIs but the operator should validate against project-specific IRI conventions.",
