        "bankings": [
          {
            "id": "B1",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "When a UI display element gains secondary-text spans (e.g., a muted IRI row appended below a primary label), existing Playwright toHaveText(exactString) assertions must be weakened to toContainText(significantFragment) because the element's full text content now concatenates primary and secondary spans. This precision reduction is inherent in the two-span rendering pattern. The recommended mitigation is a companion test using a fixture that includes rdfs:label on instances, which allows the test to assert the label text as the primary fragment and verify that label-resolution (not just iriTail fallback) is exercised. Without the labeled fixture, the toContainText assertion cannot distinguish the new iriTail-first display from a regression to raw-IRI display when the IRI contains the fragment as a substring."
          }
        ]
      },
