      "outputs": {
        "ruling": "ratified",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "C3 changes the behavioral output of emitTurtle \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the emitted Turtle string shifts from full-IRI notation to short-form prefix notation with a Writer-emitted @prefix block, altering the observable byte content of every Turtle export; JSDoc changes C1 and C2 accompany the functional change and are inseparable from the ratification scope.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM (task 275-recon-turtle-prefix). All three proposed changes are well-grounded in recon evidence and the before-snippets match the actual file content exactly.\n\nC3 (`new Writer()` \u00e2\u2020\u2019 `new Writer({ prefixes: PREFIX_MAP })`) targets precisely the single mechanical change point identified in recon F8 (the lone Writer instantiation at line 258). PREFIX_MAP already contains all 7 \u00c2\u00a75.2 prefixes with correct IRI values (recon F7); no new data is introduced. Under N3.js, passing the prefix map activates short-form compression in the body and emits a @prefix block in the Writer-generated section. URN-scheme IRIs (urn:uuid:*) match no prefix and remain as `<urn:uuid:...>` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d correct behavior confirmed by recon F8 (Writer is the sole compression site; no prefix matches urn: scheme). Datatype IRIs (xsd:string, xsd:integer) will compress to short form; content tests that check literal values via parsed-quad semantics are unaffected because N3.js Parser expands short forms back to full IRIs on parse.\n\nC2 replaces the emitTurtle JSDoc that recon F3 flagged as describing behavior that will no longer match after K1. The new JSDoc correctly describes the accepted-duplicate strategy: five of the seven Writer-emitted @prefix declarations duplicate the TBox prepend, with rdf: and xsd: as the two net-new prefixes (aligned with recon F4/F5). This addresses the JSDoc-mismatch open question from recon.\n\nC1 updates the file-header JSDoc step 4, which currently reads 'full-IRI notation'; this is a documentation consistency fix required by C3.\n\nTest impact: (a) emitters.test.ts AC7 checks for substrings 'OntologyDesignPattern' and 'isSerializationOf' in the TBox prepend block \u00e2\u20ac\u201d unaffected by K1. (b) Content checks use hasTriple() with full IRI values \u00e2\u20ac\u201d N3.js Parser expands short forms on parse, so these assertions survive. (c) AC6 idempotency \u00e2\u20ac\u201d PREFIX_MAP is a stable constant; Writer output is deterministic; continues to pass. (d) AC1 Turtle parse \u00e2\u20ac\u201d short-form Turtle is valid Turtle; N3.js Parser parses cleanly. (e) AC5 Playwright test (canvas.spec.ts lines 289-296) asserts only on canvas vocab absence (ecm:CanvasLayout, ecm:CanvasNode, ecm:CanvasEdge); these are filtered by projection before the Writer sees the quads, so the assertions remain valid even though `ecm:` short forms will appear for non-canvas vocab \u00e2\u20ac\u201d consistent with recon F9. (f) vmp-serializer.test.ts tests serializeVmp, not emitTurtle; unaffected. (g) snapshot.test.ts tests kernel transform(), not emitTurtle; unaffected.\n\nn-triples.ts imports only graphToQuads from turtle.ts, not emitTurtle, and uses its own separate Writer instantiation with `{ format: 'N-Triples' }` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d unaffected by C3 per recon F11.\n\nLayer boundaries respected: turtle.ts imports only from ../projection/index.js, ../tbox/index.js, and n3; C3 adds no new imports.\n\nResidual open item (non-blocking): N3.js Writer may emit only used prefixes rather than all declared prefixes for some versions (recon open question 2, dev open question 1). The developer's tests_recommended items address this observationally. For the MINIMAL_PROJECT fixture, rdf:type and xsd:string triples are produced, so both rdf: and xsd: prefixes will be used and thus emitted regardless of N3.js's emission strategy. The core change is correct; the advisory tests are recommended but not blocking for ratification.",
