            "content": "The developer's output separated 'changes required for K1 to land' from 'tests_recommended to close coverage gaps' without requiring the advisory tests to block ratification. This two-tier partitioning \u00e2\u20ac\u201d blocking changes in changes[] and advisory improvements in tests_recommended[] \u00e2\u20ac\u201d decouples the ratification gate from coverage-improvement work, allowing a well-scoped change to ratify cleanly while surfacing the gap-closing test work for the next cycle. This pattern is reusable for future Phase 3 emitter items where the functional change is clear but optional coverage assertions could be deferred."
          },
          {
            "id": "B2",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "All three changes (C1, C2, C3) were proposed together in a single developer pass, with C1 and C2 updating JSDoc to match the behavioral change in C3. This JSDoc-alongside-functional-change discipline prevents documentation drift at the point of landing: the before/after snippets for JSDoc changes make the ratification audit trail self-documenting, allowing a future reader of the audit chain to reconstruct the old and new behavior descriptions from the proposed changes alone without consulting git history."
          }
        ]
