        "summary": "Across four SPEC.md amendment targets, the reconnaissance finds: (1) **Item B / FR-U001**: The FR is a one-line entry ('Create a new project.') with no wizard semantics. Both SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.4.1 and IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md \u00c2\u00a72.1 specify silent creation with the ecm:UnspecifiedSubjectMatter placeholder; MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR is a post-creation export-blocking error, not a creation-time gate. A B amendment must add a new creation-time clause to FR-U001. (2) **Item F / FR-U011**: FR-U011 in SPEC.md is mechanism-neutral. The 'drag or double-click' language cited in FEEDBACK-RESPONSE.md appears only in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md \u00c2\u00a72.4 line 364, not in the SPEC itself. An F amendment should surface the mechanism specification into SPEC.md FR-U011. (3) **Item G / delete-instance**: No delete-instance FR exists anywhere in SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a718.2. FR-U031 is the highest FR-U. FR-U032 is next available. The DANGLING_* hard-error codes in \u00c2\u00a717.2 (inference: lines 1255\u00e2\u20ac\u201c1259) constrain cascade semantics: a non-cascade delete would immediately produce dangling-reference hard errors. (4) **Item J / reserved-name list**: \u00c2\u00a75.7 (lines 445\u00e2\u20ac\u201c467) is the existing Term Object section; it ends at line 467 and \u00c2\u00a75.8 begins at line 469 with no gap or existing subsections. The ecm:system-starter-example source value is spec-authorized (line 465) but never exercised in buildNewDocument(). A new \u00c2\u00a75.7.1 or insertion between \u00c2\u00a75.7 and \u00c2\u00a75.8 is the natural insertion point. (5) **Item L / FR-U011 class assignment**: SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.8 explicitly permits zero class IRIs; \u00c2\u00a717.3 classifies INSTANCE_WITHOUT_CLASS as a warning only. FR-U011 currently contains no class-assignment-at-creation requirement.",
