        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposed changes introduce new functional requirements (FR-U032), new normative subsections (\u00c2\u00a75.7.1 with eight reserved-IRI entries), new behavioral obligations (class-assignment prompts, cascade semantics, reserved-name enforcement), and new validator codes \u00e2\u20ac\u201d all of which add specification content that did not previously exist, placing the batch unambiguously outside editorial-correction scope.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present (task 280) and the batch addresses all five required items (B, F, G, J, L) with corresponding FEEDBACK-RESPONSE.md touchpoints. C2 (Item F) and C4 (Item G) are well-constructed: C2 correctly surfaces the drag-from-sidebar mechanism into SPEC.md FR-U011, and C4's FR-U032 correctly specifies the four-fold atomic cascade (ecm:instances removal + ecm:layouts[*].ecm:nodes removal + ecm:literalAssertions removal by ecm:subjectIri + ecm:relations removal by ecm:subjectIri or ecm:objectIri), with all field names verified against the \u00c2\u00a75.9 / \u00c2\u00a75.10 data model and the @context IRI bindings. However, three of the five amendments contain normative defects that preclude ratification of the batch.\n\n**C1 (Item B) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d \u00c2\u00a717.4 cross-reference error (blocking):** The proposed after-text states that ecm:UnspecifiedSubjectMatter for a newly created project is treated 'per \u00c2\u00a717.4 (LEGACY_REALIST_ANCHOR_PLACEHOLDER class).' SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.4.1 (line 392) is definitive: a project whose iao:isAbout contains ecm:UnspecifiedSubjectMatter emits MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR (\u00c2\u00a717.2 hard error, blocks export). LEGACY_REALIST_ANCHOR_PLACEHOLDER (\u00c2\u00a717.4 info) is exclusively the migration-path finding, emitted during the v0.3\u00e2\u2020\u2019v0.4 migration (\u00c2\u00a710.4 line 897). These two findings have different severities (error vs info), different blocking behavior (blocks export vs does not block save), and different provenance (new-project path vs migration path). Landing C1 as proposed would bake a normatively incorrect cross-reference into the spec. The developer flagged this as OQ2 and requested operator adjudication; that adjudication was not provided before the change was submitted. The operator must decide: (a) if the intent is \u00c2\u00a717.2/MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR (the current new-project behavior), revise C1 to cite \u00c2\u00a717.2; or (b) if the intent is to treat creation-time ecm:UnspecifiedSubjectMatter as info-severity like a migrated document, that requires an explicit operator decision AND corresponding amendments to \u00c2\u00a75.4.1, \u00c2\u00a717.2, and \u00c2\u00a717.4 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a materially larger change that must be re-recon'd.\n\n**C3 (Item L) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d ecm:source undeclared on Instance (blocking):** The proposed text adds 'The created instance MUST have ecm:source: ecm:project-created' \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a MUST obligation referencing a field that does not appear in the \u00c2\u00a75.8 Instance Object schema. \u00c2\u00a75.8 (lines 471\u00e2\u20ac\u201c485) defines: id, type, rdfs:label, ecm:classIris, rdfs:comment, ecm:createdAt, ecm:updatedAt. ecm:source is defined exclusively in \u00c2\u00a75.7 Term Object (line 456, with allowed values ecm:imported-ontology / ecm:project-created / ecm:system-starter-example). No companion \u00c2\u00a75.8 schema amendment is proposed. Landing C3 as proposed would create a MUST requirement for a field that implementations cannot satisfy without extending the \u00c2\u00a75.8 schema \u00e2\u20ac\u201d an extension that has no normative basis in the current spec. The operator should either (a) drop the ecm:source clause from the FR-U011 addition, or (b) add a companion \u00c2\u00a75.8 amendment declaring ecm:source as an allowed Instance field with its allowed values.\n\n**C5 (Item J) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION unregistered (major):** The new \u00c2\u00a75.7.1 subsection states 'The validator MUST emit a CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION finding (severity: error).' This code does not appear in the \u00c2\u00a717.2 Hard Errors table. SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a717.2 is the canonical error registry; a validator code introduced normatively in a subsection but absent from \u00c2\u00a717.2 leaves implementations without a registered code to emit and creates internal spec inconsistency. The developer acknowledged this in OQ1 and recommended a follow-up single-change task. That follow-up must be either bundled with C5 or ratified as a prerequisite before C5 lands. Additionally, \u00c2\u00a75.7.1's restriction that reserved names MUST NOT be re-minted as 'project-created or imported terms' may be overreaching: importing owl.ttl legitimately introduces owl:sameAs as an ecm:imported-ontology term \u00e2\u20ac\u201d that is not 're-minting.' The restriction should scope to project-created terms only, consistent with the FEEDBACK-RESPONSE.md Item J intent ('collision check in AddTermDialog.tsx handleSubmit()').\n\n**Recommended re-submission path:** C2 and C4 may be re-submitted unchanged. C1 requires OQ2 operator adjudication (\u00c2\u00a717.2 vs \u00c2\u00a717.4 intent) before the developer can finalize the text. C3 requires either removal of the ecm:source clause or a companion \u00c2\u00a75.8 amendment. C5 requires (a) a bundled C6 change inserting CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION into the \u00c2\u00a717.2 Hard Errors table, and (b) narrowing 'project-created or imported terms' to 'project-created terms.' The corrected batch does not require new reconnaissance if the scope of the C1 fix is limited to correcting the \u00c2\u00a717.4\u00e2\u2020\u2019\u00c2\u00a717.2 citation; if the C1 fix expands to changing the severity model for creation-time ecm:UnspecifiedSubjectMatter, that is a substantive behavioral change requiring re-reconnaissance.",
        "referenced_evidence": [
          {
