            "note": "Recon OQ2 raised the \u00c2\u00a717.4-vs-\u00c2\u00a717.2 question for C1; OQ1 raised the CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION gap for C5 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d developer re-surfaced both as OQ1/OQ2 without resolution"
          }
        ],
        "bankings": [
          {
            "id": "B1",
            "category": "discipline-correction",
            "content": "Developer-flagged open questions that affect normative correctness (cross-section citations, behavioral severity classifications) must be operator-adjudicated before the developer finalizes proposed text \u00e2\u20ac\u201d not left as ratification-time open questions with a 'Operator should confirm' note. Both C1's \u00c2\u00a717.4 misreference and C5's unregistered validator code were surfaced by the developer in their own open_questions list (OQ1, OQ2) and submitted without resolution. The ratification pass is not the right venue for first-time operator decisions on contested normative behavior; those decisions belong in the operator-decision queue before the developer chain is queued. When the developer self-assesses as 'uncertain' and lists OQs affecting normative correctness, the operator should treat those as mandatory resolution gates, not advisory notes."
          },
          {
            "id": "B2",
            "category": "methodology-refinement-candidate",
            "content": "Instance schema extension discipline: before a proposed FR adds a MUST or SHALL obligation referencing a data field on a specific entity type, the ratification pass must verify the field is declared in that entity's object schema section. C3's ecm:source-on-Instance defect was structural \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the field is defined only in \u00c2\u00a75.7 Term Object, not in \u00c2\u00a75.8 Instance Object \u00e2\u20ac\u201d and would have been caught by a simple cross-check of the proposed field name against the target entity's schema. A lightweight checklist item at developer-composition time ('for each MUST clause referencing a data field, confirm the field exists in the entity schema') would eliminate this class of defect before it reaches ratification."
          }
        ]
      },
