        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The four changes correct normative cross-references, extend a requirements row with behavioral obligations, narrow a constraint clause that overreaches into legitimately-permitted import behavior, and add a missing error-code registry entry \u00e2\u20ac\u201d all of which alter the semantic content of normative spec language, not merely its formatting or typography.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance (task 284) is present in UPSTREAM, satisfying the substantive-change prerequisite. Direct file reads of project/SPEC.md confirm all four developer before-snippets match current file state exactly, and each after-snippet correctly addresses its corresponding task-282 denial finding with no new defects introduced.\n\n**C1 (FR-U001 \u00c2\u00a717.4 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 \u00c2\u00a717.2):** Line 1324 of project/SPEC.md currently reads '\u00c2\u00a717.4 (LEGACY_REALIST_ANCHOR_PLACEHOLDER class)' \u00e2\u20ac\u201d verified. Developer C1 replaces with '\u00c2\u00a717.2 (MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR)'. \u00c2\u00a75.4.1 (line 392) establishes that new projects with ecm:UnspecifiedSubjectMatter emit MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR (error); \u00c2\u00a717.2 (line 1255) confirms the registration; \u00c2\u00a717.4 (lines 1279-1283) confirms LEGACY_REALIST_ANCHOR_PLACEHOLDER is migration-path only. Cross-reference is now correct.\n\n**C2 (FR-U011 class-assignment clause without ecm:source):** Line 1334 of project/SPEC.md currently ends with 'The dragged-from class is auto-assigned to the new instance via ecm:classIris.' \u00e2\u20ac\u201d verified as character-for-character match of C2's before-snippet (corroborating recon F4/F5). Developer C2 appends the class-assignment requirement clause ('the user MUST be prompted to select at least one owl:Class... unless no owl:Class terms exist...') with the ecm:source sentence omitted. \u00c2\u00a75.8 (lines 475-487) defines the Instance Object schema as seven fields (id, type, rdfs:label, ecm:classIris, rdfs:comment, ecm:createdAt, ecm:updatedAt) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d ecm:source is absent, confirming the architect's blocking rationale. Path (a) resolution (drop the ecm:source clause) is correctly implemented.\n\n**C3 (\u00c2\u00a75.7.1 'or imported terms' removal):** Line 471 of project/SPEC.md currently reads 'MUST NOT be re-minted as project-created or imported terms within a v0.4 project document' \u00e2\u20ac\u201d verified. Developer C3 removes 'or imported terms', leaving 'project-created terms'. The architect's rationale that importing owl.ttl legitimately introduces owl:sameAs and peers as ecm:imported-ontology terms (not re-minting) is undisturbed by this narrowing; the CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION emission clause and subsequent sentences in \u00c2\u00a75.7.1 are unchanged.\n\n**C4 (\u00c2\u00a717.2 CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION row insertion):** Lines 1263-1265 of project/SPEC.md currently read DANGLING_LITERAL_PREDICATE_REF row followed by blank line then '### 17.3 Warnings' \u00e2\u20ac\u201d verified as matching C4's before-snippet. Developer C4 inserts the CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION row immediately after DANGLING_LITERAL_PREDICATE_REF in the same two-column '| Code | Description |' format as all existing \u00c2\u00a717.2 entries. The description references 'ecm:source: ecm:project-created' in the context of term objects (which do carry ecm:source per \u00c2\u00a75.7, line 465) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this is schema-consistent and distinct from the instance-schema concern that blocked C3 in task 281. The prerequisite condition from the task-282 denial rationale ('either bundle with C5 or ratify as a prerequisite before C5 lands') is satisfied: C5 landed in task 283 (confirmed by recon F12 and direct \u00c2\u00a75.7.1 observation at line 471). Including this in the fix batch is valid.\n\n**No new defects detected.** All four changes are minimal in scope, before-anchors are confirmed live in the file, after-text is internally consistent with the surrounding spec, and the changes collectively close all four task-282 denial findings without coupling new normative obligations that lack schema backing.",
        "referenced_evidence": [
          {
