        "summary": "The src/kernel/ directory contains exactly three flat files (index.ts, transform.ts, canonicalize.ts); no delete-instance module exists. FR-U032 (SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a718.2 line 1356) explicitly places deleteInstance() in src/kernel/ and prescribes a 4-fold atomic cascade over ecm:instances, ecm:layouts[*].ecm:nodes (field: ecm:instanceIri), ecm:literalAssertions (subjectIri match), and ecm:relations (subjectIri or objectIri match). The structural precedent for a document-mutating pure function is refactorIri in src/refactor/index.ts, which returns a result object (project + referenceCount + affectedEntityTypes + optional collision); FR-U032's minimum spec says 'returns the updated document' only, so whether to add a cascade summary is an open design choice. Phase 1 spec tests live flat under tests/ as *.test.ts files compiled to dist-tests/tests/ by tsconfig.test.json; the run-tests.ts runner does a flat (non-recursive) readdir, meaning tests/delete-instance.test.ts will be auto-discovered but tests/kernel/delete-instance.test.ts would not. Inspector.tsx instance-mode currently renders: IRI \u00e2\u2020\u2019 Class Assignments \u00e2\u2020\u2019 Literal Assertions \u00e2\u2020\u2019 Add Literal button \u00e2\u2020\u2019 conditional AddLiteralDialog; there is no Delete Instance button. Existing Delete buttons (relation-delete at the bottom in a flex row with Reverse; literal-delete inline per entry) have no confirmation dialogs. The canvas-3i-2r.jsonld fixture has 3 instances with canvas nodes and 2 relations but zero literal assertions, making it a partial but useful cascade fixture; a dedicated delete-instance test fixture may need to add literals to cover the full 4-fold cascade. Both delete-instance.test.ts and tests/playwright/delete-instance.spec.ts are gaps (no existing files).",
