            "file": "src/kernel/delete-instance.ts",
            "describe": "Run 'npm run build' to confirm no TypeScript errors in the new kernel module (CascadeSummary, DeleteInstanceResult interfaces; deleteInstance function signature)."
          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "Multi-layout cascade: implementation traverses ALL layouts (all ecm:layouts[*].ecm:nodes). Recon open question left this unresolved. The spec says 'all ecm:CanvasNode entries referencing it from ecm:CanvasLayout.ecm:nodes' which reads as all layouts. If single-active-layout-only was intended, only a filter change in the kernel is needed -- no interface change.",
          "Playwright AC2 assumes .react-flow__node.nth(1) maps to instance 002 (fixture data-array order: 001 at x=100, 002 at x=400, 003 at x=700). The gw-inspector-instance-iri assertion documents this assumption and will fail-fast if ReactFlow reorders the DOM. If this assumption proves brittle, the test can be rewritten to scan all nodes and match by IRI.",
          "The App.tsx selectedInstanceId is not cleared after delete -- it retains the deleted IRI until the user clicks another node. The Inspector's selectedInstance===null guard (C5) covers this correctly (returns empty state), and the canvas node is gone so the user cannot re-click it. If explicit selectedInstanceId clearance is desired (e.g., for accessibility or keyboard navigation), an onInstanceDeleted?: () => void prop can be added to Inspector and wired in App -- deferred to architect judgment."
        ],
        "summary": "7 changes across 4 files implement FR-U032 Phase 3 G1 end-to-end. C1: new pure kernel function src/kernel/delete-instance.ts with typed CascadeSummary + DeleteInstanceResult interfaces; 4-fold atomic cascade (instances, layouts[*].nodes, literalAssertions, relations); idempotent; non-mutating. C2: new Phase 1 spec test tests/delete-instance.test.ts (flat placement for run-tests.ts auto-discovery); in-code fixture covers all 4 cascade arms including literals; 5 AC groups. C3-C6: four targeted edits to Inspector.tsx -- imports (Dialog + deleteInstance), state (deleteInstanceConfirmOpen), handler+guard (selectedInstance null guard + cascade preview counts + handleDeleteInstance), JSX bottom (Delete Instance button + Dialog confirmation). C7: Playwright spec covering AC1 (delete 001: 1 instance + 1 relation + 1 node cascade) and AC2 (delete 002: both relations cascade via subject+object match).",
        "self_assessment": "confident"
