      "outputs": {
        "ruling": "ratified",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposal introduces a new pure kernel function (src/kernel/delete-instance.ts), a new spec test (tests/delete-instance.test.ts), new Inspector.tsx state/handler/JSX, and a new Playwright spec \u00e2\u20ac\u201d all constituting new capability, not terminology or formatting corrections.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM (urn:fnsr:task:288-recon-g1). All seven changes have been evaluated against FR-U032, the recon findings, and the live codebase state. Ruling is ratified on the following basis:\n\n**C1 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d src/kernel/delete-instance.ts (new file)**\nPure function confirmed: no Date.now(), no Math.random(), no fetch, no process.env, no imports from src/adapters/ or src/composition/ or src/ui/. Four cascade arms implemented correctly: (1) ecm:instances filtered by id !== instanceIri; (2) ecm:layouts[*].ecm:nodes filtered by ecm:instanceIri !== instanceIri across ALL layouts (conservative/spec-literal interpretation of recon open question on multi-layout); (3) ecm:literalAssertions filtered by ecm:subjectIri !== instanceIri; (4) ecm:relations filtered by ecm:subjectIri !== instanceIri AND ecm:objectIri !== instanceIri (both directions). Idempotency: all four filter passes naturally produce zero removals when the IRI is already absent. Input immutability: spread operator {...doc, ...} creates a new document; input is never mutated. The cascadeSummary extension beyond FR-U032's minimum 'returns the updated document' is consistent with the refactorIri return-shape analogy (recon F14) and the developer's rationale. File confirmed absent from filesystem (before: null correct).\n\n**C2 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d tests/delete-instance.test.ts (new file)**\nPlaced flat under tests/ (not in a subdirectory), consistent with run-tests.ts flat non-recursive readdir (recon F5/F12). ESM .js extension import follows established pattern. Hand-rolled node:assert pattern follows tests/iri-refactor.test.ts (recon F6). In-code fixture covers all four cascade arms including literal assertions (addressing the canvas-3i-2r.jsonld literal gap identified in recon F17). Test groups cover AC1 (4-fold cascade), AC2 (cascadeSummary counts), AC3 (unrelated entries preserved with delete-B scenario to exercise C\u00e2\u2020\u2019A relation survival), AC4 (idempotency), AC4b (nonexistent IRI no-op), AC5 (input immutability via JSON.parse/stringify deep copy). File confirmed absent from filesystem.\n\n**C3 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Inspector.tsx import block**\nBefore snippet matches lines 1-2 of actual Inspector.tsx exactly. After snippet adds Dialog import and deleteInstance import between useState and AddLiteralDialog; lines 3-4 (narrateTriple, label-resolution imports) are preserved by the applier's before-snippet replacement semantics. Import path '../kernel/delete-instance.js' uses ESM .js convention. Layer direction: src/ui/ \u00e2\u2020\u2019 src/kernel/ is permitted; no reverse import introduced.\n\n**C4 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Inspector.tsx state declaration**\nBefore snippet matches actual lines 232-233 exactly. Adds deleteInstanceConfirmOpen state adjacent to addLiteralOpen (dialog state grouped together).\n\n**C5 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Inspector.tsx handler block**\nBefore snippet matches actual lines 290-308 (handleAddClassAssignment through 'return ('). After adds: (a) selectedInstance===null guard returning gw-inspector-empty \u00e2\u20ac\u201d correctly handles post-delete re-render where selectedInstanceId is stale (mirrors rel===undefined guard in relation mode, recon F8); (b) cascade preview counts computed from current project state for the dialog message; (c) instanceLabel using iriTail (already imported in scope at actual line 4); (d) handleDeleteInstance calling deleteInstance(project, selectedInstanceId) and onProjectChange(updated). All variables are in scope within the instance-mode branch.\n\n**C6 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Inspector.tsx JSX return body**\nBefore snippet matches actual lines 433-463 (Add literal button through closing fragment/return/brace). After inserts Delete Instance button inside gw-inspector-instance div with a visual separator div (border-top), then the conditional Dialog with cascade preview counts, cancel/confirm buttons, and data-testids following gw-btn-* convention. Dialog component props (title, onClose, children, testId) verified against Dialog.tsx interface. Cascade preview counts in the dialog message match the format 'N relations + M literal assertions + the canvas position'.\n\n**C7 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d tests/playwright/delete-instance.spec.ts (new file)**\nUses canvas-3i-2r.jsonld fixture (recon F17 identified it as the most complete cascade fixture despite zero literals). AC1 exercises delete of instance 001 (subject of REL_1, i.e., 001\u00e2\u2020\u2019002); verifies 2 instances remain, 1 relation remains (002\u00e2\u2020\u2019003), 0 literals (still empty), 2 canvas nodes remain. AC2 exercises delete of instance 002 (subject of REL_2 002\u00e2\u2020\u2019003 AND object of REL_1 001\u00e2\u2020\u2019002); verifies both relations removed. Node click via bounding-box center per Event-8 lesson (recon F10 analogy from relation-crud). IRI assertion after click documents and fast-fails the nth(1)=002 assumption. Save+parse pattern follows relation-crud AC4 (recon F10). File confirmed absent from filesystem.\n\n**Residual open items (non-blocking)**\nApp.tsx selectedInstanceId clearance after delete is deferred; the selectedInstance===null guard in C5 correctly handles this case without requiring prop plumbing changes. The nth(1)=instance-002 Playwright assumption is documented and guarded by the IRI assertion. Multi-layout cascade (all layouts) is the conservative reading of FR-U032 and is architecturally preferable to single-layout.",
