            "content": "Open questions surfaced by reconnaissance that are not resolved by the spec (here: cascadeSummary vs. minimum 'returns the updated document'; multi-layout traversal scope) are resolved by the developer in the changes rationale, not by the architect at ratification time. The architect's ratification role is to confirm the resolution is defensible against the spec and existing patterns \u00e2\u20ac\u201d not to adjudicate the design choice. Where both options are spec-compliant and one is demonstrably more conservative or better-aligned with an existing analogy, the developer's choice is ratifiable without requiring a further operator decision. This pattern should be made explicit in the developer-agent contract so future developer proposals surface open-question resolutions in changes[*].rationale rather than leaving them as unresolved open_questions."
