          {
            "id": "F3",
            "claim": "SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.7.1 defines exactly 8 canonical reserved names as compact IRIs using the normative VMP context prefixes: `rdfs:label`, `rdfs:comment`, `rdfs:seeAlso`, `rdfs:isDefinedBy`, `owl:sameAs`, `owl:differentFrom`, `owl:equivalentClass`, `owl:equivalentProperty`. The section carries three distinct MUST obligations: (a) validator emits the finding, (b) UI prevents creation, (c) emitters use canonical IRIs directly.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "project/SPEC.md",
                "lines": "469-471",
                "excerpt": "#### 5.7.1 Canonical Reserved Names\n\nThe following property IRIs are CANONICAL and MUST NOT be re-minted as project-created terms within a v0.4 project document: `rdfs:label`, `rdfs:comment`, `rdfs:seeAlso`, `rdfs:isDefinedBy`, `owl:sameAs`, `owl:differentFrom`, `owl:equivalentClass`, `owl:equivalentProperty`. The validator MUST emit a `CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION` finding (severity: error) when a project-created term has an IRI matching this list. The UI MUST prevent creation of a term whose user-entered IRI override matches an entry in this list. The semantic-jsonld and Turtle emitters MUST use these canonical IRIs directly (not via the project ecm:terms array)."
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F4",
            "claim": "The validator (`src/validate/index.ts`) uses a single `validate()` function that accumulates findings into a `findings[]` array via isolated per-code `if`-blocks, each delimited by a comment header. Two shared helpers exist: `makeError()` (severity `ecm:error`) and `makeInfo()` (severity `ecm:info`). All three currently-implemented checks (MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR / LEGACY_REALIST_ANCHOR_PLACEHOLDER, INVALID_SPEC_VERSION, NORMALIZED_ON_SAVE) are project-level; none iterate `ecm:terms`. CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION would be the first check requiring `ecm:terms` array iteration.",
            "evidence": [
