        "summary": "The Phase 3 J1 implementation surface spans three files that each need changes. (1) `src/validate/codes.ts` is missing the `CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION` constant entirely \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the \u00c2\u00a717.2 SPEC table row exists but the corresponding code export does not. `src/validate/index.ts` uses a well-established per-code `if`-block pattern with `makeError()`/`makeInfo()` helpers; the new check would be the first that iterates `ecm:terms` array entries, checking each item's `id` against the \u00c2\u00a75.7.1 eight-entry list (all compact IRIs: rdfs:label/comment/seeAlso/isDefinedBy + owl:sameAs/differentFrom/equivalentClass/equivalentProperty). (2) `src/ui/AddTermDialog.tsx` already has a two-layer duplicate-IRI check \u00e2\u20ac\u201d inline render-time warning (`isDuplicate`, `gw-iri-duplicate-warning`) and submit-time hard block \u00e2\u20ac\u201d but uses `collectExistingIris(project)` which only checks project-local IRIs; canonical reserved names would never appear there. The canonical check requires a parallel guard, either reusing or extending the existing inline+submit pattern. IRI overrides are stored verbatim (no prefix expansion), meaning both compact (`rdfs:label`) and full (`http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label`) forms may need matching. (3) `src/emit/turtle.ts` and `src/emit/n-triples.ts` do NOT iterate `ecm:terms` for canonical predicate IRIs \u00e2\u20ac\u201d they access `rdfs:label`, `rdfs:comment` etc. as direct JSON keys on `@graph` nodes from `projectSemantic()`, satisfying J1's emitter MUST structurally. However, if a canonical-name-colliding term exists in `ecm:terms`, `projectSemantic()` would include it in `@graph` as a named node and the emitters would emit rdf:type triples about that canonical IRI as a subject \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a situation the validator + UI are meant to prevent. No centralized reserved-names module exists anywhere in `src/`; the eight-entry list currently lives only in SPEC.md prose.",
