        "open_questions": [
          "Should the 8-entry canonical reserved-name list live in a shared module (e.g., `src/validate/reserved-names.ts`) importable by both `src/validate/index.ts` and `src/ui/AddTermDialog.tsx`, or should each site maintain its own copy? This is a DRY vs module-boundary question: `src/ui/AddTermDialog.tsx` already avoids importing `src/refactor/` (noted via F13 comment at line 39 of AddTermDialog.tsx), but `src/validate/` uses no Node-specific APIs and may be safe to import from a browser bundle context.",
          "Should the canonical reserved-name collision check match compact IRIs (e.g., `rdfs:label`), full expanded IRIs (e.g., `http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label`), or both? IRI overrides in AddTermDialog are stored verbatim without prefix expansion; the validator receives the raw VMP document. The VMP_CONTEXT defines canonical prefix expansions; checking both forms requires either expansion logic or a two-entry set per name.",
          "The \u00c2\u00a717.2 description restricts CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION to terms with `ecm:source: ecm:project-created`. Should the validator also check items with `ecm:source: ecm:system-starter-example`, or strictly only `ecm:project-created` per the SPEC text?",
