      "outputs": {
        "ruling": "ratified",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposed change introduces new validator logic, a new shared constraint module, new UI state and JSX, and a new test file \u00e2\u20ac\u201d none of which fall within the editorial-correction scope of typo fixes, formatting, terminology tightening, or citation format updates.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM (urn:fnsr:task:293-recon-j1) and the developer proposal (urn:fnsr:task:294-dev-j1) reconciles with all 12 recon findings. Each review focus item is satisfied:\n\n1. SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7.1 + \u00c2\u00a717.2 reconciliation: C1 encodes exactly the 8 IRIs named in \u00c2\u00a75.7.1 in full-IRI form, matching VMP_CONTEXT and PREFIX_MAP expansions confirmed in recon F11. C2 adds the CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION constant absent per recon F1, matching the \u00c2\u00a717.2 table row confirmed in recon F2. File header counts are updated consistently (26\u00e2\u2020\u201927 total, 16\u00e2\u2020\u201917 section 17.2).\n\n2. All 8 canonical IRIs present: C1 lists rdfs:label, rdfs:comment, rdfs:seeAlso, rdfs:isDefinedBy, owl:sameAs, owl:differentFrom, owl:equivalentClass, owl:equivalentProperty \u00e2\u20ac\u201d exactly the \u00c2\u00a75.7.1 set, array length = 8, AC6 in C10 enforces this at test time.\n\n3. ecm:project-created source restriction: C4's guard `if (t[\"ecm:source\"] !== \"ecm:project-created\") continue;` strictly implements the \u00c2\u00a717.2 narrowing. Terms with ecm:source: ecm:imported-ontology and ecm:source: ecm:system-starter-example are both exempt (neither equals the literal string \"ecm:project-created\"). AC2 in C10 verifies the imported-ontology exemption.\n\n4. UI inline warning + Save disabled: C8 adds `isCanonicalReserved` derived state parallel to `isDuplicate` (recon F6 pattern); C9 adds `gw-iri-canonical-warning` paragraph with `role=alert` and `data-testid`, extends `disabled={isDuplicate || isCanonicalReserved}` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d exact structural mirror of the Phase 2 task 2.5 duplicate-IRI pattern. C7 adds a submit-time hard block as an additional defense layer consistent with the existing `collectExistingIris` hard block.\n\n5. Emitter behavior: Recon F8 confirms turtle.ts and n-triples.ts access rdfs:label, rdfs:comment, etc. as direct JSON property keys on @graph nodes, NOT via ecm:terms iteration. The \u00c2\u00a75.7.1 emitter MUST is satisfied structurally without a code change. turtle.ts PREFIX_MAP (lines 33\u00e2\u20ac\u201c41) ensures canonical IRIs appearing as subjects in the defensive F9 scenario are serialized in short prefix form. No emitter change is warranted; the developer's open_question confirms this and records provenance for the audit trail.\n\n6. Spec test coverage: C10 covers six acceptance criteria including project-created + canonical (AC1), imported exempt (AC2), non-canonical no finding (AC3), empty terms no finding (AC4), ecm:target = term id and message content (AC5), all 8 IRIs trigger (AC6). The hand-rolled pattern matches structural-validator.test.ts. The test file compiles under tsconfig.test.json (includes tests/**/* and src/**/* minus src/ui) and is auto-discovered by run-tests.ts glob on *.test.js.\n\n7. Layer boundaries: src/validate/reserved-names.ts is a pure const array with zero imports \u00e2\u20ac\u201d safe in both NodeNext (main tsc build) and bundler (Vite build) contexts. AddTermDialog.tsx importing from ../validate/reserved-names.js crosses no stated GraphWrite layer boundary (the MUST NOT constraints are kernel\u00e2\u2020\u2019composition/adapters and within-kernel purity; src/ui\u00e2\u2020\u2019src/validate is unproscribed). The validate module uses no Node-specific APIs (no node: imports, no process, no fs), confirming Vite-bundle safety per C5 rationale. tsconfig.ui.json's include array does not restrict transitive imports \u00e2\u20ac\u201d TypeScript follows import statements unconditionally; the tsconfig.test.json build (which includes src/**/* minus src/ui) compiles reserved-names.ts independently.\n\n8. Single source of truth: RESERVED_CANONICAL_IRIS is defined once in src/validate/reserved-names.ts and consumed by two sites (C3 in validator, C5 in UI). The module-level Set in C6 (RESERVED_CANONICAL_IRI_SET) amortizes the O(n) construction to module-load time. This is the canonical DRY pattern for cross-component constraint sharing in this codebase.\n\nOne known limitation is documented but does not block ratification: RESERVED_CANONICAL_IRIS contains only full IRIs, so a user entering rdfs:label (compact form) verbatim in AddTermDialog would not be caught by C8's isCanonicalReserved check (recon F7; developer open_question). The developer has explicitly flagged and deferred this as a scope question. This is appropriate scoping: the primary normative IRI form in VMP documents is full IRI; the guard covers the normative case. The gap is banked below for forward-tracking.",
