        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "FR-U001 says 'implementation-determined' for block-at-creation vs nag-until-save. Current impl is nag-after-creation (banner, not a blocking dialog). BL1 scope proposes a blocking wizard with 'Skip \u00e2\u20ac\u201d use placeholder'. Does the architect ratify block-at-creation as the chosen implementation for BL1, or does the existing nag-after-creation banner satisfy FR-U001 without modification?",
          "FR-U011 MUST requirement: when the class picker dialog fires and the user has no classes yet (ecm:terms has zero owl:Class entries), the spec says the instance MAY be created class-less. Does the class picker dialog still open with an empty list (and the user must explicitly proceed), or does handlePaneClick silently skip the dialog and create class-less? This is an interaction design question, not directly settled by the MUST/carve-out language.",
          "canvas.spec.ts Chain B AC2 (line 68) uses gw-btn-new then dblclick with no prior class creation \u00e2\u20ac\u201d ecm:terms is [] so the class-picker carve-out applies and no dialog fires. Is this test's 'no dialog' expectation stable even after BL1 lands, or does the architect want to also test the 'classes present \u00e2\u2020\u2019 picker fires' scenario in canvas.spec.ts?",
          "smoke.spec.ts Smoke flow 1 (lines 67-92) adds 'Person' before doing dblclick \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the class-picker MUST would activate. The test currently asserts immediate node count without any dialog step. After BL1, this test requires a dialog-handling step (select Person \u00e2\u2020\u2019 confirm) before node count is asserted. Is this test the owner's responsibility to update, or does BL1 task delivery include test updates?",
          "If the New Project wizard is a blocking dialog that gates setProject(), the six tests that assert gw-btn-new \u00e2\u2020\u2019 gw-btn-save.toBeEnabled() without a dialog step will all fail. Does BL1 add a 'Skip \u00e2\u20ac\u201d use placeholder' path that leaves gw-btn-save enabled after closing/dismissing the wizard (making the existing assertions potentially still valid if tests don't interact with the dialog), or does the wizard gate the Save button until the user either fills or skips?",
          "Is the class picker for FR-U011 implemented as a new standalone component file (e.g., src/ui/CreateInstanceDialog.tsx) or as inline dialog state inside CanvasViewInner? Either is architecturally consistent with existing patterns, but the choice affects where the owlClass extraction logic lives and how it interacts with the project prop already available in CanvasViewInner."
        ],
        "scope_assessment": "Investigated the full current-state of handleNew(), handlePaneClick, the Dialog primitive and all existing dialog components, the FR-U001/FR-U011 ratified SPEC text, and all Playwright test files that touch New/dblclick flows and their fixtures; did not investigate the Inspector class-assignment UI (task 2.5 scope), the TermSidebar drag-from-sidebar path mentioned in FR-U011 (drag is listed as MAY, not MUST for BL1), or any kernel/validate/emit source files outside the UI layer."
      },
