        "summary": "The reconnaissance investigated eight focus areas to inform FNSR Protocol Spec 08 (Stakeholder Feedback Round Protocol) authoring. Key observations: (1) FNSR Protocol Spec docs 01\u00e2\u20ac\u201c07 all exist in `project/Routing/` using prose-frontmatter (no YAML), making 08 the next clean number; however, the planned Spec 08 will live as `surfaces/feedback-rounds/spec.md` (a surface-level spec analogous to `surfaces/retro/surface-spec.md`), not in `project/Routing/`. (2) Surface-level spec files use YAML frontmatter with `surface_id`, `question_scope`, `audit_trail_unity`, `agents_path`/`phases_path`, `canonical_reference`, and `status`. (3) The retro six-phase structure (gathering \u00e2\u2020\u2019 merge \u00e2\u2020\u2019 analysis \u00e2\u2020\u2019 consensus \u00e2\u2020\u2019 actions \u00e2\u2020\u2019 compression) is purpose-built for backward-looking team deliberation and lacks atomic-decomposition, completeness-mapping, and reconciliation steps that the task context identifies as required for feedback rounds. (4) Spec 07 already anticipates a stakeholder-feedback sub-surface as a named open question. (5) The empirical motivation \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Item J's starter-terms provision-half going missing \u00e2\u20ac\u201d is confirmed: J1 (collision detection) landed in Phase 3, J2 (starter-term population) has no Phase 3 committed-work record, consistent with no atomic-decomposition or reconciliation pass having occurred. (6) OPERATOR-MEDIATION-LOG.md events 9\u00e2\u20ac\u201c12 document four specific failure modes in the ad-hoc feedback chain that a formal protocol would need to address. (7) The canonical state-file location analog is `feedback-rounds/<round-id>/STATE.jsonld`; the directory does not yet exist.",
