          },
          {
            "id": "F9",
            "severity": "minor",
            "claim": "Frontmatter introduces three fields (`document_kind`, `spec_number`, `version`) not present in any existing surface-spec.md file, creating non-conformant schema extension.",
            "evidence": "Spec 08 YAML frontmatter: `document_kind: fnsr-protocol-spec`, `spec_number: 08`, `version: \"0.1\"`. Neither `surfaces/retro/surface-spec.md` nor `surfaces/verification/surface-spec.md` declare these fields. No surface-registry primitive doc (surfaces/_primitives/) defines these as standard surface-spec fields. The fields are not load-bearing for the substrate loader (which ignores unknown keys), but they imply a schema that no other surface follows and is not registered anywhere."
          },
          {
            "id": "F10",
            "severity": "minor",
            "claim": "No provenance section. All existing project/Routing/ specs (01-07) and surface primitives include a 'Provenance' section; Spec 08 does not.",
            "evidence": "project/Routing/05-banking-lifecycle-spec.md ends with '## Provenance' listing source documents and decision references. project/Routing/07-forward-track-surface-spec.md ends with '## Provenance' listing five source references. surfaces/_primitives/bounded-authority-orchestrator.md ends with '## Provenance'. Spec 08 has 'Empirical motivation' (covering J1/J2 only), 'Open questions', and 'v1 scope' but no provenance section listing: originating cycle(s), operator decision records, ADR references, or relationship to prior spec bundle. The spec's operator commands reference the retro surface pattern repeatedly; a provenance section would make these derivations citable."
          },
          {
            "id": "F11",
            "severity": "minor",
            "claim": "AP-5's 'SHOULD NOT be shipped before gap-16 is addressed' constraint is vacuous given both are v3.2+ implementation targets.",
            "evidence": "Spec 08, AP-5: 'The `state_admin feedback-round adjudicate` command SHOULD NOT be shipped before gap-16 is addressed.' Spec 08 implementation target (frontmatter): 'v3.2+ (state_admin commands, agent contracts, and daemon hooks are downstream chains).' OPERATOR-MEDIATION-LOG.md Event 11 identifies gap-16 as a 'v3.2 candidate.' If both the adjudicate command and gap-16 are v3.2 work, the SHOULD NOT constraint has no binding effect: it does not block a v3.1 shipment (spec is not v3.1 scope), and a v3.2 implementer would trivially satisfy it by resolving both in the same implementation sprint. The constraint as written neither enforces sequencing nor provides a deferral gate."
          },
          {
            "id": "F12",
            "severity": "advisory",
            "claim": "The BAO claim for `feedback-round-orchestrator` omits the mandatory four-bounds enumeration required by the BAO primitive spec.",
            "evidence": "Spec 08, agent table: 'feedback-round-orchestrator | Phase transitions + coordination | BAO instance over the feedback-round surface (downstream); operator-driven in v1.' surfaces/_primitives/bounded-authority-orchestrator.md \u00c2\u00a7'The four bounds (MUST hold for every BAO instance)': 'When the BAO pattern is invoked in agent contracts or substrate documentation, the four bounding properties MUST be consistently listed. Readings of \"bounded-authority\" that omit any of these four risk under-specifying the pattern.' Spec 08 does not enumerate the four bounds (surface scope, substrate enforcement, audit-chain visibility, no substrate-level privilege) for the feedback-round-orchestrator BAO claim. The retro surface-spec.md sets the pattern: it lists the BAO in the agent table and the 'Substrate primitives' section with an explicit link to the primitive doc. Spec 08's reference is thinner."
          },
          {
            "id": "F13",
            "severity": "advisory",
            "claim": "No operator path is specified for re-entering Phase 06-implement after Phase 07-reconcile records reconciliation gaps.",
            "evidence": "Spec 08, 'feedback-reconciler' subsection: 'MUST NOT propose fixes; a reconciliation_gap triggers a new implementation chain.' Anti-pattern AP-3: 'Items with `reconciliation_status: gap` block the `close` command.' The operator commands section defines 10 commands: `init`, `phase-transition`, `decompose`, `map`, `adjudicate`, `implement`, `reconcile`, `close`, `forward-track`, `status`, `list`. None of these describe re-entering Phase 06 from Phase 07 after gaps are found \u00e2\u20ac\u201d there is no `reopen`, no ability to add implementation_task_ids to a gapped item after Phase 07 runs, and no cycle back from 07 to 06 in the phase table. The resolution path for a gap is 'new implementation chain' but the mechanism for linking that new chain back to the round and re-running reconciliation is absent."
          },
          {
            "id": "F14",
            "severity": "advisory",
            "claim": "`@context: \"https://fnsr.io/feedback-round/v0.1\"` is an unregistered URI with no precedent in the existing codebase.",
            "evidence": "Spec 08, 'Top-level shape' section: '\"@context\": \"https://fnsr.io/feedback-round/v0.1\"'. Searching the codebase (state.jsonld, retros/, surfaces/), no existing state file uses `https://fnsr.io/` as a JSON-LD context base. `RETRO_STATE.jsonld` does not declare a `@context` URI in the retro surface-spec.md; the substrate relies on its own schema rather than an externally-resolvable context. The `fnsr.io` domain is not registered anywhere in the codebase. If the context URI is meant to be informational-only (non-dereferenceable), the spec should note that; if it's meant to be dereferenceable, a registration path is needed."
          }
        ],
        "summary": "The draft Spec 08 is empirically well-motivated: J1/J2 decomposition loss is confirmed by WALKTHROUGH-PHASE-3.md (J1 landed, J2 absent), and the three-guarantee structure (atomic decomposition before adjudication, completeness map before implementation, reconciliation after) directly addresses the observed failure mode. The eight-phase protocol, STATE.jsonld shape, and Spec 07 integration intent are structurally sound. Two blocking issues prevent implementation: (F1) the spec conflates operator-level item adjudication (ratify/amend/defer scoping decisions) with architect Pass 2a ratification (implementation chain gating) in Phase 05 without defining the authority boundary or the `adjudicated_by` field; and (F2) the `kind` field is assigned to two different phases by two different actors with no merge rule. Four major issues add schema extension risk: `subject.type: feedback-round-item` and `declaration_kind: operator_deliberate_deferral` both extend Spec 07 audit event schemas without acknowledgment or CLI update notes (F3, F4); `reconciliation_status: skipped` is an undefined dangling enum value (F6); and the two 'Integration with Spec 07' sections duplicate phase-boundary sequencing material with different normative weights (F7). The empirical motivation section inaccurately cites Events 9 and 12 as informing the anti-patterns section when AP-5 cites Event 11 and no anti-pattern references Events 9 or 12 (F5). Minor conformance issues include file naming deviation from the `surface-spec.md` convention (F8), non-conformant frontmatter fields (F9), and missing provenance section (F10).",
        "recommendation": "revise"
      },
      "depends_on": [
        "urn:fnsr:task:304-dev-spec-08"
      ],
      "inputs": {
        "task_context": "Structural + ontological + conformance review of FNSR Spec 08 draft (task 304's proposed surfaces/feedback-rounds/spec.md).",
        "output_envelope_constraint": "Output wrapped: outputs.findings[], outputs.summary, outputs.recommendation.",
        "goal": "Review the proposed Spec 08 draft. Identify structural gaps, contradictions with prior FNSR specs (02, 03, 05, 06, 07), ontological inconsistencies (banking vs forward-track semantics; phase vs cycle vs feedback-round semantics), and conformance issues (FNSR spec conventions; frontmatter; section ordering).",
        "review_dimensions": [
          "Structural: section completeness; phase-order coherence; agent-role bindings clear",
          "Ontological: does Spec 08 introduce any concept that overlaps or contradicts Spec 05 banking / Spec 07 forward-track / Spec 03 Pass 2a / retro-surface phases? If so, identify the disambiguation",
          "Conformance: matches existing FNSR spec frontmatter + body conventions",
          "Empirical-grounding: are the anti-pattern claims (premature bundling, lost completeness map) grounded in the demo/FEEDBACK.md + OPERATOR-MEDIATION-LOG.md evidence the spec cites?",
          "Operational: can an operator actually run this protocol with the proposed commands + state shape? Are there gaps where a phase has no clear initiator or terminator?"
        ]
