        "summary": "surfaces/feedback-rounds/spec.md at v0.1 (315 lines) has fourteen directly observable issues organized in three clusters. Structural authority/semantics gaps: Phase 05 exit criteria attribute the adjudication decision to the operator (line 53) while the Agent roles table attributes 'adjudication ratification decisions' to the architect (line 69), creating an unresolved authority boundary (F1); the `amend` adjudication value appears in item shape, event schema, and CLI but is never procedurally defined relative to the Phase 06 implementation chain (F2); and Phase 07 mentions that a reconciliation_gap 'triggers a new implementation chain' (line 84) but provides no formal loop-back to Phase 06, no re-entry state definition, and no phase-state reset description (F13). Schema extension gaps: `subject.type: feedback-round-item` (line 207) is not in Spec 07's registered enum (`banking|fixture|capability|candidacy|other`) (F3); `declaration_kind: operator_deliberate_deferral` (line 207) is not in state_admin.py's registered values (F4); the BAO invocation at line 60 names only bound #4 while the BAO primitive doc requires all four to be consistently listed (F12); `adjudicated_by` is required in the `item_adjudicated` event (line 148) but the corresponding CLI command has no `--by` flag (F6); and `feedback_round_closed` (line 151) omits `items_amended` despite `amend` being a valid adjudication outcome (F7). Surface-spec conformance gaps: the file is named `spec.md` while both existing surfaces use `surface-spec.md` (F8); frontmatter contains three non-conformant fields \u00e2\u20ac\u201d `document_kind`, `spec_number`, `version` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d absent from retro and verification surface specs (F9, lines 3-5); Events 9 and 12 are cited as informing the anti-patterns section (line 41) but no AP addresses either event's pattern, and the cited 'scope_constraints' section does not exist (F5); no `## Provenance` section exists per the Routing and primitive-doc convention (F10); Open Questions item 5 cites 'Recon finding F1' and 'recon F4' without anchor task @ids (F11, line 301); and the STATE.jsonld `@context` URI `https://fnsr.io/feedback-round/v0.1` (line 96) is inconsistent with both the `fnsr.example` placeholder domain and the `urn:fnsr:` URN scheme used by the retro state (F14). Task 305 (spec-reviewer) and 306 (architect) outputs were absent from UPSTREAM; the F-number assignments above for F2, F6, F7, and F11 are inferred from available evidence since the authoritative F-list was not accessible.",
