        "summary": "All 14 findings from the prior review (F1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cF14) are resolved cleanly in v0.2. F1 (Phase 05 split + two-actor adjudicated_by): correctly split into 05a/05b with authority-boundary prose and correct CLI flag. F2 (provisional_kind + merge rule): field added to item shape, merge rule documented, audit event and agent role table updated consistently. F3/F4 (schema extensions): dedicated Schema Extensions section registers subject.type:feedback-round-item and declaration_kind:operator_deliberate_deferral with transitional notes. F5 (empirical motivation + AP-6): Events 9 and 12 now explicitly point to AP-6; AP-6 added with correct awaiting_operator_decision contract. F6 (skipped semantics): item shape annotation block with MUST normative language. F7 (Spec 07 integration merge): two sections collapsed into one with three subsections and MUST throughout. F8 (file rename): surface-spec.md created as new file; spec.md frontmatter tombstoned \u00e2\u20ac\u201d minor residue risk (v0.1 body retained below redirect). F9 (frontmatter): document_kind/spec_number/version dropped; matches retro/verification convention confirmed by file read. F10 (Provenance): section added with seven entries. F11 (AP-5 framing + OQ-5 cleanup): bypass-reliance anti-pattern framing correct; internal review references removed from OQ-5. F12 (all four BAO bounds): enumerated in numbered list matching the canonical BAO primitive doc exactly. F13 (re-entry section): five-step operator workflow, sub-cycle framing, append-only audit-trail note, close-gate rule all present. F14 (@context): urn:fnsr: scheme adopted with explanatory note and OQ-7 for operator confirmation. Two new items flagged: ND-1 (items_amended absent from feedback_round_closed \u00e2\u20ac\u201d correctly deferred as OQ-9 but is a functional implementer gap) and ND-2 (amend flow undefined \u00e2\u20ac\u201d correctly deferred as OQ-8). Minor precision issue: Provenance cites 'Events 9--12' but Event 10 has no explicit body citation. AP-5 mitigation uses SHOULD NOT where MUST NOT may be warranted given gap-16 severity.",
