        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposed change creates a new surface-spec.md file with comprehensive structural revisions addressing 14 recon findings \u00e2\u20ac\u201d including phase splits, schema extensions, authority boundary definitions, new sections, and filename convention correction \u00e2\u20ac\u201d which is substantive spec authorship, not editorial tightening of existing text.",
        "rationale": "All preconditions for ratification are satisfied. Reconnaissance (urn:fnsr:task:308-recon-spec-08-v02) is present in UPSTREAM with 14 documented findings (F1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cF14) grounded in file paths and line ranges. The developer's proposed changes (C1: new surfaces/feedback-rounds/surface-spec.md; C2: spec.md tombstone) address all 14 findings. The reviewer (urn:fnsr:task:310-review-spec-08-v02) confirms each finding resolved at advisory severity or better and issues recommendation: accept. No blocking defects are reintroduced.\n\nFinding-by-finding confirmation:\n- F1 (Phase 05 authority split): C1 splits into 05a-adjudicate-scope (operator scoping) and 05b-adjudicate-gate (architect Pass 2a), with clear authority-boundary prose, two-actor adjudicated_by field, and --adjudicated-by CLI flag. Reviewer: advisory only (no machine-enforced 05a\u00e2\u2020\u201905b gate in v1 operator-driven model \u00e2\u20ac\u201d acceptable).\n- F2 (provisional_kind + merge rule): provisional_kind field added to item shape; merge rule block normative with MUST language; atomic_item_decomposed audit event updated. Reviewer: advisory only.\n- F3 (subject.type: feedback-round-item): Schema Extensions section added registering feedback-round-item as new Spec 07 subject.type value with transitional --subject-type other note. Reviewer: advisory only.\n- F4 (declaration_kind: operator_deliberate_deferral): Schema Extensions section registers operator_deliberate_deferral with open-string framing consistent with existing substrate practice. Reviewer: advisory only.\n- F5 (Events 9/12 citation accuracy + AP-6): Empirical motivation now cites AP-6 specifically; AP-6 added covering Events 9 and 12 escalation-shape failure pattern. Non-existent 'scope_constraints' reference removed. Reviewer: advisory only (Event 10 imprecision in range citation '9--12').\n- F6 (adjudicated_by CLI flag + reconciliation_status:skipped): Recon F6 (adjudicated_by CLI) addressed as part of F1 fix (--adjudicated-by flag added; developer confirmed in OQ). Skipped semantics annotated with MUST normative language. Reviewer: advisory only.\n- F7 (Spec 07 integration sections merged): Two prior Integration sections merged into one with three subsections and MUST normative language throughout. Reviewer: advisory only.\n- F8 (surface-spec.md rename): C1 creates surfaces/feedback-rounds/surface-spec.md (before: null); C2 tombstones spec.md frontmatter. Reviewer: minor (v0.1 body retained below tombstone per applier replace-not-delete semantics \u00e2\u20ac\u201d acknowledged and unambiguous).\n- F9 (frontmatter conformance): document_kind/spec_number/version dropped; frontmatter matches retro/verification peer convention. Reviewer: advisory only.\n- F10 (Provenance section): Provenance section added with seven entries. Reviewer: advisory only (Event 10 range precision, same as F5).\n- F11 (AP-5 framing + OQ-5 internal reference cleanup): AP-5 reframed as 'Reliance on bypass behavior' without bypass-as-workaround proposal; OQ-5 internal recon references removed and replaced with substantive text. Reviewer: advisory only (SHOULD NOT vs MUST NOT normative level in AP-5 mitigation).\n- F12 (all four BAO bounds): All four bounds enumerated in numbered list matching bounded-authority-orchestrator.md \u00c2\u00a7'The four bounds' exactly (Surface scope, Substrate enforcement, Audit-chain visibility, No substrate-level privilege). Reviewer: advisory only.\n- F13 (Phase 06 re-entry): New '## Phase 06 re-entry after reconciliation gap' section with five-step operator workflow, sub-cycle framing (round does not reset to 06-implement), append-only audit-trail note, and close-gate rule. Reviewer: advisory only.\n- F14 (@context scheme): @context changed to urn:fnsr:feedback-round:v0.1 with explanatory note and OQ-7 for operator confirmation. Reviewer: advisory only.\n\nTwo new items flagged by reviewer: ND-1 (items_amended absent from feedback_round_closed \u00e2\u20ac\u201d deferred to OQ-9, minor, non-blocking) and ND-2 (amend flow undefined in Phase 06 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d deferred to OQ-8, advisory, non-blocking). Both are correctly scoped to open questions given that implementation is downstream v3.2+ work.\n\nEvent 11 / daemon-side gap acknowledgment (per task inputs review_focus): AP-5 in C1 explicitly states 'architect denial does not currently block downstream applier dispatch because the daemon checks task status rather than outputs.ruling' and labels this as gap-16 (v3.2 candidate). The v0.1 workaround proposal (outputs.error: ratification_denied) is removed. The daemon-side gap mechanism is named, versioned, and framed as operator-discipline backstop \u00e2\u20ac\u201d not a design constraint.\n\nNo ADR-NNN citations appear in C1 content destined for surfaces/ canonical path; ADR-citation CPS check will pass. The file path surfaces/feedback-rounds/surface-spec.md is within the surfaces/ canonical prefix per CLAUDE.md \u00c2\u00a77.5. The proposed before: null new-file creation pattern is consistent with prior surface-spec authoring.\n\nThe v0.1 architect denial (task 306) was based on absent reconnaissance; the v0.2 cycle supplies that reconnaissance (task 308). The chain shape is correct: reconnaissance \u00e2\u2020\u2019 developer \u00e2\u2020\u2019 reviewer \u00e2\u2020\u2019 ratification.",
        "referenced_evidence": [
