        "summary": "Round 3 feedback from Aaron (2026-05-22, commit 32af9c9) yields 12 atomic claims across four live sections (Section 3 was 'Perfect'). Section 1 produces four claims: banner tone is too aggressive (R3-S1-01); New button should open a Title+Subject popup (R3-S1-02); Aaron's design philosophy is prevent-not-report (R3-S1-03); and the ValidationPanel does not re-validate when the realist anchor is added via Project Settings \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a confirmed bug where `validate()` is called in `handleNew`/`handleFileChange` but not in the `ProjectSettingsDialog.onSave` handler (R3-S1-04). Section 2 produces five claims: newly created instance labels are hardcoded to 'New Instance' with no edit affordance, meaning FR-U012 is unimplemented (R3-S2-01); relation edges have no visible predicate label on the canvas (R3-S2-02); React Flow connection handles are locked to one directionality so users cannot draw top-to-top or bottom-to-bottom relations (R3-S2-03); the relation inspector correctly resolves the current label but shows 'New Instance' with no in-context edit path (R3-S2-04, downstream of R3-S2-01); and the FR-C008 narration shows empty class parentheses for classless instances (R3-S2-05). Section 4 produces two claims: the existing CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION check tests the term's IRI against reserved IRIs but does not check whether the label text matches a canonical property name (R3-S4-01); and Aaron explicitly rejects the collision-detection-first approach in favor of pre-populating ~20\u00e2\u20ac\u201c30 standard RDFS+OWL+XSD terms as starter vocabulary \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a recurrence of Round 1 Item J's provision half that was lost at the Round 1 bundling stage (R3-S4-02). Section 5 produces one claim: the `iao:` prefix in SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.2, VMP_CONTEXT, turtle.ts PREFIX_MAP, and tbox/index.ts all bind to `http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao#`, causing `iao:isAbout` to expand to `http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao#isAbout` rather than the canonical IAO IRI `http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136` as identified by Aaron's coworker (R3-S5-01). The most immediately actionable item is R3-S1-04 (stale validation panel \u00e2\u20ac\u201d trivial one-line fix). The most structurally significant are R3-S5-01 (requires @context amendment propagating to canonicalize.ts/turtle.ts/tbox/index.ts/golden files), R3-S4-02 (requires new starter-terms provision infrastructure), and R3-S2-01 (FR-U012 implementation of instance label edit).",
