        "open_questions": [
          "R3-S5-01: The canonical fix for iao:isAbout IRI requires changing the `iao:` prefix namespace. However the TBox also uses `iao:OntologyDesignPattern` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a spec-introduced term that has no OBO numbered ID. If `iao:` is changed to the OBO base namespace (`http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/`), then `iao:isAbout` would resolve to `http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/isAbout` (still wrong). The correct IRI `http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136` cannot be constructed via any prefix that also supports `iao:OntologyDesignPattern`. Operator must decide: (a) use two separate prefix bindings (one for OBO numbered terms, one for spec-introduced iao: terms), (b) remove the `iao:` prefix and use full IRIs for both `iao:isAbout` and `iao:OntologyDesignPattern`, or (c) some other approach.",
          "R3-S1-03 vs R3-S1-01/R3-S2: Aaron's 'no more errors' philosophy conflicts with SPEC \u00c2\u00a717.1 which specifies three severity levels including error. Operator must decide whether \u00c2\u00a717.1 needs amendment (removing hard errors in favor of guided resolution flows) or whether R3-S1-01/R3-S1-02 are sufficient implementation-level responses that satisfy the intent without changing the spec.",
          "R3-S2-05: Is the correct fix (a) prompt for class assignment at instance creation time (FR-U011 amendment), (b) add a narration fallback label for classless instances, or (c) implement the INSTANCE_WITHOUT_CLASS validation warning (\u00c2\u00a717.3, currently unimplemented) and let the user assign the class themselves? Operator must adjudicate.",
          "R3-S4-02 vs R3-S4-01: Aaron says he does not want the collision-detection functionality AT ALL and wants pre-populated defaults instead. Operator must decide whether to keep the existing IRI-based collision check (keep and enhance with R3-S4-01 label-text check), remove it entirely once R3-S4-02 starter terms are in place, or keep both."
        ],
