        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposed change creates a new 12-item analytical document with per-item kind classifications, effort estimates, priority assignments, completeness maps, dependency chains, prior-round cross-references, and an operator adjudication table \u00e2\u20ac\u201d new analytical content, not a typo fix, formatting adjustment, or terminology tightening.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM (urn:fnsr:task:313-recon-r3) with 12 grounded findings, 4 open questions, and evidence paths across all relevant source modules. The proposed demo/FEEDBACK-ROUND-3-DECOMPOSITION.md (urn:fnsr:task:314-dev-r3-decomposition, change C1, before: null) passes all review focus criteria:\n\n**Atomic decomposition rigor:** All 12 items are genuinely single-claim. R3-S1-03 (design philosophy) is correctly separated from R3-S1-01 (banner tone) and R3-S1-02 (modal) despite governing both \u00e2\u20ac\u201d it has its own spec impact (possible \u00c2\u00a717.1 amendment) and its own adjudication gate. R3-S2-04 (inspector labels) is correctly separated from R3-S2-01 (instance label edit) and tagged as a downstream side-effect. No bundling found.\n\n**Completeness map coverage:** Every item carries all eight artifact-class slots (SPEC sections, FR numbers, source modules, spec tests, Playwright tests, demo materials, ROADMAP, IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN). Slot population is appropriate \u00e2\u20ac\u201d some slots are legitimately empty (e.g., R3-S1-01 has no demo materials) with the vacancy itself informative. High-risk items (R3-S5-01, R3-S4-02) carry golden-file and test re-baseline entries in the map.\n\n**No Item-J-style provision/prevention bundling:** R3-S4-01 (IRI-only check, missing label-text coverage) and R3-S4-02 (pre-populate starter vocabulary) are split exactly as Round 1 Item J was NOT \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the provision half and prevention half are separate atomic items with their own evidence, completeness maps, and adjudication rows. The document explicitly calls this out as the recurrence that motivated Spec 08 discipline.\n\n**Section coverage:** Section 1 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 4 items (R3-S1-01 through R3-S1-04), Section 2 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 5 items (R3-S2-01 through R3-S2-05), Section 3 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 0 items (verbatim 'Perfect'), Section 4 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 2 items (R3-S4-01, R3-S4-02), Section 5 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 1 item (R3-S5-01). Cross-checked against demo/FEEDBACK-ROUND-3.md verbatim. No claims dropped, no scope inflation.\n\n**Daemon-side gate consequence (Event 11 lesson):** The proposed change is before: null \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a new file creation. Denial here produces a clean no-op: the file is not created, the operator revises the decomposition, and re-queues. There is no pre-existing artifact in a wrong state, no partial apply, and no downstream task blocked on incorrect content. The daemon-side ratification gate is not being used as a compensating control for a structural risk \u00e2\u20ac\u201d it is functioning correctly as a quality gate on a new artifact.\n\n**Prior-round cross-references verified:** R3-S2-04 correctly cites Round 1 Quick-1 (canvas node labels) as the source fix whose label value propagates to the inspector. R3-S4-02 correctly cites demo/FEEDBACK.md lines 172\u00e2\u20ac\u201c173 and demo/FEEDBACK-RESPONSE.md lines 172\u00e2\u20ac\u201c178 as the Round 1 Item J provision-half \u00e2\u20ac\u201d verified against source files; the bundling and loss are accurately characterized.\n\n**Open questions correctly scoped:** 4 questions flagged (R3-S1-03 spec amendment scope; R3-S2-05 fix shape; R3-S4-01 vs R3-S4-02 fate; R3-S5-01 prefix strategy). Each blocks Phase 06 dispatch for its dependent items; none prematurely blocks the decomposition document from landing.\n\n**One advisory note:** R3-S4-01 is rated P3 Phase-4+ in the priority table, but the adjudication table footnote says it should be adjudicated jointly with R3-S4-02 (P2). If the operator adjudicates R3-S4-02 by removing the IRI check, R3-S4-01 becomes moot before its Phase 06 chain is ever queued \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the dependency note in R3-S4-01 correctly captures this. No structural correction needed.\n\nRuling: ratified. The document is structurally sound, evidence-grounded, atomically decomposed, and ready for Phase 05a operator adjudication.",
