            "content": "The Spec 08 decomposition artifact introduces a 'recurrence-of-prior-item' item kind (used for R3-S2-04 and R3-S4-02) that makes prior-round cross-references machine-readable at the decomposition layer. This kind designation \u00e2\u20ac\u201d with an explicit citation to the originating round's item ID and source lines \u00e2\u20ac\u201d provides a mechanism for tracking which requirements were lost during prior-round bundling and re-surfaced in later rounds. This pattern should be considered for formalization in Spec 08's item-kind taxonomy: the 'recurrence-of-prior-item' kind signals that Phase 07 reconciliation must verify not just that the current-round implementation landed, but that the prior-round omission is also addressed."
