        ],
        "summary": "Chain \u00ce\u00b1 (R3-S1-01 through S1-04) targets four touchpoints, all in src/ui/App.tsx plus the two downstream components. For S1-01: the exact accusatory text strings are 'This project needs a subject \u00e2\u20ac\u201d what real-world thing is it about? Export is blocked until a subject is added.' (missing state, App.tsx:299) and 'This project has a placeholder subject from v0.3 migration. Replace it with a real subject IRI.' (legacy state, App.tsx:300); button labels are 'Set subject' and 'Set real subject'. For S1-02: handleNew() (App.tsx:101-106) has no parameters, calls buildNewDocument() directly, and sets project state immediately \u00e2\u20ac\u201d NewProjectDialog.tsx does not exist and must be created; Dialog.tsx (src/ui/Dialog.tsx) is a ready reusable primitive already used by ProjectSettingsDialog. For S1-04 root cause: ValidationPanel.tsx is purely prop-driven (findings prop, no internal state or useEffect); the onSave callback in App.tsx (lines 349-352) calls setProject(updated) but omits setValidationReport(validate(updated)), leaving the panel stale; the banner correctly clears (it derives from project state reactively) while the panel does not. Three other mutation callbacks (TermSidebar, CanvasView, Inspector) show the same omission pattern. For the S1-03 open question on banner retention: the banner has two branches (missing / legacy); even if NewProjectDialog prevents the missing state for new projects, the legacy branch will still fire for opened v0.3 migrated files. On the test side: new-open-save.spec.ts AC2, smoke.spec.ts flows 1 and 4, and isabout-ui.spec.ts AC1/AC3/AC4 all click gw-btn-new and immediately assert project-active state or banner presence without any dialog interaction; all are affected by R3-S1-02. validation-panel.spec.ts has no test covering the onSave re-validate path (the S1-04 fix path).",
