      "outputs": {
        "ruling": "ratified",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposal creates a new React component (NewProjectDialog.tsx), redesigns the anchor-banner UX affordance, changes test behavioral flows (dialog interaction steps inserted), and adds a new Playwright regression test \u00e2\u20ac\u201d none of which are typo, formatting, terminology-tightening, or citation-format changes.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance task urn:fnsr:task:317-recon-r3-alpha is present in UPSTREAM and provides the grounding evidence for all four items. The developer's 16-change proposal (C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC16) across six files correctly and completely addresses every atomic item in Chain \u00ce\u00b1.\n\n**S1-01 (accusatory banner \u00e2\u2020\u2019 soft guidance):** C5 replaces the single `gw-anchor-banner` block (which carried error-framing text and data-testid=gw-btn-anchor-action) with two distinct muted soft-guidance elements \u00e2\u20ac\u201d `gw-subject-guidance` for the 'missing' state and `gw-subject-guidance-legacy` for the 'legacy' state. Both elements use text-link affordances into Project Settings rather than button-chrome. C8 adds the required CSS. Verified against App.tsx lines 291\u00e2\u20ac\u201c310 and App.css lines 410\u00e2\u20ac\u201c416 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d before-snippets match exactly.\n\n**S1-02 (NewProjectDialog):** C1 creates NewProjectDialog.tsx as a new file (before: null) using the Dialog.tsx primitive already confirmed by reconnaissance F9. The component provides Title field (defaulting to 'Untitled Project'), Subject IRI field (placeholder URL, optional), 'Create Project' submit, and 'Skip \u00e2\u20ac\u201d use placeholder' secondary action. C2 imports it; C3 adds newProjectDialogOpen state; C4 refactors handleNew() to open the dialog and provides handleNewConfirm (creates with user-entered title/ecm:name and subject IRI override) and handleNewSkip (creates with defaults); C7 mounts the component. This matches FR-U001's MUST-prompt behavior (modal at creation time) per the decomposition completeness map and the operator's ratification of S1-02.\n\n**S1-03 (UX-layer-only; no SPEC \u00c2\u00a717 amendment):** Verified that none of C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC16 touch project/SPEC.md. All changes are confined to src/ui/ and tests/playwright/. SPEC \u00c2\u00a717 (MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR error code and severity levels) is unchanged, consistent with the operator adjudication of open question 1 answer (b): 'implementation-level UX changes satisfy the intent; \u00c2\u00a717 stays unchanged.' There is a deliberate and operator-sanctioned spec-implementation gap: FR-U001 still carries SHOULD-level language while the implementation now enforces a MUST modal \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this is correct for Chain \u00ce\u00b1; a separate spec-amendment chain would close the FR-U001 language gap if the operator elects to pursue it.\n\n**S1-04 (re-validate on ALL mutation paths):** Verified all project-mutation call-sites in App.tsx:\n- handleNew \u00e2\u2020\u2019 C4 handleNewConfirm and handleNewSkip both call setValidationReport(validate(...)) \u00e2\u0153\u201c\n- handleFileChange (lines 114\u00e2\u20ac\u201c169) already called setValidationReport at line 154 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d not modified, no gap \u00e2\u0153\u201c\n- ProjectSettingsDialog onSave \u00e2\u2020\u2019 C7 adds setValidationReport(validate(updated)) \u00e2\u0153\u201c (direct fix for the reported bug, confirmed by recon F6)\n- TermSidebar onTermsChange \u00e2\u2020\u2019 C6 adds setValidationReport(validate(updated)) \u00e2\u0153\u201c (recon F7)\n- CanvasView onProjectChange \u00e2\u2020\u2019 C6 adds setValidationReport(validate(updated)) \u00e2\u0153\u201c (recon F7)\n- Inspector onProjectChange \u00e2\u2020\u2019 C6 adds setValidationReport(validate(updated)) \u00e2\u0153\u201c (recon F7)\n- handleAcknowledge \u00e2\u2020\u2019 correctly excluded from C6; it calls setValidationReport directly with an acknowledged-flags-updated report, not via child component props, so C6 does not interfere; calling validate() there would wipe acknowledged flags (developer's open_question reasoning verified as correct)\n\n**Test updates:** C9 (new-open-save AC2 skip path), C10 (S1-04 regression: ValidationPanel clears MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR after Project Settings save), C11 (smoke flow 1 step 1), C12 (smoke flow 4 redesigned: banner \u00e2\u2020\u2019 guidance), C13 (isabout-ui AC1), C14 (isabout-ui AC2), C15 (isabout-ui AC3 with added pre-declaration guidance assertion), C16 (isabout-ui AC4 legacy testids) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d all affected tests updated. The validation-panel.spec.ts suite is unaffected because it uses file-fixture beforeEach (gw-file-input, not gw-btn-new) and does not assert gw-anchor-banner. The data-code='MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR' attribute used in C10 is confirmed present: ValidationPanel.tsx line 72 sets data-code={code}, and validate/codes.ts exports MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR as the exact string 'MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR'. No gap.\n\nAll before-snippets verified against live files at the time of this ratification. No SPEC changes. No kernel layer violations. Chain \u00ce\u00b1 is self-contained with respect to Chains \u00ce\u00b2, \u00ce\u00b3, \u00ce\u00b4.",
