            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F6",
            "claim": "The `turtle.ts` `expandIri` function expands compact IRIs by looking up the prefix (left of `:`) in `PREFIX_MAP` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d it has no alias-resolution logic and does not consult `VMP_CONTEXT`. Applying `expandIri(\"iao:isAbout\")` under the current binding yields `http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao#isAbout`, and this calculation is independent of VMP_CONTEXT changes.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/emit/turtle.ts",
                "lines": "47-52",
                "excerpt": "function expandIri(compact: string): string {\n  const colon = compact.indexOf(\":\");\n  if (colon <= 0) return compact;\n  const ns = PREFIX_MAP[compact.slice(0, colon)];\n  return ns !== undefined ? ns + compact.slice(colon + 1) : compact;\n}"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F7",
            "claim": "Under option \u00ce\u00b1 (keep `\"iao:isAbout\"` as the JSON property key but add a `@id` alias binding in VMP_CONTEXT to `obo:IAO_0000136`), the Turtle emitter at line 181 would still produce the wrong RDF predicate IRI because `expandIri(\"iao:isAbout\")` resolves via `PREFIX_MAP[\"iao\"]`, not through the JSON-LD alias. Correct Turtle output under option \u00ce\u00b1 would require either: (a) changing the predicate string in the iteration loop from `\"iao:isAbout\"` to `\"obo:IAO_0000136\"` while also adding `obo:` to PREFIX_MAP, or (b) giving `expandIri` alias-resolution capability against VMP_CONTEXT.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/emit/turtle.ts",
                "lines": "181",
                "excerpt": "for (const pred of [\"rdfs:subClassOf\", \"rdfs:subPropertyOf\", \"iao:isAbout\", \"ecm:isSerializationOf\"]) {"
