        "summary": "The `iao:` prefix is currently bound to `http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao#` in four normative locations (SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.2, VMP_CONTEXT in canonicalize.ts, PREFIX_MAP in turtle.ts, and the Turtle @prefix block in tbox/index.ts), causing `iao:isAbout` to expand to the wrong IRI `http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao#isAbout` rather than the canonical IAO term `http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136`. The property key `\"iao:isAbout\"` is used as a literal string in twelve source-code locations (validate, migrate, canonicalize LEX_SORTED_ARRAY_KEYS, projection predicate allowlist, turtle nodeToQuads loop, markdown emitter, UI) and in at least 29 test assertion sites across nine test files \u00e2\u20ac\u201d none of these sites perform prefix expansion. The term `\"iao:OntologyDesignPattern\"` (slated for re-homing to `ecm:OntologyDesignPattern` per Aaron's adjudication) appears as a literal string in six source locations and in the tbox-bundle test's IRI constant and assertions. Nine fixture files contain `\"iao:isAbout\"` as a JSON property key; eight also embed the erroneous `iao:` prefix binding in their `@context` block. Under option \u00ce\u00b1 (keep `\"iao:isAbout\"` as property key; add `@id` alias in VMP_CONTEXT), fixtures and almost all test code require no property-key changes \u00e2\u20ac\u201d but the Turtle emitter's `expandIri(\"iao:isAbout\")` still resolves via PREFIX_MAP and would produce the wrong IRI unless the predicate string in the `nodeToQuads` loop is changed to `\"obo:IAO_0000136\"` (or `expandIri` gains alias-resolution). Under option \u00ce\u00b2 (rename key to `\"obo:IAO_0000136\"`), all nine fixtures, all 29 test assertion sites, and all twelve source locations must be updated. No ADR entry exists for the `iao:` prefix IRI choice. The SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.14 note and \u00c2\u00a75.2 prose both contain rationale referencing `iao:OntologyDesignPattern` by name that will need updating after re-homing.",
