        "open_questions": [
          "C61 SPEC.md TBox vs C7 src/tbox/index.ts byte-identity (recon F22): the applier will apply C61 and C7 independently; the operator must verify the Turtle text in SPEC.md (within the code fence) matches PROJECT_TBOX_TURTLE in src/tbox/index.ts after both changes land. A CI check or snapshot test enforcing this identity is recommended.",
          "C50 normalize-on-load NON_CANONICAL_DOC type order: after this change the non-canonical input is [ecm:Project, ecm:OntologyDesignPattern] and the canonical output is [ecm:OntologyDesignPattern, ecm:Project]. The test relies on serializeVmp producing the canonical sort. Operator should confirm no other assertion in normalize-on-load.test.ts hard-codes [iao:OntologyDesignPattern, ecm:Project] as an expected output string.",
          "C61 SPEC.md code fence: the before snippet includes the triple-backtick fence markers. The applier must not interpret backticks as Markdown; confirm the applier applies raw string replacement, not Markdown-aware replacement.",
          "Migration (src/migrate/index.ts C9): the summary records that migrate() sets type to ['ecm:Project', 'iao:OntologyDesignPattern'] for v0.3->v0.4 leg. After C9 changes this to ['ecm:Project', 'ecm:OntologyDesignPattern'], any stored v0.3 project opened by a user who previously migrated and saved under the old type will no longer be 'canonical' (their file has iao: in type). normalizeOnLoad will catch and re-sort on next open. This is the intended behavior per the re-homing decision; confirm with architect that no explicit migration leg for old-ecm-canonical files is needed."
