    {
      "@id": "urn:fnsr:task:324-rat-r3-delta",
      "agent": "architect",
      "status": "done",
      "attempts": 1,
      "outputs": {
        "ruling": "deferred",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The change renames an OWL class IRI (iao:OntologyDesignPattern \u00e2\u2020\u2019 ecm:OntologyDesignPattern across TBox, type arrays, test fixtures, and SPEC.md), corrects the JSON-LD @context expansion of iao:isAbout to bind it to the canonical IAO IRI http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136 via an obo: prefix alias, and repairs the Turtle emitter's predicate IRI output \u00e2\u20ac\u201d all of which materially alter the RDF graph the system produces and the ontological identity of the project's root class.",
        "rationale": "Ratification is deferred because the complete proposed change set cannot be evaluated from the current UPSTREAM inputs. Task 323-dev-r3-delta's output contains only C38\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC63 (26 changes covering unit-test type-array constants, SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.2/\u00c2\u00a75.4/\u00c2\u00a75.14 rewrites, and DECISIONS.md ADR-007). The developer summary explicitly states these are a 'continuation' of 'prior output C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC37' \u00e2\u20ac\u201d but no upstream task carrying C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC37 exists in the UPSTREAM block, and direct file reads confirm the codebase remains in its pre-fix state throughout.\n\nFile-level evidence of the gap: (1) src/kernel/canonicalize.ts line 72 still declares `iao: 'http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao#'` with no obo: entry, and line 89 has `'iao:isAbout': { '@type': '@id', '@container': '@set' }` with no @id alias \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the recon F1/F2 fixes are absent. (2) src/emit/turtle.ts line 39 still declares `iao: 'http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao#'` in PREFIX_MAP, line 65 still lists `'iao:OntologyDesignPattern'` in TBOX_IDS, and line 181 still routes `'iao:isAbout'` through `expandIri` which expands to the wrong IRI \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the recon F1/F6/F7 fixes and the JSON_KEY_TO_RDF_PRED constant are absent. (3) src/tbox/index.ts still contains the full `iao:OntologyDesignPattern`-based PROJECT_TBOX_TURTLE and getProjectTBoxNodes() \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the recon F5/F22 fixes are absent. (4) src/projection/index.ts line 31 still lists `'iao:OntologyDesignPattern'` in SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST. (5) src/migrate/index.ts line 190 still sets `type: ['ecm:Project', 'iao:OntologyDesignPattern']`. (6) src/ui/App.tsx line 25 still has `type: ['ecm:Project', 'iao:OntologyDesignPattern']` in buildNewDocument(). (7) tests/tbox-bundle.test.ts line 46 still declares `const IRI_ODP = IAO + 'OntologyDesignPattern'` and its six assertions reference this wrong-namespace IRI. (8) All seven Playwright fixture files confirmed at `tests/playwright/fixtures/*.jsonld` still carry `'iao:OntologyDesignPattern'` in their type arrays.\n\nConsequence of the gap for each review-focus criterion:\n\u00e2\u20ac\u201d 'obo: prefix correctly bound to http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/': C56 updates SPEC.md but the canonicalize.ts and turtle.ts PREFIX_MAP entries are unverified (C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC37). NOT CONFIRMABLE.\n\u00e2\u20ac\u201d 'iao:isAbout @context binding correctly resolves to obo:IAO_0000136': C57 updates SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.2 but the canonicalize.ts VMP_CONTEXT @id alias is unverified. NOT CONFIRMABLE.\n\u00e2\u20ac\u201d 'iao:OntologyDesignPattern \u00e2\u2020\u2019 ecm:OntologyDesignPattern propagated consistently (type arrays + tbox + tests + fixtures)': C38\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC55 cover unit-test type constants, but src/tbox, src/projection, src/migrate, App.tsx, tbox-bundle.test.ts, and all Playwright fixtures are unverified. NOT CONFIRMABLE.\n\u00e2\u20ac\u201d 'RDF triples produced via Turtle export are semantically correct': Requires the turtle.ts JSON_KEY_TO_RDF_PRED (or equivalent) fix in C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC37 to redirect `iao:isAbout`'s predicate node to `obo:IAO_0000136` at emit time; C38\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC63 contain no turtle.ts changes. NOT CONFIRMABLE.\n\u00e2\u20ac\u201d 'Fixtures consistent \u00e2\u20ac\u201d every type array using OntologyDesignPattern is updated': Playwright fixture files (`canvas-3i-2r.jsonld`, `canvas-3i-2r-with-ops.jsonld`, `imported-term.jsonld`, `literal-crud-1i-1dp.jsonld`, `term-sidebar-2c-1op-1dp.jsonld`, `term-sidebar-cross-refs.jsonld`, `validation-3-findings.jsonld`) still carry `iao:OntologyDesignPattern`; `test/fixtures/canonical-v0.4/minimal.jsonld` is not updated in C38\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC63. NOT CONFIRMABLE.\n\u00e2\u20ac\u201d 'SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.2 documents the obo: prefix + design decision': C56/C57/C58 correctly address this. CONFIRMABLE.\n\u00e2\u20ac\u201d 'Validator behavior preserved (MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR still fires correctly)': Under option \u00ce\u00b1 the property key `'iao:isAbout'` is unchanged; the validator's literal key lookup is unaffected. CONFIRMABLE (no change required in validate/index.ts).\n\u00e2\u20ac\u201d 'ADR-007 in DECISIONS.md before any SPEC.md citation': C63 adds ADR-007 correctly; SPEC.md changes in C56\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC62 do not introduce an ADR-007 citation string that would trigger the CPS ADR-citation check. CONFIRMABLE.\n\nAdditional concern: C61 updates the SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.14 TBox Turtle block and must be byte-identical to the updated PROJECT_TBOX_TURTLE string in src/tbox/index.ts (recon F22). The tbox/index.ts change is in C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC37 (unverified); byte-identity cannot be confirmed.\n\nApplying C38\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC63 without C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC37 would produce an inconsistent state: test-file type constants reference `ecm:OntologyDesignPattern` while the source code emits `iao:OntologyDesignPattern`, causing immediate test suite failures across tbox-bundle, emitters, semantic-projection, normalize-on-load, and multiple Playwright tests.\n\nForward path: The operator should either (a) produce a new developer task that emits the COMPLETE C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC63 change set in a single UPSTREAM-visible output, then re-queue ratification; or (b) confirm that C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC37 were produced and applied in a prior round (if so, the codebase would already show the fixes \u00e2\u20ac\u201d which it does not), which would make this a brief-confirmation scenario (see Spec 03). Given that the codebase reads confirm neither scenario holds, option (a) is the correct path.",
        "referenced_evidence": [
          {
