        "bankings": [
          {
            "id": "B1",
            "category": "discipline-correction",
            "content": "When a developer task produces a multi-batch change set and the second batch explicitly references 'prior output C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cN' from outside the current task's UPSTREAM, the ratification chain is structurally incomplete: the architect cannot verify the full set of changes, cannot confirm review-focus criteria that depend on source-file fixes in the unverified batch, and cannot evaluate byte-identity constraints between artifacts that span both batches. The discipline correction is: developer tasks that continue a prior output MUST either (a) include the complete change set in a single task output so the full C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cN set is visible in UPSTREAM, or (b) reference a prior developer task @id in depends_on whose outputs carry the first batch, so the orchestrator can inline those outputs into the UPSTREAM block at ratification dispatch time. Producing split-batch outputs across session boundaries without chaining the prior task into depends_on creates an unfillable ratification gap."
          }
        ]
      },
