      "attempts": 1,
      "outputs": {
        "ruling": "ratified",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposed changes alter runtime-behavioral source code: VMP_CONTEXT IRI prefix registrations, JSON-LD @id alias bindings, Turtle PREFIX_MAP entries, TBox class IRI identifiers, SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST membership, migration type-array emissions, and UI document scaffold \u00e2\u20ac\u201d none of these are typo fixes, formatting changes, or terminology tightening; they change how the system expands IRIs, what RDF triples it emits, and which type strings nodes carry.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM (urn:fnsr:task:327-recon-r3-delta-2). All 25 proposed changes (C1a\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC18) are directly grounded in one or more of the 22 reconnaissance findings.\n\nC1a/C1b (canonicalize.ts VMP_CONTEXT): F6 confirms the two required mutations \u00e2\u20ac\u201d swap `iao:` for `obo:` prefix (line 72) and add `\"@id\": \"obo:IAO_0000136\"` to the `iao:isAbout` term entry (line 89). These exactly match ADR-007's stated decision and SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.2 lines 285\u00e2\u20ac\u201c319 (as verified by F1).\n\nC2a\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC2e (turtle.ts): F7 confirms PREFIX_MAP has `iao:` at line 39 and TBOX_IDS has `\"iao:OntologyDesignPattern\"` at line 65. F19 establishes the inference that dropping `iao:` from PREFIX_MAP breaks `expandIri(\"iao:isAbout\")` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d making the JSON_KEY_TO_RDF_PRED side-table (C2c) a necessary correctness fix, not an over-engineering. C2d routes the predicate through this table before `expandIri()`. C2e updates the JSDoc duplicate-prefix count from 5 to 4 (verified: TBox after C3a has ecm, cco, owl, rdfs = 4; net-new from emitter = rdf, xsd, obo = 3 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d arithmetic is correct).\n\nC3a/C3b (tbox/index.ts): F8 confirms both PROJECT_TBOX_TURTLE and getProjectTBoxNodes() are unchanged post-\u00ce\u00b4-1 with stale `iao:OntologyDesignPattern`. C3a removes the `@prefix iao:` declaration and renames all three occurrences (class subject, rdfs:subClassOf target, rdfs:range target) to match SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.14 verbatim. C3b fixes getProjectTBoxNodes() in the same three positions, directly resolving the one currently-failing test identified in F4.\n\nC4 (project-tbox.ttl): F9 confirms the standalone .ttl file is unchanged. C4 makes it consistent with the updated C3a Turtle string and SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.14.\n\nC5 (projection/index.ts SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST): F10 confirms `\"iao:OntologyDesignPattern\"` is still in the allowlist at line 31. C5 replaces it with `\"ecm:OntologyDesignPattern\"` per ADR-007.\n\nC6 (migrate/index.ts): F11 confirms migrateV3toV4 still emits `\"iao:OntologyDesignPattern\"` at line 190. C6 corrects this to align with the test expectation legacy-migration.test.ts:290 (already updated by \u00ce\u00b4-1 per F14).\n\nC7 (ui/App.tsx): F12 confirms buildNewDocument() still carries `\"iao:OntologyDesignPattern\"` at line 25. C7 corrects this, which is required for C9 to pass.\n\nC8a/C8b/C8c (tbox-bundle.test.ts): F15 explicitly confirms these tests were NOT updated by \u00ce\u00b4-1 and are currently passing against the stale `iao:OntologyDesignPattern` TBox. Updating the source (C3a/C3b/C4) without also updating these tests would turn currently-passing tests into failures. Inclusion of C8a/b/c is correct and necessary for test-suite integrity; the developer's constraint interpretation (that the \u00ce\u00b4-1 'do not modify tests' constraint referred to tests \u00ce\u00b4-1 actually modified, not tests \u00ce\u00b4-1 was supposed to modify) is the only coherent reading that preserves a passing test suite.\n\nC9 (new-open-save.spec.ts): F17 confirms this Playwright spec assertion at line 65 still checks for `\"iao:OntologyDesignPattern\"`. Without C9, C7 would break this currently-passing test. Inclusion is correct.\n\nC10\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC18 (fixture files): F18 identifies all 9 fixture files with stale `\"iao:OntologyDesignPattern\"` in type arrays. The new canonical sort order `[\"ecm:OntologyDesignPattern\", \"ecm:Project\"]` is correctly applied per ADR-007 F22 (lexicographic: 'O'=79 < 'P'=80 within shared `ecm:` namespace).\n\nAdditional verification on developer open question 5 (emitters.test.ts Turtle string assertions): Direct file read confirms AC7 checks `turtleOut.includes(\"OntologyDesignPattern\")` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a substring match without prefix, not `\"iao:OntologyDesignPattern\"` or `\"@prefix iao:\"`. After C3a, the TBox Turtle contains `ecm:OntologyDesignPattern`, so the substring match continues to pass. The risk the developer flagged is resolved.\n\nResidual operational concerns noted but outside ratification scope:\n- project-tbox.ttl trailing newline (apply-time applier before-match concern; operator should verify per developer's guidance)\n- SPEC.md prose inconsistencies at lines 323, 345, 692, and semantic-projection.test.ts AC4 comment (correctly deferred by developer; requires a separate doc-fix chain)\n- vmp-serializer.test.ts fixtures (F16 recon inference: sort-behavior tests continue to pass since they test against their own stale fixture values, not source code behavior)",
