        "summary": "Inspector.tsx instance mode does not display or expose the instance's rdfs:label as any UI element \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the computed instanceLabel variable (lines 344-348) is referenced only in the delete confirmation dialog (line 529), not in the main instance section body. The section renders IRI (static), Class Assignments, Literal Assertions, and Delete controls with no label row at all. No data-testid for a label input (e.g., gw-inspector-instance-label-input) exists anywhere in the file. The closest existing mutable-field pattern in the Inspector is the inline <select> for predicate (relation mode, lines 639-651); no inline text <input> pattern currently exists. For S2-02, CanvasView.tsx deriveEdges() (lines 168-185) produces edge objects that store predicateIri in the data bag but set no label property on the edge, so React Flow renders edges with no visible text. The project parameter is already passed to deriveEdges(), so ecm:terms access for label resolution requires no new parameter. label-resolution.ts has no buildTermLabelMap or predicate-oriented helper; the inline term-scanning pattern used three times already in Inspector.tsx (lines 100-109, 133-149, 440-443) is the existing precedent. The canvas-3i-2r-with-ops.jsonld fixture already contains ObjectProperty terms with rdfs:label values (Has Role, Relates To), so no new fixture is required for edge-label tests. relation-crud.spec.ts AC2 asserts only on ecm:predicateIri in saved JSON; it does not reference any canvas edge label text and would not require modification if a label is added to deriveEdges().",
