      "outputs": {
        "ruling": "ratified",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposed changes introduce new interactive UI affordances (instance label editing, edge predicate label rendering), wire a new controlled-input mutation path through onProjectChange, and create a new Playwright specification file \u00e2\u20ac\u201d these are behavioral additions to the subject project, not editorial corrections.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM (urn:fnsr:task:332-recon-r3-beta); the refusal contract is satisfied. All three changes are grounded in verified reconnaissance evidence and confirmed against the live source files.\n\n**C1 (Inspector.tsx \u00e2\u20ac\u201d handleLabelChange + label input):** The `before` snippet beginning at `function handleDeleteInstance()` (line 350) matches the disk state exactly as confirmed by direct file read. The inserted `handleLabelChange` function follows the established immutable-update pattern of `handleRemoveClassAssignment` (lines 281\u00e2\u20ac\u201c291): map over `rawInstances`, spread-replace the matching entry, call `onProjectChange`. The controlled `<input type=\"text\">` reads `selectedInstance[\"rdfs:label\"]` directly from project state, consistent with the predicate `<select>` pattern at lines 639\u00e2\u20ac\u201c651. The `EcmInstance` interface in Inspector.tsx declares `\"rdfs:label\"?: string` (line 55\u00e2\u20ac\u201c60 per F14), and `onProjectChange` is available as a prop. The data-testid `gw-inspector-instance-label-input` is new (confirmed absent from the file per F3). No additional `useState` is required \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the controlled input derives from project state on every render. Reconnaissance open question on inline-vs-dialog is resolved by the implementation direction selecting inline.\n\n**S2-04 auto-resolution confirmed:** Once `handleLabelChange` writes `\"rdfs:label\"` via `onProjectChange`, the React state update triggers re-render. `deriveNodes()` in CanvasView.tsx reads `inst[\"rdfs:label\"]` with a `length > 0` guard (lines 154\u00e2\u20ac\u201c157, confirmed) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d canvas node labels update immediately. `resolveInstanceDisplay` in label-resolution.ts calls `buildInstanceLabelMap(project)` which scans `project[\"ecm:instances\"]` for `\"rdfs:label\"` (lines 19\u00e2\u20ac\u201c36, confirmed) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the relation inspector's Subject/Object fields pick up the updated label on re-render. No additional wiring required; S2-04 auto-resolves correctly.\n\n**C2 (CanvasView.tsx \u00e2\u20ac\u201d deriveEdges with term-label map):** The `before` snippet for `deriveEdges()` (lines 168\u00e2\u20ac\u201c185) matches disk exactly. The inline `ecm:terms` scan follows the established precedent used three times in Inspector.tsx (lines 100\u00e2\u20ac\u201c109, 133\u00e2\u20ac\u201c149, 440\u00e2\u20ac\u201c443 per F9). `iriTail` is already imported at CanvasView.tsx line 13 (F8 confirmed). The `edge.label` property is on React Flow's `Edge<T>` base type (not in the `data` bag), so the `RelationEdgeData` interface requires no modification. The `canvas-3i-2r-with-ops.jsonld` fixture already carries ObjectProperty terms with `rdfs:label` values `\"Has Role\"` and `\"Relates To\"` (F12, confirmed), so no fixture changes are needed. The `ecm:UnassignedPredicate` fallback to `iriTail` is consistent with the stated implementation direction; the inconsistency with the Inspector's `\"(unassigned)\"` display is acknowledged and deferred.\n\n**C3 (new instance-label.spec.ts):** `before: null` is correct for a new file. AC1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cAC4 are exercisable with existing fixtures (no new fixture required). AC1 uses the new-project Skip flow to produce a `\"New Instance\"`-labelled node, consistent with canvas.spec.ts AC2 precedent (F16). AC2 verifies `rdfs:label` persistence in saved JSON using `canvas-3i-2r.jsonld`. AC3 verifies live canvas propagation (S2-04 end-to-end). AC4 verifies edge predicate label rendering using `canvas-3i-2r-with-ops.jsonld` fixture (F12). Existing relation-crud.spec.ts AC2 asserts only on `ecm:predicateIri` in saved JSON and is unaffected by the addition of `edge.label` (F11).\n\n**Layer boundaries:** All three changes are scoped to `src/ui/` (adapter layer). No `src/kernel/` files are modified. The `handleLabelChange \u00e2\u2020\u2019 onProjectChange` mutation path flows through the established prop interface, not through any kernel import. Layer boundary constraints from CLAUDE.md \u00c2\u00a79 and \u00c2\u00a76 are respected.\n\n**Self-consistency of developer proposal:** The developer's `self_assessment: confident` is supported by the evidence. The three open questions from reconnaissance are explicitly resolved in the proposal with rationale. No unresolved design decisions remain blocking this chain.",
