          }
        ],
        "bankings": [
          {
            "id": "B1",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "S2-04 auto-resolution demonstrated a broader design principle: when multiple UI views derive their display labels reactively from a single canonical project-state key (`\"rdfs:label\"` on `ecm:instances`), a mutation to that key via `onProjectChange` propagates to all dependent views on the next render without any explicit inter-component wiring. In this chain, a single `handleLabelChange` call updated the canvas node label (via `deriveNodes`), the Inspector's delete-confirmation dialog (via `instanceLabel`), and the relation inspector Subject/Object fields (via `resolveInstanceDisplay`) simultaneously. The pattern is load-bearing: any future feature that reads instance labels should consume `resolveInstanceDisplay` or `buildInstanceLabelMap` (which scan `project[\"ecm:instances\"]`) rather than caching labels locally, or it will not benefit from this auto-resolution property."
          },
          {
            "id": "B2",
            "category": "methodology-refinement-candidate",
            "content": "The `ecm:terms` inline-scan pattern (scan `project[\"ecm:terms\"]`, build a `Map<string, string>` of IRI \u00e2\u2020\u2019 rdfs:label, fallback to IRI or iriTail) now appears four times across the UI layer: Inspector.tsx lines 100\u00e2\u20ac\u201c109 (relation narration), Inspector.tsx lines 133\u00e2\u20ac\u201c149 (getObjectPropertyOptions), Inspector.tsx lines 440\u00e2\u20ac\u201c443 (literal predicate display), and the new CanvasView.tsx `deriveEdges()` (C2). The developer explicitly deferred DRY consolidation into a `buildTermLabelMap` export in `label-resolution.ts` as a future refactor. The accumulation count has crossed the threshold where a shared utility would have structural value \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the next chain touching either `label-resolution.ts` or `CanvasView.tsx` should evaluate whether to promote this pattern to a shared export, applying the same locality-vs-DRY reasoning used for `buildInstanceLabelMap`."
          }
        ]
      },
