        "summary": "The codebase is ready to receive starter terms in ecm:terms with minimal integration surface. The canonical integration point is buildNewDocument() (App.tsx:22-40), which initializes ecm:terms as [] and is consumed by both handleNewConfirm() and handleNewSkip(). The Open flow (handleFileChange) does not inject terms. TermSidebar.tsx already handles ecm:system-starter-example rendering (badge='starter', CSS=gw-badge--starter, non-clickable). The validator exempts non-project-created terms from CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION. The canonical IRIs for starter terms use the VMP_CONTEXT prefix expansions: rdfs:\u00e2\u2020\u2019http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#, owl:\u00e2\u2020\u2019http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#. The full candidate list from Aaron's Round 3 verbatim request yields 16 terms (8 RDFS properties + 5 OWL properties + 3 OWL meta-classes) when XSD datatypes are excluded as a separate ecm:datatype concern. One classification inconsistency exists between the chain's recon-task specific_questions and the developer-task implementation_directions: rdfs:isDefinedBy is placed in owl:ObjectProperty by the former and owl:DatatypeProperty by the latter. The 8 additional proposed starter IRIs beyond the J1 reserved-name set (rdfs:domain, rdfs:range, rdfs:subClassOf, rdfs:subPropertyOf, owl:inverseOf, owl:Class, owl:ObjectProperty, owl:DatatypeProperty) are not in the current reserved-names guard. No existing fixture uses a canonical RDFS/OWL IRI as an ecm:system-starter-example term, so there is no reference implementation shape to match. ecm:terms must be sorted lexicographically by id per SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.3 rule 4.",
