        "open_questions": [
          "rdfs:seeAlso and rdfs:isDefinedBy type classification: implementation_directions assign both to owl:DatatypeProperty. The recon's open questions note that rdfs:seeAlso has an IRI range in strict RDFS (links to a resource) and rdfs:isDefinedBy was placed in owl:ObjectProperty by the chain's specific_questions. This proposal follows the implementation_directions (both \u00e2\u2020\u2019 owl:DatatypeProperty). If the operator prefers owl:ObjectProperty for either, C1 needs a targeted one-line type change per affected term.",
          "rdfs:domain and rdfs:range inclusion: SPEC section 7.5 defers these as first-class TBox fields for MVP, but the implementation_directions explicitly include them as ecm:system-starter-example sidebar entries. This proposal includes them. If the operator decides SPEC section 7.5 deference applies to sidebar visibility as well, two terms should be removed from STARTER_TERMS.",
          "AC3 roundtrip test (Open v0.4 fixture -> Save -> bytewise identical): this test opens test/fixtures/canonical-v0.4/minimal.jsonld which has ecm:terms: []. Since the Open flow does not inject starter terms, the existing AC3 test continues to pass. However, if any future workflow re-saves an opened fixture after injecting starter terms, the AC3 fixture would need updating. No action required now.",
          "reserved-names.ts guard scope: the 8 additional starter IRIs (rdfs:domain, rdfs:range, rdfs:subClassOf, rdfs:subPropertyOf, owl:inverseOf, owl:Class, owl:ObjectProperty, owl:DatatypeProperty) are NOT in RESERVED_CANONICAL_IRIS. A user who manually enters one of these IRIs in the IRI override field will be blocked only by the duplicate-IRI check (collectExistingIris), not by the canonical-reserved-name warning. The implementation_directions say 'Verify' not 'extend', so reserved-names.ts is unchanged here. Operator should decide if a follow-up task should extend RESERVED_CANONICAL_IRIS to cover all 16 starter IRIs."
        ],
        "summary": "Five changes across four files implement S4-02 starter terms. C1 creates src/validate/starter-terms.ts exporting EcmTerm interface and STARTER_TERMS (16 entries: 8 rdfs:, 5 owl: properties, 3 owl: meta-classes; sorted lexicographically; epoch timestamps; ecm:system-starter-example source). C2a/C2b wire STARTER_TERMS into buildNewDocument() in App.tsx via a shallow-clone map (primitives-only, so equivalent to deep clone). C3 adds tests/starter-terms.test.ts verifying count, per-entry field validity, and lexicographic sort. C4 adds a Playwright test to new-open-save.spec.ts asserting ecm:terms.length >= 15 on a freshly created project. The Open flow is untouched. The CANONICAL_RESERVED_NAME_COLLISION validator and AC6 test (exactly 8 reserved IRIs) are unmodified and continue to pass. TermSidebar's existing starter-badge rendering, non-clickable guard, and validator source-exemption all work correctly for the new terms without code changes.",
        "self_assessment": "confident"
      },
