        "bankings": [
          {
            "id": "B1",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "Shallow-clone sufficiency for mutation isolation: when a TypeScript interface constrains all fields to primitive types (string, string literals, null) with no nested objects or arrays, a spread-object shallow clone ({ ...t }) is semantically equivalent to structuredClone for shared-state mutation isolation purposes. The architect can confirm mutation safety at ratification time by inspecting the interface definition rather than requiring an explicit deep-copy call. This pattern recurs wherever static-const arrays of primitive-shaped records (STARTER_TERMS, future enum-like vocabulary arrays) are injected into mutable project state at runtime."
          },
          {
            "id": "B2",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "src/validate/ as cross-layer vocabulary host in GraphWrite: the validate layer (src/validate/) serves as a shared vocabulary host accessible to both src/ui/ and the unit-test build (which excludes src/ui/ via tsconfig.test.json). Placing new data modules \u00e2\u20ac\u201d reserved-names.ts, and now starter-terms.ts \u00e2\u20ac\u201d in src/validate/ rather than src/ui/ preserves unit-test accessibility without violating layer boundaries. Future vocabulary-style modules (structural constants, canonical enum lists, well-formedness fixtures) should be evaluated for src/validate/ placement before defaulting to src/ui/."
          },
          {
            "id": "B3",
            "category": "methodology-refinement-candidate",
            "content": "SPEC deferral language scope disambiguation: SPEC \u00c2\u00a77.5 defers 'rdfs:domain / rdfs:range as first-class TBox fields.' At ratification, this language must be read narrowly \u00e2\u20ac\u201d it defers schema-level TBox modeling (the ecm:Term data model treating domain/range as first-class structural fields), not incidental appearance of those IRIs as ecm:system-starter-example reference vocabulary in the sidebar. The two operations are structurally distinct: one is a modeling commitment; the other is a UI vocabulary population. Future SPEC deferral language should specify whether the deferral applies to (a) the data model field, (b) the UI control, or (c) any system production of the IRI, to eliminate ambiguity at ratification time and avoid requiring per-instance scope adjudication."
          }
        ]
      },
