            "claim": "VERDICT confirm-aaron-correct-with-additional-detail on F4. Removal of the three meta-class entries is correct. Additional type-assignment error recon did not flag: owl:DatatypeProperty and owl:ObjectProperty are typed 'owl:Class' in STARTER_TERMS. Per OWL 2 built-in vocabulary (Structural Specification Table 6.1), owl:ObjectProperty is typed rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty and owl:DatatypeProperty is typed rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty \u00e2\u20ac\u201d neither is an instance of owl:Class. The current representation conflates the meta-property category with the domain-class category. owl:Class typed as owl:Class is a vacuous tautology (OWL Full self-membership) but is equally inappropriate as a user starter term.",
            "evidence": "src/validate/starter-terms.ts:127-152 (three entries with ids owl#Class, owl#DatatypeProperty, owl#ObjectProperty all assigned type 'owl:Class'). OWL 2 Structural Specification Table 6.1: owl:ObjectProperty rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty; owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty.",
            "correction": "Remove all three entries from STARTER_TERMS array: the entry with id 'http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class', the entry with id 'http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty', and the entry with id 'http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty'. No reclassification is viable; meta-vocabulary entities are not domain-ontology terms expressible in the project's type system."
