            "claim": "VERDICT confirm-aaron-correct on F13. The regex ^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_.-]*$ is an ontologically sound ASCII-subset NCName constraint. It correctly requires an alphabetic or underscore start character and permits alphanumeric, underscore, dot, and hyphen in subsequent positions \u00e2\u20ac\u201d matching the practical local-name conventions for OWL ontologies. The composite-key uniqueness check (Namespace + Property Name = composed IRI) is correct: two terms sharing a local name but differing in namespace are distinct IRIs and must not share a project-uniqueness constraint.",
