      "outputs": {
        "ruling": "ratified",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposed change creates a new analytical document (demo/FEEDBACK-ROUND-4-DECOMPOSITION.md with before: null) that synthesizes reconnaissance and semantic-sme findings into 19 actionable atomic items with operator-adjudication instructions \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this is new normative content for a deliberative workflow, not a typo fix, formatting adjustment, or terminology tightening.",
        "rationale": "The proposed change satisfies all material requirements for ratification under Spec 08 v0.3-amendment-in-effect. Reconnaissance (task 342) is present in UPSTREAM, satisfying the substantive-change refusal contract. Semantic-sme review (task 343) is also present in UPSTREAM, satisfying the Spec 08 v0.3 requirement that ontology-content atomic items carry SME review upstream of developer decomposition \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the first chain to operationalize this amendment.\n\nStructural verification against all review_focus criteria:\n\n1. ATOMIC DECOMPOSITION / COUNT: The document produces 19 atomic items (3 meta + 5 starter + 3 type-system + 8 mini-spec). The INPUTS target was '~15-18'; 19 is one above the upper bound. However the excess is fully justified: TYPESYS-3 originates from SME finding SA4 (rdfs:seeAlso IRI-vs-literal semantics), which was absent from recon despite coverage of turtle.ts. This is precisely the class of finding the v0.3 amendment is designed to surface. No bundling: every item is genuinely atomic and independently actionable.\n\n2. SEMANTIC-SME VERDICTS ON ONTOLOGY-CONTENT ITEMS: All 16 ontology-content items carry a 'Semantic-sme verdict:' field populated from task 343. Verdict distribution: 6 confirm, 10 confirm-with-detail, 0 dispute \u00e2\u20ac\u201d matches the SME task summary exactly. Blocking items (R4-STARTER-4 via S4+SA1, R4-TYPESYS-1 via S5+SA3) are correctly marked and their atomic co-deployment requirement is stated in both the dependency fields and the adjudication queue.\n\n3. ROUND 3 CHAIN \u00ce\u00b3 RECURRENCE: Cross-references to 'Round 3 Chain \u00ce\u00b3 (R3-S4-02)' appear in R4-STARTER-1, R4-STARTER-2, R4-STARTER-3, R4-STARTER-4, R4-STARTER-5, R4-TYPESYS-1, and R4-MINISPEC-7. The Spec 08 Amendment Summary section additionally traces the full causal chain: Round 1 Item J provision-half \u00e2\u2020\u2019 Round 3 Chain \u00ce\u00b3 type-assignment errors \u00e2\u2020\u2019 Round 4 corrections, establishing these not merely as individual bugs but as a classification error cohort.\n\n4. AARON'S META-CONCERN: Captured as R4-META-1 (AP-6 numbering collision + v0.3 amendment scope). The AP-6 collision is verified: surfaces/feedback-rounds/surface-spec.md lines 334-341 confirms AP-6 is already assigned to the substrate-escalation-shape anti-pattern. The document correctly leaves AP numbering resolution as an open Phase 05a adjudication item (AP-7 candidate) rather than resolving it unilaterally.\n\n5. REFINED MINI SPEC ATOMIC DECOMPOSITION: All 8 components from Aaron's verbatim spec (demo/FEEDBACK-ROUND-4.md lines 55-98) are decomposed into distinct atomic items: Property Type Toggle \u00e2\u2020\u2019 R4-MINISPEC-1; Prefix/Namespace Selector \u00e2\u2020\u2019 R4-MINISPEC-2; Local Name regex \u00e2\u2020\u2019 R4-MINISPEC-3; Label+Lang \u00e2\u2020\u2019 R4-MINISPEC-4; Target Data Type Dropdown \u00e2\u2020\u2019 R4-MINISPEC-5; JSON payload shape \u00e2\u2020\u2019 R4-MINISPEC-6; Turtle Annotation \u00e2\u2020\u2019 R4-MINISPEC-7; Turtle Datatype \u00e2\u2020\u2019 R4-MINISPEC-8. Each carries independent completeness maps and correct dependency wiring.\n\n6. COMPLETENESS MAPS AT PHASE 06: Every ontology-content item includes 'semantic-sme review at Phase 06 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d complete (this task)' in its completeness map, satisfying the v0.3 amendment's insertion requirement.\n\n7. SUBSTANTIVE CLASSIFICATION: Confirmed. New analytical document, no prior version to compare against (before: null).\n\nOne advisory observation: R4-MINISPEC-2 correctly removes 'rdf:' from the namespace dropdown per SME finding S9 (W3C reserved prefix), but the document's completeness map for R4-MINISPEC-2 states 'confirm rdf: removal' as an operator-facing note rather than recording it as an SME-mandated correction. The substantive direction (remove rdf:) is correctly captured in the body text and SME verdict field. This does not affect ratification.\n\nAll material requirements satisfied. Ratified for Pass 2b proceed.",
        "referenced_evidence": [
