        "bankings": [
          {
            "id": "B1",
            "category": "methodology-refinement-candidate",
            "content": "Spec 08 v0.3 amendment operationalized for the first time in task chain 342\u00e2\u2020\u2019343\u00e2\u2020\u2019344\u00e2\u2020\u2019345. The SME step (task 343) surfaced SA4 (rdfs:seeAlso IRI-vs-literal semantics in turtle.ts) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a genuine structural defect absent from the reconnaissance (task 342) despite full coverage of turtle.ts. This confirms that content-domain routing (does this item touch ontology vocabulary or semantic predicates?) catches issues that file-extension routing misses. A secondary discipline: when SME precedes developer, the decomposition document can carry pre-computed SME verdicts that the operator reads at Phase 05a adjudication without requiring a separate SME dispatch at Phase 06 per-item. This collapses a previously-implicit two-dispatch pattern into a single document. The methodology gain is only realized when the SME scope is broad enough to review the full impact surface, not just the items the developer would have proposed independently."
          },
          {
            "id": "B2",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "The Round 4 blocking pair (R4-STARTER-4 + R4-TYPESYS-1) exhibits a structural pattern: a type-system extension (adding owl:AnnotationProperty to a union) must propagate atomically across five locations in four files \u00e2\u20ac\u201d EcmTermType (starter-terms.ts), AddTermType (AddTermDialog.tsx), SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST (projection/index.ts), SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7 allowed type values, and SPEC \u00c2\u00a76.1 semantic type allowlist. Partial application leaves the system in an inconsistent state where the type is representable in some layers but silently dropped by others. The decomposition document's atomic co-deployment annotation ('Dependencies: R4-TYPESYS-1 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d atomic co-deployment required') is the primary mechanism preventing partial-application inconsistency at the Phase 06 developer dispatch level. This pattern generalizes: type-system evolution in layered TypeScript+SPEC architectures requires identifying the full propagation surface at decomposition time, not at implementation time."
          }
        ]
