      "outputs": {
        "findings": [
          {
            "id": "S1",
            "severity": "major",
            "category": "naming_iri",
            "claim": "C1 (\u00c2\u00a75.7 after-text) cites 'OWL 2 RDF-Based Semantics Table 6.2' as the normative source for rdfs:label, rdfs:comment, rdfs:seeAlso, and rdfs:isDefinedBy being typed as owl:AnnotationProperty. The OWL 2 RDF-Based Semantics document (https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-rdf-based-semantics/) uses sequential table numbering (Table 1, Table 2 \u00e2\u20ac\u00a6) and has no section-qualified 'Table 6.2'. The correct normative locus for built-in OWL 2 annotation properties is the OWL 2 Structural Specification \u00c2\u00a710.2, which enumerates all nine built-in annotation properties including the four cited. The substantive claim (those four IRIs are canonical owl:AnnotationProperty) is ontologically correct; only the citation is wrong.",
            "evidence": "C1 after-text: 'Per OWL 2 RDF-Based Semantics Table 6.2, rdfs:label, rdfs:comment, rdfs:seeAlso, and rdfs:isDefinedBy are canonically typed as owl:AnnotationProperty'",
            "correction": "Replace 'OWL 2 RDF-Based Semantics Table 6.2' with 'OWL 2 Structural Specification \u00c2\u00a710.2 (https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-syntax/#Annotation_Properties)'. The corrected sentence reads: 'Per OWL 2 Structural Specification \u00c2\u00a710.2, rdfs:label, rdfs:comment, rdfs:seeAlso, and rdfs:isDefinedBy are canonically typed as owl:AnnotationProperty; \u00e2\u20ac\u00a6'"
          },
          {
            "id": "S2",
            "severity": "major",
            "category": "representation_reality",
            "claim": "C3 amends \u00c2\u00a76.1 but preserves 'iao:OntologyDesignPattern' in the semantic type allowlist bullet. ADR-007 (DECISIONS.md lines 124\u00e2\u20ac\u201c133) renamed this term to ecm:OntologyDesignPattern and removed the iao: prefix. The implementation already reflects the rename: src/projection/index.ts SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST (line 33) contains 'ecm:OntologyDesignPattern', not 'iao:OntologyDesignPattern'. The \u00c2\u00a76.1 allowlist as amended by C3 names a type IRI that the code does not recognize, meaning the project root would be excluded from semantic projection under strict allowlist checking. The \u00c2\u00a75.14 Turtle block and the \u00c2\u00a75.4 JSON example already use 'ecm:OntologyDesignPattern' correctly; \u00c2\u00a76.1 is the outstanding textual holdover.",
            "evidence": "C3 after-text bullet: '- `ecm:Project` / `iao:OntologyDesignPattern` (the project root)'; src/projection/index.ts:33 SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST has 'ecm:OntologyDesignPattern'; DECISIONS.md ADR-007 states iao:OntologyDesignPattern is renamed to ecm:OntologyDesignPattern",
            "correction": "In C3's after-text, change the allowlist bullet from '`ecm:Project` / `iao:OntologyDesignPattern` (the project root)' to '`ecm:Project` / `ecm:OntologyDesignPattern` (the project root)'. This aligns \u00c2\u00a76.1 with ADR-007, \u00c2\u00a75.14, the \u00c2\u00a75.4 JSON example, and the code."
          },
          {
