            "severity": "minor",
            "category": "dl_conformance",
            "claim": "C5 (\u00c2\u00a77.1 annotation-properties bullet) states '`rdfs:range` MUST NOT be emitted on annotation properties' without qualifying this as a scope/design decision. In OWL 2 Structural Specification \u00c2\u00a710.4, AnnotationPropertyRange axioms (i.e., rdfs:range on annotation properties) are syntactically legal and are processed in OWL 2 Full with formal semantics; they are treated as annotation axioms in OWL 2 DL with annotation-layer semantics only. OWL 2 DL does not prohibit them. A spec reader or downstream implementer may incorrectly conclude that OWL 2 itself forbids rdfs:range on annotation properties, which is false.",
            "evidence": "C5 after-text: 'Annotation properties carry free-form metadata values. `rdfs:range` MUST NOT be emitted on annotation properties.'",
            "correction": "Change the sentence to: '`rdfs:range` is not in scope for `owl:AnnotationProperty` terms in v0.3 (AnnotationPropertyRange axioms are valid OWL 2 syntax but have annotation-layer semantics only; formal range enforcement is deferred \u00e2\u20ac\u201d see \u00c2\u00a77.5).' This accurately attributes the prohibition to scope, not to OWL 2 DL syntax."
          },
          {
            "id": "S4",
            "severity": "advisory",
            "category": "dl_conformance",
            "claim": "C8 (FR-U033 Target Data Type Dropdown) introduces the label 'Lists XSD primitives: xsd:string, xsd:boolean, xsd:integer, xsd:decimal, xsd:double, xsd:date, xsd:dateTime, xsd:anyURI, rdf:langString'. The term rdf:langString is not an XSD primitive; it is an RDF-defined datatype with IRI http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString, normatively defined in the RDF 1.1 Concepts specification and listed in the OWL 2 datatype map (OWL 2 Structural Specification \u00c2\u00a74 Table 1) as a supported datatype but NOT as an XSD type. All nine listed types are valid OWL 2 DataRange values and valid as rdfs:range on owl:DatatypeProperty; the ontological correctness is not affected. Only the category label is wrong.",
            "evidence": "C8 after-text FR-U033 subsection (e): 'Lists XSD primitives: xsd:string, xsd:boolean, xsd:integer, xsd:decimal, xsd:double, xsd:date, xsd:dateTime, xsd:anyURI, rdf:langString'",
            "correction": "Change the description label from 'Lists XSD primitives' to 'Lists supported OWL 2 datatypes (XSD types and rdf:langString)'. No change to the enumerated types themselves."
          }
        ],
        "summary": "The R4-1 amendments are ontologically sound in their substantive claims. The core DL positions are correct: (a) owl:DatatypeProperty rdfs:range must be a DataRange (XSD type or OWL DataRange), not an owl:Class IRI \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this is accurate per OWL 2 Structural Specification \u00c2\u00a79.4; (b) the three property-type IRI sets (owl:ObjectProperty, owl:DatatypeProperty, owl:AnnotationProperty) must be pairwise-disjoint per OWL 2 Structural Specification \u00c2\u00a711.1 typed-IRI restrictions; (c) adding owl:AnnotationProperty as a fourth term type is structurally correct; (d) ADR-009 rationale that DatatypeProperty range cannot be a ClassExpression is accurate. Four defects require correction before ratification: S1 (major) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d wrong document and non-existent table number cited for built-in annotation properties in C1; the correct citation is OWL 2 Structural Specification \u00c2\u00a710.2. S2 (major) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d C3 amends \u00c2\u00a76.1 but leaves 'iao:OntologyDesignPattern' in the type allowlist, contradicting ADR-007's rename to 'ecm:OntologyDesignPattern' and the live projection code; the project root would be misidentified under strict allowlist enforcement. S3 (minor) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the 'MUST NOT be emitted on annotation properties' phrasing for rdfs:range in C5 reads as an OWL 2 prohibition rather than a scope decision; AnnotationPropertyRange axioms are legal OWL 2. S4 (advisory) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d rdf:langString is mislabeled as an 'XSD primitive' in FR-U033; it is an RDF-defined datatype. BFO/CCO/IAO grounding is unaffected: no new IAO or CCO terms are introduced, and the obo:IAO_0000136 binding from ADR-007 is untouched.",
        "recommendation": "revise"
      },
      "depends_on": [
        "urn:fnsr:task:348-dev-r4-1"
      ],
