    {
      "@id": "urn:fnsr:task:350-rat-r4-1",
      "agent": "architect",
      "status": "done",
      "attempts": 1,
      "outputs": {
        "ruling": "denied",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposed changes amend normative SPEC sections (\u00c2\u00a75.7, \u00c2\u00a76.1, \u00c2\u00a77.1, \u00c2\u00a77.5), add a new functional requirement (FR-U033), register two new ADRs (ADR-008, ADR-009), and introduce a new SPEC subsection (\u00c2\u00a75.7.2), all of which alter defined terms, constraint clauses, and the normative allowlists that govern semantic projection \u00e2\u20ac\u201d none of this falls within editorial-correction scope.",
        "rationale": "Two major defects identified by the upstream semantic-SME review (task 349-sme-r4-1) prevent ratification.\n\n**S2 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Frozen ADR-007 conflict in C3 (blocking):** C3 amends \u00c2\u00a76.1 to add `owl:AnnotationProperty` to the semantic type allowlist. However, C3's `after` text retains `iao:OntologyDesignPattern` as the project-root allowlist entry. ADR-007 (registered 2026-05-22, final entry in DECISIONS.md) explicitly renamed `iao:OntologyDesignPattern` to `ecm:OntologyDesignPattern` throughout the codebase. The live code at `src/projection/index.ts:31` (SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST) already contains `ecm:OntologyDesignPattern`, not `iao:OntologyDesignPattern`. If C3 lands as proposed, the \u00c2\u00a76.1 normative type allowlist will contain an IRI that (a) conflicts with frozen ADR-007, (b) does not match any IRI the live code emits or recognizes in the SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST, and (c) contradicts SPEC sections \u00c2\u00a75.4 (line 362) and \u00c2\u00a75.14 (line 643 prose and Turtle block) that already carry the corrected `ecm:OntologyDesignPattern`. Under strict allowlist enforcement, the project root would be excluded from semantic projection. The developer's own open question 4 acknowledges this inconsistency but flags it as \"out of scope for R4-1\" \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this is not acceptable when C3 is already amending the precise section where the ADR-007 violation lives. A section amendment that passes through a frozen-ADR violation without correcting it compounds inconsistency debt.\n\n**S1 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Non-existent normative citation in C1 (major):** C1's `after` text in \u00c2\u00a75.7 states \"Per OWL 2 RDF-Based Semantics Table 6.2, rdfs:label, rdfs:comment, rdfs:seeAlso, and rdfs:isDefinedBy are canonically typed as owl:AnnotationProperty.\" The OWL 2 RDF-Based Semantics document uses sequential table numbering (Table 1, Table 2, \u00e2\u20ac\u00a6) with no section-qualified \"Table 6.2\". The correct normative locus is the OWL 2 Structural Specification \u00c2\u00a710.2 (https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-syntax/#Annotation_Properties), which enumerates the nine built-in annotation properties including all four cited. The substantive claim is ontologically correct; the citation mechanism implementers use to verify the claim does not exist at the given location. A normative SPEC text citing a non-existent table in the wrong document fails the normative-authority test.\n\n**S3 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Misleading MUST NOT language in C5 (minor, supporting):** C5's annotation-properties bullet states \"`rdfs:range` MUST NOT be emitted on annotation properties.\" OWL 2 Structural Specification \u00c2\u00a710.4 defines AnnotationPropertyRange axioms as syntactically legal OWL 2 with annotation-layer semantics in OWL 2 DL. The MUST NOT should attribute the restriction to scope (this version does not support AnnotationPropertyRange), not to OWL 2 syntax. A spec reader or downstream implementer may incorrectly conclude OWL 2 DL prohibits this, which is false.\n\n**C1 forward reference to \u00c2\u00a710.4 (minor, flagged):** C1 adds a migration note pointing to \u00c2\u00a710.4 for plain-string rdfs:label \u00e2\u2020\u2019 {text,lang} migration. \u00c2\u00a710.4 (\"Legacy Documents\") currently describes only v0.2 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 v0.3 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 v0.4 schema-version migration (iao: prefix addition, OntologyDesignPattern type, isAbout initialization) and contains no description of rdfs:label shape migration. The forward reference is therefore a dangling cross-reference within the proposed change. The developer's open question 2 acknowledges this and defers the \u00c2\u00a710.4 amendment to Chain R4-3; at minimum, the C1 migration note should be written to survive the current \u00c2\u00a710.4 state without implying normative coverage that doesn't exist there yet.\n\n**Correctly-handled items (not grounds for denial):** The \u00c2\u00a77.1 cross-reference bug (\u00c2\u00a77.6 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 \u00c2\u00a77.5) is correctly fixed in C5. FR-U033 is correctly numbered per recon F14. ADR-008 and ADR-009 are correctly the next available numbers per recon F15. The three sidebar-partition sites (FR-U004 via C7, \u00c2\u00a726 via C9, \u00c2\u00a729 via C10) are all updated. The rdfs:range XSD/DataRange constraint is correctly stated in C4 and C6. The OWL 2 DL pairwise-disjointness constraint in C3 is correctly scoped. The S4 advisory (rdf:langString labeled as \"XSD primitive\" in FR-U033) does not affect validity but should be corrected in the revision.\n\n**Required corrections before re-ratification:** (1) C3 `after` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d change `iao:OntologyDesignPattern` to `ecm:OntologyDesignPattern` in the \u00c2\u00a76.1 type allowlist bullet, aligning with ADR-007 and live code. (2) C1 `after` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d replace \"Per OWL 2 RDF-Based Semantics Table 6.2\" with \"Per OWL 2 Structural Specification \u00c2\u00a710.2 (https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-syntax/#Annotation_Properties)\". (3) C5 `after` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d replace \"rdfs:range MUST NOT be emitted on annotation properties\" with scope-attributed language (e.g., \"`rdfs:range` is not in scope for `owl:AnnotationProperty` terms in v0.3; AnnotationPropertyRange axioms are valid OWL 2 syntax but carry annotation-layer semantics only \u00e2\u20ac\u201d deferred, see \u00c2\u00a77.5\"). (4) Advisory: C8 `after` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d change \"Lists XSD primitives\" to \"Lists supported OWL 2 datatypes (XSD types and rdf:langString)\". No reconnaissance re-run is required; the substance is ratified in principle. Re-ratification against the corrected developer output is the appropriate next step.",
        "referenced_evidence": [
          {
            "type": "upstream_task",
            "id": "urn:fnsr:task:347-recon-r4-1",
            "field": "outputs.findings"
          },
