        "ruling": "denied",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "This change batch modifies normative term-type unions, starter-term content and count, projection allowlists, UI rendering partitions, turtle-emitter logic, and associated test suites \u00e2\u20ac\u201d all behavioral changes to defined system contracts under normative SPEC sections, not typographic or formatting corrections.",
        "rationale": "The semantic-sme upstream review (task 354) returns recommendation: revise with one blocking (S1) and one major (S2) finding. Both must be resolved before ratification can proceed. On-disk file inspection confirms both defects independently.\n\n--- S1 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d BLOCKING: SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7 conformance violation (rdfs:isDefinedBy omission) ---\n\nC2 reduces STARTER_TERMS to 3 entries: rdfs:comment, rdfs:label, rdfs:seeAlso \u00e2\u20ac\u201d all reclassified as owl:AnnotationProperty. However, project/SPEC.md \u00c2\u00a75.7 (line 479), as amended by R4-1, normatively states: 'rdfs:label, rdfs:comment, rdfs:seeAlso, and rdfs:isDefinedBy are canonically typed as owl:AnnotationProperty; they appear in starter examples with ecm:source: ecm:system-starter-example.' The referent of 'they' is unambiguously all four named IRIs. SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7.1 (line 489) further reinforces rdfs:isDefinedBy as a canonical reserved name that MUST NOT be re-minted as a project-created term. The implementation_directions' 'R4-STARTER-5 = Remove rdfs:isDefinedBy' entry in FEEDBACK-ROUND-4-DECOMPOSITION.md is a decomposition artifact of sub-SPEC authority; it cannot override normative SPEC prose without a prior SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7 amendment ratified through the standard chain. The implementation as proposed is non-conformant with the SPEC. The tests updated in C11/C13 (AC1 threshold >= 3) would lock in the non-conformant count. Resolution requires the operator to choose one of: (a) SPEC authority is binding \u00e2\u2020\u2019 developer adds rdfs:isDefinedBy as the 4th owl:AnnotationProperty entry (fragment order: comment < isDefinedBy < label < seeAlso), updates JSDoc count to 4, and raises AC1 to >= 4; or (b) decomposition intent is authoritative \u00e2\u2020\u2019 a SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7 amendment task must first amend the 'they appear in starter examples' sentence to exclude rdfs:isDefinedBy, ratify that amendment, then re-ratify C2 with 3 entries.\n\n--- S2 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d MAJOR: C10 is dead code; SA4 structurally unresolved end-to-end ---\n\nC10 adds dedicated rdfs:seeAlso IRI-or-literal handling inside turtle.ts/nodeToQuads(). On-disk inspection confirms: (1) src/projection/index.ts SEMANTIC_PREDICATE_ALLOWLIST (lines 55-76, verified on disk) does not contain 'rdfs:seeAlso'; (2) SPEC \u00c2\u00a76.1 predicate allowlist (project/SPEC.md lines 732-739, verified on disk) does not list rdfs:seeAlso. The applyPredicateFilter() function (src/projection/index.ts:112-122) strips every predicate absent from the allowlist before any entity reaches nodeToQuads(). Therefore, any rdfs:seeAlso field stored on a semantic entity is eliminated at the projection layer and the C10 code path is never reached. SA4 is not fixed end-to-end; C10 is dead code in this chain. Two parallel changes are prerequisites for C10 to have runtime effect: (a) add 'rdfs:seeAlso' to SEMANTIC_PREDICATE_ALLOWLIST in src/projection/index.ts; (b) amend SPEC \u00c2\u00a76.1 predicate allowlist prose in project/SPEC.md to include rdfs:seeAlso. The SPEC \u00c2\u00a76.1 amendment is a canonical-doc mutation requiring its own reconnaissance \u00e2\u2020\u2019 ratification chain. C10 must be removed from the current change set and deferred to a follow-on chain (R4-3 as the developer's open_questions suggest, or a dedicated amendment task). Including dead code that appears to resolve SA4 while the defect persists is worse than deferral: it creates false confidence in test coverage and obscures the actual unresolved defect.\n\n--- S3 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d MINOR: IRI-detection heuristic in C10 is over-broad ---\n\nThe 'seeAlsoVal.includes(\":\")' fallback in C10's isIri condition fires on any colon-containing string, including natural-language text ('Note: see related concept') and ISBN-style tokens, producing namedNode quads with non-absolute-IRI strings in violation of RDF 1.1 \u00c2\u00a72.3. This is downstream of S2 (C10 is dead code until allowlist gaps are fixed) but must be corrected when C10 is reintroduced in R4-3. Fix: remove the includes(':') arm; retain only scheme-prefix matching (startsWith 'http://', 'https://', 'urn:').\n\n--- Confirming evidence (S4): positive changes are ontologically correct ---\n\nThe following changes are confirmed clean and may land once S1 and S2 are resolved: C1 (EcmTermType gains 'owl:AnnotationProperty'), C3 (SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST gains 'owl:AnnotationProperty' \u00e2\u20ac\u201d correctly closes SA3 per SPEC \u00c2\u00a76.1 line 724 which already includes owl:AnnotationProperty on disk), C4\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC7 (TermSidebar 4th bucket), C8\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC9 (AddTermType + TERM_TYPE_LABEL extension), C11\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC14 (test updates, pending S1 resolution for correct threshold), C15 (SA3 regression test in semantic-projection.test.ts), C16 (Playwright 4th section assertion). The meta-class punning removal (owl:Class/DatatypeProperty/ObjectProperty typed owl:Class in old STARTER_TERMS) is ontologically correct and clean.\n\n--- Ruling: DENIED ---\n\nThe chain must be revised. Operator must resolve the rdfs:isDefinedBy disposition (S1) and remove or complete C10 (S2) before re-ratification. Reconnaissance is already in UPSTREAM from task 352; the re-ratification chain may proceed directly from developer revision \u00e2\u2020\u2019 semantic-sme \u00e2\u2020\u2019 ratification (reconnaissance re-run is at operator discretion if the scope of developer revisions materially expands beyond S1 and S2 resolution).",
