        "summary": "The codebase contains rdfs:label as a plain string in all current source files, fixtures, inline test fixtures, and the demo file. SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7 and ADR-008 define the target shape as { \"text\": <string>, \"lang\": <BCP-47-tag> } for ecm:terms entries with a default lang of \"en\". The ADR-008 consequences clause and SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7 text explicitly scope this change to term objects in ecm:terms; SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.8 (Instance Object) still shows plain string for instance labels. The clean-break migration touches: 5 Playwright fixture files (10 plain-string term labels across canvas-3i-2r-with-ops, term-sidebar-2c-1op-1dp, literal-crud-1i-1dp, imported-term, term-sidebar-cross-refs), 1 demo file (7 term labels + 5 instance labels if instances are in scope), all 3 canonical test fixtures in test/fixtures/ are label-free and require no changes. On the source side: src/ui/label-resolution.ts, CanvasView.tsx, Inspector.tsx, TermSidebar.tsx, AddTermDialog.tsx, EditTermDialog.tsx, AddLiteralDialog.tsx (7 UI files), src/emit/turtle.ts (must emit language-tagged literal), src/emit/triple-narration.ts, src/emit/markdown.ts (2 narration/output files), src/validate/index.ts and starter-terms.ts (2 validate files) all read or write rdfs:label as plain string and require attention. src/migrate/index.ts lacks a label-shape coercion step despite SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7 referencing \u00c2\u00a710.4, and src/normalize/index.ts has no label coercion. On the test side: tests/starter-terms.test.ts AC5 explicitly asserts typeof t[\"rdfs:label\"] === \"string\" (would break), and 3 Playwright tests (instance-label.spec.ts, smoke.spec.ts, term-crud.spec.ts) assert on plain-string label values from downloaded JSON. Two gaps are identified: (1) SPEC \u00c2\u00a710.4 migration step list does not enumerate label-shape coercion; (2) ADR-008 scopes to terms but SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.8 + task context are ambiguous about whether instance labels also convert.",
