        "open_questions": [
          "Does the {text, lang} shape apply to ecm:instances rdfs:label as well as ecm:terms rdfs:label? ADR-008 says 'term objects in ecm:terms' only; SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.8 still shows plain string for instances; but the task context says 'affects every fixture'. A definitive ruling on instance scope is needed before fixtures like demo/library-catalog.jsonld (5 instance labels) and the Playwright AC2 test in instance-label.spec.ts can be updated.",
          "Should src/migrate/index.ts v0.3\u00e2\u2020\u2019v0.4 leg include a label-shape coercion step (iterating ecm:terms and converting plain-string rdfs:label to {text, lang: 'en'})? SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7 references \u00c2\u00a710.4 for this migration but \u00c2\u00a710.4 does not list the step. Alternatively, should this be a normalizeOnLoad step in src/normalize/index.ts?",
          "If label-shape normalization belongs in normalizeOnLoad rather than migrate, does the canonical form check (serializeVmp round-trip comparison) need to be updated, since {text, lang} objects will not be detected as non-canonical by the current string-equality approach?",
          "Does the {text, lang} shape apply to the rdfs:label fields on ecm:RelationAssertion objects in SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.9 (example shows plain string 'participates in')? The ADR-008 scope says 'term objects in ecm:terms' only, which would exclude relation labels.",
          "src/tbox/index.ts defines rdfs:label as plain strings in hardcoded TBox node objects (getProjectTBoxNodes) and in the Turtle block. These are not in ecm:terms. Should TBox node objects also use {text, lang} shape, or is the ADR-008 scope limited to user-authored ecm:terms entries?",
          "Total estimated change count: 6 fixture files (10 term labels + 5 instance labels if in scope), 12 source files (UI readers/writers, emitters, validate, migrate/normalize), 5+ spec test files, 3 Playwright test files. Does this exceed the operator's desired change scope per chain? No split has been performed here as the content fits within output limits; the operator can confirm."
        ],
        "scope_assessment": "All files enumerated in focus_areas were read; additionally src/projection/index.ts, src/tbox/index.ts, src/validate/index.ts, src/validate/starter-terms.ts, src/emit/markdown.ts, src/ui/AddLiteralDialog.tsx, tests/normalize-on-load.test.ts, tests/legacy-migration.test.ts, tests/snapshot.test.ts, examples/input.jsonld, and examples/expected-output.jsonld were read to confirm presence or absence of rdfs:label; SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7, \u00c2\u00a75.8, \u00c2\u00a710.4 and ADR-008 were read for normative scope; no files outside the GraphWrite subject codebase were investigated."
      },
      "depends_on": [],
      "inputs": {
        "task_context": "Round 4 Chain R4-3: clean-break migration of rdfs:label from plain string to {text, lang} object shape per ADR-008. Aaron explicitly picked clean break in Phase 05a + reconfirmed when shown the scope. Affects every fixture, every label-reader, every label-asserting test.",
        "output_envelope_constraint": "Output wrapped: outputs.findings[], outputs.summary, outputs.evidence_paths.",
        "goal": "Read-only investigation. EXHAUSTIVE enumeration: every file in the repo that touches rdfs:label, by category (fixtures / source code / spec tests / Playwright tests / migrate / demo). For each: brief note on what must change.",
        "focus_areas": [
          "All fixtures: test/fixtures/canonical-v0.4/*.jsonld + test/fixtures/malformed/*.jsonld + tests/playwright/fixtures/*.jsonld + demo/library-catalog.jsonld",
