        "ruling": "denied",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "R4-3a implements ADR-008 across 14 source files \u00e2\u20ac\u201d changing the stored schema type of rdfs:label from plain string to {text, lang} object on ecm:terms entries, updating all read/write/emit paths, and adding migration and normalization steps \u00e2\u20ac\u201d constituting a schema-level behavioral change across the application boundary, not a typo fix, formatting correction, or terminology tightening.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance (358-recon-r4-3) is present and comprehensive. The proposed 26 changes across 14 source files correctly implement the ADR-008 {text, lang} shape at the application layer: normalizeLabelShape is idempotent; normalizeOnLoad applies label coercion before the structural serializeVmp comparison; migrateV3toV4 gains the coercion step; all UI read paths gain resolveTermLabel; turtle.ts C12 correctly splits rdfs:label handling to emit literal(text, lang) via N3.js for the {text, lang} shape; narration and markdown emitters gain local resolveLabel helpers. The scope boundary (tbox/index.ts untouched per ADR-008) is respected across all 26 changes. Build is expected to pass; test-suite failures deferred to R4-3b and R4-3c are correctly scoped.\n\nRatification is denied on two major grounds surfaced by the semantic SME (365-sme-r4-3a):\n\n**S1 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d VMP_CONTEXT missing JSON-LD compact aliases (blocking):** The proposed 26 changes do NOT include a modification to src/kernel/canonicalize.ts. VMP_CONTEXT (verified at canonicalize.ts:66\u00e2\u20ac\u201c92) defines the normative JSON-LD @context bundled into every serialized VMP document per SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.2. It contains no compact alias mapping 'text' to '@value' or 'lang' to '@language'. After R4-3a lands, all ecm:terms entries on disk carry \"rdfs:label\": {\"text\": \"...\", \"lang\": \"en\"}. A conformant JSON-LD 1.1 processor consuming projectSemantic() output (confirmed at projection/index.ts:202, docstring: 'Canonical UTF-8 JSON-LD string') would interpret the {text, lang} object as a blank node with unknown properties, NOT as the rdf:langString literal \"...\"@en. The SPEC header declares 'Canonical representation: JSON-LD 1.1'; this claim is violated for the JSON-LD path across all term labels once R4-3a lands. The Turtle/N-Triples path (via nodeToQuads \u00e2\u2020\u2019 C12) is architecturally correct and produces well-formed language-tagged literals; the JSON-LD path is not. The fix \u00e2\u20ac\u201d adding '\"lang\": \"@language\"' and '\"text\": \"@value\"' to VMP_CONTEXT immediately after the existing 'type': '@type' alias \u00e2\u20ac\u201d is a kernel-layer change in canonicalize.ts. It must be included in the revised R4-3a proposal or factored into a blocking prerequisite chain before R4-3a can be ratified.\n\n**S2 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d SPEC \u00c2\u00a710.4 migration step list gap (major, canonical-doc):** SPEC \u00c2\u00a710.4 (verified at SPEC.md:928\u00e2\u20ac\u201c935) enumerates six explicit v0.3\u00e2\u2020\u2019v0.4 migration steps; rdfs:label coercion is not among them. SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7 (SPEC.md:485) cross-references \u00c2\u00a710.4 as the location where label-shape migration occurs, creating a self-contradiction in normative spec text. The developer implementation (C2, migrateV3toV4) correctly adds the coercion and records it in transformedFields, but the implementation now diverges from the normative step list. A seventh bullet must be added to \u00c2\u00a710.4 in project/SPEC.md via a separate canonical-doc chain (ratification \u00e2\u2020\u2019 applier path) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d it is not required to block R4-3a source-code landing but should be queued immediately after.\n\n**S4 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d empty-text guard in turtle.ts C12 (minor, should address in revised proposal):** The normalizeLabelShape fallback returns {text: '', lang: 'en'} for malformed input. The proposed C12 nodeToQuads branch unconditionally emits literal(lv['text'], lv['lang']) without guarding against empty text, which would assert rdfs:label \"\"@en \u00e2\u20ac\u201d an ontologically spurious valid-but-misleading RDF statement. A length > 0 guard before the makeQuad call resolves this with a one-line addition.\n\n**S3 (advisory, not blocking):** BCP 47 primary-subtag validation is absent from normalizeLabelShape; all current write paths hardcode 'en' (valid), so this is not a correctness issue for R4-3a scope but should be noted for the revised proposal.\n\nThe operator should revise the developer proposal to add a 27th change for VMP_CONTEXT in canonicalize.ts (adding the '@value'/'@language' aliases), add the S4 guard in C12, re-queue the developer task, re-run the SME, and re-queue ratification. The SPEC \u00c2\u00a710.4 canonical-doc gap should proceed as a separate chain.",
