            "id": "B1",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "When a new structured value type representing an RDF concept is introduced at the application layer (here: {text, lang} to represent rdf:langString on rdfs:label), VMP_CONTEXT must declare the corresponding compact aliases ('text'\u00e2\u2020\u2019'@value', 'lang'\u00e2\u2020\u2019'@language') or the JSON-LD intermediate diverges from the intended RDF semantics while the Turtle/N-Triples path may remain correct. TypeScript compilation, unit tests, and Turtle output verification do not catch this gap \u00e2\u20ac\u201d it is invisible until a conformant JSON-LD processor consumes the JSON-LD output. The SME pass is the gate that reliably surfaces this class of JSON-LD context completeness failure."
          },
          {
            "id": "B2",
            "category": "methodology-refinement-candidate",
            "content": "Scope statements in review_focus constraints (e.g., 'tbox/index.ts NOT touched per ADR-008 scope boundary') should enumerate all kernel-layer files explicitly in or out of scope, not just the immediately obvious ones. In R4-3a, canonicalize.ts was implicitly treated as out-of-scope alongside tbox/index.ts, but the VMP_CONTEXT in canonicalize.ts is structurally required by the shape change. A refined discipline: when a review_focus lists excluded files as out-of-scope, the architect and SME should explicitly check whether those exclusions are complete with respect to the change's full semantic surface."
          },
          {
            "id": "B3",
            "category": "discipline-correction",
            "content": "The reconnaissance \u00e2\u2020\u2019 developer \u00e2\u2020\u2019 SME \u00e2\u2020\u2019 ratification chain successfully caught a critical kernel gap (missing VMP_CONTEXT aliases in canonicalize.ts) before code landing. The SME's 'revise' recommendation was the correct signal and the ratification denial correctly operationalizes it. This confirms that the SME role is load-bearing specifically for JSON-LD semantic correctness \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a class of correctness that is not verifiable by TypeScript compilation, unit tests, or structural review alone. The chain's design (independent SME pass upstream of ratification) provided the correct containment."
          }
        ]
      },
