        "summary": "The implementation surface for Chain R4-4 (Property Creation Module, FR-U033) centers on modifying AddTermDialog.tsx \u00e2\u20ac\u201d not creating a new file \u00e2\u20ac\u201d plus targeted additions to src/emit/turtle.ts, src/validate/codes.ts, and src/validate/index.ts. FR-U033 is fully specified at SPEC.md:1390 (ratified); its differences from the original FEEDBACK-ROUND-4.md include: (a) rdf: removed from namespace selector, (b) XSD datatype list expanded to 8 (added xsd:double, xsd:anyURI), (c) language tag changed from fixed dropdown to free-text with BCP 47 regex. The decomposition document (FEEDBACK-ROUND-4-DECOMPOSITION.md, R4-MINISPEC-1 completeness map) directs that AddTermDialog receives an internal Property Type Toggle replacing the fixed termType prop, and TermSidebar's Class creation path may retain a pre-determined initializer. The three namespace entries are hardcoded app-level constants (not per-project schema fields): ex\u00e2\u2020\u2019http://example.org/, foaf\u00e2\u2020\u2019http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/, schema\u00e2\u2020\u2019https://schema.org/ (per SME S9 finding; confirmed by SPEC.md FR-U033 exclusion of rdf:). Prerequisites from prior chains are partially satisfied: rdfs:range is already in the SEMANTIC_PREDICATE_ALLOWLIST (projection/index.ts:64) and owl:AnnotationProperty is in SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST (projection/index.ts:35). Outstanding R4-4 gaps: (1) rdfs:range absent from turtle.ts IRI-valued predicates loop (line 191); (2) RANGE_CLASS_ON_DATATYPE_PROPERTY absent from validate/codes.ts; (3) no validator logic for XSD-vs-class constraint on rdfs:range; (4) foaf: and schema: absent from PREFIX_MAP (turtle.ts:33-41); (5) no tests for either rdfs:range emission or range-class constraint. The JSON payload shape (FR-U033 \u00c2\u00a73) maps cleanly to the existing ecm:Term structure via namespace+localName\u00e2\u2020\u2019id, label.{text,lang}\u00e2\u2020\u2019rdfs:label, range\u00e2\u2020\u2019rdfs:range (null means omit field), propertyType+'owl:'\u00e2\u2020\u2019type.",
