        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposed change introduces a new React component (PropertyCreationDialog.tsx), modifies five existing source files across UI, emitter, serialization, and validation layers, adds a new validation error code, and implements ADR-009 Turtle and validator obligations \u00e2\u20ac\u201d all of which constitute behavioral specification implementation, not editorial correction.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present (urn:fnsr:task:368-recon-r4-4). The substantive-change requirement is satisfied. Denial is grounded in three unresolved issues surfaced by the SME (urn:fnsr:task:370-sme-r4-4), all confirmed against the live codebase and SPEC text:\n\n**S1 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d BLOCKING (VMP_CONTEXT missing `\"rdfs:range\": { \"@type\": \"@id\" }`):** Developer change C8 (src/kernel/canonicalize.ts) adds foaf and schema prefix entries to VMP_CONTEXT but does not add the necessary `\"rdfs:range\": { \"@type\": \"@id\" }` entry. File-read confirmation: VMP_CONTEXT lines 66\u00e2\u20ac\u201c94 show every other IRI-valued predicate (rdfs:subClassOf, rdfs:subPropertyOf, ecm:subjectIri, ecm:classIris, iao:isAbout, etc.) carries `\"@type\": \"@id\"`, but rdfs:range is entirely absent. Without this entry, a conformant JSON-LD 1.1 processor interprets `\"rdfs:range\": \"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal\"` as a plain string literal \u00e2\u20ac\u201d producing `<termIRI> rdfs:range \"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal\"^^xsd:string` rather than `<termIRI> rdfs:range xsd:decimal`. A literal object is not a DataRange; this voids the OWL 2 DL range axiom in the normative canonical format (SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.2). The Turtle emitter (C7) handles IRI expansion correctly via its own PREFIX_MAP, but the Turtle and JSON-LD paths are independent serializers; both must be correct. The review focus criterion \"SME confirms OWL 2 DL conformance\" is explicitly unmet.\n\n**S2 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d MAJOR (ANNOTATION_DATATYPE_IRI_COLLISION absent):** SPEC \u00c2\u00a76.1 line 730 mandates: \"The validator MUST emit an `ANNOTATION_DATATYPE_IRI_COLLISION` finding (severity: error) on violation\" of the pairwise-disjoint IRI constraint across owl:AnnotationProperty / owl:DatatypeProperty / owl:ObjectProperty sets. File-read confirmation: validate/codes.ts lists exactly 17 hard-error codes; ANNOTATION_DATATYPE_IRI_COLLISION is not among them. The PropertyCreationDialog (C1) introduces a non-blocking IRI uniqueness check that warns but does not block submit; a user who ignores this warning can create two property terms with the same IRI but different types, producing an OWL 2 DL entity-type partition violation (OWL 2 DL \u00c2\u00a73.1) that the validator will not flag. RANGE_CLASS_ON_DATATYPE_PROPERTY (C9) is added but ANNOTATION_DATATYPE_IRI_COLLISION is not \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the R4-4 chain leaves pairwise disjointness unenforced.\n\n**S3 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d MAJOR (RANGE_CLASS_ON_DATATYPE_PROPERTY trigger logic is wrong):** Developer change C11 (src/validate/index.ts) implements the range constraint using an XSD-prefix string heuristic: `const isXsd = rangeVal.startsWith(XSD_NS_FULL) || rangeVal.startsWith(\"xsd:\"); if (!isXsd) { findings.push(...) }`. SPEC \u00c2\u00a77.5 line 817 defines the normative trigger as: \"when an owl:DatatypeProperty term carries a rdfs:range value that **resolves to an IRI typed as owl:Class in ecm:terms**\" \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a data-driven Set lookup, not a string-prefix guard. The heuristic produces false positives for valid OWL 2 DL datatypes outside the XSD namespace (owl:real, owl:rational, rdf:PlainLiteral, rdfs:Literal, custom rdfs:Datatype instances). The correct implementation is: (1) build a Set of owl:Class IRIs from rawTerms; (2) emit RANGE_CLASS_ON_DATATYPE_PROPERTY only when the range value is a member of that Set. The XSD-prefix guard is not in the SPEC normative trigger and must be removed.\n\n**S4 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d ADVISORY (BCP47 regex rejects private-use and grandfathered tags):** BCP47_RE rejects RFC 5646 \u00c2\u00a72.1 private-use (`x-...`) and grandfathered (`i-...`) primary subtags. Advisory for the ontology-modeling domain; does not block ratification on its own.\n\nAll three issues (S1 blocking, S2 major, S3 major) require a revised developer pass. The SME recommendation is explicitly \"revise.\" Ratification is denied pending corrected changes addressing at minimum S1 (C8 must be extended with `\"rdfs:range\": { \"@type\": \"@id\" }`), S2 (ANNOTATION_DATATYPE_IRI_COLLISION code + validator), and S3 (C11 trigger logic replaced with owl:Class Set lookup).",
