            "evidence": "src/emit/turtle.ts:80-83 (JSON_KEY_TO_RDF_PRED maps iao:isAbout -> obo:IAO_0000136), src/kernel/canonicalize.ts:93 (VMP_CONTEXT iao:isAbout @id alias -> obo:IAO_0000136), ADR-007 (canonical IAO IRI binding; explicit rationale for obo: prefix)",
            "correction": "Under Option gamma (recommended): no change. Retain obo:IAO_0000136 as the emitted predicate. Under Option alpha only: change JSON_KEY_TO_RDF_PRED[\"iao:isAbout\"] from \"obo:IAO_0000136\" to \"cco:ont00001808\" in src/emit/turtle.ts:81, AND change VMP_CONTEXT iao:isAbout \"@id\" value from \"obo:IAO_0000136\" to \"cco:ont00001808\" in src/kernel/canonicalize.ts:93. Do not apply the Option alpha correction under Option gamma.",
            "sme_verdict": "confirm-with-detail",
            "sme_verdict_note": "The coworker is correct that cco:ont00001808 is the CCO-native choice under strict CCO reuse. The SME discipline notes that obo:IAO_0000136 is the canonical source IRI (the term that CCO's wrapper cites as its provenance), and using the source IRI avoids CCO namespace lock-in. If the project later imports other CCO-adjacent ontologies that use obo:IAO_0000136 directly, the canonical IRI provides better cross-ontology alignment. Under Option gamma, retaining obo:IAO_0000136 is the SME-preferred approach. This is an advisory gap \u00e2\u20ac\u201d no OWL 2 DL conformance violation exists under either choice."
          },
          {
            "id": "R5-B2",
            "severity": "minor",
            "category": "representation_reality",
