            "evidence": "src/tbox/index.ts:36-38 (PROJECT_TBOX_TURTLE ecm:Serialization rdfs:comment), src/tbox/index.ts:95-97 (getProjectTBoxNodes ecm:Serialization rdfs:comment)",
            "correction": "In src/tbox/index.ts update BOTH locations: (1) PROJECT_TBOX_TURTLE string line 37: change rdfs:comment value to \"An Information Content Entity that represents a project according to the syntax of some serialization format.\" (2) getProjectTBoxNodes() array, ecm:Serialization entry line 96: change \"rdfs:comment\" value to \"An Information Content Entity that represents a project according to the syntax of some serialization format.\"",
            "sme_verdict": "confirm",
            "sme_verdict_note": "Coworker's reading is correct per CCO. The phrase 'concrete encoding' conflates the ICE (the content) with its format/medium (the bearer-side feature). The proposed replacement text is ontologically clean: 'represents a project according to the syntax of some serialization format' grounds the ICE in its aboutness relation to the project (what it is about) and names the syntactic-convention relationship without implying any format-specific subtyping. Important scoping correction: the decomposition's scope field says 'likely src/kernel/canonicalize.ts' \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this is wrong. The target file is src/tbox/index.ts, and the developer must update BOTH the raw Turtle string AND the getProjectTBoxNodes() array, as each feeds a separate output path (Turtle prepend vs. JSON-LD @graph)."
          },
