            "evidence": "src/tbox/index.ts:40-44 (PROJECT_TBOX_TURTLE isSerializationOf with domain/range), src/tbox/index.ts:99-105 (getProjectTBoxNodes isSerializationOf), src/emit/turtle.ts:194 (emitted in predicate IRI loop)",
            "correction": "Under Option gamma (recommended): retain ecm:isSerializationOf. Add to PROJECT_TBOX_TURTLE in src/tbox/index.ts after the existing rdfs:range triple: skos:definition \"Relates an Information Content Entity (the serialization) to the Ontology Design Pattern it represents; the serialization encodes the ODP according to the syntax of a specific serialization format and was generated from it.\" ; Also add skos: prefix declaration to PROJECT_TBOX_TURTLE: @prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> . Under Option alpha: remove ecm:isSerializationOf from TBox and rewrite all ecm:isSerializationOf usage sites to emit cco:ont00001808 assertions instead.",
            "sme_verdict": "confirm-with-detail",
            "sme_verdict_note": "Do NOT replace ecm:isSerializationOf with cco:ont00001808 under Option gamma. The relationship 'this Turtle file is the serialization of this project' is a specific sub-relation of 'this ICE is about that entity.' The more specific property preserves information that the generic one loses. The coworker's note that 'a serialization ICE can be modeled as about the project' is correct but argues for declaring ecm:isSerializationOf as a sub-property of some aboutness property, not for eliminating it. Adding skos:definition is the correct gap-closure for the 'needs justification' concern."
