          {
            "id": "R5-B5",
            "severity": "major",
            "category": "dl_conformance",
            "claim": "ecm:Instance is emitted as an rdf:type assertion on every domain individual in the Turtle export. ecm:Instance is not declared as owl:Class in the TBox (src/tbox/index.ts contains no ecm:Instance declaration). This produces two problems: (1) domain individuals carry a type membership claim in an undeclared tool-vocabulary class, conflating tool bookkeeping with domain ontology membership; (2) any domain reasoner consuming the export will treat ecm:Instance as an unanchored class by open-world assumption, potentially introducing unwanted entailments if the ecm: ontology is later imported. This is the most significant OWL 2 DL hygiene issue in the Round 5 batch.",
            "evidence": "src/emit/turtle.ts:178-181 (nodeToQuads type loop emits all typesOf(node) values with no ecm:Instance filter), src/emit/turtle.ts:66-72 (TBOX_IDS does not include ecm:Instance), src/projection/index.ts:36 (ecm:Instance in SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST \u00e2\u20ac\u201d correct for internal projection but means it reaches the Turtle emitter), demo/library-catalog.jsonld:74-117 (all five instances typed ecm:Instance)",
            "correction": "Under Options alpha and gamma (recommended): In src/emit/turtle.ts, inside the nodeToQuads() function, add one guard in the rdf:type emission loop at line 178: for (const t of typesOf(node)) { if (expandIri(t) === 'https://edgecanonical.org/ns/modeler#Instance') continue; result.push(makeQuad(subj, rdfTypeNode, termForIri(t))); } This strips ecm:Instance from Turtle type assertions while preserving it in the internal JSON-LD format (where SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST correctly retains it for projection). Under Option beta only: add to PROJECT_TBOX_TURTLE in src/tbox/index.ts: ecm:Instance a owl:Class ; rdfs:comment \"GraphWrite tool-internal bookkeeping class. Marks an entity as a modeler instance node. Not a domain classifier.\" .",
            "sme_verdict": "confirm",
            "sme_verdict_note": "This is the clearest OWL 2 DL hygiene violation in the round. A domain individual typed as 'a ecm:Instance, <SomeDomainClass>' is asserting membership in two classes simultaneously: a tool-infrastructure class and a domain class. The tool-infrastructure class assertion has no domain ontology meaning and should not appear in the consumer-facing export. The ecm:Instance type marker is needed internally (the projection layer uses it to identify which ecm:instances array members to retain; the Inspector.tsx isEcmInstance guard relies on it; CanvasView.tsx uses it for canvas node binding). Stripping it from the Turtle emission path in nodeToQuads() is the minimal correct fix that preserves all internal tooling while producing a clean consumer-facing graph."
