            "state": 1,
            "content": "Recon-front cascade deadlock pattern: when I cascade-abandon chain tail tasks, the chain front (recon depending on prior-chain's abandoned test) remains pointing at the abandoned ID and the next chain wedges. This bit Round 5 four times (v2/v3/v4/v5 cascades) \u2014 each cascade fix only repaired the side I was looking at, leaving the other side broken. Detection: state_admin verify-deps-graph would catch this immediately by reporting ready tasks with non-done deps. The fnsr_stall_watch.py v3.1.0-bridge now detects it as stall_dispatch_impossible. Substrate-discipline lesson: when abandoning a task and replacing it, walk BOTH the downstream deps (tasks that depend on the abandoned task \u2014 known cascade) AND the upstream deps (tasks the abandoned task depended on \u2014 likely fine but tracked) AND the SIBLING-chain front deps (the recon-front pattern \u2014 frequently missed).",
