      "inputs": {
        "round": 5,
        "chain_label": "R5-Chain-2: Upload-path starter terms (R5-A2) (v5)",
        "item_ids": [
          "R5-A2"
        ],
        "purpose": "Read src/projection/, src/composition/, or wherever the JSON-LD upload-deserialization path lives. Identify where loaded projects bypass the New-project starter-term injection. Read STARTER_TERMS in src/validate/starter-terms.ts to understand the canonical shape (EPOCH timestamp; ecm:source: ecm:system-starter-example; ecm:ontologyId: null).",
        "files_to_read": [
          "src/validate/starter-terms.ts",
          "src/projection/index.ts",
          "src/composition/"
        ],
        "spec_refs": [
          "FNSR Spec 03 (recon requirement)",
          "Spec 08 v0.3 AP-7"
        ]
      },
      "attempts": 1,
      "outputs": {
        "findings": [
          {
            "id": "F1",
            "claim": "STARTER_TERMS canonical shape: 3 entries (rdfs:comment < rdfs:label < rdfs:seeAlso, lexicographic), all typed owl:AnnotationProperty, ecm:source: 'ecm:system-starter-example', ecm:ontologyId: null, ecm:createdAt/ecm:updatedAt both set to EPOCH = '1970-01-01T00:00:00Z', rdfs:label as { text, lang } object.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/validate/starter-terms.ts",
                "lines": "33-71",
                "excerpt": "const EPOCH = \"1970-01-01T00:00:00Z\";\nexport const STARTER_TERMS: ReadonlyArray<EcmTerm> = [\n  { id: \"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment\", type: \"owl:AnnotationProperty\", \"ecm:source\": \"ecm:system-starter-example\", \"ecm:ontologyId\": null, \"ecm:createdAt\": EPOCH, \"ecm:updatedAt\": EPOCH, \"rdfs:label\": { text: \"comment\", lang: \"en\" } },\n  { id: \"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label\", ... },\n  { id: \"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso\", ... }\n];"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/validate/starter-terms.ts",
                "lines": "23-31",
                "excerpt": "export interface EcmTerm {\n  id: string;\n  type: EcmTermType;\n  \"ecm:source\": \"ecm:system-starter-example\";\n  \"ecm:ontologyId\": null;\n  \"ecm:createdAt\": string;\n  \"ecm:updatedAt\": string;\n  \"rdfs:label\": { text: string; lang: string };\n}"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F2",
            "claim": "The new-project path injects STARTER_TERMS via buildNewDocument() in src/ui/App.tsx, which sets ecm:terms to STARTER_TERMS.map((t) => ({ ...t })).",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/ui/App.tsx",
                "lines": "23-41",
                "excerpt": "function buildNewDocument(): Record<string, unknown> {\n  return {\n    ...\n    \"ecm:terms\": STARTER_TERMS.map((t) => ({ ...t })),\n    ...\n  };\n}"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/ui/App.tsx",
                "lines": "10",
                "excerpt": "import { STARTER_TERMS } from \"../validate/starter-terms.js\";"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F3",
            "claim": "The upload-deserialization path (FR-U002) is handleFileChange() in src/ui/App.tsx:137-192; its pipeline is JSON.parse \u00e2\u2020\u2019 migrate() \u00e2\u2020\u2019 normalizeOnLoad() \u00e2\u2020\u2019 validate() \u00e2\u2020\u2019 setProject(), with no starter-term injection step anywhere in the chain.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/ui/App.tsx",
                "lines": "136-192",
                "excerpt": "// FR-U002: File selected -- read, migrate, normalize, validate, set state\nfunction handleFileChange(event: ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) {\n  ...\n  parsed = JSON.parse(raw);\n  const migrateResult = migrate(parsed);\n  ...\n  const { document: migrated, migrationReport } = migrateResult;\n  const { document: normalized } = normalizeOnLoad(migrated);\n  setValidationReport(validate(normalized));\n  setProject(normalized);\n  ...\n}"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F4",
            "claim": "No starter-term injection function for the upload path exists anywhere in the src/ tree; STARTER_TERMS is imported in only two files \u00e2\u20ac\u201d App.tsx (used only inside buildNewDocument()) and tests/starter-terms.test.ts.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/validate/starter-terms.ts",
                "lines": "7-10",
                "excerpt": "* Shared by:\n*   src/ui/App.tsx  -- buildNewDocument() injects these into ecm:terms\n*   tests/starter-terms.test.ts -- well-formedness verification"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F5",
            "claim": "src/composition/ contains only two README stub files (src/composition/concepts/README.md, src/composition/synchronizations/README.md); no TypeScript files exist in that directory.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/composition/concepts/README.md",
                "lines": "1",
                "excerpt": "(stub only \u00e2\u20ac\u201d confirmed by Glob returning no .ts files under src/composition/)"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/composition/synchronizations/README.md",
                "lines": "1",
                "excerpt": "(stub only)"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F6",
            "claim": "src/projection/index.ts implements projectSemantic(), a pure semantic-projection algorithm (SPEC \u00c2\u00a76.3 steps 1\u00e2\u20ac\u201c6); it is not the upload-deserialization handler and is not called during the handleFileChange() pipeline.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/projection/index.ts",
                "lines": "1-16",
                "excerpt": "/**\n * Semantic Projection (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md section 1.4)\n * ...\n * projectSemantic(project) implements the section 6.3 steps 1-6 algorithm:\n * ...\n * Pure function: no I/O, no Date.now(), no Math.random().\n * Layer boundary: MUST NOT import from src/adapters/ or src/composition/.\n */"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/projection/index.ts",
                "lines": "202-307",
                "excerpt": "export function projectSemantic(\n  project: Record<string, unknown>,\n): string { ... return serializeVmp(doc); }"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F7",
            "claim": "The decomposition document describes R5-A2 scope as 'project-load handler in src/projection/ or src/composition/'; the actual upload-deserialization handler is handleFileChange() in src/ui/App.tsx \u00e2\u20ac\u201d neither src/projection/index.ts nor src/composition/ participates in the upload pipeline.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "demo/FEEDBACK-ROUND-5-DECOMPOSITION.md",
                "lines": "119",
                "excerpt": "- **Scope:** project-load handler in `src/projection/` or `src/composition/` (wherever upload-deserialization lands). Add: after deserialize, if `rdfs:label` / `rdfs:comment` / `rdfs:seeAlso` are absent from the term table, inject them with the same starter-term shape used at New-project time."
              },
              {
                "file": "src/ui/App.tsx",
                "lines": "137-192",
                "excerpt": "// FR-U002: File selected -- read, migrate, normalize, validate, set state\nfunction handleFileChange(...) { ... }"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F8",
            "claim": "The EcmTerm interface has no read-only flag field; the read-only behavior for starter (and imported) terms is enforced at the UI layer in TermSidebar.tsx:153-155 via ecm:source === 'ecm:project-created' check (only project-created terms are clickable/editable).",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/validate/starter-terms.ts",
                "lines": "23-31",
                "excerpt": "export interface EcmTerm {\n  id: string;\n  type: EcmTermType;\n  \"ecm:source\": \"ecm:system-starter-example\";\n  \"ecm:ontologyId\": null;\n  \"ecm:createdAt\": string;\n  \"ecm:updatedAt\": string;\n  \"rdfs:label\": { text: string; lang: string };\n}  // no readOnly / isReadOnly field"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/ui/TermSidebar.tsx",
                "lines": "152-157",
                "excerpt": "// Only project-created terms are clickable; imported/starter are not.\nconst isClickable =\n  onTermClick !== undefined &&\n  term[\"ecm:source\"] === \"ecm:project-created\";\n// Imported-ontology terms carry an affirmative read-only signal (FR-U010; Chain C).\nconst isImported = term[\"ecm:source\"] === \"ecm:imported-ontology\";"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F9",
            "claim": "The migrate() function in src/migrate/index.ts does not inject starter terms during any migration leg (v0.2\u00e2\u2020\u2019v0.3 or v0.3\u00e2\u2020\u2019v0.4); it only handles: ecm:literalAssertions init, ecm:settings defaults, rdfs:subClassOf/subPropertyOf stubs, iao:isAbout init, ecm:serializations init, ecm:_legacyAnchorPlaceholder marker, and label-shape coercion.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/migrate/index.ts",
                "lines": "139-227",
                "excerpt": "function migrateV2toV3(...) { ... } // adds literalAssertions, settings, subclass stubs; no STARTER_TERMS\nfunction migrateV3toV4(...) { ... } // adds iao:isAbout, serializations, _legacyAnchorPlaceholder, label coercion; no STARTER_TERMS"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F10",
            "claim": "normalizeOnLoad() in src/normalize/index.ts only normalizes ecm:terms rdfs:label plain-string-to-{text,lang} shape and structural canonicalization; it does not add missing terms, inject STARTER_TERMS, or alter the ecm:terms length.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/normalize/index.ts",
                "lines": "92-135",
                "excerpt": "export function normalizeOnLoad(\n  doc: Record<string, unknown>,\n): NormalizeOnLoadResult {\n  ...\n  // Step 1: Apply label-shape normalization to ecm:terms.\n  // Plain-string rdfs:label values are coerced to {text, lang: 'en'}.\n  ...\n  // Step 2: Structural canonicalization via serializeVmp round-trip.\n  ...\n  // No STARTER_TERMS injection; no new term insertion.\n}"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F11",
            "claim": "The three STARTER_TERMS IDs (rdfs:comment, rdfs:label, rdfs:seeAlso) match the ids named in the R5-A2 defect report; their presence can be checked at load time by testing for ecm:source === 'ecm:system-starter-example' OR by testing IRI membership, since STARTER_TERMS uses well-known rdfs: IRIs.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/validate/starter-terms.ts",
                "lines": "44-70",
                "excerpt": "id: \"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment\"\nid: \"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label\"\nid: \"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso\""
              },
              {
                "file": "demo/FEEDBACK-ROUND-5-DECOMPOSITION.md",
                "lines": "115-116",
                "excerpt": "- **Atomic claim:** The 3 starter annotation properties (`rdfs:label`, `rdfs:comment`, `rdfs:seeAlso` per R4-2 starter-terms cleanup) are injected on **New project** but are NOT injected when the user uploads an existing JSON-LD file that doesn't already contain them."
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          }
        ],
        "summary": "The upload-deserialization path (FR-U002) is entirely contained in handleFileChange() at src/ui/App.tsx:137-192. Its pipeline is: JSON.parse \u00e2\u2020\u2019 migrate() \u00e2\u2020\u2019 normalizeOnLoad() \u00e2\u2020\u2019 validate() \u00e2\u2020\u2019 setProject(). None of these steps inject STARTER_TERMS. The new-project path (buildNewDocument()) is the only site that calls STARTER_TERMS, and it is not reached by the upload flow. No injection helper function for the upload path exists anywhere in the codebase \u00e2\u20ac\u201d STARTER_TERMS is imported only in App.tsx (for buildNewDocument()) and in the test file. The decomposition document R5-A2 scope field names 'src/projection/ or src/composition/' as the upload-deserialization location; both are incorrect \u00e2\u20ac\u201d src/composition/ has no TypeScript files, and src/projection/index.ts implements a semantic-projection algorithm that is not called during upload. The actual injection gap is in App.tsx between the normalizeOnLoad() call (line 175) and the setProject() call (line 179). The STARTER_TERMS canonical shape is fully observable: EPOCH timestamps for determinism, ecm:source: 'ecm:system-starter-example', ecm:ontologyId: null, owl:AnnotationProperty type, rdfs:label as {text, lang} object. The 'read-only' property mentioned in the SME note for R5-A2 is not a field in the EcmTerm interface; read-only enforcement is implemented as a source-discriminated UI gate in TermSidebar.tsx:153-155 (only ecm:project-created terms are editable).",
        "evidence_paths": [
          "src/validate/starter-terms.ts",
          "src/ui/App.tsx",
          "src/projection/index.ts",
          "src/normalize/index.ts",
          "src/migrate/index.ts",
          "src/ui/TermSidebar.tsx",
          "src/composition/concepts/README.md",
          "src/composition/synchronizations/README.md",
          "tests/starter-terms.test.ts",
          "tests/normalize-on-load.test.ts",
          "demo/FEEDBACK-ROUND-5.md",
          "demo/FEEDBACK-ROUND-5-DECOMPOSITION.md"
        ],
        "referenced_evidence": [
          {
            "type": "spec_section",
            "id": "\u00c2\u00a75.7",
            "source": "project/SPEC.md"
          },
