            "type": "adr",
            "id": "ADR-008",
            "source": "project/DECISIONS.md"
          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "Should starter-term injection on upload be idempotent with respect to existing ecm:terms entries? Specifically: if a loaded project already has an entry with id 'http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label' but ecm:source != 'ecm:system-starter-example' (e.g., a project-created term that shadows the starter IRI), should the existing entry be preserved, overwritten, or should both entries coexist?",
          "Should starter-term injection for the upload path happen before or after normalizeOnLoad()? (Affects whether injected terms are guaranteed to be in canonical form on first pass or require a second normalization round.)",
          "The decomposition SME note for R5-A2 mentions 'including owl:AnnotationProperty typing and read-only-flag' \u00e2\u20ac\u201d there is no ecm:readOnly or equivalent field in the current EcmTerm interface; read-only behavior is source-discriminated at the TermSidebar UI layer. Does the injection need to introduce a new read-only field, or is the ecm:source === 'ecm:system-starter-example' discrimination already sufficient to enforce the invariant?",
          "The injection function will need to live somewhere in the codebase \u00e2\u20ac\u201d is it a new helper in src/validate/starter-terms.ts (collocated with STARTER_TERMS), a new module, or an inline expansion inside handleFileChange()? The decomposition's stated scope file (src/projection/ or src/composition/) does not match any existing upload-path code."
        ],
        "scope_assessment": "Investigated STARTER_TERMS canonical shape (src/validate/starter-terms.ts), the new-project injection site (src/ui/App.tsx buildNewDocument()), the complete upload-deserialization pipeline (src/ui/App.tsx handleFileChange() + migrate() + normalizeOnLoad()), the composition and projection directories, and the R5-A2 decomposition entry; did not investigate test fixtures for upload behavior or the full validate/index.ts validation logic beyond what was needed to trace the upload pipeline."
      },
