        ],
        "purpose": "After deserialize on upload, if rdfs:label / rdfs:comment / rdfs:seeAlso are absent from the term table, inject them with the EXACT shape from STARTER_TERMS (per SME R5-A2 verdict-note: must use EPOCH timestamp, not live timestamp; must include ecm:source: ecm:system-starter-example; ecm:ontologyId: null). Determinism MUST be preserved (same document loaded twice MUST produce identical canonical form).",
        "files_in_scope": [
          "src/projection/index.ts",
          "src/composition/",
          "src/validate/starter-terms.ts"
        ],
        "sme_findings_source": "task 374 outputs.findings (UPSTREAM); filter by id matching this chain's item_ids",
        "constraint": "Produce minimal change set (changes[] with before/after); honor SME verdict_note constraints; ensure non-overlapping BEFORE-snippet regions (lesson from chain 1 C6 overlap)."
      },
      "attempts": 1,
      "outputs": {
        "changes": [
          {
            "id": "C1",
            "file": "src/validate/starter-terms.ts",
            "rationale": "Update the module-level doc comment to list handleFileChange() / injectStarterTerms() as a new consumer, so the 'Shared by' block stays accurate.",
            "before": " * Shared by:\n *   src/ui/App.tsx  -- buildNewDocument() injects these into ecm:terms\n *   tests/starter-terms.test.ts -- well-formedness verification",
            "after": " * Shared by:\n *   src/ui/App.tsx  -- buildNewDocument() injects these into ecm:terms;\n *                      handleFileChange() calls injectStarterTerms() on upload\n *   tests/starter-terms.test.ts -- well-formedness verification",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C2",
            "file": "src/validate/starter-terms.ts",
            "rationale": "Add injectStarterTerms() collocated with STARTER_TERMS. The function checks presence by id only (preserves any existing entry with the same IRI regardless of ecm:source), injects missing entries as shallow copies of STARTER_TERMS (EPOCH timestamps, ecm:source: ecm:system-starter-example, ecm:ontologyId: null), re-sorts by id, and returns the original array reference unchanged when all three IRIs are already present. Placing injection BEFORE normalizeOnLoad() in the call-site allows a single serializeVmp round-trip to canonicalize key order for injected terms.",
            "before": "    \"rdfs:label\": { text: \"seeAlso\", lang: \"en\" },\n  },\n];",
            "after": "    \"rdfs:label\": { text: \"seeAlso\", lang: \"en\" },\n  },\n];\n\n/**\n * Inject any missing STARTER_TERMS entries into an ecm:terms array.\n *\n * Idempotent: if an entry with a matching id already exists (regardless of\n * ecm:source or other fields), it is preserved as-is; no duplicate is\n * inserted. Injected entries are shallow copies of STARTER_TERMS constants,\n * including EPOCH timestamps (1970-01-01T00:00:00Z) for determinism: the\n * same document loaded twice must produce identical canonical form.\n *\n * The returned array is sorted lexicographically by id. If all three starter\n * terms are already present, the original array reference is returned unchanged.\n *\n * Used on the upload-deserialization path (FR-U002) to ensure rdfs:label,\n * rdfs:comment, and rdfs:seeAlso are always present after loading a document\n * that predates or omits them (R5-A2).\n *\n * @param terms - The ecm:terms array from the loaded document (entries may be\n *   any object shape from JSON.parse; only the id field is consulted for\n *   presence detection).\n * @returns The merged and sorted terms array, or the original if unchanged.\n */\nexport function injectStarterTerms(terms: unknown[]): unknown[] {\n  const existingIds = new Set<unknown>(\n    terms.map((t) =>\n      typeof t === \"object\" && t !== null\n        ? (t as Record<string, unknown>)[\"id\"]\n        : undefined,\n    ),\n  );\n  const missing = STARTER_TERMS.filter((st) => !existingIds.has(st.id));\n  if (missing.length === 0) return terms;\n  const merged: unknown[] = [\n    ...terms,\n    ...missing.map((st): Record<string, unknown> => ({ ...st })),\n  ];\n  merged.sort((a, b) => {\n    const idOf = (v: unknown): string =>\n      typeof v === \"object\" && v !== null\n        ? String((v as Record<string, unknown>)[\"id\"] ?? \"\")\n        : \"\";\n    const ai = idOf(a);\n    const bi = idOf(b);\n    return ai < bi ? -1 : ai > bi ? 1 : 0;\n  });\n  return merged;\n}",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C3",
            "file": "src/ui/App.tsx",
            "rationale": "Add injectStarterTerms to the existing starter-terms import. STARTER_TERMS is still consumed by buildNewDocument() so the existing name is retained.",
            "before": "import { STARTER_TERMS } from \"../validate/starter-terms.js\";",
            "after": "import { STARTER_TERMS, injectStarterTerms } from \"../validate/starter-terms.js\";",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C4",
            "file": "src/ui/App.tsx",
            "rationale": "Call injectStarterTerms() inside handleFileChange() BEFORE normalizeOnLoad(), so the injected terms are canonicalized by the existing serializeVmp round-trip in a single pass. The identity check (injected !== rawTerms) avoids creating a new document object when no injection is needed. EPOCH timestamps come from STARTER_TERMS constants \u00e2\u20ac\u201d no Date.now() \u00e2\u20ac\u201d so loading the same document twice always produces identical canonical form (SPEC \u00c2\u00a79 / ADR-001).",
            "before": "      const { document: normalized } = normalizeOnLoad(migrated);\n      // Call validate per FR-U002; findings displayed in ValidationPanel (task 2.10).\n      setValidationReport(validate(normalized));\n\n      setProject(normalized);",
            "after": "      // FR-U002 / R5-A2: Inject missing starter terms before normalization.\n      // Preserves EPOCH timestamps from STARTER_TERMS for determinism: the same\n      // document loaded twice produces identical canonical form (SPEC \u00c2\u00a79 / ADR-001).\n      const rawTerms = migrated[\"ecm:terms\"];\n      let withStarters = migrated;\n      if (Array.isArray(rawTerms)) {\n        const injected = injectStarterTerms(rawTerms);\n        if (injected !== rawTerms) {\n          withStarters = { ...migrated, \"ecm:terms\": injected };\n        }\n      }\n\n      const { document: normalized } = normalizeOnLoad(withStarters);\n      // Call validate per FR-U002; findings displayed in ValidationPanel (task 2.10).\n      setValidationReport(validate(normalized));\n\n      setProject(normalized);",
            "scope": "minimal"
          }
        ],
        "tests_recommended": [
          {
            "file": "tests/inject-starter-terms.test.ts",
            "describe": "Unit tests for injectStarterTerms() following the hand-rolled pattern in tests/starter-terms.test.ts. AC1: all 3 absent \u00e2\u2020\u2019 all 3 injected with EPOCH timestamps, ecm:source: ecm:system-starter-example, ecm:ontologyId: null. AC2: 1 of 3 present \u00e2\u2020\u2019 only the 2 missing are injected. AC3: all 3 present \u00e2\u2020\u2019 original array reference returned (=== identity check). AC4: shadowed entry (same id, ecm:source: ecm:project-created) \u00e2\u2020\u2019 preserved as-is, no duplicate. AC5: result is sorted lexicographically by id regardless of input order. AC6: determinism \u00e2\u20ac\u201d calling twice on the same input produces structurally identical output (no live timestamps). AC7: after injection, calling normalizeOnLoad() on a document with the injected terms returns wasNormalized: false on a second call (idempotency preserved end-to-end)."
          },
          {
            "file": "tests/normalize-on-load.test.ts",
            "describe": "Extend existing test suite with AC4: upload-path integration. Build a minimal project document without any ecm:terms starter entries (e.g., ecm:terms: []), call injectStarterTerms() then normalizeOnLoad() on it, and assert: (1) all three STARTER_TERMS IRIs are present in the result's ecm:terms; (2) each injected entry has ecm:createdAt === '1970-01-01T00:00:00Z'; (3) a second injectStarterTerms() + normalizeOnLoad() pass on the result produces an identical document (determinism invariant)."
          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "Shadowed starter IRI policy: the proposal preserves any existing ecm:terms entry whose id matches a STARTER_TERM IRI (regardless of ecm:source). If a pre-existing project-created term shadows rdfs:label (same IRI, source ecm:project-created), it will be treated as editable by TermSidebar.tsx (source-based gate). Should injection instead overwrite shadowed entries to enforce ecm:source: ecm:system-starter-example on all three starter IRIs? Overwriting is stronger correctness but silently replaces user-authored data; preserving is safer but allows the non-starter shape through.",
          "Sequencing confirmation: this proposal injects BEFORE normalizeOnLoad() so a single serializeVmp round-trip canonicalizes injected term key order. An alternative is to inject AFTER normalizeOnLoad() and run normalizeOnLoad() a second time. The pre-normalize approach is preferred here for efficiency, but confirm this is acceptable to the operator before apply."
        ],
        "summary": "4 minimal changes across 2 files implement R5-A2. (1) injectStarterTerms() is added to src/validate/starter-terms.ts collocated with STARTER_TERMS \u00e2\u20ac\u201d checks presence by id, injects missing entries as STARTER_TERMS shallow copies (EPOCH timestamps, ecm:system-starter-example source, null ontologyId), sorts by id, returns original reference if unchanged. (2) src/ui/App.tsx handleFileChange() calls injectStarterTerms() on the migrated document's ecm:terms BEFORE normalizeOnLoad(), so the single existing serializeVmp round-trip canonicalizes injected key order in one pass. The import is updated to add injectStarterTerms alongside the existing STARTER_TERMS import. No new fields added to EcmTerm; no new Date() or live timestamps introduced; no layer-boundary violations (src/validate/ is at Layer 0 reach from src/ui/). The src/composition/ files noted in the task's files_in_scope have no TypeScript content (confirmed by recon F5) and require no changes.",
        "self_assessment": "confident"
      },
