      "outputs": {
        "ruling": "ratified",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposal adds a new exported function (injectStarterTerms), modifies the upload-deserialization pipeline in handleFileChange(), and changes runtime behavior so that uploaded projects receive starter terms they previously lacked \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this is new behavioral logic, not a typo or formatting correction.",
        "rationale": "All preconditions for ratification are satisfied. Reconnaissance (urn:fnsr:task:452-recon-r5-c2-v5) is present in UPSTREAM and provides the necessary evidentiary grounding. SME-374 finding R5-A2 is confirmed-with-detail and supplies the critical implementation constraint (EPOCH timestamps; inject STARTER_TERMS verbatim; re-sort by id). The developer's four-change proposal correctly implements all of these requirements. Detailed assessment of each change follows.\n\nC1 (doc comment update): The before-snippet at src/validate/starter-terms.ts:8-10 matches the file exactly. The update correctly adds the new handleFileChange()/injectStarterTerms() consumer to the 'Shared by' block.\n\nC2 (injectStarterTerms function): Placed in src/validate/starter-terms.ts, collocated with STARTER_TERMS \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the SME-preferred location for consistency with STARTER_TERMS consumers. The function (a) builds a Set of existing ids using the id field of each entry, preserving any existing entry with a matching IRI regardless of ecm:source (the safer policy for shadowed-IRI edge cases); (b) filters STARTER_TERMS for missing entries; (c) returns the original array reference unchanged if none are missing \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this identity-check is load-bearing for C4's efficient short-circuit; (d) when injection is needed, merges existing + missing as shallow copies of STARTER_TERMS constants, which carry EPOCH timestamps ('1970-01-01T00:00:00Z') satisfying the SME's determinism requirement (same document loaded twice \u00e2\u2020\u2019 identical canonical form, per SPEC \u00c2\u00a79 / ADR-001); (e) sorts the merged array lexicographically by id, satisfying the SME 're-sort by id' requirement. No Date.now(), no new Date(), no live timestamps introduced. TypeScript types (unknown[]) are appropriate for raw-JSON-boundary input.\n\nC3 (import update): The before-snippet at src/ui/App.tsx:10 matches the file exactly. Adding injectStarterTerms to the existing import is minimal and correct; STARTER_TERMS remains in the import for buildNewDocument().\n\nC4 (handleFileChange call-site): The before-snippet at src/ui/App.tsx:175-179 matches the file exactly (confirmed by direct file read: lines 175-179 show normalizeOnLoad(migrated) \u00e2\u2020\u2019 validate \u00e2\u2020\u2019 setProject). The after inserts the injection step BETWEEN migrate() completion and normalizeOnLoad(), which is the correct sequencing: (a) injection before normalizeOnLoad() allows the single existing serializeVmp round-trip inside normalizeOnLoad() to canonicalize injected term key order in one pass; (b) the identity check (injected !== rawTerms) avoids creating a new document object when all three starter IRIs are already present; (c) the null guard (Array.isArray(rawTerms)) is correct \u00e2\u20ac\u201d if ecm:terms is absent or not an array, injection is skipped without error.\n\nLayer boundaries: src/validate/starter-terms.ts is not Layer 0 kernel (kernel is src/kernel/); it is a validate-layer module. src/ui/App.tsx already imports from src/validate/ (confirmed line 10: import { STARTER_TERMS } from '../validate/starter-terms.js'). No new cross-layer violations are introduced. No imports from src/adapters/ or src/composition/ are added to any kernel module.\n\nDeterminism: STARTER_TERMS entries use EPOCH = '1970-01-01T00:00:00Z' as both createdAt and updatedAt; the shallow-copy ({...st}) propagates these constants into injected entries. No nondeterministic API is introduced. The function is pure (no I/O, no time, no randomness). Idempotent: calling injectStarterTerms twice on the same input produces the same output.\n\nReconnaissance alignment: Recon F3 confirmed handleFileChange() pipeline (JSON.parse \u00e2\u2020\u2019 migrate() \u00e2\u2020\u2019 normalizeOnLoad() \u00e2\u2020\u2019 validate() \u00e2\u2020\u2019 setProject()) with no injection step. Recon F7 confirmed the decomposition scope error (src/projection/ and src/composition/ named as target; actual target is App.tsx). Recon F4 confirmed no injection helper exists anywhere in src/. Recon F1 confirmed STARTER_TERMS canonical shape (EPOCH timestamps, ecm:source: ecm:system-starter-example, ecm:ontologyId: null, owl:AnnotationProperty). The developer's implementation addresses every reconnaissance finding precisely.\n\nSME alignment: SME R5-A2 (confirm-with-detail) requires: inject full STARTER_TERMS entry verbatim (satisfied by shallow copies of STARTER_TERMS constants), EPOCH timestamps (satisfied), re-sort by id (satisfied), inject only if absent (satisfied by id-based presence check). The developer's open question on shadowed IRI policy (preserve vs overwrite) defaults to preserve \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this is the safer behavior (no silent data loss) and is within ratified scope; it can be revisited if the shadowing case materialises with user complaints.\n\nNo blocking issues identified. The two open questions (shadowing policy; pre- vs post-normalizeOnLoad sequencing) are resolved by the developer's chosen defaults (preserve; pre-normalize) and do not require operator adjudication before apply.",
