            "content": "The decomposition document named 'src/projection/ or src/composition/' as the upload-deserialization scope for R5-A2; reconnaissance (F5, F6, F7) established that src/composition/ has no TypeScript files and src/projection/index.ts is a semantic-projection algorithm not called during upload \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the actual handler is handleFileChange() in src/ui/App.tsx. The reconnaissance task caught a factual scope error that would have sent the developer to the wrong file with high confidence in the wrong target. This is a repeatable pattern: decomposition scope fields written without direct code inspection are systematically unreliable when the decomposition author does not trace the actual call graph. Reconnaissance's role in establishing the true injection site before developer dispatch was not ceremonial \u00e2\u20ac\u201d it was blocking-error prevention."
