            "id": "B2",
            "category": "methodology-refinement-candidate",
            "content": "The SME finding for R5-A2 elevated EPOCH-timestamp injection as a first-class determinism constraint: any code path that reconstructs or re-inserts system-issued terms (ecm:source: ecm:system-starter-example) must use the STARTER_TERMS constant timestamps (EPOCH = '1970-01-01T00:00:00Z'), not a live timestamp. The developer's implementation correctly operationalised this by using shallow copies ({...st}) of STARTER_TERMS entries rather than reconstructing term objects. This pattern \u00e2\u20ac\u201d 'system-issued canonical entries must carry canonical timestamps regardless of when they are materialised into a document' \u00e2\u20ac\u201d is likely to recur in any future feature that reconstructs or merges system-authored entries (e.g., migration legs that add default terms, import-ontology merging of system vocabulary). A methodology refinement candidate: formalise this as a rule in the developer dispatch template for any task touching ecm:terms injection or system-term reconstruction."
