        "summary": "The Instance-mode Inspector in src/ui/Inspector.tsx (lines 364\u00e2\u20ac\u201c573) currently uses a flat, single-section layout: the rdfs:label input sits at the very top (lines 367\u00e2\u20ac\u201c378, data-testid='gw-inspector-instance-label-input'), followed by IRI display, Class Assignments, and a single 'Literal Assertions' section (lines 447\u00e2\u20ac\u201c507) that renders all ecm:LiteralAssertion entries regardless of whether their predicate is a DatatypeProperty or AnnotationProperty. The rdfs:label is stored as a plain string directly on the ecm:Instance object (not as a LiteralAssertion and not using the ADR-008 {text, lang} shape that was applied to ecm:terms). The only property lookup helper in Inspector.tsx is getDatatypePropertyOptions() (lines 158\u00e2\u20ac\u201c173), which filters exclusively to owl:DatatypeProperty; no getAnnotationPropertyOptions() counterpart exists. AddLiteralDialog.tsx has the same restriction. The R5-A3 requirement calls for: (1) renaming/splitting the 'Literal Assertions' section into 'DataType Assertion' (owl:DatatypeProperty predicates) and 'Annotation Assertion' (owl:AnnotationProperty predicates), and (2) relocating the rdfs:label input from top-of-inspector into the Annotation Assertion section. The R4-2 dependency is satisfied (rdfs:label, rdfs:comment, rdfs:seeAlso are correctly typed owl:AnnotationProperty in starter-terms.ts). Three existing Playwright tests (instance-label.spec.ts lines 63, 91, 139) assert the current data-testid='gw-inspector-instance-label-input' by name only; their positional assumptions about the label input's location in the panel are not currently tested. The SME verdict for R5-A3 is PENDING (FNSR Spec 08 v0.3 AP-7 governs this as an ontology-content item).",
