            "rationale": "Add getAnnotationPropertyOptions() (parallel to getDatatypePropertyOptions) and getTermTypeByIri() (partition lookup that checks ecm:terms first, then STARTER_TERMS fallback). These are required to partition ecm:LiteralAssertion entries by OWL 2 DL axiom type per SME R5-A3.",
            "before": "/** Shape of an owl:Class option for the class-assignment <select>. */\ninterface OwlClassOption {\n  iri: string;\n  label: string;\n}",
            "after": "/** Shape of an owl:AnnotationProperty option for the annotation predicate display. */\ninterface AnnotationPropOption {\n  iri: string;\n  label: string;\n}\n\n/**\n * Extract all owl:AnnotationProperty entries from the project's ecm:terms, with\n * STARTER_TERMS fallback for system annotation properties not yet in ecm:terms.\n * Per SME R5-A3: partition lookup must check ecm:terms by id, falling back to\n * STARTER_TERMS for system properties.\n */\nfunction getAnnotationPropertyOptions(project: Record<string, unknown>): AnnotationPropOption[] {\n  const raw = project[\"ecm:terms\"];\n  const seen = new Set<string>();\n  const result: AnnotationPropOption[] = [];\n  if (Array.isArray(raw)) {\n    for (const item of raw as unknown[]) {\n      if (typeof item !== \"object\" || item === null) continue;\n      const obj = item as Record<string, unknown>;\n      if (typeof obj[\"id\"] !== \"string\") continue;\n      if (obj[\"type\"] !== \"owl:AnnotationProperty\") continue;\n      const iri = obj[\"id\"] as string;\n      seen.add(iri);\n      const labelText = resolveTermLabel(obj[\"rdfs:label\"]);\n      const label = labelText.length > 0 ? labelText : iriTail(iri);\n      result.push({ iri, label });\n    }\n  }\n  // Fallback: include STARTER_TERMS annotation properties not already in ecm:terms.\n  for (const st of STARTER_TERMS) {\n    if (st.type === \"owl:AnnotationProperty\" && !seen.has(st.id)) {\n      const labelText = resolveTermLabel(st[\"rdfs:label\"]);\n      const label = labelText.length > 0 ? labelText : iriTail(st.id);\n      result.push({ iri: st.id, label });\n    }\n  }\n  return result;\n}\n\n/**\n * Build a map from predicate IRI to OWL term type, checking ecm:terms first\n * then STARTER_TERMS as fallback. Used to partition ecm:LiteralAssertion entries\n * by OWL 2 DL axiom type (AnnotationAssertion vs DataPropertyAssertion).\n */\nfunction getTermTypeByIri(project: Record<string, unknown>): Map<string, string> {\n  const map = new Map<string, string>();\n  // Seed with STARTER_TERMS (lower priority; ecm:terms entries override).\n  for (const st of STARTER_TERMS) {\n    map.set(st.id, st.type);\n  }\n  const raw = project[\"ecm:terms\"];\n  if (Array.isArray(raw)) {\n    for (const item of raw as unknown[]) {\n      if (typeof item !== \"object\" || item === null) continue;\n      const obj = item as Record<string, unknown>;\n      if (typeof obj[\"id\"] !== \"string\" || typeof obj[\"type\"] !== \"string\") continue;\n      map.set(obj[\"id\"] as string, obj[\"type\"] as string);\n    }\n  }\n  return map;\n}\n\n/** Shape of an owl:Class option for the class-assignment <select>. */\ninterface OwlClassOption {\n  iri: string;\n  label: string;\n}",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C3",
            "file": "src/ui/Inspector.tsx",
            "rationale": "Compute annPropOptions, termTypeMap, and the two partitioned literal lists in the instance-mode section. annotationLiterals collects ecm:LiteralAssertions whose predicateIri resolves to owl:AnnotationProperty; datatypeLiterals collects the rest (owl:DatatypeProperty and unknown). This is the runtime partitioning required by R5-A3.",
            "before": "    const dtPropOptions = getDatatypePropertyOptions(project);",
            "after": "    const dtPropOptions = getDatatypePropertyOptions(project);\n    const annPropOptions = getAnnotationPropertyOptions(project);\n    const termTypeMap = getTermTypeByIri(project);\n    const annotationLiterals = instanceLiterals.filter(\n      (la) => termTypeMap.get(la[\"ecm:predicateIri\"]) === \"owl:AnnotationProperty\",\n    );\n    const datatypeLiterals = instanceLiterals.filter(\n      (la) => termTypeMap.get(la[\"ecm:predicateIri\"]) !== \"owl:AnnotationProperty\",\n    );",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C4",
            "file": "src/ui/Inspector.tsx",
            "rationale": "Remove the top-of-inspector Label section. Per SME R5-A3: 'The rdfs:label entry is rendered within the Annotation Assertion section \u00e2\u20ac\u201d not as a special top-of-inspector Label input.' The label input is relocated into the Annotation Assertions section (C5) while the handleLabelChange handler and EcmInstance storage model are unchanged.",
            "before": "          <p style={{ fontWeight: 600, marginBottom: \"0.5rem\" }}>Instance</p>\n          <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n            Label\n          </p>\n          <input\n            type=\"text\"\n            value={typeof selectedInstance[\"rdfs:label\"] === \"string\" ? selectedInstance[\"rdfs:label\"] : \"\"}\n            onChange={(e) => { handleLabelChange(e.target.value); }}\n            data-testid=\"gw-inspector-instance-label-input\"\n            placeholder=\"(no label)\"\n            style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", width: \"100%\", marginBottom: \"0.75rem\", boxSizing: \"border-box\" }}\n          />\n          <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n            IRI\n          </p>",
            "after": "          <p style={{ fontWeight: 600, marginBottom: \"0.5rem\" }}>Instance</p>\n          <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n            IRI\n          </p>",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C5",
            "file": "src/ui/Inspector.tsx",
            "rationale": "Replace the single flat 'Literal Assertions' section with two OWL 2 DL-aligned sections: (1) Annotation Assertions \u00e2\u20ac\u201d contains the relocated rdfs:label input plus any ecm:LiteralAssertion entries whose predicateIri resolves to owl:AnnotationProperty; (2) DataType Assertions \u00e2\u20ac\u201d contains ecm:LiteralAssertion entries whose predicateIri resolves to owl:DatatypeProperty, plus the existing 'Add literal' button (AddLiteralDialog already scoped to DatatypeProperty predicates). data-testid='gw-inspector-instance-label-input' is preserved at its new location to avoid breaking the three instance-label.spec.ts tests (recon F8). data-testid='gw-inspector-no-literals' is preserved in the DataType section for backward test compatibility.",
            "before": "          <p style={{ fontWeight: 600, marginBottom: \"0.5rem\", marginTop: \"0.75rem\" }}>\n            Literal Assertions\n          </p>\n          {instanceLiterals.length === 0 && (\n            <p\n              style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", color: \"#94a3b8\" }}\n              data-testid=\"gw-inspector-no-literals\"\n            >\n              No literal assertions.\n            </p>\n          )}\n          {instanceLiterals.map((la) => {\n            const predLabel =\n              dtPropOptions.find((dp) => dp.iri === la[\"ecm:predicateIri\"])?.label ??\n              iriTail(la[\"ecm:predicateIri\"]);\n            return (\n              <div\n                key={la.id}\n                data-testid=\"gw-literal-entry\"\n                style={{\n                  borderBottom: \"1px solid #e2e8f0\",\n                  paddingBottom: \"0.5rem\",\n                  marginBottom: \"0.5rem\",\n                }}\n              >\n                <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n                  {predLabel}\n                </p>\n                <p\n                  style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", marginBottom: \"0.25rem\" }}\n                  data-testid=\"gw-literal-value\"\n                >\n                  {la[\"ecm:value\"]}\n                  {la[\"ecm:language\"] !== null && la[\"ecm:language\"] !== undefined && (\n                    <span\n                      style={{ color: \"#64748b\", fontSize: \"0.7rem\", marginLeft: \"0.25rem\" }}\n                      data-testid=\"gw-literal-lang\"\n                    >\n                      @{la[\"ecm:language\"]}\n                    </span>\n                  )}\n                </p>\n                <button\n                  type=\"button\"\n                  data-testid=\"gw-btn-delete-literal\"\n                  onClick={() => { handleDeleteLiteral(la.id); }}\n                  style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\" }}\n                >\n                  Delete\n                </button>\n              </div>\n            );\n          })}\n          <button\n            type=\"button\"\n            data-testid=\"gw-btn-add-literal\"\n            onClick={() => { setAddLiteralOpen(true); }}\n            style={{ marginTop: \"0.5rem\", width: \"100%\" }}\n          >\n            Add literal\n          </button>",
            "after": "          {/* ---- Annotation Assertions (owl:AnnotationProperty axioms; no semantic entailments) ---- */}\n          <p\n            style={{ fontWeight: 600, marginBottom: \"0.5rem\", marginTop: \"0.75rem\" }}\n            data-testid=\"gw-inspector-annotation-assertions\"\n          >\n            Annotation Assertions\n          </p>\n          <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n            Label (rdfs:label)\n          </p>\n          <input\n            type=\"text\"\n            value={typeof selectedInstance[\"rdfs:label\"] === \"string\" ? selectedInstance[\"rdfs:label\"] : \"\"}\n            onChange={(e) => { handleLabelChange(e.target.value); }}\n            data-testid=\"gw-inspector-instance-label-input\"\n            placeholder=\"(no label)\"\n            style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", width: \"100%\", marginBottom: \"0.75rem\", boxSizing: \"border-box\" }}\n          />\n          {annotationLiterals.map((la) => {\n            const predLabel =\n              annPropOptions.find((ap) => ap.iri === la[\"ecm:predicateIri\"])?.label ??\n              iriTail(la[\"ecm:predicateIri\"]);\n            return (\n              <div\n                key={la.id}\n                data-testid=\"gw-annotation-literal-entry\"\n                style={{\n                  borderBottom: \"1px solid #e2e8f0\",\n                  paddingBottom: \"0.5rem\",\n                  marginBottom: \"0.5rem\",\n                }}\n              >\n                <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n                  {predLabel}\n                </p>\n                <p\n                  style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", marginBottom: \"0.25rem\" }}\n                  data-testid=\"gw-literal-value\"\n                >\n                  {la[\"ecm:value\"]}\n                  {la[\"ecm:language\"] !== null && la[\"ecm:language\"] !== undefined && (\n                    <span\n                      style={{ color: \"#64748b\", fontSize: \"0.7rem\", marginLeft: \"0.25rem\" }}\n                      data-testid=\"gw-literal-lang\"\n                    >\n                      @{la[\"ecm:language\"]}\n                    </span>\n                  )}\n                </p>\n                <button\n                  type=\"button\"\n                  data-testid=\"gw-btn-delete-literal\"\n                  onClick={() => { handleDeleteLiteral(la.id); }}\n                  style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\" }}\n                >\n                  Delete\n                </button>\n              </div>\n            );\n          })}\n          {/* ---- DataType Assertions (owl:DatatypeProperty axioms; participate in datatype reasoning) ---- */}\n          <p\n            style={{ fontWeight: 600, marginBottom: \"0.5rem\", marginTop: \"0.75rem\" }}\n            data-testid=\"gw-inspector-datatype-assertions\"\n          >\n            DataType Assertions\n          </p>\n          {datatypeLiterals.length === 0 && (\n            <p\n              style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", color: \"#94a3b8\" }}\n              data-testid=\"gw-inspector-no-literals\"\n            >\n              No literal assertions.\n            </p>\n          )}\n          {datatypeLiterals.map((la) => {\n            const predLabel =\n              dtPropOptions.find((dp) => dp.iri === la[\"ecm:predicateIri\"])?.label ??\n              iriTail(la[\"ecm:predicateIri\"]);\n            return (\n              <div\n                key={la.id}\n                data-testid=\"gw-literal-entry\"\n                style={{\n                  borderBottom: \"1px solid #e2e8f0\",\n                  paddingBottom: \"0.5rem\",\n                  marginBottom: \"0.5rem\",\n                }}\n              >\n                <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n                  {predLabel}\n                </p>\n                <p\n                  style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", marginBottom: \"0.25rem\" }}\n                  data-testid=\"gw-literal-value\"\n                >\n                  {la[\"ecm:value\"]}\n                  {la[\"ecm:language\"] !== null && la[\"ecm:language\"] !== undefined && (\n                    <span\n                      style={{ color: \"#64748b\", fontSize: \"0.7rem\", marginLeft: \"0.25rem\" }}\n                      data-testid=\"gw-literal-lang\"\n                    >\n                      @{la[\"ecm:language\"]}\n                    </span>\n                  )}\n                </p>\n                <button\n                  type=\"button\"\n                  data-testid=\"gw-btn-delete-literal\"\n                  onClick={() => { handleDeleteLiteral(la.id); }}\n                  style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\" }}\n                >\n                  Delete\n                </button>\n              </div>\n            );\n          })}\n          <button\n            type=\"button\"\n            data-testid=\"gw-btn-add-literal\"\n            onClick={() => { setAddLiteralOpen(true); }}\n            style={{ marginTop: \"0.5rem\", width: \"100%\" }}\n          >\n            Add literal\n          </button>",
            "scope": "moderate"
          }
        ],
        "tests_recommended": [
          {
            "file": "tests/playwright/instance-label.spec.ts",
            "describe": "Existing tests assert data-testid='gw-inspector-instance-label-input' by name; after C4+C5 the element exists at its new location inside the Annotation Assertions section. Verify all three existing assertions still pass (getByTestId finds the element regardless of DOM position). Add a new assertion that the label input is a descendant of the element with data-testid='gw-inspector-annotation-assertions' to lock in the new structural placement."
          },
          {
            "file": "tests/playwright/literal-crud.spec.ts",
            "describe": "Verify that data-testid='gw-inspector-no-literals' still appears when there are no ecm:LiteralAssertion entries for the selected instance (now scoped to the DataType Assertions section). Verify data-testid='gw-literal-entry' entries appear only under the DataType Assertions section heading. Add a new test using fixture literal-crud-1i-1dp.jsonld: confirm the 'DataType Assertions' section heading is visible and the 'Annotation Assertions' section heading is visible."
          },
          {
            "file": "tests/playwright/fixtures/literal-crud-1i-1ap-1dp.jsonld",
            "describe": "New fixture (does not yet exist): a project with one instance, one owl:DatatypeProperty term, and one owl:AnnotationProperty term (e.g., rdfs:comment from STARTER_TERMS), plus one ecm:LiteralAssertion for each. Needed to test that the partition renders annotation literals under 'Annotation Assertions' (data-testid='gw-annotation-literal-entry') and datatype literals under 'DataType Assertions' (data-testid='gw-literal-entry') in separate sections."
          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "Storage model for rdfs:label: this proposal keeps rdfs:label as a plain string on the EcmInstance object (not migrated to ecm:LiteralAssertion) to minimize change scope. If the intent is to unify all annotation assertions (including rdfs:label) into the ecm:LiteralAssertion model for a uniform storage and edit path, that is a separate task requiring changes to handleLabelChange, EcmInstance interface, AddLiteralDialog predicate options, and migration logic.",
          "AddLiteralDialog annotation support: AddLiteralDialog.tsx currently excludes owl:AnnotationProperty predicates (recon F5). The annotationLiterals partition in C5 is structurally ready to receive annotation ecm:LiteralAssertion entries, but there is currently no UI affordance to create them (only the label input is visible in the Annotation Assertions section). Should a separate 'Add annotation assertion' button/dialog be introduced as a follow-on task?",
          "data-testid for the 'gw-inspector-no-literals' element: it is preserved in the DataType Assertions section for backward compatibility. If existing Playwright tests assert its text content ('No literal assertions.'), they will still pass. If a future sprint wants the text to read 'No datatype assertions.' for clarity, that is a separate test-coordinated change.",
          "Fixture gap: no existing Playwright fixture exercises both a DataType Assertion and an Annotation Assertion on the same instance (recon F11). The new fixture described in tests_recommended should be created before writing Playwright tests that target the two-section split."
        ],
        "summary": "Five non-overlapping changes to src/ui/Inspector.tsx implement R5-A3 per SME verdict. C1 adds the STARTER_TERMS import for fallback lookup. C2 adds getAnnotationPropertyOptions() and getTermTypeByIri() helpers. C3 adds partitioning locals (annPropOptions, termTypeMap, annotationLiterals, datatypeLiterals) in the instance-mode render path. C4 removes the top-of-inspector Label section. C5 replaces the flat 'Literal Assertions' section with two OWL 2 DL-aligned sections: 'Annotation Assertions' (label input + annotation ecm:LiteralAssertions) and 'DataType Assertions' (datatype ecm:LiteralAssertions + Add literal button). Storage model for rdfs:label (plain string on EcmInstance) is unchanged; EcmInstance interface and handleLabelChange are untouched. data-testid='gw-inspector-instance-label-input' is preserved at its new location to avoid breaking the three instance-label.spec.ts tests.",
        "self_assessment": "confident"
