      "outputs": {
        "ruling": "ratified",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The change codifies the OWL 2 DL distinction between AnnotationAssertion and DataPropertyAssertion axiom types at the UI surface, relocates a load-bearing input (rdfs:label), adds two new lookup helpers, and introduces a partitioning of ecm:LiteralAssertion entries \u00e2\u20ac\u201d these are semantics-bearing modifications to user-facing behavior, not typo/formatting/terminology-tightening that preserves meaning.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance evidence (urn:fnsr:task:457-recon-r5-c3-v5) is present and grounds all fifteen findings in file:line citations across Inspector.tsx, AddLiteralDialog.tsx, starter-terms.ts, migrate/index.ts, and the existing Playwright suite. SME review (urn:fnsr:task:374-sme-r5-decomposition) explicitly confirms R5-A3 (sme_verdict: 'confirm') with the substantive note that the split enforces the ontological commitment that rdfs:label is an AnnotationProperty whose value is a non-semantic decoration, consistent with the landed R4-2 typing fix \u00e2\u20ac\u201d closing the PENDING status flagged in recon F12. The developer's five-change proposal (urn:fnsr:task:458-dev-r5-c3-v5) implements the SME's correction with high fidelity: (a) C1 imports STARTER_TERMS for the SME-mandated fallback lookup; (b) C2 introduces getAnnotationPropertyOptions() and getTermTypeByIri() that check ecm:terms by id with STARTER_TERMS fallback exactly as SME prescribed; (c) C3 computes the annotationLiterals/datatypeLiterals partition by checking term type === 'owl:AnnotationProperty' (annotation section) with everything else falling to the datatype section, which is a defensible default for unknown predicates; (d) C4 removes the top-of-inspector standalone Label input per SME's explicit instruction that 'The rdfs:label entry is rendered within the Annotation Assertion section \u00e2\u20ac\u201d not as a special top-of-inspector Label input'; (e) C5 renders the two named sections with stable data-testids ('gw-inspector-annotation-assertions', 'gw-inspector-datatype-assertions', 'gw-annotation-literal-entry'). The storage model for rdfs:label is left unchanged (plain string on EcmInstance), preserving the existing handleLabelChange path and the three instance-label.spec.ts tests that pin data-testid='gw-inspector-instance-label-input' (recon F8). The developer's open question about migrating rdfs:label into the ecm:LiteralAssertion model and the AddLiteralDialog annotation-creation affordance are correctly scoped as follow-on tasks, not gating defects for R5-A3 as defined in FEEDBACK-ROUND-5.md. The proposal is scoped to Inspector.tsx only \u00e2\u20ac\u201d within the 3-file boundary in CLAUDE.md \u00c2\u00a76 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d and contains no canonical-doc edits, so no ADR-citation registry concerns arise. No frozen contract or prior ruling conflicts; Spec 08 v0.3 AP-7's SME-upstream-of-developer requirement is satisfied. Ratified for Pass 2b commit-finalize via the operator-applier path; the recommended new fixture literal-crud-1i-1ap-1dp.jsonld and Playwright additions should be queued as separate chains.",
        "referenced_evidence": [
