        "rationale": "Reconnaissance (urn:fnsr:task:462-recon-r5-c4-v5) is present in UPSTREAM and supplies the exact pre-edit text for all four target lines (F1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cF6), confirming the synchronized Turtle-string + JSON-LD-node-array dual-representation discipline noted by SME-R5-02. The developer's four changes (C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC4) implement the SME-prescribed text verbatim: C1+C2 carry the exact wording SME-recommended for R5-B2 (confirm verdict, ontologically clean replacement that drops the 'concrete encoding' phrasing CCO's ICE scope note rejects); C3+C4 carry the exact wording SME-recommended for R5-B4 under Option gamma (confirm verdict; obo:IAO_0000136 retention is the Q-R5-X gamma-path stance ratified across the R5 chain set). The developer correctly targets src/tbox/index.ts in both representations, avoiding the decomposition's scoping error flagged by SME-R5-02. Before-snippets in C1/C2/C3/C4 are character-identical to reconnaissance F2 and F4 evidence excerpts, satisfying applier strict-match preconditions. All four before-snippets are non-overlapping and each is unique within the file (single occurrence per representation per class). Pre-edit baseline is green per F8 (130/130 tests passing at urn:fnsr:task:461-test-r5-c3-v5). No canonical-doc citations are introduced (rdfs:comment is annotation surface, not ADR-citation surface). The chain composition (reconnaissance \u00e2\u2020\u2019 ratification \u00e2\u2020\u2019 applier with downstream test-runner) is appropriate for code-artifact editorial work per CLAUDE.md \u00c2\u00a77.8 artifact-kind table. Proceed to Pass 2b applier.",
