            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F12",
            "claim": "There is no second rdf:type emission path for instance nodes in nodeToQuads() beyond the typesOf(node) loop and the ecm:classIris loop; the change location is uniquely lines 178-180 of turtle.ts.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/emit/turtle.ts",
                "lines": "174-190",
                "excerpt": "const subj = termForIri(nodeId);\nconst rdfTypeNode = namedNode(RDF_TYPE_IRI);\n\n// rdf:type from `type` field\nfor (const t of typesOf(node)) {\n  result.push(makeQuad(subj, rdfTypeNode, termForIri(t)));\n}\n\n// rdf:type from ecm:classIris (SPEC section 5.8: each classIri -> rdf:type assertion)\nconst classIris = node[\"ecm:classIris\"];\nif (Array.isArray(classIris)) {\n  for (const c of classIris as unknown[]) {\n    if (typeof c === 'string') {\n      result.push(makeQuad(subj, rdfTypeNode, termForIri(c)));\n    }\n  }\n}"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          }
        ],
        "summary": "In src/emit/turtle.ts, the nodeToQuads() function emits rdf:type quads for every value in a node's 'type' field via an unconditional loop (lines 178-180). TBOX_IDS (lines 66-72) skips five whole-node entries by node id but does not include 'ecm:Instance', and the TBOX_IDS guard (line 151) checks node id \u00e2\u20ac\u201d not type values \u00e2\u20ac\u201d so ecm:Instance-typed nodes pass through unimpeded. The SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST in src/projection/index.ts (lines 29-40) retains 'ecm:Instance' entities, and the predicate allowlist retains 'type', so instance nodes arrive at graphToQuads() with type: 'ecm:Instance' intact, causing the current code to emit <instance-iri> rdf:type <https://edgecanonical.org/ns/modeler#Instance> into Turtle. Inspector.tsx's isEcmInstance guard (lines 63-71) reads from the internal project document's ecm:instances array \u00e2\u20ac\u201d not from Turtle \u00e2\u20ac\u201d so it is insulated from any Turtle-layer change. No existing test assertion in emitters.test.ts checks for presence or absence of rdf:type ecm:Instance triples, meaning no existing test would break from adding the filter, but also no test currently guards the desired post-change invariant. The sole change point is the typesOf(node) loop at turtle.ts lines 178-180; a skip condition on the value 'ecm:Instance' within that loop is the narrowest possible intervention. The pre-change baseline is 130/130 tests green.",
