      "attempts": 1,
      "outputs": {
        "changes": [
          {
            "id": "C1",
            "file": "src/emit/turtle.ts",
            "rationale": "R5-B5: ecm:Instance is a tool-internal bookkeeping type used by the projection layer and Inspector.tsx to identify modeler instance nodes. It has no domain-ontology meaning and must not appear as an rdf:type assertion in the consumer-facing Turtle export. The fix adds a single skip guard inside the typesOf(node) loop at lines 178-180 (the unique type-emission path for non-TBox nodes, per reconnaissance F12). expandIri is already in scope at the call site and correctly resolves 'ecm:Instance' to 'https://edgecanonical.org/ns/modeler#Instance' via PREFIX_MAP. The ecm:classIris loop immediately below (lines 183-190) is unaffected and continues to emit domain class membership triples. The internal JSON-LD representation is unchanged: SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST in projection/index.ts retains ecm:Instance, and Inspector.tsx reads from the internal project document, not from Turtle output.",
            "before": "  // rdf:type from `type` field\n  for (const t of typesOf(node)) {\n    result.push(makeQuad(subj, rdfTypeNode, termForIri(t)));\n  }",
            "after": "  // rdf:type from `type` field\n  for (const t of typesOf(node)) {\n    // R5-B5: strip tool-internal bookkeeping class from consumer-facing Turtle export.\n    // ecm:Instance is retained in the internal JSON-LD projection (SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST)\n    // and in Inspector.tsx type guards; it must not appear as a domain type assertion.\n    if (expandIri(t) === \"https://edgecanonical.org/ns/modeler#Instance\") continue;\n    result.push(makeQuad(subj, rdfTypeNode, termForIri(t)));\n  }",
            "scope": "minimal"
          }
        ],
        "tests_recommended": [
          {
            "file": "tests/emitters.test.ts",
            "describe": "Add an assertion that no rdf:type triple with object <https://edgecanonical.org/ns/modeler#Instance> (i.e., ecm:Instance) appears in the Turtle quads produced by nodeToQuads() for any ecm:Instance-typed node. Reconnaissance finding F9 confirmed no such assertion currently exists, leaving the post-change invariant uncovered. A negative assertion \u00e2\u20ac\u201d !quads.some(q => q.predicate.value === RDF+'type' && q.object.value === 'https://edgecanonical.org/ns/modeler#Instance') \u00e2\u20ac\u201d against the existing INST_A fixture (lines 82-92) is the minimal coverage."
          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "Recon open question (F12/Q1): Should the ecm:Instance skip in the typesOf loop be conditioned on the node having at least one ecm:classIris entry, so domain class membership is always conveyed before the tool type is suppressed? The SME correction is unconditional; this proposal matches that. If a node has type ecm:Instance but no ecm:classIris values, the Turtle output will carry no rdf:type assertions for that node \u00e2\u20ac\u201d acceptable per SME but worth operator confirmation.",
          "Recon open question (Q2): The N-Triples emitter shares the same graphToQuads() / nodeToQuads() path (per turtle.ts architecture). This change will also strip ecm:Instance from N-Triples output. If N-Triples is intended to be a lossless internal serialization rather than a consumer-facing export, this may be undesirable. Scoping this chain to turtle.ts only is not architecturally possible given the shared emitter. Operator should confirm the N-Triples behavior is acceptable."
        ],
