        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "Adding rdfs:subClassOf cco:ont00000064 to the Book class introduces a new semantic axiom (CCO IBA anchoring) that changes ontological commitments in the consumer-facing fixture; this exceeds editorial scope (typo/formatting/terminology-tightening) and properly required reconnaissance, which is present in UPSTREAM.",
        "rationale": "Pass 2a ratification per FNSR Spec 03. The chain is structurally complete: reconnaissance (urn:fnsr:task:477-recon-r5-c7-v5) gathers direct file evidence (F1-F11) confirming six @context divergences and the absent Book rdfs:subClassOf; SME decomposition (urn:fnsr:task:374-sme-r5-decomposition) confirms SME-R5-01 (major; stale fixture @context) and R5-B6 (minor; CCO Book anchoring under Option gamma). The developer's proposal aligns precisely with the SME-prescribed corrections: C1 replaces the pre-ADR-007 @context wholesale with a faithful transcription of VMP_CONTEXT (src/kernel/canonicalize.ts:66-98), repairing all six recon-confirmed divergences (stale iao prefix, missing obo prefix, missing @id:obo:IAO_0000136 alias on iao:isAbout, missing text/lang compact aliases, missing foaf/schema/skos, missing rdfs:range typed entry); C2 adds rdfs:subClassOf [\"cco:ont00000064\"] to the Book term entry at lines 219-224 per Option gamma. C1 (lines 2-64) and C2 (lines 219-224) are non-overlapping, so the applier's strict before-snippet matching will not collide. ADR-007's canonical-IAO-IRI binding is preserved (the developer correctly retains obo:IAO_0000136 rather than substituting cco:ont00001808, consistent with SME R5-B1 detail under Option gamma). Author/Publisher classes are deliberately excluded per Aaron's \u00ce\u00b3-1 adjudication; SME-R5-03's advisory extension is appropriately forward-track material, not in-scope for Chain-7. The change is artifact-kind canonical-doc-adjacent (demo fixture; consumer audience per surface-audience primitive) and the developer surfaces a legitimate operator-decision flag in open_questions about snapshot-test alignment-whitespace sensitivity, but the runtime path (serializeVmp unconditionally rewrites @context per F9) means the change is safe at the test boundary. No conflict with frozen ADR text, no contract violation, no scope outside prior ratifications.",
        "referenced_evidence": [
          {
            "type": "upstream_task",
            "id": "urn:fnsr:task:477-recon-r5-c7-v5",
            "field": "outputs.findings"
          },
          {
