        "bankings": [
          {
            "id": "B1",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "Fixture-as-standalone-artifact vs runtime-rewritten-artifact divergence: when serializeVmp unconditionally overwrites @context (canonicalize.ts:265), the on-disk fixture's embedded @context becomes invisible to all runtime tests yet remains the surface third-party JSON-LD processors consume. This produced a class of silent divergence (SME-R5-01) where the recon F12 'all 130 tests pass' signal is consistent with a semantically defective fixture. The pattern: any artifact destined for consumer-audience surfaces whose canonical interpretation is mediated by a runtime rewrite step requires standalone-document conformance testing in addition to round-trip testing. The developer's tests_recommended[2] (new tests/fixture-context.test.ts) operationalizes this discipline."
          },
          {
            "id": "B2",
            "category": "discipline-correction",
            "content": "Option gamma layer-decomposition discipline reaffirmed: the SME (374) explicitly reframed \u00ce\u00b3 from 'compromise' to 'correct layer decomposition' \u00e2\u20ac\u201d ecm:* TBox is legitimately CCO-anchored (subClassOf cco:ont00000958); the actual fault was per-individual ecm:Instance type-pollution leaking into consumer-facing output. Chain-7's CCO Book anchoring is the consumer-side complement: adding rdfs:subClassOf cco:ont00000064 in the consumer-audience fixture without disturbing tool-internal IRIs. Future ratifications touching the ecm: vocabulary should cite this distinction rather than re-litigating the 'remove all ecm: terms' framing."
          }
        ]
      },
