        "summary": "Five risks and one advisory are surfaced for Phase 2 exit. The three most operationally urgent entering Phase 3 are: (1) the state_admin write-race \u00e2\u20ac\u201d every PLO phase-tracking command and banking event issued while the daemon is running is a race against the daemon's polling read/write cycle, with no locking between the two processes; Phase 3 will increase this frequency because PLO adoption is now a first-class Phase 3 discipline; corrupted audit chain is the worst case. (2) PLO v3.1.0-bridge's missing auto-chain \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the AP-PLO-2 gate (refusing close without drift-reconciled) is the only structural enforcement; nothing prevents the operator from queueing Phase 4 chains immediately after declaring Phase 3 PO-satisfied, leaving the retro, drift reconciliation, and close steps unemitted indefinitely; Phase 2 demonstrated this pattern before PLO existed. (3) SVG predicate exception downgrade to info \u00e2\u20ac\u201d git subprocess failures on the OneDrive filesystem are caught silently and reported as info findings, not errors; the has_blocking_drift flag stays false and --blocking-only shows nothing, making the gate report false-clean on the environment where it is most needed. Below the top three: the ADR-007 cascade left stale iao:OntologyDesignPattern IRIs in vmp-serializer.test.ts unit fixtures that will only fail when Phase 3 introduces strict @type validation; SVG-4/5 lifecycle predicates are unimplemented (v3.2-deferred) so Phase 3 banking drift will accumulate without detection; N3.js is in devDependencies only and will fail in packaged CLI scenarios without Human Orchestrator approval to promote it."
