        "editorial_verdict_reason": "Introduces three new files implementing a new core capability (importOntology), defines new public types (ImportedTermType, ImportedTermObject, ImportedOntologyRecord, ImportResult), and adds normative behavior (50MB hard-reject, rdfs:Class\u00e2\u2020\u2019owl:Class normalization, blank-node exclusion, sha256 content hash) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d clearly outside the editorial-correction scope of typo/formatting/terminology-tightening.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM (urn:fnsr:task:488-recon-p3-c1) and is comprehensive: 19 findings citing SPEC \u00c2\u00a714.1, \u00c2\u00a712.2, \u00c2\u00a75.6, \u00c2\u00a715.4, FR-C011, IMPL \u00c2\u00a73.1, plus inference F12 establishing kernel-purity ineligibility and F13/F14 establishing module-placement and node:crypto patterns. The developer's proposal (urn:fnsr:task:489-dev-p3-c1) maps cleanly onto every IMPL \u00c2\u00a73.1 acceptance criterion and respects every recon-surfaced constraint: (1) \u00c2\u00a712.2 size-guard fires before parsing via Buffer.from + length check; (2) \u00c2\u00a715.4 N3.js Parser used (same pattern as src/emit/n-triples.ts, F8); (3) \u00c2\u00a75.6 record shape complete with all nine fields in correct types; (4) \u00c2\u00a714.1 scope honored \u00e2\u20ac\u201d owl:Class wins unconditionally over property types, rdfs:Class normalized, blank-node subjects and blank-node subClassOf/subPropertyOf targets excluded, owl:imports unhandled (and thus not followed); (5) `sha256-` + hex hash via node:crypto matches src/manifest/index.ts precedent (F11); (6) generateIri('ecm:uuid-urn', {}) call shape exactly matches src/manifest/index.ts:118 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d confirmed by re-read. The 4th-parameter `createdAt` threading is NOT a signature deviation: it is the established codebase pattern (src/manifest/index.ts ArtifactInput.generatedAt; SPEC \u00c2\u00a79.3 --clock threading; src/iri/index.ts module-doc explicitly cites \u00c2\u00a79.3 for explicit-parameter discipline). Layer-boundary compliance: src/import/ is a new top-level non-kernel module matching the F13 src/<module>/index.ts pattern; no imports from src/adapters/ or src/composition/; node:crypto and N3.js usage parallels existing non-kernel modules and is appropriately marked non-browser in module-doc. Tests cover all six \u00c2\u00a73.1 acceptance criteria using the hand-rolled node:assert + counters + process.exit(1) pattern auto-discovered by tests/run-tests.ts via *.test.js (confirmed); AC4 uses an independent reference-hash computed inside the test module, matching the manifest-entries.test.ts AC3 verification discipline. Developer's open questions are appropriate scope-flags for \u00c2\u00a73.5 CLI wiring (browser-context resolution; deterministic-mode IRI policy threading; ecm:name derivation strategy; cli-integration AC7 update) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d none block \u00c2\u00a73.1 core-module ratification. No frozen-contract conflict; no ADR conflict.",
