            "id": "B1",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "Non-kernel domain modules that produce timestamped + content-hashed records follow a four-element discipline now visible in three places (src/iri/index.ts, src/manifest/index.ts, src/import/turtle-import.ts): (1) caller-threaded ISO-8601 timestamp parameter to satisfy SPEC \u00c2\u00a79.3 even though the module is non-kernel; (2) `generateIri('ecm:uuid-urn', {})` for non-deterministic IDs with the \u00c2\u00a79.2 acknowledgment recorded in module-doc; (3) node:crypto createHash with `sha256-` + hex prefix; (4) module-doc preamble stating layer-boundary refusal (no src/adapters or src/composition imports) and non-browser status. IMPL plan signatures consistently document only the semantic inputs (turtleSource, fileName, projectId) and omit the determinism-thread parameter (createdAt / generatedAt); the latter is added by codebase discipline rather than written into the IMPL plan. The Phase 3 \u00c2\u00a73.5 CLI wiring task will need to thread `--clock` into the createdAt argument and (if deterministic mode is required for imports) elevate the IRI policy from hardcoded 'ecm:uuid-urn' to a parameter \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this is the same shape as the existing export deterministic-mode wiring."
          },
          {
