        "chain_label": "Phase 3 Chain 1b \u2014 TS-error fix (brief-confirmation follow-up to Chain 1)",
        "purpose": "Chain 1 landed src/import/turtle-import.ts (9441 bytes), src/import/index.ts (260 bytes), tests/import-turtle.test.ts (8919 bytes) via applier 491. Test-runner 492 caught 2 TypeScript compile errors that block npm test from running. Errors (from 492's raw_stdout_tail): (1) src/import/turtle-import.ts(143,5): 'Type Quad[] is not assignable to type void' \u2014 parser.parse() typed return is void; (2) src/import/turtle-import.ts(159,22): 'Type void must have a Symbol.iterator method'. Root cause: N3.js Parser.parse() typing is void (results delivered via callback) but dev's code uses it as if returning Quad[] synchronously. Fix per N3.js callback pattern: collect quads via callback parameter (parser.parse(input, (err, quad, _prefixes) => { if (err) throw err; if (quad) quads.push(quad); })). Read the existing src/emit/turtle.ts for the established N3.js usage pattern in this codebase. Produce a SINGLE minimal change to src/import/turtle-import.ts that fixes both TS errors by switching from sync-return to callback-collection pattern.",
        "files_in_scope": [
