            "content": "Watchdog Category B (hung_in_progress) detection gap: task 493 was picked by daemon (status ready->in_progress) but the claude subprocess died silently with NO history audit entry recorded. The watchdog's hung-in-progress detector requires last_ts from history to compute elapsed-minutes vs HUNG_IN_PROGRESS_MINUTES threshold. With empty history, the watchdog skipped this task \u2014 reported stall_kind=running because in_progress > 0, but the in_progress was effectively dead. Aaron 2026-05-26 surfaced it: 'It looks like we have been on the same task for a very long time.' Detection time: ~unknown (probably 5-10 min); cost: one daemon restart cycle to invoke crash-recovery. v3.2 substrate refinement candidate: extend watchdog Category B to also detect 'in_progress + empty history + > N min since state.jsonld mtime touched by daemon' \u2014 proxies the lifetime via the file mtime when history is empty. Also: improve daemon dispatch to ALWAYS write an audit event when transitioning status to in_progress (single 'dispatch_started' event), so empty-history hung tasks become impossible.",
