      "outputs": {
        "ruling": "ratified",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The change mutates executable code in src/import/turtle-import.ts to alter runtime semantics of the parser invocation (sync vs async overload) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d well outside typo/formatting/terminology-tightening scope.",
        "rationale": "The developer's proposal (urn:fnsr:task:753-dev-p3-c1c, change C1) is the minimal, targeted fix for the root cause identified by reconnaissance (urn:fnsr:task:752-recon-p3-c1c, findings F1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cF10). Recon's evidence is concrete and directly verifiable: N3Lexer.js:477 defers tokenization via queueMicrotask when parse() is called with a callback on a string input (F1, F7); turtle-import.ts:143\u00e2\u20ac\u201c146 uses that async overload, so the local quads[] is still empty when the term-extraction loop runs (F2); and the same codebase already uses the synchronous overload successfully at src/emit/n-triples.ts:35 (F3, F4, F10). The proposed diff swaps to exactly that synchronous form \u00e2\u20ac\u201d `quads = parser.parse(turtleSource)` returning Quad[] directly \u00e2\u20ac\u201d preserving the surrounding try/catch (which now actually functions, eliminating the F6 throw-in-microtask bug) and the const\u00e2\u2020\u2019let adjustment required for the reassignment. I independently read turtle-import.ts:120\u00e2\u20ac\u201c209 and n-triples.ts:32\u00e2\u20ac\u201c49 and confirmed the recon excerpts are accurate to the current file state. The change touches no other file and leaves the term-extraction logic (lines 162\u00e2\u20ac\u201c205), contentHash path (F5), and SIZE_EXCEEDED path (\u00c2\u00a712.2) untouched, so the working AC4/AC5 paths are preserved by construction. Layer boundaries (CLAUDE.md \u00c2\u00a79) are unaffected \u00e2\u20ac\u201d src/import/ is not src/kernel/, and the n3 dependency was already present. SPEC \u00c2\u00a714.1 term-extraction semantics and \u00c2\u00a715.4 normative-RDF-library obligations are preserved. FR-C011 (per IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN \u00c2\u00a73.1) is the failing requirement this fix targets; no other contract is impacted. The two developer open questions (cosmetic Quad-import redundancy; task 507's original TS error) are explicitly non-blocking and align with recon's open questions. Substantive-change criteria are met and reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM, satisfying the Spec 03 \u00c2\u00a7Reconnaissance refusal contract.",
        "referenced_evidence": [
          {
            "type": "upstream_task",
            "id": "urn:fnsr:task:752-recon-p3-c1c",
            "field": "outputs.findings"
          },
