    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:fnsr:task:770-rat-p3-c2",
      "agent": "architect",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": 10,
      "depends_on": [
        "urn:fnsr:task:769-dev-p3-c2",
        "urn:fnsr:task:768-recon-p3-c2"
      ],
      "inputs": {
        "phase": "phase-3",
        "mode": "ratification",
        "chain_label": "Phase 3 Chain 2 \u2014 Pass 2a ratification (sub-task 3.5)",
        "purpose": "Pass 2a ratification per FNSR Spec 03 for Phase 3 Chain 2. Read developer's proposed src/cli/index.ts modification + tests/cli-import-ontology.test.ts from UPSTREAM. Walk reconnaissance evidence. Produce six-field ruling (ruling, editorial_verdict, editorial_verdict_reason, rationale, referenced_evidence, bankings). Verify: (1) the merge-into-project semantics align with project-document type definitions and don't break the project JSON-LD canonical shape; (2) error-handling exit codes match the existing CLI convention; (3) the CLI integration test exercises both acceptance criteria from IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN \u00a73.5; (4) no layer-boundary violations.",
        "spec_refs": [
          "FNSR Spec 03 \u00a7Architect refusal contract",
          "IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN \u00a73.5",
          "CLAUDE.md \u00a79 layer boundaries"
        ]
      },
      "attempts": 1,
      "outputs": {
        "ruling": "ratified",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposal replaces a stub with a real CLI command, threads a new createdAt at an adapter boundary, augments term shapes flowing into project canonical state, and adds a new test file \u00e2\u20ac\u201d none of which are typo/formatting/terminology-tightening edits.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance (urn:fnsr:task:768-recon-p3-c2) is present in UPSTREAM and grounds every load-bearing decision in the proposal. The four verification axes hold: (1) Merge-into-project semantics align with SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.6 and \u00c2\u00a75.7. ImportedTermObject (recon F5) lacks ecm:source and ecm:ontologyId; the proposal's C2 augments each term with `ecm:source: \"ecm:imported-ontology\"` and `ecm:ontologyId: result.ontology.id` before appending to ecm:terms, satisfying SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7 (recon F6) and the validate() check at src/validate/index.ts:205. The spread merge `{...project, \"ecm:ontologies\": [...existing, result.ontology], \"ecm:terms\": [...existing, ...augmentedTerms]}` preserves the @context, id, type, and all unrelated project fields \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the canonical v0.4 shape (recon F17) is not perturbed. (2) Exit-code mapping is internally consistent and SPEC-aligned: SIZE_EXCEEDED \u00e2\u2020\u2019 2 (matches IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN \u00c2\u00a73.5 AC2 directly); PARSE_ERROR \u00e2\u2020\u2019 3 (matches SPEC \u00c2\u00a723 'malformed input / parse failure', recon F19); missing required positionals / --out \u00e2\u2020\u2019 3; file I/O failure on the TTL \u00e2\u2020\u2019 2. The \u00c2\u00a73.5 ACs are silent on PARSE_ERROR; the developer's open_question flags this transparently and the SPEC \u00c2\u00a723 mapping is the conservative, audit-defensible choice. (3) C6 (tests/cli-import-ontology.test.ts) exercises both \u00c2\u00a73.5 ACs directly: testValidTurtleProducesValidProject covers AC1 by running import-ontology then validate on the output and asserting both exit 0 plus absence of `\"ecm:error\"` strings in validate stdout; testOversizedInputExits2 writes 51 MB ASCII and asserts exit 2 with non-empty stderr (matches AC2 'clear message' phrasing). The test harness pattern (recon F16) is faithfully reproduced; the test file will be auto-discovered (recon F20) without runner changes. C4/C5 correctly retire the stub assertion at tests/cli-integration.test.ts AC7 (recon F15) by converting it to a missing-arg guard, preserving the AC7 label so test-count reporting is stable. (4) No layer-boundary violations: src/cli/ is Layer 2 (adapter) and may import from Layer 0 (kernel/canonicalize) and Layer 1 (import, validate, refactor) per CLAUDE.md \u00c2\u00a79; the only new wall-clock call (`new Date().toISOString()`) is at the CLI boundary, with --clock providing a deterministic override \u00e2\u20ac\u201d importOntology() itself remains free of Date.now() per recon F18, preserving kernel purity. Three loose ends are operator-acknowledged open questions (PARSE_ERROR exit code, ecm:updatedAt non-mutation, term deduplication) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d all are \u00c2\u00a73.5-silent and the proposal follows existing-command convention (recon F13) which is the right default. The C4 stale-header note is acknowledged as benign editorial drift, not a ratification blocker.",
        "referenced_evidence": [
          {
            "type": "upstream_task",
