            "state": 1,
            "content": "v3.5.0 demo-doc auto-generation convention observation (surfaced 2026-06-02 first real exercise on Chain 2): the existence-check _existing_demo_doc_for_phase scans for demo/PHASE-N-*.md globally per-phase, treating any matching file as 'demo doc already exists.' This fits when a phase ships ONE demo (matches PLO state-machine grain: phase enters demo-released once before po-satisfied). It does NOT fit multi-chain phases where each chain is independently demoable (Phase 3 ships Chain 1=Turtle import then Chain 2=CLI integration; PO reviews each chain landing). For multi-chain demos the operator must opt-in via --regenerate-demo-doc + --demo-doc-descriptor chain-N-xxx to disambiguate. The v3.5.0 implementation supports both modes correctly via the flags; the discipline-question is whether the DEFAULT should change. Two candidates: (a) per-chain convention: scan for demo/PHASE-N-{descriptor}.md where descriptor matches the build_ref or anchor task; (b) operator declares chain identity in --demo-doc-descriptor and substrate auto-checks for that specific filename collision rather than PHASE-N substring. Both require more data: how often will multi-chain phases happen vs single-chain phases? Defer to v3.5.1 / v3.6 after Phase 4 friction observation per the established >= 2 phase cycles rule.",
