        "summary": "Phase 3 Chain 2 (build_ref=439d69d, anchor task 772-test-p3-c2, completed 2026-06-02) delivered exactly one sub-task: IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN \u00c2\u00a73.5 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the real CLI `import-ontology` command, replacing the Phase 1 stub at src/cli/index.ts. The command reads a project JSON-LD file and a Turtle ontology file, calls the importOntology() engine shipped in Chain 1, augments each extracted term with ecm:source and ecm:ontologyId, merges the result into the project's ecm:ontologies and ecm:terms arrays, and writes the canonical output to --out. Both \u00c2\u00a73.5 acceptance criteria pass: AC1 (valid Turtle \u00e2\u2020\u2019 merged project validates clean) and AC2 (51 MB input \u00e2\u2020\u2019 exit 2 with message). The full test suite is 140/140 across 19 files (Chain 1 was 137/137 across 18 files; Chain 2 added cli-import-ontology.test.js). SPEC \u00c2\u00a723 exit codes are implemented (0/2/3). The --clock flag enables deterministic createdAt for reproducible test runs. What is NOT yet delivered in Phase 3: imported-term immutability/remap UI (\u00c2\u00a73.2), LARGE_IMPORT warning/degraded mode (\u00c2\u00a73.3), term search/filter UI (\u00c2\u00a73.4), OED-303 closure, and formal Phase 3 exit gate. The demo doc for Chain 2 should document Chain 2's scope narrowly: the CLI command, its two ACs, how to invoke it, and what remains deferred in Phase 3.",
