      "inputs": {
        "phase": "phase-3",
        "chain_label": "Phase 3 Chain 3 -- Imported-Term Immutability + Remap Workflow (sub-task 3.2)",
        "purpose": "Reconnaissance for Phase 3 sub-task 3.2 (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN). Investigate: (1) how terms are currently typed/stored in the project JSON-LD (term-shape; ecm:source semantics; ecm:ontologyId field); (2) the existing term-edit affordances surfaced in src/ui/ (EditTermDialog.tsx, Inspector.tsx, TermSidebar.tsx) -- where edit/delete buttons live, how they are gated, and what state controls their disabled state; (3) the SPEC reference for imported-term immutability (SPEC section 13.3) and the remap-references workflow (SPEC section 13.6); (4) existing Playwright test scaffolding in tests/playwright/ -- the test runner pattern, fixture conventions, and where new playwright tests should land; (5) Chain 2 already augmented imported terms with ecm:source = 'ecm:imported-ontology' and ecm:ontologyId at CLI-import time -- verify this lands in the project document; the immutability check downstream should read those flags. Identify the minimal surface area where read-only rendering should be gated on the ecm:source field and where the remap workflow should be exposed (likely a new affordance on the Inspector or a new RemapDialog component). Document the IRI-rewrite scope: which fields contain class IRIs (ecm:classIris) and predicate IRIs (ecm:predicateIri) that need rewriting, vs which fields are preserved-on-round-trip-only.",
        "files_to_read": [
          "project/SPEC.md",
          "project/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md",
          "src/ui/EditTermDialog.tsx",
          "src/ui/Inspector.tsx",
          "src/ui/TermSidebar.tsx",
          "src/ui/CanvasView.tsx",
          "src/cli/index.ts",
          "src/import/turtle-import.ts",
          "tests/",
