        ]
      },
      "attempts": 1,
      "outputs": {
        "findings": [
          {
            "id": "F1",
            "claim": "SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7 defines the term object shape with `ecm:source` (three allowed values: `ecm:imported-ontology`, `ecm:project-created`, `ecm:system-starter-example`) and `ecm:ontologyId` (null for non-imported; ontology record UUID for imported terms).",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "project/SPEC.md",
                "lines": "445-481",
                "excerpt": "Allowed `ecm:source` values: `ecm:imported-ontology`, `ecm:project-created`, `ecm:system-starter-example`. ... `ecm:ontologyId`: null"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F2",
            "claim": "The CLI `import-ontology` command already augments every extracted term with `ecm:source: 'ecm:imported-ontology'` and `ecm:ontologyId: result.ontology.id` before appending them to the project's `ecm:terms` array.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/cli/index.ts",
                "lines": "323-328",
                "excerpt": "const augmentedTerms = result.terms.map((term) => ({\n  ...term,\n  \"ecm:source\": \"ecm:imported-ontology\" as const,\n  \"ecm:ontologyId\": result.ontology.id,\n}));"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F3",
            "claim": "The `ImportedTermObject` interface in `src/import/turtle-import.ts` does NOT include `ecm:source` or `ecm:ontologyId`; those fields are added only at the CLI adapter boundary, not inside the core import function.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/import/turtle-import.ts",
                "lines": "60-67",
                "excerpt": "export interface ImportedTermObject {\n  readonly id: string;\n  readonly type: ImportedTermType;\n  readonly \"rdfs:label\"?: ...;\n  readonly \"rdfs:comment\"?: string;\n  readonly \"rdfs:subClassOf\"?: ...;\n  readonly \"rdfs:subPropertyOf\"?: ...;\n}"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F4",
            "claim": "`TermSidebar.tsx` already gates the click handler on `ecm:source === 'ecm:project-created'`; imported terms receive `aria-disabled=\"true\"` and no `role=\"button\"`, blocking EditTermDialog from opening.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/ui/TermSidebar.tsx",
                "lines": "152-170",
                "excerpt": "const isClickable = onTermClick !== undefined && term[\"ecm:source\"] === \"ecm:project-created\";\nconst isImported = term[\"ecm:source\"] === \"ecm:imported-ontology\";\n...\nrole={isClickable ? \"button\" : undefined}\naria-disabled={isImported ? \"true\" : undefined}\nonClick={isClickable ? () => { onTermClick(term); } : undefined}"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F5",
            "claim": "A Playwright test (AC4 in `tests/playwright/term-crud.spec.ts`) already verifies that imported terms carry `aria-disabled=\"true\"`, lack `role=\"button\"`, and clicking them does not open `EditTermDialog`; this test passes against the `imported-term.jsonld` fixture.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "tests/playwright/term-crud.spec.ts",
                "lines": "219-246",
                "excerpt": "\"AC4: Imported term read-only: aria-disabled present; click does not open EditTermDialog (FR-U010; Chain C)\"\n...await expect(importedItem).toHaveAttribute(\"aria-disabled\", \"true\");\nawait expect(importedItem).not.toHaveAttribute(\"role\", \"button\");\nawait importedItem.click();\nawait expect(page.getByTestId(\"gw-dialog-edit-term\")).not.toBeVisible();"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F6",
            "claim": "The `imported-term.jsonld` Playwright fixture has `ecm:ontologyId: null` (not a real ontology UUID), meaning it was hand-crafted and does not reflect the actual project state produced by the CLI `import-ontology` command (which sets `ecm:ontologyId` to a real UUID).",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "tests/playwright/fixtures/imported-term.jsonld",
                "lines": "82-88",
                "excerpt": "\"ecm:createdAt\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\n\"ecm:ontologyId\": null,\n\"ecm:source\": \"ecm:imported-ontology\",\n\"ecm:updatedAt\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\n\"id\": \"https://example.org/ontology/ImportedClass\""
              },
              {
                "file": "src/cli/index.ts",
                "lines": "323-328",
                "excerpt": "\"ecm:ontologyId\": result.ontology.id"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F7",
            "claim": "SPEC \u00c2\u00a713.3 declares imported term IRIs immutable in v0.3 and states the MVP supports project-local replacement terms only (not copy-to-project-created or remove-and-re-import paths).",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "project/SPEC.md",
                "lines": "1032-1041",
                "excerpt": "### 13.3 Imported Term IRI Change\nImported ontology term IRIs are immutable in v0.3. The user has three options for substitution:\n- create a project-local replacement term with a new IRI and migrate references manually;\n- copy the imported term into the project-created vocabulary;\n- remove the ontology and re-import a corrected version.\nThe MVP supports project-local replacement terms only."
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F8",
            "claim": "SPEC \u00c2\u00a713.6 defines the remap-references operation as user-invocable: the user first creates a project-created term, then invokes remap to rewrite all `ecm:classIris`/`ecm:predicateIri` references from the imported IRI to the new IRI; the imported ontology record and imported term entry remain untouched.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "project/SPEC.md",
                "lines": "1056-1058",
                "excerpt": "If a project-created term is created with the intent to supersede an imported term, the user may invoke a \"remap references\" operation that rewrites instance and relation references from the imported IRI to the project-created IRI. The imported term remains in the project (as immutable imported metadata) but is no longer referenced."
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F9",
            "claim": "No `RemapDialog` component, no `remapReferences` function, and no remap-related UI affordance exists anywhere under `src/`; the remap workflow described in SPEC \u00c2\u00a713.6 and IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN \u00c2\u00a73.2 is entirely absent from the current codebase.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/ui/TermSidebar.tsx",
                "lines": "1-343",
                "excerpt": "(no remap affordance; imported terms have no click handler, only aria-disabled)"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/ui/Inspector.tsx",
                "lines": "1-888",
                "excerpt": "(no term-inspection mode; Inspector only handles selectedRelationId and selectedInstanceId)"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "gap"
          },
          {
            "id": "F10",
            "claim": "The existing `refactorIri` function in `src/refactor/index.ts` rewrites four reference field types: `ecm:classIris` array entries on instances, `ecm:predicateIri` on relations and literal assertions, `ecm:subjectIri` on relations and literal assertions, and `ecm:objectIri` on relations; it does NOT rewrite entity `id` fields.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/refactor/index.ts",
                "lines": "8-14",
                "excerpt": "Cascade-updates all occurrences of oldIri in:\n  ecm:classIris    -- array entries on ecm:instances items\n  ecm:predicateIri -- string on ecm:relations and ecm:literalAssertions\n  ecm:subjectIri   -- string on ecm:relations and ecm:literalAssertions\n  ecm:objectIri    -- string on ecm:relations items only"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "observation"
          },
          {
            "id": "F11",
            "claim": "`refactorIri` contains a collision check (lines 168-178) that aborts and returns unmodified project if `newIri` already exists in `ecm:terms` or `ecm:instances`; because the remap workflow requires `newIri` (the project-created replacement) to already exist in `ecm:terms`, calling `refactorIri(project, importedIri, projectCreatedIri)` directly will always trigger this collision guard.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/refactor/index.ts",
                "lines": "167-178",
                "excerpt": "const existingIds = collectSemanticEntityIds(project);\nif (existingIds.has(newIri)) {\n  return {\n    project,\n    oldIri,\n    newIri,\n    referenceCount: 0,\n    affectedEntityTypes: [],\n    collision: { collidingIri: newIri, collidingEntityId: newIri },\n  };\n}"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/refactor/index.ts",
                "lines": "120-132",
                "excerpt": "function collectSemanticEntityIds(...) {\n  for (const key of [\"ecm:terms\", \"ecm:instances\"] as const) {\n    for (const entity of getEntityArray(project, key)) {\n      const id = getStr(entity, \"id\");\n      if (id !== undefined) map.set(id, key);\n    }\n  }\n}"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "inference"
          },
          {
