        "summary": "Chain 2 (sub-task 3.1) already landed the CLI `import-ontology` command, which augments extracted terms with `ecm:source: 'ecm:imported-ontology'` and `ecm:ontologyId: <ontology-UUID>` at the adapter boundary (`src/cli/index.ts:323-328`). The read-only rendering side of sub-task 3.2 is partially shipped: `TermSidebar.tsx` already gates the click handler on `ecm:source === 'ecm:project-created'`, applies `aria-disabled=\"true\"` to imported terms, and a Playwright test (term-crud.spec.ts AC4) verifies the structural read-only signal. The outstanding work for 3.2 is: (1) the remap-references workflow per SPEC \u00c2\u00a713.6 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d no `RemapDialog` component or `remapReferences` function exists anywhere in `src/`; (2) a read-only inspector panel for imported terms when clicked (Inspector.tsx currently has no selected-term mode); and (3) the unit tests (AC3 remap A\u00e2\u2020\u2019B IRI rewrite, AC4 ontology record preservation) and the Playwright AC1/AC2 tests. A critical structural gap: the existing `refactorIri` function in `src/refactor/index.ts` has a collision check that fires when `newIri` already exists in `ecm:terms`, which is exactly the state during remap (the project-created replacement term already exists), so the remap operation cannot simply delegate to `refactorIri` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d it requires either a separate pure-function reference-rewrite path or a flag to bypass the collision gate. The IRI fields in scope for the remap rewrite are `ecm:classIris` (instances), `ecm:predicateIri` (relations and literal assertions); `rdfs:subClassOf`, `rdfs:subPropertyOf`, and `rdfs:range` on the term object itself are round-trip-preserved fields and are not rewrite targets. The existing `imported-term.jsonld` and `term-sidebar-2c-1op-1dp.jsonld` fixtures both use `ecm:ontologyId: null` rather than real ontology UUIDs, which is an acceptable fixture simplification but means they do not reflect the actual project state produced by the CLI import path.",
