        "open_questions": [
          "The remap workflow semantics differ from `refactorIri` semantics: `refactorIri` aborts when `newIri` already exists in `ecm:terms` (collision guard), but remap requires the project-created replacement to already exist. Should the developer implement a separate `remapReferences(project, importedIri, projectCreatedIri)` pure function (bypassing the collision gate), or should `refactorIri` be extended with a `skipCollisionCheck` flag? The architect must choose the correct shape before the developer proposes the implementation.",
          "Where should the remap affordance be surfaced in the UI? Two candidates: (a) a new context menu / action button on imported term items in TermSidebar when clicked, opening a new `RemapDialog`; (b) an extension to Inspector to add a 'selected term' mode when the user clicks an imported term. The IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN says 'invokes remap' but does not specify the UI entry point. The operator must decide before the developer can propose the component shape.",
