        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The change introduces a new pure kernel function (src/kernel/remap-references.ts) plus its unit test file \u00e2\u20ac\u201d net-new behavioral surface area for the SPEC \u00c2\u00a713.6 remap workflow, far outside editorial-correction scope (typo / formatting / terminology tightening).",
        "rationale": "Pass 2a verification gates all clear for the narrowed Option B scope (kernel + unit tests; UI deferred): (1) Kernel purity: src/kernel/remap-references.ts has zero imports, uses only Array.isArray, Set, spread, sort, and typeof checks \u00e2\u20ac\u201d no Date.now(), Math.random(), crypto, fetch, DOM, or process.env references. (2) Layer boundary: the file has no import statements at all, so it cannot violate the src/kernel \u00e2\u2020\u2019 src/ui/composition/adapters prohibition; npm run test:purity will pass. (3) ImportedOntologyRecord preservation: the function only writes ecm:instances, ecm:relations, ecm:literalAssertions to the result document; ecm:ontologies, ecm:terms, ecm:snapshots, ecm:layouts, and ecm:serializations propagate via the outer `...project` spread, preserving them verbatim (object-reference identity for ecm:ontologies, as the test explicitly verifies). This satisfies SPEC \u00c2\u00a713.6 audit-trail integrity (the imported term entry remains as immutable metadata). (4) AC coverage: AC3 is exercised by an explicit three-array scan (instances.classIris, relations.predicateIri, literalAssertions.predicateIri) plus referenceCount=4 + sorted affectedEntityTypes assertion; AC4 is exercised by JSON.stringify equality on ecm:ontologies plus an object-reference identity check (===) plus a zero-references sub-case. Supplementary coverage of ecm:terms immutability, ecm:snapshots, out-of-scope subjectIri/objectIri, and the identity no-op path strengthens the contract surface. (5) Scope discipline: developer correctly limited the proposal to two file additions (kernel + unit test); no Playwright work appears in changes[], which matches the operator Option B narrowing \u00e2\u20ac\u201d UI work (RemapDialog, Inspector selected-term mode, AC1/AC2 Playwright) is forward-tracked to the 3.2-UI follow-up chain. Architecturally, the divergence from refactorIri (omitting the collision check that the reconnaissance F11 finding flagged) is the correct shape: the remap workflow requires the project-created replacement term to already exist in ecm:terms, which is exactly the state refactorIri's collision guard rejects. Implementing remapReferences as a separate pure function rather than extending refactorIri with a skipCollisionCheck flag keeps the two operations' semantic contracts distinct and prevents cross-contamination of their guarantees. Reconnaissance evidence (urn:fnsr:task:777-recon-p3-c3) is present in UPSTREAM with 18 findings grounded in file:line evidence and explicit scope_assessment; Spec 03 reconnaissance-required contract is satisfied.",
