        "bankings": [
          {
            "id": "B1",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "When two cascade-style kernel operations share rewrite-target field overlap but have semantically incompatible preconditions (refactorIri requires newIri to NOT exist; remapReferences requires projectCreatedIri to ALREADY exist), implementing them as separate pure functions with shared internal helpers (getEntityArray, getStr) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d rather than parameterizing one with a behavior flag \u00e2\u20ac\u201d preserves each function's contract guarantees independently and makes the divergent semantics legible at the import site. Worth noting as a discipline for future kernel-surface decisions where 'extend with flag' vs 'split into sibling' is the design question."
