        "rationale": "Reconnaissance evidence (urn:fnsr:task:790-recon-p3-c3.2) is present in UPSTREAM, satisfying the Spec 03 reconnaissance-required contract for substantive change. Each of the five ratification criteria is satisfied by the proposed changes[]: (1) C1 declares `onImportedTermClick?: (term: TermEntry) => void` with `?` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the prop is optional and existing call sites (App.tsx line 369-371 per F3; the negative-invariant test setup which passes no callback) continue to type-check and run; (2) C3 introduces `hasImportedClickHandler = isImported && onImportedTermClick !== undefined` and conditionally wires `onClick={... : hasImportedClickHandler ? () => { onImportedTermClick?.(term); } : undefined}`, so imported terms fire the callback when one is provided; (3) `aria-disabled={isImported ? \"true\" : undefined}` is preserved verbatim in C3 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the attribute set is unchanged; (4) the term-crud.spec.ts:219-246 negative invariant is preserved on three axes \u00e2\u20ac\u201d aria-disabled stays 'true' (axis 1, see above); `role={isClickable ? \"button\" : undefined}` is unchanged and `isClickable` still requires `ecm:source === \"ecm:project-created\"` (per F11), so imported terms still carry no role='button' (axis 2); and the new callback (when later wired in sub-task C) routes to the Inspector read-only view, not to EditTermDialog, so the `gw-dialog-edit-term` non-visibility assertion holds (axis 3 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d additionally, in the existing test no `onImportedTermClick` is passed via App.tsx, so onClick resolves to `undefined` and click remains a no-op in that test context); (5) all edits are confined to `src/ui/TermSidebar.tsx` (UI layer) and reuse `TermEntry` already in scope at file level \u00e2\u20ac\u201d no kernel/composition imports added, GraphWrite layer boundary intact. C2 + C4\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC8 are mechanical pass-through plumbing through TermSection's four call sites and the exported TermSidebar destructure \u00e2\u20ac\u201d required to make C1+C3 reachable end-to-end. The developer's two open_questions are deferred-to-downstream-subtask concerns (TermEntry export ergonomics for sub-task C; onKeyDown for the read-only path) and are not in sub-task B scope; neither blocks ratification. The change set is minimal (~16 lines, one file), self-contained, and the existing AC4 invariant test serves as the immediate regression guard at apply time.",
