            "before": "interface InspectorProps {\n  selectedRelationId: string | null;\n  selectedInstanceId: string | null;\n  project: Record<string, unknown> | null;\n  /**\n   * Called with the updated project document on relation or literal mutation.\n   * Accepted here so App can pass it unconditionally and the prop shape is\n   * stable across chains.\n   */\n  onProjectChange?: (updated: Record<string, unknown>) => void;\n}",
            "after": "interface InspectorProps {\n  selectedRelationId: string | null;\n  selectedInstanceId: string | null;\n  /**\n   * When non-null, Inspector renders a read-only term-metadata view instead\n   * of the relation or instance panel. Term mode takes priority when set.\n   * FR-U010; IMPL PLAN section 3.2 AC2.\n   */\n  selectedTermId: string | null;\n  project: Record<string, unknown> | null;\n  /**\n   * Called with the updated project document on relation or literal mutation.\n   * Accepted here so App can pass it unconditionally and the prop shape is\n   * stable across chains.\n   */\n  onProjectChange?: (updated: Record<string, unknown>) => void;\n}",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C3",
            "file": "src/ui/Inspector.tsx",
            "rationale": "Destructure selectedTermId from props, add remapOpen useState (must be unconditional per React hook rules), then insert the term-mode early-return block before the existing empty guard. The term-mode block finds the term entry, renders read-only metadata + imported badge + Remap affordance, and mounts RemapDialog when open. Existing empty/instance/relation branches are untouched.",
            "before": "export function Inspector({\n  selectedRelationId,\n  selectedInstanceId,\n  project,\n  onProjectChange,\n}: InspectorProps) {\n  const [addLiteralOpen, setAddLiteralOpen] = useState(false);\n  const [addAnnotationOpen, setAddAnnotationOpen] = useState(false);\n  const [deleteInstanceConfirmOpen, setDeleteInstanceConfirmOpen] = useState(false);\n  const [selectedAddClassIri, setSelectedAddClassIri] = useState<string>(\"\");\n\n  if ((selectedRelationId === null && selectedInstanceId === null) || project === null) {\n    return (\n      <p className=\"gw-placeholder\" data-testid=\"gw-inspector-empty\">\n        Select a node or relation to inspect.\n      </p>\n    );\n  }",
            "after": "export function Inspector({\n  selectedRelationId,\n  selectedInstanceId,\n  selectedTermId,\n  project,\n  onProjectChange,\n}: InspectorProps) {\n  const [addLiteralOpen, setAddLiteralOpen] = useState(false);\n  const [addAnnotationOpen, setAddAnnotationOpen] = useState(false);\n  const [deleteInstanceConfirmOpen, setDeleteInstanceConfirmOpen] = useState(false);\n  const [selectedAddClassIri, setSelectedAddClassIri] = useState<string>(\"\");\n  // remapOpen is declared unconditionally (React hook ordering); only set/read in term mode.\n  const [remapOpen, setRemapOpen] = useState(false);\n\n  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  // Term mode (FR-U010; IMPL PLAN section 3.2 AC2) -- takes priority when set.\n  // Renders read-only term metadata + imported badge + Remap affordance button.\n  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  if (selectedTermId !== null && project !== null) {\n    const allTerms = Array.isArray(project[\"ecm:terms\"])\n      ? (project[\"ecm:terms\"] as unknown[])\n      : [];\n    const termEntry =\n      allTerms.find(\n        (t): t is Record<string, unknown> =>\n          typeof t === \"object\" &&\n          t !== null &&\n          (t as Record<string, unknown>)[\"id\"] === selectedTermId,\n      ) ?? null;\n    const isImportedTerm =\n      termEntry !== null && termEntry[\"ecm:source\"] === \"ecm:imported-ontology\";\n    const rawLabel = termEntry !== null ? resolveTermLabel(termEntry[\"rdfs:label\"]) : \"\";\n    const displayTermLabel = rawLabel.length > 0 ? rawLabel : iriTail(selectedTermId);\n    const termType =\n      termEntry !== null && typeof termEntry[\"type\"] === \"string\"\n        ? (termEntry[\"type\"] as string)\n        : \"\";\n    const termComment =\n      termEntry !== null && typeof termEntry[\"rdfs:comment\"] === \"string\"\n        ? (termEntry[\"rdfs:comment\"] as string)\n        : null;\n    const projectCreatedTerms = allTerms.filter(\n      (t): t is Record<string, unknown> =>\n        typeof t === \"object\" &&\n        t !== null &&\n        (t as Record<string, unknown>)[\"ecm:source\"] === \"ecm:project-created\",\n    );\n\n    return (\n      <>\n        <div data-testid=\"gw-inspector-imported-term\">\n          <p style={{ fontWeight: 600, marginBottom: \"0.5rem\" }}>Term</p>\n          {isImportedTerm && (\n            <span\n              className=\"gw-badge gw-badge--imported\"\n              aria-label=\"ecm:imported-ontology\"\n              style={{ marginBottom: \"0.5rem\", display: \"inline-block\" }}\n              data-testid=\"gw-inspector-term-imported-badge\"\n            >\n              imported\n            </span>\n          )}\n          <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n            Label\n          </p>\n          <p\n            style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}\n            data-testid=\"gw-inspector-term-label\"\n          >\n            {displayTermLabel}\n          </p>\n          <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n            IRI\n          </p>\n          <p\n            style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", wordBreak: \"break-all\", marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}\n            data-testid=\"gw-inspector-term-iri\"\n          >\n            {selectedTermId}\n          </p>\n          {termType.length > 0 && (\n            <>\n              <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n                Type\n              </p>\n              <p\n                style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}\n                data-testid=\"gw-inspector-term-type\"\n              >\n                {termType}\n              </p>\n            </>\n          )}\n          {termComment !== null && (\n            <>\n              <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n                Comment\n              </p>\n              <p\n                style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}\n                data-testid=\"gw-inspector-term-comment\"\n              >\n                {termComment}\n              </p>\n            </>\n          )}\n          {isImportedTerm && (\n            <button\n              type=\"button\"\n              data-testid=\"gw-btn-remap\"\n              onClick={() => { setRemapOpen(true); }}\n              style={{ marginTop: \"0.5rem\", width: \"100%\" }}\n            >\n              Remap References\n            </button>\n          )}\n        </div>\n        {remapOpen && termEntry !== null && (\n          <RemapDialog\n            importedTerm={termEntry}\n            projectCreatedTerms={projectCreatedTerms}\n            project={project}\n            onConfirm={(updated) => {\n              if (onProjectChange !== undefined) onProjectChange(updated);\n              setRemapOpen(false);\n            }}\n            onClose={() => { setRemapOpen(false); }}\n          />\n        )}\n      </>\n    );\n  }\n\n  if ((selectedRelationId === null && selectedInstanceId === null) || project === null) {\n    return (\n      <p className=\"gw-placeholder\" data-testid=\"gw-inspector-empty\">\n        Select a node or relation to inspect.\n      </p>\n    );\n  }",
            "scope": "moderate"
          },
          {
            "id": "C4",
            "file": "src/ui/App.tsx",
            "rationale": "Add selectedTermId state hook alongside existing selection state hooks. Placed after selectedInstanceId for logical grouping.",
            "before": "  const [project, setProject] = useState<Record<string, unknown> | null>(null);\n  const [migrationBannerText, setMigrationBannerText] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [selectedRelationId, setSelectedRelationId] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [selectedInstanceId, setSelectedInstanceId] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [projectSettingsOpen, setProjectSettingsOpen] = useState(false);\n  const [newProjectDialogOpen, setNewProjectDialogOpen] = useState(false);\n  const [validationReport, setValidationReport] = useState<ValidationReport | null>(null);",
            "after": "  const [project, setProject] = useState<Record<string, unknown> | null>(null);\n  const [migrationBannerText, setMigrationBannerText] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [selectedRelationId, setSelectedRelationId] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [selectedInstanceId, setSelectedInstanceId] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  // selectedTermId: IRI of the imported term selected in TermSidebar (FR-U010; sub-task C).\n  const [selectedTermId, setSelectedTermId] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [projectSettingsOpen, setProjectSettingsOpen] = useState(false);\n  const [newProjectDialogOpen, setNewProjectDialogOpen] = useState(false);\n  const [validationReport, setValidationReport] = useState<ValidationReport | null>(null);",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C5",
            "file": "src/ui/App.tsx",
            "rationale": "Clear selectedTermId when a canvas edge or node is selected, enforcing mutual exclusion between the three selection modes at the App level. Pattern matches how onEdgeSelect/onNodeSelect already clear each other.",
            "before": "            onEdgeSelect={(id) => { setSelectedRelationId(id); setSelectedInstanceId(null); }}\n            onNodeSelect={(id) => { setSelectedInstanceId(id); setSelectedRelationId(null); }}",
            "after": "            onEdgeSelect={(id) => { setSelectedRelationId(id); setSelectedInstanceId(null); setSelectedTermId(null); }}\n            onNodeSelect={(id) => { setSelectedInstanceId(id); setSelectedRelationId(null); setSelectedTermId(null); }}",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C6",
            "file": "src/ui/App.tsx",
            "rationale": "Wire the onImportedTermClick callback to TermSidebar. When fired, sets selectedTermId to the clicked term's IRI and clears the other two selection modes, maintaining mutual exclusion.",
            "before": "          <TermSidebar\n            project={project}\n            onTermsChange={(updated) => { setProject(updated); setValidationReport(validate(updated)); }}\n          />",
            "after": "          <TermSidebar\n            project={project}\n            onTermsChange={(updated) => { setProject(updated); setValidationReport(validate(updated)); }}\n            onImportedTermClick={(term) => {\n              setSelectedTermId(term.id);\n              setSelectedRelationId(null);\n              setSelectedInstanceId(null);\n            }}\n          />",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C7",
            "file": "src/ui/App.tsx",
            "rationale": "Pass selectedTermId to Inspector so the new term-mode branch can render.",
            "before": "          <Inspector\n            selectedRelationId={selectedRelationId}\n            selectedInstanceId={selectedInstanceId}\n            project={project}\n            onProjectChange={(updated) => { setProject(updated); setValidationReport(validate(updated)); }}\n          />",
            "after": "          <Inspector\n            selectedRelationId={selectedRelationId}\n            selectedInstanceId={selectedInstanceId}\n            selectedTermId={selectedTermId}\n            project={project}\n            onProjectChange={(updated) => { setProject(updated); setValidationReport(validate(updated)); }}\n          />",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C8",
            "file": "src/ui/RemapDialog.tsx",
            "rationale": "New Dialog component. Receives importedTerm, projectCreatedTerms, project. Filters candidates to same OWL type as importedTerm (SPEC 13.6 same-kind replacement; see open_questions re: OQ2). Calls remapReferences on apply and propagates the updated project via onConfirm. Follows Dialog.tsx mount/unmount pattern and testId convention established by EditTermDialog.",
            "before": null,
            "after": "/**\n * RemapDialog -- Remap References affordance (FR-U010; IMPL PLAN section 3.2).\n *\n * Presents a drop-down of project-created terms with the same OWL type as the\n * imported term and invokes remapReferences on confirm.\n *\n * SPEC refs: section 13.3, section 13.6, FR-U010.\n * Dialog testId: \"gw-dialog-remap\".\n */\n\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { Dialog } from \"./Dialog.js\";\nimport { remapReferences } from \"../kernel/remap-references.js\";\nimport { resolveTermLabel, iriTail } from \"./label-resolution.js\";\n\ninterface RemapDialogProps {\n  /** The imported-ontology term whose references will be remapped (source term A). */\n  importedTerm: Record<string, unknown>;\n  /** All project-created terms passed from Inspector; filtered here by OWL type. */\n  projectCreatedTerms: Record<string, unknown>[];\n  /** Current project document passed to remapReferences on confirm. */\n  project: Record<string, unknown>;\n  /**\n   * Called with the updated project document after remapReferences succeeds.\n   * Parent controls visibility: unmount after onConfirm fires.\n   */\n  onConfirm: (updatedProject: Record<string, unknown>) => void;\n  onClose: () => void;\n}\n\nexport function RemapDialog({\n  importedTerm,\n  projectCreatedTerms,\n  project,\n  onConfirm,\n  onClose,\n}: RemapDialogProps) {\n  const [selectedTargetIri, setSelectedTargetIri] = useState<string>(\"\");\n\n  const importedIri =\n    typeof importedTerm[\"id\"] === \"string\" ? (importedTerm[\"id\"] as string) : \"\";\n  const importedType =\n    typeof importedTerm[\"type\"] === \"string\" ? (importedTerm[\"type\"] as string) : \"\";\n  const importedLabel = resolveTermLabel(importedTerm[\"rdfs:label\"]);\n  const displayImportedLabel =\n    importedLabel.length > 0 ? importedLabel : iriTail(importedIri);\n\n  // Filter to project-created terms with matching OWL type (SPEC section 13.6).\n  // See open_questions: operator may wish to show all project-created terms instead.\n  const candidateTerms = projectCreatedTerms.filter(\n    (t) => typeof t[\"type\"] === \"string\" && t[\"type\"] === importedType,\n  );\n\n  function handleApply() {\n    if (selectedTargetIri === \"\") return;\n    const result = remapReferences(project, importedIri, selectedTargetIri);\n    onConfirm(result.project);\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <Dialog title=\"Remap References\" onClose={onClose} testId=\"gw-dialog-remap\">\n      <p style={{ marginBottom: \"0.75rem\", fontSize: \"0.85rem\" }}>\n        Replace all references to <strong>{displayImportedLabel}</strong> with a\n        project-created term.\n      </p>\n      <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.25rem\" }}>\n        Replace with\n      </p>\n      <select\n        value={selectedTargetIri}\n        onChange={(e) => { setSelectedTargetIri(e.target.value); }}\n        data-testid=\"gw-select-remap-target\"\n        style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", width: \"100%\", marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}\n      >\n        <option value=\"\">(select replacement term)</option>\n        {candidateTerms.map((t) => {\n          const iri = typeof t[\"id\"] === \"string\" ? (t[\"id\"] as string) : \"\";\n          const lbl = resolveTermLabel(t[\"rdfs:label\"]);\n          const display = lbl.length > 0 ? lbl : iriTail(iri);\n          return (\n            <option key={iri} value={iri}>\n              {display}\n            </option>\n          );\n        })}\n      </select>\n      {candidateTerms.length === 0 && (\n        <p\n          style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", color: \"#94a3b8\", marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}\n          data-testid=\"gw-remap-no-candidates\"\n        >\n          No project-created {importedType} terms available.\n        </p>\n      )}\n      <div style={{ display: \"flex\", gap: \"0.5rem\", justifyContent: \"flex-end\" }}>\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          className=\"gw-btn gw-btn--secondary\"\n          onClick={onClose}\n          data-testid=\"gw-btn-remap-cancel\"\n        >\n          Cancel\n        </button>\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          className=\"gw-btn\"\n          onClick={handleApply}\n          disabled={selectedTargetIri === \"\"}\n          data-testid=\"gw-btn-remap-apply\"\n        >\n          Apply\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    </Dialog>\n  );\n}",
            "scope": "moderate"
          }
        ],
        "tests_recommended": [
          {
            "file": "tests/playwright/imported-term-read-only.spec.ts",
            "describe": "Sub-task E Playwright spec (AC1 + AC2). AC1: open imported-term.jsonld fixture, save, re-parse -- assert ecm:source: 'ecm:imported-ontology' is preserved in the downloaded file. AC2: load fixture, click the imported 'Imported Class' term in the Classes section, assert gw-inspector-imported-term is visible, assert gw-inspector-term-imported-badge is visible, assert no edit controls (no input, no Delete button) are present in the inspector panel, assert gw-btn-remap is visible. Negative invariant: assert gw-dialog-edit-term is NOT visible after the click (per recon F4 / existing term-crud.spec.ts AC4). Remap flow: assert clicking gw-btn-remap opens gw-dialog-remap; assert gw-select-remap-target is present; assert gw-btn-remap-cancel closes the dialog."
          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "OQ2 (RemapDialog candidate filtering): RemapDialog currently filters projectCreatedTerms to same OWL type as importedTerm (e.g., only owl:Class candidates shown for an imported owl:Class). If the operator prefers showing ALL project-created terms regardless of type, remove the `t['type'] === importedType` filter in RemapDialog's candidateTerms derivation. Current same-type default is semantically conservative and matches SPEC 13.6 intent.",
          "OQ5 (Inspector term-mode testId): The read-only term panel uses data-testid='gw-inspector-imported-term' (per recon OQ5 suggestion). Sub-task E Playwright spec should assert this testId is visible when a term is selected. Confirm this ID before authoring the spec.",
          "remapOpen stale-state edge case: if the user opens RemapDialog (remapOpen=true) then navigates away by clicking a canvas node or edge, remapOpen stays true in state. When they return to a term selection, the dialog re-appears immediately. This is consistent with the existing deleteInstanceConfirmOpen pattern in Inspector but may surprise users. A future improvement could reset remapOpen whenever selectedTermId changes via a useEffect."
        ],
        "summary": "Three-file change implementing sub-task C. Inspector.tsx: extended InspectorProps with selectedTermId, added remapOpen useState (unconditional per hook rules), inserted a term-mode early-return block that renders read-only metadata + imported badge + Remap affordance, mounts RemapDialog on button click. App.tsx: added selectedTermId useState, wired mutual exclusion (CanvasView onEdgeSelect/onNodeSelect clear selectedTermId; TermSidebar onImportedTermClick clears the other two), passed selectedTermId to Inspector. RemapDialog.tsx: new Dialog component matching EditTermDialog pattern; filters candidates to same OWL type; calls remapReferences kernel on apply; propagates updated project via onConfirm. Existing instance/relation/empty branches in Inspector are untouched; the negative-invariant Playwright test (term-crud.spec.ts AC4, lines 219-246) is unaffected because aria-disabled and the absence of role='button' on imported term list items are unchanged by sub-task B.",
        "self_assessment": "uncertain"
      },
