        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "Introduces a new UI component (RemapDialog), extends InspectorProps with a new selectedTermId prop, adds a new App-level state hook, and wires a new affordance path; this changes behavioral surface area and component contracts, not just text.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM (urn:fnsr:task:790-recon-p3-c3.2) per Spec 03 \u00c2\u00a7'Reconnaissance requirement'. The proposed change satisfies all five architect concerns in INPUTS.purpose: (1) ADDITIVE INSPECTOR BRANCH -- C3 inserts the term-mode early-return BEFORE the existing empty/relation/instance branches; the original `if ((selectedRelationId === null && selectedInstanceId === null) || project === null)` guard and downstream paths are unchanged. The new `remapOpen` useState hook is declared at component top alongside the existing four useState calls, satisfying React hook-ordering rules (rules-of-hooks holds; recon F10 anticipated this constraint). (2) APP.TSX WIRING -- C4 adds selectedTermId state adjacent to existing selection hooks; C5 clears selectedTermId on canvas edge/node select; C6 wires onImportedTermClick to set selectedTermId and clear the other two selection modes; C7 propagates to Inspector. The mutual-exclusion pattern is symmetric across the three selection-clearing sites; nothing is silently retained. (3) KERNEL PURITY OF REMAPDIALOG -- C8's RemapDialog imports `remapReferences` from `../kernel/remap-references.js` and invokes it directly in handleApply; no remapping logic is reimplemented in the dialog. The dialog's local concerns (candidate filter by OWL type, target-IRI useState, button disabled state) are presentation-only. The kernel remains the single source of remap behavior (recon F7/F8). (4) AFFORDANCE GATING -- The Remap button is wrapped in `{isImportedTerm && (...)}`; for project-created or unresolved terms, no Remap button renders. The RemapDialog mount is doubly gated by `{remapOpen && termEntry !== null && (...)}`. The affordance is structurally unreachable for non-imported terms. (5) LAYER BOUNDARY -- RemapDialog lives in src/ui/ and imports from src/kernel/; direction is ui->kernel, which is permitted per CLAUDE.md section 9 (Layer 2 may import Layer 0). No kernel file is modified; no kernel->ui edge is introduced. ADDITIONAL OBSERVATIONS: the developer's self_assessment of 'uncertain' is acknowledged; the three open_questions (OQ2 candidate-filter strictness, OQ5 testId convention, remapOpen stale-state on selection change) are non-blocking -- OQ2 is a deliberate conservative default matching SPEC section 13.6, OQ5 is a downstream sub-task E concern, and the remapOpen stale-state mirrors the existing deleteInstanceConfirmOpen pattern (consistency over novel behavior). Per CLAUDE.md section 7.8 'Chain-shape variation by artifact kind', this is TypeScript code; verification-ritual is correctly omitted upstream and the substrate's test-runner is the proper verification step queued downstream of applier.",
        "referenced_evidence": [
          {
