        "bankings": [
          {
            "id": "B1",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "Inspector multi-mode early-return ordering is the load-bearing pattern for additive mode introductions: hooks declared unconditionally at top, then mode branches return in priority order (term -> empty -> relation -> instance). Sub-task C correctly placed the new `remapOpen` useState alongside the existing four hooks BEFORE any branch, preserving rules-of-hooks invariants. Future sub-tasks adding Inspector modes (e.g., literal-mode, snapshot-mode) should follow the same declare-then-branch pattern; violating it produces silent runtime hook-mismatch errors that would not be caught by `npm run build`."
          },
          {
            "id": "B2",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "Cross-selection mutual-exclusion in App.tsx is currently maintained by spreading the clears across each selection-setting site (CanvasView onEdgeSelect/onNodeSelect, TermSidebar onImportedTermClick) rather than centralizing in a `selectExactlyOne(kind, id)` helper. With three selection modes the pattern is still manageable; at four or more it becomes a structural defect candidate (one omitted clear creates a phantom dual-selection). Worth surfacing as a refactor candidate if a fourth selection axis is introduced (e.g., snapshot selection or ontology-record selection)."
          },
          {
            "id": "B3",
            "category": "discipline-correction",
            "content": "The proposed change correctly threads remap business logic through the kernel pure function (`remapReferences`) rather than reimplementing inside RemapDialog. This is the architectural commitment from CLAUDE.md section 9 working as intended: when a UI affordance corresponds to a transformation already implemented in the kernel, the dialog is a thin presentation layer over a kernel call. Any future affordance landing in ui/ that performs entity-graph mutation should mirror this shape -- if the operation does not yet exist in the kernel, add the kernel function first, ratify it, then build the dialog."
          }
        ]
      },
