        "rationale": "The proposed single-file addition (tests/playwright/imported-term-read-only.spec.ts) satisfies all four task-purpose invariants and is grounded in upstream reconnaissance (urn:fnsr:task:790-recon-p3-c3.2). (1) AC1 is implemented as a fixture round-trip: Open via setInputFiles(IMPORTED_TERM_FIXTURE) -> Save via gw-btn-save download capture -> JSON.parse the downloaded content -> assert ecm:source === 'ecm:imported-ontology' on the ImportedClass term entry. No CLI import path is invoked; this exactly matches the round-trip discipline (recon F13) and the testIds gw-file-input / gw-btn-save are confirmed present in App.tsx lines 277/307. (2) AC2 verifies a positive invariant: after click, the test asserts gw-inspector-imported-term is visible (confirmed at Inspector.tsx line 345) and gw-inspector-term-imported-badge is visible (confirmed at line 352). The test correctly distinguishes the new positive invariant ('Inspector opens read-only for imported term') from the existing AC4 negative invariant ('click does not open EditTermDialog' -- which is also reasserted as a non-regression guard within the new test). (3) tests/playwright/term-crud.spec.ts is not modified -- the changes[] entry has before: null and a single file path that is distinct from term-crud.spec.ts; AC4 (lines 219-246) and its three asserted invariants (aria-disabled='true', no role='button', no EditTermDialog on click) remain intact and remain TRUE because sub-task B routes the click to the Inspector path rather than to EditTermDialog (recon F4, F11; confirmed in TermSidebar.tsx lines 168-186 where the imported-click handler is separate from the edit-click handler and EditTermDialog is never invoked for imported terms). (4) The fixture used (tests/playwright/fixtures/imported-term.jsonld) already exists in canonical shape (recon F12; verified: ecm:terms contains 'Imported Class' with ecm:source='ecm:imported-ontology' at IRI https://example.org/ontology/ImportedClass) and the path-construction pattern path.join(process.cwd(), 'tests', 'playwright', 'fixtures', ...) matches the existing convention used by term-crud.spec.ts and term-sidebar.spec.ts (recon F16). Playwright auto-discovery (recon F15) requires no config edit. Cross-subtask dependency (recon F17): the developer's tests_recommended correctly notes AC2 depends on sub-tasks B and C, both of which are upstream of this ratification per the UPSTREAM chain. Artifact-kind chain composition (CLAUDE.md section 7.8 gap-3): this is code, so verification-ritual is appropriately skipped; mojibake-repair is appropriately skipped (file is ASCII-only); test-runner downstream of applier is the verification path. No purity, no determinism, no layer-boundary concerns -- the file lives at tests/playwright/ and imports only @playwright/test, path, fs.",
