        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM (task 804-recon-demo-doc-phase-3) per Spec 03's architect refusal contract, so the substantive-change reconnaissance gate is satisfied. The proposed file demo/PHASE-3-chain-3.2-ui-immutability-remap.md conforms to the v3.5.0 demo-doc-author stakeholder-review structure: H1 title, what-delivered narrative, AC table (3.2 AC1-AC4 with explicit test references), how-to-verify (npm install/build/test + separate npx playwright command), what-works-end-to-end, NOT-in-scope (mirroring the recon's open_questions on Exit Gate items 3/5/7/8/9/11 + OED-303 + RemapDialog filter strictness + remapOpen stale-state), and a sign-off prompt with four explicit PO questions (OQ-1 candidate filter, Exit Gate framing, Playwright self-verification, pass/revise/pivot). Every citation in the after-payload is grounded in the reconnaissance evidence: SPEC sections 13.3, 13.6, FR-U010, FR-C011, sections 14.1/12.2/5.6/5.7/23 (F14); IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN sections 3.1/3.2/3.3/3.4/3.5 (F3/F4/F5/F13/F16); ADR-003 cited as discharged (F15). Test-gate claim (148/148 across 20 files, exit_code=0) is anchored in F2 evidence from urn:fnsr:task:803-test-p3-c3.2. The doc correctly flags that the Playwright AC1+AC2 spec is wired but operator-run, not substrate-verified -- this preserves audit honesty per recon open_question #2. surface_audience=\"consumer\" is appropriate per CLAUDE.md section 7.13 (PO is the reader). ASCII-only is respected (uses '->' and 'section' rather than arrows or section glyphs). One file change per dispatch; create-only with before=null; path is not a canonical-doc prefix per CLAUDE.md section 7.5 (demo/ is not in the canonical list), so the ADR-citation CPS check will not fire on this path, but the citations are nonetheless real and consistent with the registry. One minor factual discrepancy noted (see bankings B1): the body says '3 architect-ratified developer tasks' while the substrate-audit-curious paragraph and F21 evidence say 4 (792-rat-B, 795-rat-D, 798-rat-C, 801-rat-E). The discrepancy traces back to the original operator phase-released note ('3 architects ratified') and propagated through reconnaissance F1 into the author output. It does not invalidate the PO-facing content -- the AC coverage, test gate, sign-off questions, and surface description are all correct -- so it is ratification-safe to land and flag as a forward-banking-worthy substrate-discipline pattern rather than a refusal cause. No invented citations; no out-of-scope claims; no semantic-memory mutation; ratify.",
