        "open_questions": [
          "Sub-task A: Should the browser-compat change be (a) an optional 5th parameter on importOntology making it async only when digestFn is provided (TypeScript overloads required), or (b) a separate src/import/turtle-import-browser.ts file with a new async function that the UI imports instead? Option (a) minimizes duplication but requires overload signatures; option (b) avoids any change to the existing synchronous contract but duplicates parsing logic.",
          "Sub-task A: The injectable digest function would naturally receive a Uint8Array (browser TextEncoder output) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d but the size check error message currently embeds sourceBytes.length (line 133). Should the error message in the browser path also reflect the Uint8Array.length (same value for pure UTF-8 content), or is a simplified 'source too large' message acceptable for the browser path?",
          "Sub-task B: Should the Import Ontology button be disabled only when project === null, or also when a project is loaded but has blocking validation errors (MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR etc.)? The current Save button only guards project === null.",
          "Sub-task C: Does the import flow require a dialog at all for the happy path (one owl:Class found, merge succeeds) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d or does inline toast/banner feedback suffice? A dialog may be required for LARGE_IMPORT (>10,000 terms per \u00c2\u00a714.2), but that is Chain 3.3 scope. Does Chain 4 need to pre-wire the LARGE_IMPORT dialog, or just the baseline file-pick-and-merge flow?",
          "Sub-task D: The minimal-ontology.ttl fixture for Playwright: should it contain only owl:Class terms (sufficient to verify the import pipeline), or also owl:ObjectProperty and owl:DatatypeProperty to exercise all three term-type paths in a single fixture? The inline SMALL_TTL in tests/import-turtle.test.ts only has owl:Class \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a richer fixture would increase coverage but adds fixture maintenance.",
          "Vite bundler config (vite.config.ts lines 8-13): no explicit `resolve.alias` or `optimizeDeps` settings exist. When src/ui imports from src/import (which contains node:crypto), Vite will fail at bundle time unless the import path resolves to a browser-safe file. The developer must confirm that the browser entry point does NOT import from node:crypto-bearing modules at all."
        ],
