    {
      "@id": "urn:fnsr:task:809-dev-p3-c4-A",
      "agent": "developer",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": 10,
      "depends_on": [
        "urn:fnsr:task:808-recon-p3-c4"
      ],
      "inputs": {
        "phase": "phase-3",
        "chain_label": "Phase 3 Chain 4 sub-task A -- browser-compat SHA-256 shim + injectable digest in importOntology",
        "purpose": "Sub-task A: enable importOntology to run in the browser. (1) Create src/kernel/sha256.ts as a tiny pure module that exposes two functions: sha256Hex(bytes: Uint8Array | string) for node and sha256HexAsync(bytes: Uint8Array | string) for browser (Web Crypto API). Implementation: node path uses node:crypto.createHash; browser path uses crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256', ...). Both return hex strings matching the existing 'sha256-<64-hex>' format that Chain 1 produces. (2) Tweak src/import/turtle-import.ts to accept an optional digestHexFn parameter; if absent, fall back to the existing node:crypto-based path (preserving Chain 1 CLI behavior verbatim). Browser callers pass the sha256HexAsync function. This is a NON-BREAKING refactor: existing CLI tests must continue passing without modification. Add tests/sha256.test.ts unit tests verifying the node path (browser path tested via Playwright in sub-task D).",
        "files_in_scope": [
          "src/kernel/sha256.ts (new)",
          "src/import/turtle-import.ts (modify: accept optional digestHexFn; non-breaking)",
          "tests/sha256.test.ts (new)"
        ],
        "spec_refs": [
          "SPEC section 5.6 ecm:contentHash format",
          "NFR-003 determinism"
        ],
        "constraint": "Non-breaking refactor. src/kernel/ layer purity: no DOM, no Date.now, no Math.random. The browser-compat path uses Web Crypto API which is browser-only; ship it as a separate exported function so the existing node path doesn't import any browser globals. Per CLAUDE.md section 9 layer boundaries: src/kernel/ may not import from src/ui/ or src/adapters/. The sha256.ts module ships both functions but consumers pick the right one for their runtime.",
        "ft_anchor": null
      },
      "attempts": 1,
      "outputs": {
        "changes": [
          {
            "id": "C1",
            "file": "src/kernel/sha256.ts",
            "rationale": "New module exporting sha256Hex (sync, node:crypto) and sha256HexAsync (async, globalThis.crypto.subtle). Both accept Uint8Array|string and return a 64-char lowercase hex string \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the value placed after the 'sha256-' prefix in ecm:contentHash (SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.6). Placing the module in src/kernel/ lets the purity checker validate it and keeps it importable by the test suite via tsconfig.test.json (which includes src/**/*). The node:crypto import passes the purity checker's node:-builtin allowlist. sha256HexAsync uses no import \u00e2\u20ac\u201d globalThis.crypto.subtle is a global in both browsers and Node >= 19; Node 22 is the engine floor per package.json.",
            "before": null,
            "after": "/**\n * SHA-256 utilities \u2014 two runtimes, two functions.\n *\n * sha256Hex      \u2013 synchronous; Node path (node:crypto.createHash).\n *                  Import this in Node-only CLI / server code.\n * sha256HexAsync \u2013 async; browser-safe path (globalThis.crypto.subtle).\n *                  Import this in browser / Vite bundles where node:crypto\n *                  is unavailable.\n *\n * Both accept a Uint8Array or a string (UTF-8 encoded before hashing) and\n * return a lowercase 64-character hex digest \u2014 the value placed after the\n * \"sha256-\" prefix in ecm:contentHash (SPEC \u00a75.6, NFR-003).\n *\n * Layer boundary: MUST NOT import from src/adapters/ or src/composition/.\n * sha256Hex depends on node:crypto (Node-only runtime).\n * sha256HexAsync uses globalThis.crypto.subtle (available in Node >= 19\n * and all modern browsers; no import required).\n */\n\nimport { createHash } from \"node:crypto\";\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Public API\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n/**\n * Compute a SHA-256 hex digest synchronously using node:crypto.\n *\n * Node-only. Do NOT bundle into browser / Vite builds.\n *\n * @param input - Raw bytes or a UTF-8 string (encoded with Buffer.from before hashing).\n * @returns Lowercase 64-character hex string.\n */\nexport function sha256Hex(input: Uint8Array | string): string {\n  const bytes =\n    typeof input === \"string\" ? Buffer.from(input, \"utf8\") : input;\n  return createHash(\"sha256\").update(bytes).digest(\"hex\");\n}\n\n/**\n * Compute a SHA-256 hex digest asynchronously using the Web Crypto API.\n *\n * Browser-safe (uses globalThis.crypto.subtle \u2014 no import required).\n * Also available in Node >= 19 without additional imports.\n *\n * @param input - Raw bytes or a UTF-8 string (encoded with TextEncoder before hashing).\n * @returns Promise resolving to a lowercase 64-character hex string.\n */\nexport async function sha256HexAsync(\n  input: Uint8Array | string,\n): Promise<string> {\n  const bytes =\n    typeof input === \"string\"\n      ? new TextEncoder().encode(input)\n      : input;\n  const buffer = await globalThis.crypto.subtle.digest(\"SHA-256\", bytes);\n  return Array.from(new Uint8Array(buffer))\n    .map((b) => b.toString(16).padStart(2, \"0\"))\n    .join(\"\");\n}\n",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C2",
            "file": "src/import/turtle-import.ts",
            "rationale": "Update the module-level compatibility comment (line 18) to reflect that a browser-safe async code path is now available via the optional digestHexFn parameter. The before snippet is unique in the file and contains no mojibake.",
            "before": " * Uses node:crypto; not browser-compatible (node:crypto).",
            "after": " * Synchronous path uses node:crypto (Node-only). Supply digestHexFn (e.g.\n * sha256HexAsync from src/kernel/sha256.ts) for the async browser-safe path.",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C3",
            "file": "src/import/turtle-import.ts",
            "rationale": "Add two TypeScript overload signatures before the implementation signature so call sites without digestHexFn keep the existing synchronous ImportResult return type, while browser callers that pass digestHexFn receive Promise<ImportResult>. Simultaneously replace Buffer.from() with new TextEncoder().encode() for sourceBytes: TextEncoder is browser-compatible and produces byte-for-byte identical UTF-8 output for valid text, preserving the AC4 and AC5 hash/size-check invariants. The before snippet spans lines 121-128 inclusive; line 127 contains the \u00c3\u201a\u00c2\u00a7 mojibake sequence that must be matched verbatim.",
            "before": "export function importOntology(\n  turtleSource: string,\n  fileName: string,\n  projectId: string,\n  createdAt: string,\n): ImportResult {\n  // \u00c2\u00a712.2: hard-reject > 50 MB before parsing\n  const sourceBytes = Buffer.from(turtleSource, \"utf8\");",
            "after": "export function importOntology(\n  turtleSource: string,\n  fileName: string,\n  projectId: string,\n  createdAt: string,\n): ImportResult;\nexport function importOntology(\n  turtleSource: string,\n  fileName: string,\n  projectId: string,\n  createdAt: string,\n  digestHexFn: (bytes: Uint8Array) => Promise<string>,\n): Promise<ImportResult>;\nexport function importOntology(\n  turtleSource: string,\n  fileName: string,\n  projectId: string,\n  createdAt: string,\n  digestHexFn?: (bytes: Uint8Array) => Promise<string>,\n): ImportResult | Promise<ImportResult> {\n  // \u00a712.2: hard-reject > 50 MB before parsing\n  // TextEncoder is browser-compatible; byte count is identical to Buffer.from for UTF-8.\n  const sourceBytes = new TextEncoder().encode(turtleSource);",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C4",
            "file": "src/import/turtle-import.ts",
            "rationale": "Branch the digest/ontology build block: when digestHexFn is provided, an async IIFE awaits it and returns Promise<ImportResult>; when absent, the existing synchronous createHash path runs unchanged. A narrowed local `fn` reference ensures TypeScript control-flow analysis inside the async IIFE resolves digestHexFn as non-undefined. The before snippet starts at line 232 (first clean line after the \u00c3\u201a\u00c2\u00a75.6 mojibake comment) and is unique in the file.",
            "before": "  const digest = createHash(\"sha256\").update(sourceBytes).digest(\"hex\");\n  const ontology: ImportedOntologyRecord = {\n    id: generateIri(\"ecm:uuid-urn\", {}),\n    type: \"ecm:ImportedOntology\",\n    \"ecm:projectId\": projectId,\n    \"ecm:name\": deriveOntologyName(fileName),\n    \"ecm:sourceFileName\": fileName,\n    \"ecm:format\": \"text/turtle\",\n    \"ecm:contentHash\": `sha256-${digest}`,\n    \"ecm:content\": turtleSource,\n    \"ecm:createdAt\": createdAt,\n    \"ecm:importStatus\": \"ecm:parsed\",\n  };\n\n  return { ok: true, ontology, terms };\n}",
            "after": "  if (digestHexFn !== undefined) {\n    // Async browser path: caller supplies Web Crypto digest function.\n    const fn = digestHexFn;\n    return (async (): Promise<ImportResult> => {\n      const digest = await fn(sourceBytes);\n      const ontology: ImportedOntologyRecord = {\n        id: generateIri(\"ecm:uuid-urn\", {}),\n        type: \"ecm:ImportedOntology\",\n        \"ecm:projectId\": projectId,\n        \"ecm:name\": deriveOntologyName(fileName),\n        \"ecm:sourceFileName\": fileName,\n        \"ecm:format\": \"text/turtle\",\n        \"ecm:contentHash\": `sha256-${digest}`,\n        \"ecm:content\": turtleSource,\n        \"ecm:createdAt\": createdAt,\n        \"ecm:importStatus\": \"ecm:parsed\",\n      };\n      return { ok: true, ontology, terms };\n    })();\n  }\n\n  // Synchronous node path (default; preserves existing behaviour verbatim).\n  const digest = createHash(\"sha256\").update(sourceBytes).digest(\"hex\");\n  const ontology: ImportedOntologyRecord = {\n    id: generateIri(\"ecm:uuid-urn\", {}),\n    type: \"ecm:ImportedOntology\",\n    \"ecm:projectId\": projectId,\n    \"ecm:name\": deriveOntologyName(fileName),\n    \"ecm:sourceFileName\": fileName,\n    \"ecm:format\": \"text/turtle\",\n    \"ecm:contentHash\": `sha256-${digest}`,\n    \"ecm:content\": turtleSource,\n    \"ecm:createdAt\": createdAt,\n    \"ecm:importStatus\": \"ecm:parsed\",\n  };\n\n  return { ok: true, ontology, terms };\n}",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C5",
            "file": "tests/sha256.test.ts",
            "rationale": "Unit tests for src/kernel/sha256.ts covering both exports. Follows the hand-rolled pattern (node:assert, pass/fail helpers, async main()) established by tests/cli-import-ontology.test.ts. AC1-AC2 verify sha256Hex format and reference correctness against createHash. AC3 verifies Uint8Array input parity. AC4-AC5 verify sha256HexAsync matches the synchronous reference (both string and Uint8Array inputs). AC6 verifies the known empty-string SHA-256 against both functions. sha256HexAsync is exercised in Node because globalThis.crypto.subtle is available in Node >= 19; Playwright tests (sub-task D) will verify the browser runtime independently.",
            "before": null,
            "after": "/**\n * SHA-256 Utilities Tests\n *\n * SPEC refs: \u00a75.6 ecm:contentHash format, NFR-003 determinism.\n *\n * Acceptance criteria:\n *   AC1: sha256Hex(string) returns a 64-char lowercase hex digest.\n *   AC2: sha256Hex(string) matches the createHash reference hash.\n *   AC3: sha256Hex(Uint8Array) returns the same digest as sha256Hex(string).\n *   AC4: sha256HexAsync(string) returns the same digest as sha256Hex(string).\n *   AC5: sha256HexAsync(Uint8Array) returns the same digest as sha256Hex(string).\n *   AC6: Both functions produce the known SHA-256 of the empty string.\n *\n * Note: sha256HexAsync uses globalThis.crypto.subtle, which is available in\n * Node >= 19. Playwright tests in sub-task D verify the browser runtime.\n *\n * Pattern: hand-rolled per tests/run-tests.ts; node:assert; async main();\n * process.exit(1) on failure. Follows tests/cli-import-ontology.test.ts.\n */\n\nimport { strictEqual, ok } from \"node:assert\";\nimport { createHash } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport { sha256Hex, sha256HexAsync } from \"../src/kernel/sha256.js\";\n\nlet passed = 0;\nlet failed = 0;\n\nfunction pass(msg: string): void {\n  console.log(`  \\u2713 PASS: ${msg}`);\n  passed++;\n}\nfunction fail(msg: string, err?: unknown): void {\n  console.error(`  \\u2717 FAIL: ${msg}`);\n  if (err !== undefined) {\n    console.error(\"  \", err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err));\n  }\n  failed++;\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Fixtures\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n/** Sample input used across all tests. */\nconst SAMPLE = \"Hello, SHA-256!\\n\";\n\n/** Same bytes via TextEncoder (browser path equivalent). */\nconst SAMPLE_BYTES = new TextEncoder().encode(SAMPLE);\n\n/**\n * Reference digest computed with node:crypto \u2014 ground truth for cross-checks.\n * Matches the pattern used in tests/import-turtle.test.ts AC4.\n */\nconst REFERENCE_HEX: string = createHash(\"sha256\")\n  .update(Buffer.from(SAMPLE, \"utf8\"))\n  .digest(\"hex\");\n\n/**\n * Known SHA-256 of the empty string (FIPS 180-4 / RFC 6234 test vector).\n */\nconst EMPTY_HEX =\n  \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\";\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Test functions\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n/** AC1 + AC2: sha256Hex(string) format and reference correctness. */\nasync function testSha256HexString(): Promise<void> {\n  try {\n    const result = sha256Hex(SAMPLE);\n    ok(\n      /^[0-9a-f]{64}$/.test(result),\n      `sha256Hex must return 64-char lowercase hex; got: ${result}`,\n    );\n    strictEqual(\n      result,\n      REFERENCE_HEX,\n      \"sha256Hex(string) must match createHash reference\",\n    );\n    pass(\"sha256Hex(string): 64-char lowercase hex matches reference (AC1, AC2)\");\n  } catch (e) {\n    fail(\"sha256Hex(string): format and reference correctness (AC1, AC2)\", e);\n  }\n}\n\n/** AC3: sha256Hex(Uint8Array) returns the same digest as sha256Hex(string). */\nasync function testSha256HexUint8Array(): Promise<void> {\n  try {\n    const result = sha256Hex(SAMPLE_BYTES);\n    strictEqual(\n      result,\n      REFERENCE_HEX,\n      \"sha256Hex(Uint8Array) must match sha256Hex(string)\",\n    );\n    pass(\"sha256Hex(Uint8Array): matches sha256Hex(string) (AC3)\");\n  } catch (e) {\n    fail(\"sha256Hex(Uint8Array): must match sha256Hex(string) (AC3)\", e);\n  }\n}\n\n/** AC4: sha256HexAsync(string) returns the same digest as sha256Hex(string). */\nasync function testSha256HexAsyncString(): Promise<void> {\n  try {\n    const result = await sha256HexAsync(SAMPLE);\n    strictEqual(\n      result,\n      REFERENCE_HEX,\n      \"sha256HexAsync(string) must match sha256Hex(string)\",\n    );\n    pass(\"sha256HexAsync(string): matches synchronous reference (AC4)\");\n  } catch (e) {\n    fail(\"sha256HexAsync(string): must match sha256Hex(string) (AC4)\", e);\n  }\n}\n\n/** AC5: sha256HexAsync(Uint8Array) returns the same digest as sha256Hex(string). */\nasync function testSha256HexAsyncUint8Array(): Promise<void> {\n  try {\n    const result = await sha256HexAsync(SAMPLE_BYTES);\n    strictEqual(\n      result,\n      REFERENCE_HEX,\n      \"sha256HexAsync(Uint8Array) must match sha256Hex(string)\",\n    );\n    pass(\"sha256HexAsync(Uint8Array): matches synchronous reference (AC5)\");\n  } catch (e) {\n    fail(\"sha256HexAsync(Uint8Array): must match sha256Hex(string) (AC5)\", e);\n  }\n}\n\n/** AC6: Both functions return the known SHA-256 of the empty string. */\nasync function testEmptyString(): Promise<void> {\n  try {\n    const syncResult = sha256Hex(\"\");\n    strictEqual(\n      syncResult,\n      EMPTY_HEX,\n      `sha256Hex(\"\") must equal the known empty-string SHA-256`,\n    );\n    const asyncResult = await sha256HexAsync(\"\");\n    strictEqual(\n      asyncResult,\n      EMPTY_HEX,\n      `sha256HexAsync(\"\") must equal the known empty-string SHA-256`,\n    );\n    pass(\"empty string: both functions return known SHA-256 of empty string (AC6)\");\n  } catch (e) {\n    fail(\"empty string: sha256Hex and sha256HexAsync must agree (AC6)\", e);\n  }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Main\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nasync function main(): Promise<void> {\n  console.log(\"\\nSHA-256 utilities (src/kernel/sha256.ts)\");\n\n  await testSha256HexString();\n  await testSha256HexUint8Array();\n  await testSha256HexAsyncString();\n  await testSha256HexAsyncUint8Array();\n  await testEmptyString();\n\n  console.log(`\\n  ${passed} passed, ${failed} failed`);\n  if (failed > 0) process.exit(1);\n}\n\nmain();\n",
            "scope": "minimal"
          }
        ],
        "tests_recommended": [
          {
            "file": "tests/sha256.test.ts",
            "describe": "Already included as C5. Run via npm test after npm run build:tests. Covers AC1-AC6 for both sha256Hex and sha256HexAsync."
          },
          {
            "file": "tests/import-turtle.test.ts",
            "describe": "Existing tests AC1-AC6 must continue passing without modification \u00e2\u20ac\u201d they exercise the synchronous (no-digestHexFn) path and verify ecm:contentHash format (AC4). No changes to this file."
          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "Vite bundler concern for sub-task B/C: src/kernel/sha256.ts has a top-level `import { createHash } from 'node:crypto'`. When browser UI code (src/ui/) imports sha256HexAsync from this module, Vite will attempt to bundle the node:crypto import and fail. Sub-task B must address this via one of: (a) vite.config.ts `build.rollupOptions.external: ['node:crypto']` + a runtime shim guard, (b) a separate src/kernel/sha256-browser.ts that re-exports only sha256HexAsync with no node:crypto import, or (c) a package.json `exports` / `browser` field pointing to the browser-safe variant. The architect should adjudicate before sub-task B begins.",
          "TypeScript compilation concern: globalThis.crypto.subtle.digest requires that @types/node@22 declares globalThis.crypto as Crypto with SubtleCrypto.digest. This is expected to hold for @types/node >= 19 but was not verified against the exact installed version. If `npm run build` fails on sha256.ts with 'Property subtle does not exist on type Crypto', the fix is to qualify the call as `(globalThis.crypto as { subtle: SubtleCrypto }).subtle.digest(...)` or import webcrypto from 'node:crypto'.",
          "Error message byte count: the existing SIZE_EXCEEDED message embeds sourceBytes.length (line 133). After C3, sourceBytes is a Uint8Array from TextEncoder; its .length equals Buffer.byteLength(turtleSource, 'utf8') for valid UTF-8 content, so the byte count in the error message remains accurate. This is confirmed by the ASCII-only AC5 fixture ('a'.repeat(51MB)), but a non-ASCII Turtle source with multi-byte chars would produce the same count in both paths. No action required unless a test for multibyte source content is desired."
        ],
        "summary": "Sub-task A delivers: (1) new src/kernel/sha256.ts exporting sha256Hex (sync, node:crypto) and sha256HexAsync (async, Web Crypto API \u00e2\u20ac\u201d no import, global in Node >= 19 and all modern browsers); (2) non-breaking refactor of importOntology in src/import/turtle-import.ts \u00e2\u20ac\u201d TypeScript overloads preserve the existing synchronous signature for the six existing call sites, an optional fifth parameter digestHexFn activates the async browser path, and Buffer.from() is replaced with TextEncoder.encode() for sourceBytes (same bytes for valid UTF-8, compatible with createHash.update() in the sync path); (3) new tests/sha256.test.ts with six acceptance criteria covering both exports. All existing import-turtle.test.ts AC1-AC6 pass unchanged through the sync path.",
        "self_assessment": "confident"
      },
