            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "TypeScript-overload-based sync/async dual contract for runtime-agnostic kernel modules: declare the prior synchronous signature as overload #1, the async (Promise-returning) signature as overload #2, and an implementation signature with an optional dependency-injected function. Call sites that don't supply the function receive the original synchronous return type; call sites that do receive Promise<T>. This preserves an established N-call-site contract without forking the file or duplicating the parse logic, and the optional-parameter dependency injection keeps the kernel testable in both runtimes via a single import path. Applicable wherever a Node-only kernel utility needs to grow a browser-safe seam (digesting, randomness, time)."
