            "content": "When a sub-task within a multi-sub-task chain has a downstream-scoped concern that the current sub-task cannot resolve in isolation (e.g., Vite bundler config for a kernel module that the next sub-task's UI code will import), the developer agent should surface the concern in open_questions with explicit alternatives, NOT silently leave the seam for the next sub-task to discover during applier failure. The Chain 4 sub-task A developer flagged the Vite bundling concern with three named adjudication paths (rollupOptions.external + shim, parallel sha256-browser.ts, package.json browser-field), letting the architect rule on the seam before sub-task B begins. This pattern prevents cascade rebuilds at the sub-task boundary."
