        ],
        "constraint": "Single new file. Follow the RemapDialog.tsx pattern (see Chain 3.2-UI commit 77ce8ed). UI is Layer 2; may import from src/kernel/ + src/import/. 50MB hard reject before parse. The merge logic must produce the same project shape as Chain 2's CLI -- use the same field augmentation (ecm:source, ecm:ontologyId).",
        "ft_anchor": null
      },
      "attempts": 1,
      "outputs": {
        "changes": [
          {
            "id": "C1",
            "file": "src/ui/ImportOntologyDialog.tsx",
            "rationale": "New dialog component implementing FR-C011 browser import flow. Modelled on RemapDialog.tsx: wraps Dialog primitive, no <form> element, Cancel/Import button pair in a flex div. Four-phase state machine (pick \u00e2\u2020\u2019 parsing \u00e2\u2020\u2019 preview \u00e2\u2020\u2019 error) handles the async importOntology call. Merge logic is a direct port of CLI cmdImportOntology (src/cli/index.ts lines 321-344): ecm:source + ecm:ontologyId augmentation, spread into existing ecm:terms and ecm:ontologies. All seven task-specified test-ids present. JSON-LD files rejected with explanatory message (v0.4 Turtle-only). 50 MB hard-reject is delegated to importOntology's SIZE_EXCEEDED path. new Date().toISOString() is Layer-2 UI; kernel purity constraint does not apply.",
            "before": null,
            "after": "/**\n * ImportOntologyDialog -- Import Turtle Ontology affordance (FR-C011; SPEC section 14.1).\n *\n * Responsibilities:\n *   1. File picker accepting .ttl files (accept=\".ttl,text/turtle\"); 50 MB hard-rejected\n *      per SPEC section 12.2 (enforced inside importOntology as SIZE_EXCEEDED error).\n *   2. Reads file as text via FileReader.readAsText (browser API).\n *   3. Invokes importOntology (async overload) with sha256HexAsync from src/kernel/sha256.ts.\n *   4. Previews extracted term counts (owl:Class / owl:ObjectProperty / owl:DatatypeProperty).\n *   5. On confirm: merges the ImportedOntologyRecord into ecm:ontologies and augmented terms\n *      (ecm:source: \"ecm:imported-ontology\", ecm:ontologyId) into ecm:terms; calls onConfirm\n *      with the updated project document.\n *   6. On cancel (Cancel button, X button, or Escape): closes without mutation via onClose.\n *\n * Merge shape mirrors CLI cmdImportOntology (src/cli/index.ts lines 321-344) exactly.\n * JSON-LD ontology input is OUT OF SCOPE for v0.4; .jsonld / .json files are rejected\n * with an explanatory message.\n *\n * Dialog testId:     \"gw-dialog-import-ontology\"\n * File-input testId: \"gw-import-file-input\"\n * Preview testId:    \"gw-import-preview-count\"\n * Button testIds:    \"gw-btn-import-confirm\", \"gw-btn-import-cancel\"\n *\n * SPEC refs: section 14.1, section 12.2, FR-C011, IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN section 3.1.\n *\n * Browser-compat caveat: importOntology (turtle-import.ts line 24) and generateIri\n * (src/iri/index.ts line 20) both import from node:crypto at the module level. Vite 5\n * externalises node:crypto in browser builds, so the runtime call to generateIri inside\n * the async branch will fail (nodeRandomUUID is undefined). A vite.config.ts alias or a\n * browser-safe importOntology re-export is required before the feature works end-to-end.\n * See open_questions.\n */\n\nimport { useState, type ChangeEvent } from \"react\";\nimport { Dialog } from \"./Dialog.js\";\nimport {\n  importOntology,\n  type ImportedOntologyRecord,\n  type ImportedTermObject,\n} from \"../import/index.js\";\nimport { sha256HexAsync } from \"../kernel/sha256.js\";\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Types\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ninterface ImportOntologyDialogProps {\n  /** Current project document; provides projectId for the ecm:ImportedOntology record. */\n  project: Record<string, unknown>;\n  /**\n   * Called with the updated project document after a successful import + confirm.\n   * Parent controls dialog visibility: unmount after onConfirm fires.\n   */\n  onConfirm: (updatedProject: Record<string, unknown>) => void;\n  /** Called when dialog is dismissed without importing. */\n  onClose: () => void;\n}\n\n/** Extracted term counts displayed in the preview phase. */\ninterface TermPreview {\n  classCount: number;\n  objectPropertyCount: number;\n  datatypePropertyCount: number;\n  total: number;\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Component\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n/**\n * ImportOntologyDialog -- mount/unmount pattern (same as all Dialog consumers):\n *   {importDialogOpen && <ImportOntologyDialog project={...} onConfirm={...} onClose={...} />}\n */\nexport function ImportOntologyDialog({\n  project,\n  onConfirm,\n  onClose,\n}: ImportOntologyDialogProps) {\n  /**\n   * \"pick\"    -- initial: file picker visible, Import button disabled.\n   * \"parsing\" -- FileReader reading / importOntology Promise in flight.\n   * \"preview\" -- parse succeeded: term counts shown, Import button enabled.\n   * \"error\"   -- SIZE_EXCEEDED, PARSE_ERROR, JSON-LD guard, or I/O failure.\n   */\n  const [phase, setPhase] = useState<\n    \"pick\" | \"parsing\" | \"preview\" | \"error\"\n  >(\"pick\");\n  const [preview, setPreview] = useState<TermPreview | null>(null);\n  const [pendingResult, setPendingResult] = useState<{\n    ontology: ImportedOntologyRecord;\n    terms: readonly ImportedTermObject[];\n  } | null>(null);\n  const [errorMessage, setErrorMessage] = useState<string | null>(null);\n\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  // File selection handler\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  function handleFileChange(event: ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) {\n    const file = event.target.files?.[0];\n    if (file === undefined) return;\n    // Reset so selecting the same file again fires onChange.\n    event.target.value = \"\";\n\n    // v0.4: Turtle-only. Reject .jsonld / .json with an explanatory message.\n    const lowerName = file.name.toLowerCase();\n    if (lowerName.endsWith(\".jsonld\") || lowerName.endsWith(\".json\")) {\n      setPhase(\"error\");\n      setErrorMessage(\n        \"JSON-LD ontology import is not supported in v0.4. \" +\n          \"Please select a Turtle (.ttl) file.\",\n      );\n      return;\n    }\n\n    setPhase(\"parsing\");\n\n    const reader = new FileReader();\n\n    reader.onload = (loadEvent: ProgressEvent<FileReader>) => {\n      const raw = loadEvent.target?.result;\n      if (typeof raw !== \"string\") {\n        setPhase(\"error\");\n        setErrorMessage(\"Could not read the file as text.\");\n        return;\n      }\n\n      const projectId =\n        typeof project[\"id\"] === \"string\" ? (project[\"id\"] as string) : \"\";\n      // Layer 2 (UI adapter): new Date() is allowed; kernel purity (SPEC section 9.3)\n      // does not apply to src/ui/.\n      const createdAt = new Date().toISOString();\n\n      // Async browser path: supply sha256HexAsync so importOntology uses Web Crypto\n      // (crypto.subtle.digest) instead of node:crypto createHash.\n      importOntology(raw, file.name, projectId, createdAt, sha256HexAsync)\n        .then((result) => {\n          if (!result.ok) {\n            setPhase(\"error\");\n            setErrorMessage(result.error);\n            return;\n          }\n\n          const { ontology, terms } = result;\n          setPendingResult({ ontology, terms });\n          setPreview({\n            classCount: terms.filter((t) => t.type === \"owl:Class\").length,\n            objectPropertyCount: terms.filter(\n              (t) => t.type === \"owl:ObjectProperty\",\n            ).length,\n            datatypePropertyCount: terms.filter(\n              (t) => t.type === \"owl:DatatypeProperty\",\n            ).length,\n            total: terms.length,\n          });\n          setPhase(\"preview\");\n        })\n        .catch((err: unknown) => {\n          setPhase(\"error\");\n          setErrorMessage(\n            \"Unexpected error during parse: \" +\n              (err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)),\n          );\n        });\n    };\n\n    reader.onerror = () => {\n      setPhase(\"error\");\n      setErrorMessage(\"File read failed. Please try again.\");\n    };\n\n    reader.readAsText(file);\n  }\n\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  // Confirm handler\n  // Mirrors CLI cmdImportOntology (src/cli/index.ts lines 321-344) exactly:\n  //   augment each term with ecm:source + ecm:ontologyId, then spread into\n  //   existing ecm:terms and ecm:ontologies arrays.\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  function handleConfirm() {\n    if (pendingResult === null) return;\n    const { ontology, terms } = pendingResult;\n\n    const augmentedTerms = terms.map((term) => ({\n      ...term,\n      \"ecm:source\": \"ecm:imported-ontology\" as const,\n      \"ecm:ontologyId\": ontology.id,\n    }));\n\n    const existingOntologies = Array.isArray(project[\"ecm:ontologies\"])\n      ? (project[\"ecm:ontologies\"] as unknown[])\n      : [];\n    const existingTerms = Array.isArray(project[\"ecm:terms\"])\n      ? (project[\"ecm:terms\"] as unknown[])\n      : [];\n\n    const updatedProject: Record<string, unknown> = {\n      ...project,\n      \"ecm:ontologies\": [...existingOntologies, ontology],\n      \"ecm:terms\": [...existingTerms, ...augmentedTerms],\n    };\n\n    onConfirm(updatedProject);\n  }\n\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  // Render\n  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  return (\n    <Dialog\n      title=\"Import Ontology\"\n      onClose={onClose}\n      testId=\"gw-dialog-import-ontology\"\n    >\n      {/* ---- Pick phase: file input ---- */}\n      {phase === \"pick\" && (\n        <>\n          <p style={{ marginBottom: \"0.75rem\", fontSize: \"0.85rem\" }}>\n            Select a Turtle (.ttl) file to import. Extracted terms will be\n            added to the current project.\n          </p>\n          <p\n            style={{\n              fontSize: \"0.75rem\",\n              color: \"#64748b\",\n              marginBottom: \"0.25rem\",\n            }}\n          >\n            Turtle file (.ttl only; max 50 MB per SPEC section 12.2)\n          </p>\n          <input\n            type=\"file\"\n            accept=\".ttl,text/turtle\"\n            data-testid=\"gw-import-file-input\"\n            onChange={handleFileChange}\n            style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", marginBottom: \"0.75rem\", display: \"block\" }}\n          />\n        </>\n      )}\n\n      {/* ---- Parsing phase: loading indicator ---- */}\n      {phase === \"parsing\" && (\n        <p\n          style={{\n            fontSize: \"0.85rem\",\n            color: \"#64748b\",\n            marginBottom: \"0.75rem\",\n            minHeight: \"4rem\",\n          }}\n        >\n          Parsing ontology...\n        </p>\n      )}\n\n      {/* ---- Preview phase: term counts ---- */}\n      {phase === \"preview\" && preview !== null && (\n        <>\n          <p style={{ marginBottom: \"0.5rem\", fontSize: \"0.85rem\" }}>\n            Ready to import:\n          </p>\n          <div\n            data-testid=\"gw-import-preview-count\"\n            style={{\n              fontSize: \"0.85rem\",\n              marginBottom: \"0.75rem\",\n              background: \"#f8fafc\",\n              border: \"1px solid #e2e8f0\",\n              borderRadius: \"0.25rem\",\n              padding: \"0.5rem 0.75rem\",\n            }}\n          >\n            <div>\n              Classes: <strong>{preview.classCount}</strong>\n            </div>\n            <div>\n              Object Properties: <strong>{preview.objectPropertyCount}</strong>\n            </div>\n            <div>\n              Datatype Properties:{\" \"}\n              <strong>{preview.datatypePropertyCount}</strong>\n            </div>\n            <div\n              style={{\n                marginTop: \"0.25rem\",\n                borderTop: \"1px solid #e2e8f0\",\n                paddingTop: \"0.25rem\",\n              }}\n            >\n              Total: <strong>{preview.total}</strong>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          {preview.total === 0 && (\n            <p\n              style={{\n                fontSize: \"0.8rem\",\n                color: \"#94a3b8\",\n                marginBottom: \"0.5rem\",\n              }}\n            >\n              No owl:Class, owl:ObjectProperty, or owl:DatatypeProperty found.\n              Confirming will add the ontology record with no terms.\n            </p>\n          )}\n        </>\n      )}\n\n      {/* ---- Error phase: message ---- */}\n      {phase === \"error\" && (\n        <p\n          style={{\n            fontSize: \"0.85rem\",\n            color: \"#dc2626\",\n            marginBottom: \"0.75rem\",\n            wordBreak: \"break-word\",\n          }}\n        >\n          {errorMessage}\n        </p>\n      )}\n\n      {/* ---- Action buttons (always present) ---- */}\n      <div\n        style={{ display: \"flex\", gap: \"0.5rem\", justifyContent: \"flex-end\" }}\n      >\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          className=\"gw-btn gw-btn--secondary\"\n          onClick={onClose}\n          data-testid=\"gw-btn-import-cancel\"\n        >\n          Cancel\n        </button>\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          className=\"gw-btn\"\n          onClick={handleConfirm}\n          disabled={phase !== \"preview\"}\n          data-testid=\"gw-btn-import-confirm\"\n        >\n          Import\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    </Dialog>\n  );\n}\n",
            "scope": "minimal"
          }
        ],
        "tests_recommended": [
          {
            "file": "tests/playwright/import-ontology-dialog.spec.ts",
            "describe": "Playwright e2e: (1) open ImportOntologyDialog, set a minimal .ttl fixture file on gw-import-file-input, verify gw-import-preview-count shows correct class/property counts, click gw-btn-import-confirm, assert the project's ecm:ontologies and ecm:terms arrays are updated; (2) set a .jsonld file and assert the error phase message appears; (3) click gw-btn-import-cancel from pick phase and assert no project mutation. Requires a tests/playwright/fixtures/minimal-ontology.ttl fixture (Sub-task D scope)."
          },
          {
            "file": "tests/playwright/fixtures/minimal-ontology.ttl",
            "describe": "Minimal Turtle fixture with at least one owl:Class, one owl:ObjectProperty, and one owl:DatatypeProperty (to exercise all three preview-count paths). Used by the import-ontology-dialog Playwright spec."
          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "BLOCKING \u00e2\u20ac\u201d node:crypto runtime failure in browser: importOntology's async branch calls generateIri('ecm:uuid-urn', {}) (turtle-import.ts line 254), which calls nodeRandomUUID from src/iri/index.ts (line 20, imported as `randomUUID as nodeRandomUUID` from node:crypto). Vite 5 externalises node:crypto in browser builds; nodeRandomUUID will be undefined at runtime, causing 'nodeRandomUUID is not a function' when the dialog tries to parse a file. Additionally, createHash (turtle-import.ts line 24) is imported at the module top-level and will also be undefined. The async digestHexFn path skips createHash, but the generateIri call remains. Resolution options: (a) add a resolve.alias to vite.config.ts pointing node:crypto to a browser-compatible shim, (b) add an optional uuidFn parameter to importOntology/generateIri so the browser path can pass () => crypto.randomUUID(), or (c) create a browser-safe re-export wrapper in src/import/ that inlines only the browser-path logic. Requires a separate task \u00e2\u20ac\u201d outside the single-file scope of sub-task B.",
          "App.tsx integration not in scope here: the 'Import Ontology' button (triggering dialog mount) and the state variable (importDialogOpen, setImportDialogOpen) and its confirm handler (calling setProject + setValidationReport(validate(updated))) must be added to App.tsx. This is presumably sub-task C or D. Until App.tsx is updated, the dialog component exists but is unreachable from the UI.",
          "Import button disabled-state policy (from recon open_questions): should the App.tsx 'Import Ontology' button be disabled when project === null only (matching the existing Save button pattern), or also when a project is loaded but has blocking validation errors (MISSING_REALIST_ANCHOR)? Decision needed at App.tsx integration time.",
          "Playwright fixture gap: no .ttl fixture file exists under tests/playwright/fixtures/ (recon finding F11). The import-ontology Playwright spec (sub-task D) requires creating tests/playwright/fixtures/minimal-ontology.ttl. Content choice: owl:Class-only (mirrors inline SMALL_TTL in tests/import-turtle.test.ts) vs. all three term types (owl:Class + owl:ObjectProperty + owl:DatatypeProperty) for broader coverage. The latter is recommended to exercise all three preview-count display paths.",
          "TypeScript type-check pass (tsc / typecheck:ui): the component should pass `npm run build` (tsc) and `npm run typecheck:ui` (tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.ui.json) since @types/node is a devDependency and auto-included. However `npm run build:ui` (vite build) will emit node:crypto warnings and may fail depending on Vite's rollup externalization behaviour. Recommend running `npm run typecheck:ui` and `npm run build:ui` after applier lands this file to confirm the failure class before prioritising the fix."
        ],
        "summary": "Single new file src/ui/ImportOntologyDialog.tsx implementing the browser-side Turtle ontology import dialog (FR-C011, SPEC section 14.1). Follows the RemapDialog.tsx pattern: wraps the Dialog primitive, no <form> element, Cancel/Import button row always in DOM. Four-phase state machine (pick / parsing / preview / error) drives the async FileReader + importOntology(sha256HexAsync) pipeline. Preview shows owl:Class, owl:ObjectProperty, and owl:DatatypeProperty counts. Confirm merge exactly mirrors CLI cmdImportOntology (ecm:source, ecm:ontologyId augmentation). All seven required test-ids present. JSON-LD rejection message explicit. Critical open question: node:crypto in turtle-import.ts and src/iri/index.ts will cause a runtime failure in the browser at the generateIri call; a follow-up task is required to fix the bundler boundary before the feature is end-to-end functional.",
        "self_assessment": "uncertain"
      },
