            "content": "v3.5.3 substrate-discipline closure: classifier predicates must mirror daemon dispatch predicates. Aaron 2026-06-02 caught the gap on Phase 3 Chain 4 sub-task B: architect 813 denied; applier 814 correctly blocked by Event 11 gating; but fnsr.status.md reported 'working' with '1 dispatchable' because _dispatchable_counts only checked deps=done, not the architect-ruling gate. Substrate was doing the right thing; classifier was lying. Pattern: every daemon-side refuse-to-dispatch branch needs a matching classifier-side state. Currently covered: awaiting_operator_decision (v3.4.0), demo-released phase state (v3.4.0), chain-complete (v3.5.2), ratification-denied (v3.5.3). Remaining forward-track candidates: chain-validator-vetoed proposals (would fire if append-tasks --verify-first found defects); CPS-vetoed structured-error tasks; fixer-recursion-bound-exhausted tasks. Pattern is recurring; consider a v3.6 unified 'classifier-daemon predicate parity' refactor.",
