        "rationale": "All five verification points from the task purpose are satisfied: (1) Import button placement and test-id \u00e2\u20ac\u201d C3 inserts the new <button> in gw-btn-group between gw-btn-open and gw-btn-save with data-testid='gw-btn-import-ontology', a clean nominal extension consistent with the five-button group documented in recon F7. (2) Disabled state matches Save/Project-Settings \u00e2\u20ac\u201d C3 uses `disabled={project === null}` verbatim, identical to gw-btn-save / gw-btn-save-turtle / gw-btn-project-settings per F7; the answered open question about coupling to blocking validation errors was deliberately decided in favor of matching the Save baseline (no scope creep). (3) Merge handler is a pure state update \u00e2\u20ac\u201d C4's onConfirm body is exactly `setProject(updatedProject); setValidationReport(validate(updatedProject)); setImportOntologyDialogOpen(false);` with no I/O or side effects beyond setState, and the setProject+setValidationReport(validate(...)) pairing precisely matches the invariant established in F16. The actual merge (CLI-equivalent per F9) is delegated to the dialog component, which is correct separation of concerns for this sub-task's App.tsx-wiring scope. (4) Existing button order and test-ids unchanged \u00e2\u20ac\u201d gw-btn-new, gw-btn-open, gw-btn-save, gw-btn-save-turtle, gw-btn-project-settings are all preserved with identical attributes; only one new button is inserted. (5) Dialog state hook follows existing pattern \u00e2\u20ac\u201d C2's `const [importOntologyDialogOpen, setImportOntologyDialogOpen] = useState(false);` is a parallel-construction copy of the adjacent newProjectDialogOpen declaration, and C4's conditional mount `{importOntologyDialogOpen && project !== null && (...)}` mirrors the projectSettingsOpen block exactly. The before-snippet anchors in all four changes are unambiguous and well-bounded for applier consumption. Substantive-change reconnaissance contract satisfied: 808-recon-p3-