        "rationale": "The proposal satisfies the three purpose-stated verification criteria. (1) End-to-end coverage: the AC1-5 test exercises the full path \u00e2\u20ac\u201d load minimal-v0.3.jsonld via gw-file-input, click gw-btn-import-ontology, attach sample-ontology.ttl via gw-import-file-input, assert gw-import-preview-count text, click gw-btn-import-confirm, assert dialog dismissal, and verify sidebar state across all three term sections (Classes / Object Properties / Datatype Properties). This walks the user-visible flow from button-click to merged-project rendering. (2) Fixture validity: sample-ontology.ttl declares owl/rdfs/xsd prefixes correctly, contains exactly 5 importable terms (Animal/Dog/Cat as owl:Class with rdfs:label + rdfs:subClassOf, hasPet as owl:ObjectProperty, petName as owl:DatatypeProperty with rdfs:range xsd:string), and matches the inline SMALL_TTL pattern that recon F11 cites as the existing convention. The 5-term count is consistent with the 'gw-import-preview-count' assertion of '5 terms ready to import.' (3) Dual assertion of dialog behavior + sidebar state: dialog visibility transitions are explicitly checked (visible after click, not-visible after confirm), and post-import sidebar state is verified per-section with aria-disabled='true' confirming the FR-U010 / SPEC \u00c2\u00a713.3 imported-read-only treatment (matching the existing imported-term-read-only.spec.ts pattern per recon F12). AC6 round-trip adds a complementary save-and-reparse path that verifies ecm:source='ecm:imported-ontology' on all five terms and ecm:ontologies populated with ecm:format='text/turtle' \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this exercises the persistence-layer contract that IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN \u00c2\u00a73.1 AC6 names. Reconnaissance task 808 is present in UPSTREAM, satisfying Spec 03's reconnaissance requirement for substantive changes. Per CLAUDE.md \u00c2\u00a77.8, this is a code artifact, so verification-ritual is not required in the chain; test-runner (Playwright) is the appropriate downstream verification gate. The developer's three open questions are correctly self-classified as no-action-needed: createdAt non-determinism is not asserted, rdfs:range is not asserted, and aria-disabled='true' provides disambiguation against any same-labeled starter terms. No conflict with frozen contracts; the testIds named in the spec match those produced by the prior sub-task chain.",
