        "open_questions": [
          "turtle-import.ts is NOT listed in files_in_scope but is the only call site that needs uuidFn threading (recon F1/evidence turtle-import.ts:254). Changes C2 and C3 are included because the sub-task description explicitly requires threading through call sites; operator should confirm they are authorized before apply.",
          "The node:crypto import at src/iri/index.ts:20 (`import { createHash, randomUUID as nodeRandomUUID } from 'node:crypto'`) remains a module-level static import. Adding uuidFn injection prevents nodeRandomUUID from being *called* at runtime on the browser path, but Vite still externalizes the entire node:crypto import at bundle time. If the browser build fails to load src/iri/index.ts as a module (import-time error), this sub-task alone is insufficient and a follow-up is needed to make the node:crypto imports lazy (e.g., dynamic import inside generateUuidV4) or to restructure src/iri/ into separate browser/node entry points. Sub-task A2's value is establishing the injection contract; the module-level import problem may require a separate structural task.",
          "Should the JSDoc at turtle-import.ts lines 111-121 (the importOntology block comment) be updated to document the new uuidFn parameter? Sub-task A did not update it for digestHexFn; this proposal follows the same pattern and omits the JSDoc update for minimality.",
          "Should the file-level comment at turtle-import.ts lines 17-20 (which mentions digestHexFn) be updated to also mention uuidFn? Omitted here for minimality; operator can request as a follow-up editorial correction."
