      "inputs": {
        "phase": "phase-3",
        "chain_label": "Phase 3 Chain 4 sub-task B v2 -- ImportOntologyDialog with R1 + R2 fixes",
        "purpose": "Sub-task B v2 (re-do after architect 813 denial). Replaces the file at src/ui/ImportOntologyDialog.tsx that sub-task B's original dev produced. Two architect-identified fixes are MANDATORY: (R1) Add a 50MB byte-length pre-check IMMEDIATELY before reader.readAsText(file) in handleFileChange. Concretely: between the .jsonld-extension guard and reader.readAsText, insert `if (file.size > 50 * 1024 * 1024) { setPhase('error'); setErrorMessage('File exceeds 50 MB limit (SPEC section 12.2). Reject before parsing.'); return; }`. This makes the architectural intent (cheap pre-check before loading multi-GB files into the renderer) explicit. (R2) Thread the uuidFn from sub-task A2 into the importOntology call. Concretely: when invoking importOntology, pass both digestHexFn=sha256HexAsync AND uuidFn=() => crypto.randomUUID(). The dialog must compile cleanly and run end-to-end in the browser without throwing on crypto.randomUUID or node:crypto module access. All other criteria from the original sub-task B remain unchanged (RemapDialog structural pattern; merge shape matching CLI cmdImportOntology; .jsonld rejection; gw-* test-ids; Cancel/Apply layout). The original 812-dev-p3-c4-B output is in audit history as the v1 baseline; this v2 produces a NEW changes[] entry that REPLACES src/ui/ImportOntologyDialog.tsx (mode=create OR mode=replace per applier semantics).",
        "files_in_scope": [
          "src/ui/ImportOntologyDialog.tsx (replace; v1 was authored by 812-dev-p3-c4-B but denied at 813-rat-p3-c4-B)"
        ],
        "spec_refs": [
          "SPEC section 14.1",
          "SPEC section 12.2",
          "FR-C011",
          "IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN section 3.1"
        ],
        "constraint": "Single new file (replacing 812's output). R1 + R2 fixes are MANDATORY per architect 813 denial. Follow the RemapDialog.tsx pattern; preserve all five gw-* test-ids from v1 (gw-dialog-import-ontology, gw-import-file-input, gw-import-preview-count, gw-btn-import-cancel, gw-btn-import-confirm). Threading uuidFn=() => crypto.randomUUID() requires A2 (824-apply-p3-c4-A2) to have landed.",
        "remediation_for": "813-rat-p3-c4-B denial R1 + R2",
        "prior_developer_output": "urn:fnsr:task:812-dev-p3-c4-B"
      },
      "attempts": 1,
      "outputs": {
        "changes": [
          {
            "id": "C1",
            "file": "src/ui/ImportOntologyDialog.tsx",
            "rationale": "New file. Replaces the denied 812-dev-p3-c4-B v1 output. Applies both architect-mandatory fixes: R1 (file.size > 50 MB pre-check via file.size BEFORE reader.readAsText, setting error phase with the exact message from the task spec) and R2 (importOntology called with digestHexFn=sha256HexAsync and uuidFn=() => crypto.randomUUID(), so the async browser path uses only injected crypto functions and never calls node:crypto createHash or nodeRandomUUID at runtime). sha256HexAsync is inlined (globalThis.crypto.subtle) rather than imported from src/kernel/sha256.ts to minimise the node:crypto import chain pulled into the Vite browser bundle. Merge shape matches CLI cmdImportOntology (src/cli/index.ts:324-344, F9 evidence): terms augmented with ecm:source + ecm:ontologyId, spread into existing ecm:terms and ecm:ontologies. All five gw-* test-ids preserved. RemapDialog structural pattern followed (Dialog primitive, inline styles, flex Cancel/Import footer).",
            "before": null,
            "after": "/**\n * ImportOntologyDialog -- Import Turtle ontology file (FR-C011; SPEC section 14.1).\n *\n * Presents a file picker for .ttl files, pre-checks file size (SPEC section 12.2),\n * parses with importOntology (async browser path; digestHexFn + uuidFn injected),\n * shows a term-count preview, and on confirm merges ecm:terms + ecm:ontologies\n * per the CLI cmdImportOntology reference (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN section 3.1).\n *\n * Browser-safe:\n *   - sha256HexAsync: inlined Web Crypto (globalThis.crypto.subtle.digest).\n *   - uuidFn: () => crypto.randomUUID() (Web Crypto API; lib:DOM typed).\n * node:crypto is NOT invoked at runtime -- importOntology async path uses only\n * the injected digest and uuid functions (R2 fix per architect 813 denial).\n *\n * SPEC refs: section 14.1, section 12.2, FR-C011, IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN section 3.1.\n * Dialog testId: \"gw-dialog-import-ontology\".\n */\n\nimport { useState, useRef, type ChangeEvent } from \"react\";\nimport { Dialog } from \"./Dialog.js\";\nimport {\n  importOntology,\n  type ImportedOntologyRecord,\n  type ImportedTermObject,\n} from \"../import/turtle-import.js\";\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Browser-safe SHA-256 (Web Crypto API; no node:crypto dependency)\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n/**\n * Compute a SHA-256 hex digest using globalThis.crypto.subtle.\n * Available in all modern browsers and Node >= 19.\n * Inlined here (rather than imported from src/kernel/sha256.ts) so that the\n * browser bundle does not pull in sha256.ts's top-level node:crypto import.\n */\nasync function sha256HexAsync(bytes: Uint8Array): Promise<string> {\n  const buffer = await globalThis.crypto.subtle.digest(\"SHA-256\", bytes);\n  return Array.from(new Uint8Array(buffer))\n    .map((b) => b.toString(16).padStart(2, \"0\"))\n    .join(\"\");\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Types\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ntype DialogPhase = \"idle\" | \"reading\" | \"preview\" | \"error\";\n\ninterface PendingImport {\n  ontology: ImportedOntologyRecord;\n  terms: readonly ImportedTermObject[];\n  fileName: string;\n}\n\ninterface ImportOntologyDialogProps {\n  /** Current project document; provides the ecm:projectId for the import record. */\n  project: Record<string, unknown>;\n  /**\n   * Called with the merged project document after import is confirmed.\n   * Parent controls visibility: unmount the dialog after onConfirm fires.\n   */\n  onConfirm: (updatedProject: Record<string, unknown>) => void;\n  onClose: () => void;\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Component\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nexport function ImportOntologyDialog({\n  project,\n  onConfirm,\n  onClose,\n}: ImportOntologyDialogProps) {\n  const [phase, setPhase] = useState<DialogPhase>(\"idle\");\n  const [errorMessage, setErrorMessage] = useState<string>(\"\");\n  const [pending, setPending] = useState<PendingImport | null>(null);\n\n  const fileInputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);\n\n  const termCount = pending?.terms.length ?? 0;\n\n  function handleBrowse() {\n    fileInputRef.current?.click();\n  }\n\n  async function handleFileChange(event: ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) {\n    const file = event.target.files?.[0];\n    if (file === undefined) return;\n    // Reset so the same file can be re-selected after an error.\n    event.target.value = \"\";\n\n    // Reject non-.ttl files (SPEC section 14.1: Turtle format only).\n    if (!file.name.toLowerCase().endsWith(\".ttl\")) {\n      setPhase(\"error\");\n      setErrorMessage(\n        \"Only .ttl (Turtle) files are supported (SPEC section 14.1).\",\n      );\n      return;\n    }\n\n    // R1: 50 MB byte-length pre-check BEFORE reader.readAsText (SPEC section 12.2).\n    // Uses file.size (cheap; no I/O) to reject oversized files before loading\n    // multi-gigabyte content into the renderer's memory.\n    if (file.size > 50 * 1024 * 1024) {\n      setPhase(\"error\");\n      setErrorMessage(\n        \"File exceeds 50 MB limit (SPEC section 12.2). Reject before parsing.\",\n      );\n      return;\n    }\n\n    setPhase(\"reading\");\n    setPending(null);\n\n    const reader = new FileReader();\n    reader.onload = async (loadEvent: ProgressEvent<FileReader>) => {\n      const raw = loadEvent.target?.result;\n      if (typeof raw !== \"string\") {\n        setPhase(\"error\");\n        setErrorMessage(\"Failed to read file content.\");\n        return;\n      }\n\n      const projectId =\n        typeof project[\"id\"] === \"string\" ? (project[\"id\"] as string) : \"\";\n      const createdAt = new Date().toISOString();\n\n      // R2: Thread digestHexFn (sha256HexAsync) AND uuidFn (() => crypto.randomUUID())\n      // into importOntology. Async browser path; createHash / nodeRandomUUID from\n      // node:crypto are never called at runtime (SPEC section 12.2, section 14.1).\n      const result = await importOntology(\n        raw,\n        file.name,\n        projectId,\n        createdAt,\n        sha256HexAsync,\n        () => crypto.randomUUID(),\n      );\n\n      if (!result.ok) {\n        setPhase(\"error\");\n        setErrorMessage(result.error);\n        return;\n      }\n\n      setPending({\n        ontology: result.ontology,\n        terms: result.terms,\n        fileName: file.name,\n      });\n      setPhase(\"preview\");\n    };\n\n    reader.onerror = () => {\n      setPhase(\"error\");\n      setErrorMessage(\"File read failed. Please try again.\");\n    };\n\n    reader.readAsText(file);\n  }\n\n  function handleConfirm() {\n    if (pending === null) return;\n\n    // Merge per CLI cmdImportOntology reference (src/cli/index.ts:324-344; F9 evidence).\n    // Augment each extracted term with ecm:source + ecm:ontologyId before appending.\n    const augmented = pending.terms.map((t) => ({\n      ...t,\n      \"ecm:source\": \"ecm:imported-ontology\" as const,\n      \"ecm:ontologyId\": pending.ontology.id,\n    }));\n    const existingOntologies = Array.isArray(project[\"ecm:ontologies\"])\n      ? (project[\"ecm:ontologies\"] as unknown[])\n      : [];\n    const existingTerms = Array.isArray(project[\"ecm:terms\"])\n      ? (project[\"ecm:terms\"] as unknown[])\n      : [];\n    const updatedProject: Record<string, unknown> = {\n      ...project,\n      \"ecm:ontologies\": [...existingOntologies, pending.ontology],\n      \"ecm:terms\": [...existingTerms, ...augmented],\n    };\n\n    onConfirm(updatedProject);\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <Dialog\n      title=\"Import Ontology\"\n      onClose={onClose}\n      testId=\"gw-dialog-import-ontology\"\n    >\n      {/* Hidden file input: .ttl only (SPEC section 14.1). */}\n      <input\n        ref={fileInputRef}\n        type=\"file\"\n        accept=\".ttl\"\n        style={{ display: \"none\" }}\n        data-testid=\"gw-import-file-input\"\n        onChange={handleFileChange}\n      />\n\n      {/* Idle / reading: browse prompt */}\n      {(phase === \"idle\" || phase === \"reading\") && (\n        <>\n          <p style={{ marginBottom: \"0.75rem\", fontSize: \"0.85rem\" }}>\n            Select a Turtle (.ttl) ontology file. Extracted terms will be\n            merged into the current project.\n          </p>\n          <button\n            type=\"button\"\n            className=\"gw-btn gw-btn--secondary\"\n            onClick={handleBrowse}\n            disabled={phase === \"reading\"}\n            style={{ marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}\n          >\n            {phase === \"reading\" ? \"Reading\\u2026\" : \"Browse\\u2026\"}\n          </button>\n        </>\n      )}\n\n      {/* Preview: term count and re-select affordance */}\n      {phase === \"preview\" && pending !== null && (\n        <>\n          <p style={{ marginBottom: \"0.5rem\", fontSize: \"0.85rem\" }}>\n            File: <strong>{pending.fileName}</strong>\n          </p>\n          <p\n            data-testid=\"gw-import-preview-count\"\n            style={{ marginBottom: \"0.75rem\", fontSize: \"0.85rem\" }}\n          >\n            {termCount === 0\n              ? \"No importable terms found (owl:Class, owl:ObjectProperty, owl:DatatypeProperty).\"\n              : `${termCount} term${termCount === 1 ? \"\" : \"s\"} ready to import.`}\n          </p>\n          <button\n            type=\"button\"\n            className=\"gw-btn gw-btn--secondary\"\n            onClick={() => {\n              setPhase(\"idle\");\n              setPending(null);\n            }}\n            style={{ marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}\n          >\n            Choose a different file\n          </button>\n        </>\n      )}\n\n      {/* Error: message and retry affordance */}\n      {phase === \"error\" && (\n        <>\n          <p\n            style={{\n              marginBottom: \"0.75rem\",\n              fontSize: \"0.85rem\",\n              color: \"#dc2626\",\n            }}\n          >\n            {errorMessage}\n          </p>\n          <button\n            type=\"button\"\n            className=\"gw-btn gw-btn--secondary\"\n            onClick={() => {\n              setPhase(\"idle\");\n              setErrorMessage(\"\");\n            }}\n            style={{ marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}\n          >\n            Try again\n          </button>\n        </>\n      )}\n\n      {/* Cancel / Import button row (RemapDialog layout pattern) */}\n      <div style={{ display: \"flex\", gap: \"0.5rem\", justifyContent: \"flex-end\" }}>\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          className=\"gw-btn gw-btn--secondary\"\n          onClick={onClose}\n          data-testid=\"gw-btn-import-cancel\"\n        >\n          Cancel\n        </button>\n        <button\n          type=\"button\"\n          className=\"gw-btn\"\n          onClick={handleConfirm}\n          disabled={phase !== \"preview\" || termCount === 0}\n          data-testid=\"gw-btn-import-confirm\"\n        >\n          Import\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    </Dialog>\n  );\n}\n",
            "scope": "minimal"
          }
        ],
        "tests_recommended": [
          {
            "file": "tests/playwright/import-ontology.spec.ts",
            "describe": "Playwright E2E: (a) open a project, trigger Import Ontology dialog (gw-dialog-import-ontology visible), set a .ttl fixture on gw-import-file-input, wait for gw-import-preview-count to contain 'ready to import', click gw-btn-import-confirm, verify TermSidebar shows the imported term with the 'imported' badge. (b) Set a file >50 MB (mock via File constructor with a large size property if Playwright supports it) and verify the error message contains 'exceeds 50 MB limit'. (c) Set a .jsonld file and verify the error message contains '.ttl'. (d) gw-btn-import-cancel dismisses without mutating project state."
          },
          {
            "file": "tests/playwright/fixtures/minimal-ontology.ttl",
            "describe": "Minimal .ttl fixture for the import Playwright test: one owl:Class with rdfs:label 'TestClass'. Mirrors the inline SMALL_TTL constant from tests/import-turtle.test.ts but stored as a fixture file for Playwright's setInputFiles() API."
          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "Vite bundler / node:crypto chain: turtle-import.ts imports createHash from node:crypto and generateIri from src/iri/index.ts which also imports nodeRandomUUID from node:crypto at module level. The dialog imports importOntology from turtle-import.js, pulling that chain into the Vite browser bundle. Vite 4/5 stubs unresolvable node: built-ins rather than failing the build, and the async path (digestHexFn provided) never calls createHash or nodeRandomUUID at runtime, so the runtime behaviour should be correct. However, if the project's Vite version emits a build error (not a warning) for unresolved node: imports, vite.config.ts will need build.rollupOptions.external for node:crypto \u00e2\u20ac\u201d which is outside this file's scope. Recommend confirming with npm run build after apply.",
          "App.tsx wiring not in scope for this task: the dialog must be mounted from App.tsx (state for importOntologyOpen, an Import Ontology button in the header, and a handler that calls setProject + setValidationReport after onConfirm). That wiring is a separate sub-task (sub-task C per the chain description). This proposal delivers only the dialog component.",
          "createdAt sourcing: the dialog calls new Date().toISOString() to produce the ecm:createdAt timestamp for the ImportedOntology record. This is intentional (UI layer; not kernel), matching the pattern of other UI-layer mutation sites. If the SPEC or a future ADR requires ecm:createdAt to be threaded from outside (e.g. a clock prop), the dialog signature would need to accept a clockFn prop \u00e2\u20ac\u201d surfacing as an open question for architect review."
        ],
