        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The change extends the import engine's behavior (new extraction case in the rdf:type switch), widens an exported type union (ImportedTermType), and adds a new acceptance test \u00e2\u20ac\u201d all behavioral / contract changes that exceed the editorial-correction scope (typo / formatting / terminology-tightening / citation-format-update).",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance evidence is present in UPSTREAM (urn:fnsr:task:832-recon-p3-c4.1 with agent=reconnaissance, 15 findings grounded in file:line citations across 10 evidence paths), so the Spec 03 substantive-change reconnaissance requirement is satisfied. The seven proposed changes in urn:fnsr:task:833-dev-p3-c4.1 are evaluated against the eight task requirements: (1) C1 adds OWL_ANNOTATION_PROP constant immediately after OWL_DATA_PROP, preserving the existing naming and ordering pattern \u00e2\u20ac\u201d \u00e2\u0153\u201c. (2) C3 adds an else-if branch for OWL_ANNOTATION_PROP in the rdf:type switch with the `!termTypes.has(subj)` guard, exactly mirroring OWL_OBJECT_PROP and OWL_DATA_PROP \u00e2\u20ac\u201d same 'first wins' semantic \u00e2\u20ac\u201d \u00e2\u0153\u201c. (3) owl:Class precedence is preserved structurally: the owl:Class / rdfs:Class branch sets termTypes UNCONDITIONALLY (no guard), so any prior AnnotationProperty assignment is overwritten when a Class triple is encountered; conversely, the new AnnotationProperty branch's guard prevents it from overwriting a prior Class assignment. Class wins regardless of triple order \u00e2\u20ac\u201d \u00e2\u0153\u201c. (4) C2 extends ImportedTermType to include 'owl:AnnotationProperty' as the fourth member; per recon F13, ImportedTermObject.type is the only type-system constraint that propagates downstream, and consumers (ImportOntologyDialog, cli/index.ts) spread rather than re-type \u00e2\u20ac\u201d no further type-system change needed \u00e2\u20ac\u201d \u00e2\u0153\u201c. (5) C6+C7 add a hand-rolled ANNOTATION_PROP_TTL fixture and an AC7 test block following the established AC1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cAC6 inline-fixture pattern (recon F11, F12); the test asserts both type='owl:AnnotationProperty' and id='http://example.org/note' \u00e2\u20ac\u201d \u00e2\u0153\u201c. (6) C4 updates the module-level JSDoc and C5 updates the test file JSDoc to declare AC7 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d \u00e2\u0153\u201c. (7) The changes touch only src/import/turtle-import.ts and tests/import-turtle.test.ts; neither file lives in src/kernel/, and the import layer's purity boundary (CLAUDE.md \u00c2\u00a79) is not crossed \u00e2\u20ac\u201d \u00e2\u0153\u201c. (8) The Object/Data/Class branches are untouched and the new branch is purely additive (else-if at the tail of the chain), so AC1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cAC6 cannot regress \u00e2\u20ac\u201d \u00e2\u0153\u201c. Two upstream open questions are handled correctly: (a) SPEC \u00c2\u00a714.1 / IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN \u00c2\u00a73.1 doc misses (recon F8, F9) are FNSR_CANONICAL_DOCS paths and are deliberately scoped out of this two-file chain per the task INPUTS \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a follow-on editorial-correction chain is the right disposition; (b) the rdfs:label preservation question is not blocking \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the build loop unconditionally walks collected predicates regardless of term kind, and minimal AC7 scope is appropriate. One discipline observation: the developer flagged that the existing module-header JSDoc contains mojibake characters and that this is NOT a mojibake-repair task, so the before/after of C4 preserves them \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this is the correct disposition per CLAUDE.md \u00c2\u00a77.8 chain-shape-variation guidance (cleaning before+after uniformly would break the applier's before-match). Proceed to Pass 2b.",
