        "summary": "Phase 3 at build_ref=7475066 (anchor task urn:fnsr:task:841-test-p3-c4.1-tsfix) represents a focused gap-closure chain (Chain 4.1) on top of the previously documented Phase 3 surface. The prior five chains delivered the importOntology() engine (Chain 1; AC1-AC6), the real CLI import-ontology command discharging ADR-003 (Chain 2), the remapReferences() pure kernel function (Chain 3-A), the full imported-term immutability and Remap dialog browser UI (Chain 3.2-UI), and the browser-side ImportOntologyDialog with SHA-256/UUID injection shims (Chain 4). Chain 4.1 adds exactly one capability: owl:AnnotationProperty extraction in importOntology, filling a gap discovered when Aaron tested BFO (dc11:contributor, dc11:identifier) against the Chain 4 browser import and found those terms silently dropped. All downstream layers (TermSidebar, EcmTermType, SEMANTIC_TYPE_ALLOWLIST, SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7) already accepted owl:AnnotationProperty before Chain 4.1 landed; the gap was purely in the import engine. The fix is 7 changes across two files (src/import/turtle-import.ts: OWL_ANNOTATION_PROP constant, ImportedTermType union extension, rdf:type switch branch, module JSDoc; tests/import-turtle.test.ts: AC7 declaration, ANNOTATION_PROP_TTL fixture, AC7 test block). The full test gate is 160/160 tests across 22 files (exit_code=0). NOT in scope at this build: IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN \u00c2\u00a73.3 (LARGE_IMPORT/degraded-mode), \u00c2\u00a73.4 (term search/filter), SPEC \u00c2\u00a714.1 canonical-doc update for owl:AnnotationProperty, Phase 3 Exit Gate items 3/5/7/8/9/11, and forward-tracked ergonomic improvements ft-821-test-p3-c4-1 (sidebar max-height+search) and ft-821-test-p3-c4-2 (Inspector enriched metadata).",
