        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM (task 844-recon-demo-doc-phase-3) and satisfies the Spec 03 refusal contract for substantive changes. The demo-doc-author proposal (task 845) produces a single changes[] entry creating demo/PHASE-3-chain-4.1-annotation-property.md, matching the file path declared in the chain label and adhering to the demo/PHASE-N-{descriptor}.md convention per CLAUDE.md \u00c2\u00a77.14/\u00c2\u00a77.15. Stakeholder-review structure is complete and correctly ordered: H1 title, what-delivered narrative, acceptance-criteria table, how-to-verify, what-works-end-to-end, NOT-in-scope, sign-off prompt. Citations are grounded in the reconnaissance evidence \u00e2\u20ac\u201d SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.7, \u00c2\u00a713.3, \u00c2\u00a714.1, IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN \u00c2\u00a73.1/\u00c2\u00a73.3/\u00c2\u00a73.4, forward-tracks ft-821-test-p3-c4-1 and ft-821-test-p3-c4-2, build_ref 7475066, and the 160/160 test gate (anchor 841-test-p3-c4.1-tsfix) all resolve to recon findings F1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cF12. No ADR-NNN citations are invented; the doc cites no ADRs, consistent with the developer's self_assessment note that recon surfaced no Chain-4.1-specific ADR. Content is ASCII-only as required by the demo-doc-author contract; no mojibake risk in this path. The four recon open_questions are translated into the sign-off prompt (BFO regression validation, SPEC \u00c2\u00a714.1 trail acknowledgment, deferred forward-tracks acceptance, pass/revise/pivot verdict), correctly handing PO judgment back to Aaron. The doc properly characterizes Chain 4.1 as a gap-closure patch on Chain 4 rather than a new structurally-separate chain and links the prior Chain 4 demo doc as a companion read \u00e2\u20ac\u201d resolving recon open_question #1 toward 'sixth standalone doc with companion link', which is a reasonable authoring choice. The phase scope boundary is honored: SPEC \u00c2\u00a714.1 canonical-doc misalignment, Playwright AC for browser annotation-property