            "content": "The demo-doc-author agent's contract explicitly assigns substrate-self-validation narrative (mojibake-recovery sagas, brief-confirmation chain task IDs, applier failure modes) to the audit chain and NOT the consumer-audience demo doc. The Chain 4.1 demo doc includes a 'For the substrate-audit-curious' section narrating the 835\u00e2\u2020\u2019837\u00e2\u2020\u2019839\u00e2\u2020\u2019840\u00e2\u2020\u2019841 recovery arc. The section is clearly demarcated and the primary stakeholder-review structure is intact, so the consumer signal is not corrupted \u00e2\u20ac\u201d but the contract boundary was crossed. Worth observing whether this is a recurring pattern across demo-doc-author dispatches; if it is, the agent contract needs sharpening (e.g., explicit forbidden-content enumeration) or an automated check at the verification-ritual layer. Single-instance observation today; classification escalates if it recurs."
