        "summary": "Phase 3 Chain 5 targets three sub-tasks. Sub-task A (importer SKOS extensions): turtle-import.ts has a well-defined extension pattern \u00e2\u20ac\u201d five constants, five Maps, five capture branches, five build-loop assignments \u00e2\u20ac\u201d and adding skos:definition + skos:scopeNote requires adding two new constants (SKOS namespace http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#), two new Maps, two new capture branches, two new interface fields, and two new build-loop assignments. The key open question is whether skos fields should use the {text, lang} shape (like rdfs:label) or the plain string shape (like rdfs:comment); rdfs:comment's lang-tag asymmetry versus rdfs:label is the structural precedent to reason from. SPEC \u00c2\u00a714.1 does not currently list SKOS properties, making this a spec gap. Sub-task B (TermSidebar max-height + per-section search): TermSection accepts no search props and renders no search input; gw-term-list has no max-height/overflow-y CSS; the whole gw-sidebar has overflow-y:auto but no per-section constraint; IMPL PLAN \u00c2\u00a73.4 scopes a global search+scope-filter, not per-section \u00e2\u20ac\u201d per-section search is a new requirement from BFO feedback. The gw-term-section-* test-id pattern is established by four Playwright tests. Sub-task C (Inspector enriched metadata): the Inspector term mode has five rendered test-ids (label, IRI, type, comment, imported-badge) with data-testid conventions already established; termEntry is typed as Record<string,unknown> so new field reads require no interface change; only new extraction + conditional render blocks are needed for skos:definition and skos:scopeNote. No existing fixture carries SKOS fields; new fixture content will be required for both unit and Playwright tests.",
