        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposal adds new IRI constants, two new fields to a public exported interface (ImportedTermObject), two new Maps + capture branches in the importer iteration loop, two new conditional assignments in the build loop, and two new acceptance-criteria test sections \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this is new behavioral surface (importer now preserves skos:definition and skos:scopeNote), not editorial cleanup of existing semantics.",
        "rationale": "All seven task-stated requirements are met. (1) SKOS_DEFINITION and SKOS_SCOPE_NOTE constants in C2 use the canonical IRIs http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition and http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote \u00e2\u20ac\u201d verified against the SKOS namespace; placement after the RDFS constants block preserves the existing IRI-namespace grouping convention. (2) Preservation logic in C4/C5/C6 mirrors the rdfs:label pattern exactly \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Map declaration, Literal guard + first-occurrence guard + lang fallback to 'en' in capture, conditional assignment in build loop. The five-step extension pattern documented in reconnaissance F21 is followed step-for-step. (3) Language tag handling in C3/C4/C5 uses { text, lang } matching rdfs:label's shape, per the explicit task instruction to mirror rdfs:label not rdfs:comment. (4) C3's interface fields are declared `readonly \"skos:definition\"?: { readonly text: string; readonly lang: string }` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d optional + readonly at both outer and inner positions, matching the rdfs:label declaration precisely. (5) Unit tests T2/T3 cover the canonical single-language case for both SKOS predicates with explicit text and lang assertions; the proposal does not include an explicit multi-language assertion (e.g., two @lang tags for the same predicate verifying first-occurrence-wins), which is noted but does not block \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the first-occurrence guard semantics are tested indirectly via the pattern equivalence with rdfs:label and can be augmented in a follow-up. (6) Layer purity is preserved by construction \u00e2\u20ac\u201d changes are in src/import/, not src/kernel/; no Date.now / Math.random / DOM / I/O introduced; no new dependencies. (7) The mojibake preservation on line 9 of turtle-import.ts (untouched in both `before` and `after` of C1) follows the documented mojibake-recovery editorial-correction discipline (CLAUDE.md \u00c2\u00a77.8 chain-shape table) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d disk content is preserved byte-for-byte where not under change. The C1 edit narrowly updates only the RDFS-preservation list on lines 11-12. The SPEC \u00c2\u00a714.1 scope gap noted in reconnaissance F6 and the developer's open_question 1 is acknowledged: \u00c2\u00a714.1 enumerates rdfs:label / rdfs:comment / rdfs:subClassOf / rdfs:subPropertyOf only. The task explicitly proceeds under IMPL PLAN \u00c2\u00a73.1 authority; SPEC \u00c2\u00a714.1 amendment is a separate forward-trackable concern, not a blocker for this chain. The change pattern is the canonical importer-extension shape and is internally consistent. Proceed to Pass 2b (applier + test-runner).",
        "referenced_evidence": [
