        "open_questions": [
          "Search input placement: the task spec says 'above each section title', which this proposal implements literally (the <input> appears before the <div class=\"gw-term-section-header\"> in DOM order). If the intent was 'between the section title and the term list' (a more conventional placement), the only change needed is to move the <input> element to after the </div>. Please confirm the intended visual order.",
          "Max-height value: 12rem (~10 visible rows) was chosen as a small step above the existing gw-iri-list precedent of 10rem (recon F18). If a different value is preferred for the BFO/CCO use case (e.g., 16rem, 20rem, or a vh-relative value), this is a one-line CSS change.",
          "type='search' vs type='text': using type='search' gives a native browser \u00c3\u2014 clear button at no cost. If the team prefers to control the clear affordance explicitly (or avoid browser-native styling interference), change to type='text'. No logic change required.",
          "IMPL PLAN \u00c2\u00a73.4 open question (surfaced by recon F7): IMPL PLAN \u00c2\u00a73.4 scopes a global search + scope filter, not per-section search. This sub-task B introduces per-section search. Clarify whether \u00c2\u00a73.4 global search is still planned as a separate feature (additive) or whether per-section search replaces \u00c2\u00a73.4 global search. If additive, the \u00c2\u00a73.4 AC criteria (e.g., 'Typing person shows only terms...') may need updating to specify global vs per-section context."
        ],
