            "rationale": "Replace the existing comment fragment (loose <p> pair inside <></>) with three consistently-patterned <div data-testid> sections: definition, comment, scope-note. Each renders only when the field is present (no empty headers). skos:definition and skos:scopeNote show a lang badge since their shape is {text, lang}; rdfs:comment renders as plain text (plain-string shape, no lang preserved in importer). The comment test-id moves from the inner <p> to the outer <div> wrapper \u00e2\u20ac\u201d no existing Playwright or unit test asserts on gw-inspector-term-comment content per recon F13/F14. The three preserved test-ids from Chain 3.2-UI (gw-inspector-imported-term, gw-inspector-term-imported-badge, gw-btn-remap) are untouched.",
            "before": "          {termComment !== null && (\n            <>\n              <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n                Comment\n              </p>\n              <p\n                style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}\n                data-testid=\"gw-inspector-term-comment\"\n              >\n                {termComment}\n              </p>\n            </>\n          )}",
            "after": "          {termDefinition !== null && (\n            <div data-testid=\"gw-inspector-term-definition\" style={{ marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}>\n              <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n                Definition\n              </p>\n              <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n                {termDefinition.text}\n              </p>\n              {termDefinition.lang.length > 0 && (\n                <span\n                  style={{\n                    fontSize: \"0.7rem\",\n                    color: \"#64748b\",\n                    background: \"#f1f5f9\",\n                    borderRadius: \"3px\",\n                    padding: \"0 0.25rem\",\n                  }}\n                >\n                  @{termDefinition.lang}\n                </span>\n              )}\n            </div>\n          )}\n          {termComment !== null && (\n            <div data-testid=\"gw-inspector-term-comment\" style={{ marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}>\n              <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n                Comment\n              </p>\n              <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\" }}>\n                {termComment}\n              </p>\n            </div>\n          )}\n          {termScopeNote !== null && (\n            <div data-testid=\"gw-inspector-term-scope-note\" style={{ marginBottom: \"0.75rem\" }}>\n              <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.75rem\", color: \"#64748b\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n                Scope note\n              </p>\n              <p style={{ fontSize: \"0.8rem\", marginBottom: \"0.125rem\" }}>\n                {termScopeNote.text}\n              </p>\n              {termScopeNote.lang.length > 0 && (\n                <span\n                  style={{\n                    fontSize: \"0.7rem\",\n                    color: \"#64748b\",\n                    background: \"#f1f5f9\",\n                    borderRadius: \"3px\",\n                    padding: \"0 0.25rem\",\n                  }}\n                >\n                  @{termScopeNote.lang}\n                </span>\n              )}\n            </div>\n          )}",
            "scope": "minimal"
          }
        ],
        "tests_recommended": [
          {
            "file": "tests/playwright/imported-term-read-only.spec.ts",
            "describe": "Add a fixture term that carries skos:definition, rdfs:comment, and skos:scopeNote fields (extend imported-term.jsonld or inline a new fixture). Assert gw-inspector-term-definition, gw-inspector-term-comment, and gw-inspector-term-scope-note are visible with correct text content and the lang badge appears. Also assert that when fields are absent the corresponding section is not present in the DOM."
