          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "The importer defaults lang to 'en' when no language tag is present (turtle-import.ts line 226). This means termDefinition.lang and termScopeNote.lang will always be 'en' (never empty string) for terms imported from Turtle. The lang badge will therefore always appear. If the product requirement is 'omit the badge for untagged literals', a separate change to the importer to store null/empty when no tag is present would be needed. Surface to PO."
        ],
        "summary": "Two minimal changes to src/ui/Inspector.tsx. C1 adds termDefinition and termScopeNote extraction variables using the same guard pattern as termComment, typed as { text: string; lang: string } matching the shape stored by sub-task A. C2 replaces the existing loose-fragment comment section with three consistently-structured <div data-testid> sections (definition \u00e2\u2020\u2019 comment \u00e2\u2020\u2019 scope-note), each rendering only when the field is present. Multi-lingual fields (definition, scope-note) show a lang badge; comment remains plain-text. All three Chain 3.2-UI test-ids (gw-inspector-imported-term, gw-inspector-term-imported-badge, gw-btn-remap) are preserved. No CSS changes needed \u00e2\u20ac\u201d inline styles match the existing Inspector pattern throughout.",
