        "rationale": "Reconnaissance evidence is present in UPSTREAM (urn:fnsr:task:848-recon-p3-c5), satisfying the Spec 03 reconnaissance-required contract for substantive change. The proposed Inspector changes are minimal and pattern-consistent: (a) C1's extraction guard mirrors the existing termComment guard pattern (recon F12); (b) C2's conditional-render-only-when-present matches the recon F11 established Inspector convention and answers recon open_question 6 in the lighter direction (no empty-state placeholders); (c) test-id naming gw-inspector-term-definition / gw-inspector-term-comment / gw-inspector-term-scope-note follows the gw-inspector-term-<field> convention established by recon F11; (d) the lang-badge-when-non-empty rule for skos:definition + skos:scopeNote correctly reflects the multi-lingual {text, lang} shape (asymmetric with rdfs:comment's plain-string shape per recon F16, which justifies the no-badge treatment of comment); (e) the three preserved Chain 3.2-UI test-ids (gw-inspector-imported-term, gw-inspector-term-imported-badge, gw-btn-remap) are untouched; (f) the rdfs:comment test-id move from <p> to outer <div> is acceptable because recon F13 confirms no existing Playwright spec asserts on gw-inspector-term-comment content or tag-name, and getByTestId-based queries will still match the wrapper. Three caveats noted but not blocking: (1) The change depends on sub-task A landing skos:definition + skos:scopeNote in the {text, lang} object shape; if sub-task A chose plain strings, C1's typeof === 'object' guard silently returns null and the new sections never render \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a UI-degradation failure mode, not a hard error, but operator should confirm A's shape decision matches before applying C. (2) The developer's surfaced open_question about the importer defaulting lang to 'en' (turtle-import.ts line 226) is a sub-task-A-scope product question, not a sub-task-C concern \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the C-side rendering correctly honors whatever 