            "id": "C2",
            "file": "src/import/turtle-import.ts",
            "rationale": "Two coordinated type changes: (1) widen ImportedOntologyRecord.ecm:importStatus from the narrow literal 'ecm:parsed' to 'ecm:parsed' | 'ecm:degraded' per SPEC section 14.2 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the dialog (sub-task B) will write 'ecm:degraded' on Continue; (2) extend ImportResult ok:true variant with warning? (optional, 'LARGE_IMPORT'), termCount (required, number), and thresholdExceeded (required, boolean) so the dialog receives the LARGE_IMPORT signal without re-counting terms. Both variants are in adjacent lines; combining into one change avoids interleaved before/after confusion.",
            "before": "export interface ImportedOntologyRecord {\n  readonly id: string;\n  readonly type: \"ecm:ImportedOntology\";\n  readonly \"ecm:projectId\": string;\n  readonly \"ecm:name\": string;\n  readonly \"ecm:sourceFileName\": string;\n  readonly \"ecm:format\": \"text/turtle\";\n  readonly \"ecm:contentHash\": string;\n  readonly \"ecm:content\": string;\n  readonly \"ecm:createdAt\": string;\n  readonly \"ecm:importStatus\": \"ecm:parsed\";\n}\n\n/** Discriminated-union result of importOntology. */\nexport type ImportResult =\n  | {\n      readonly ok: true;\n      readonly ontology: ImportedOntologyRecord;\n      readonly terms: readonly ImportedTermObject[];\n    }\n  | {\n      readonly ok: false;\n      readonly error: string;\n      readonly code: \"SIZE_EXCEEDED\" | \"PARSE_ERROR\";\n    };",
            "after": "export interface ImportedOntologyRecord {\n  readonly id: string;\n  readonly type: \"ecm:ImportedOntology\";\n  readonly \"ecm:projectId\": string;\n  readonly \"ecm:name\": string;\n  readonly \"ecm:sourceFileName\": string;\n  readonly \"ecm:format\": \"text/turtle\";\n  readonly \"ecm:contentHash\": string;\n  readonly \"ecm:content\": string;\n  readonly \"ecm:createdAt\": string;\n  readonly \"ecm:importStatus\": \"ecm:parsed\" | \"ecm:degraded\";\n}\n\n/** Discriminated-union result of importOntology. */\nexport type ImportResult =\n  | {\n      readonly ok: true;\n      readonly ontology: ImportedOntologyRecord;\n      readonly terms: readonly ImportedTermObject[];\n      readonly warning?: \"LARGE_IMPORT\";\n      readonly termCount: number;\n      readonly thresholdExceeded: boolean;\n    }\n  | {\n      readonly ok: false;\n      readonly error: string;\n      readonly code: \"SIZE_EXCEEDED\" | \"PARSE_ERROR\";\n    };",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C3",
            "file": "src/import/turtle-import.ts",
            "rationale": "Update async (browser) return path to populate the three new required/optional fields. Threshold check runs after terms array is fully built. The importer sets ecm:importStatus to 'ecm:parsed' unconditionally \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the dialog (sub-task B) is responsible for overwriting to 'ecm:degraded' on Continue. Anchored on the unique `})();` IIFE close which only exists in the async path.",
            "before": "      return { ok: true, ontology, terms };\n    })();\n  }",
            "after": "      if (terms.length > LARGE_IMPORT_THRESHOLD) {\n        return { ok: true, ontology, terms, termCount: terms.length, thresholdExceeded: true, warning: \"LARGE_IMPORT\" };\n      }\n      return { ok: true, ontology, terms, termCount: terms.length, thresholdExceeded: false };\n    })();\n  }",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C4",
            "file": "src/import/turtle-import.ts",
            "rationale": "Update synchronous (Node) return path to mirror C3. Anchored via the 4-space-indented 'ecm:importStatus' line (async path uses 8-space indent) plus the closing `};` / `return` / `}` sequence unique to the sync path tail.",
            "before": "    \"ecm:importStatus\": \"ecm:parsed\",\n  };\n\n  return { ok: true, ontology, terms };\n}",
            "after": "    \"ecm:importStatus\": \"ecm:parsed\",\n  };\n\n  if (terms.length > LARGE_IMPORT_THRESHOLD) {\n    return { ok: true, ontology, terms, termCount: terms.length, thresholdExceeded: true, warning: \"LARGE_IMPORT\" };\n  }\n  return { ok: true, ontology, terms, termCount: terms.length, thresholdExceeded: false };\n}",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C5",
            "file": "tests/import-turtle.test.ts",
            "rationale": "Add three LARGE_IMPORT threshold unit tests per IMPL section 3.3: LARGE-1 (exactly 10000 terms: boundary, no warning), LARGE-2 (10001 terms: just-over, warning fired + thresholdExceeded=true), LARGE-3 (SMALL_TTL 2 terms: no warning). Programmatic Turtle generation via makeLargeTtl() follows the established 'a'.repeat() synthetic-fixture pattern from AC5. Anchored by replacing the Summary block and prepending new tests + summary, keeping the file's pass/fail counter pattern intact.",
            "before": "// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Summary\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nconsole.log(`\\n  ${passed} passed, ${failed} failed`);\nif (failed > 0) process.exit(1);",
            "after": "// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// LARGE_IMPORT threshold tests (SPEC section 14.2; IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN section 3.3)\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n/** Generate a Turtle ontology with exactly `count` owl:Class terms (one per IRI). */\nfunction makeLargeTtl(count: number): string {\n  const lines: string[] = [\n    \"@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .\",\n    \"\",\n  ];\n  for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n    lines.push(`<https://example.org/Class${i}> a owl:Class .`);\n  }\n  return lines.join(\"\\n\");\n}\n\nconsole.log(\"\\nLARGE-1: exactly 10000 terms -- no LARGE_IMPORT warning (boundary)\");\n\ntry {\n  const ttl = makeLargeTtl(10_000);\n  const result = importOntology(ttl, \"large-exact.ttl\", PROJECT_ID, CREATED_AT);\n  ok(result.ok, \"importOntology must succeed on 10000-term ontology\");\n  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(\"result.ok is false\");\n  strictEqual(result.thresholdExceeded, false, \"10000 terms must NOT exceed threshold (boundary case)\");\n  strictEqual(result.termCount, 10_000, \"termCount must equal 10000\");\n  ok(result.warning === undefined, \"warning must be absent at exactly 10000 terms\");\n  pass(\"exactly 10000 terms: thresholdExceeded=false, no warning (LARGE-1)\");\n} catch (e) {\n  fail(\"exactly 10000 terms must not trigger LARGE_IMPORT warning (LARGE-1)\", e);\n}\n\nconsole.log(\"\\nLARGE-2: 10001 terms -- LARGE_IMPORT warning fired (just-over threshold)\");\n\ntry {\n  const ttl = makeLargeTtl(10_001);\n  const result = importOntology(ttl, \"large-over.ttl\", PROJECT_ID, CREATED_AT);\n  ok(result.ok, \"importOntology must succeed on 10001-term ontology\");\n  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(\"result.ok is false\");\n  strictEqual(result.thresholdExceeded, true, \"10001 terms must exceed threshold\");\n  strictEqual(result.termCount, 10_001, \"termCount must equal 10001\");\n  strictEqual(result.warning, \"LARGE_IMPORT\", \"warning must be 'LARGE_IMPORT' when threshold exceeded\");\n  pass(\"10001 terms: thresholdExceeded=true, warning='LARGE_IMPORT' (LARGE-2)\");\n} catch (e) {\n  fail(\"10001 terms must trigger LARGE_IMPORT warning (LARGE-2)\", e);\n}\n\nconsole.log(\"\\nLARGE-3: small ontology (2 terms) -- no LARGE_IMPORT warning\");\n\ntry {\n  const result = importOntology(SMALL_TTL, \"small.ttl\", PROJECT_ID, CREATED_AT);\n  ok(result.ok, \"importOntology must succeed on small ontology\");\n  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(\"result.ok is false\");\n  strictEqual(result.thresholdExceeded, false, \"small ontology must not exceed threshold\");\n  ok(result.termCount < 10_000, \"termCount must be below threshold for small ontology\");\n  ok(result.warning === undefined, \"warning must be absent for small ontology\");\n  pass(\"small ontology: thresholdExceeded=false, no warning (LARGE-3)\");\n} catch (e) {\n  fail(\"small ontology must not trigger LARGE_IMPORT warning (LARGE-3)\", e);\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Summary\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nconsole.log(`\\n  ${passed} passed, ${failed} failed`);\nif (failed > 0) process.exit(1);",
            "scope": "minimal"
          }
        ],
        "tests_recommended": [
          {
            "file": "tests/playwright/large-import-warning.spec.ts",
            "describe": "Playwright E2E tests for IMPL section 3.3 AC2\u00e2\u20ac\u201cAC5: upload a >10000-term .ttl fixture via the dialog, assert the large_import_warning phase appears with correct term count, click Continue, assert ecm:importStatus='ecm:degraded' in serialized project state, assert DOM node count for term list is <= 200 (AC5). Requires a generated fixture at a real filesystem path (globalSetup or beforeAll hook). These tests are out of scope for sub-task A (importer layer) and belong to sub-tasks B/C/D."
          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "SPEC section 5.6 schema (reconnaissance finding F18) shows only ecm:importStatus: 'ecm:parsed'. The C2 type widening adds 'ecm:degraded' at the code level. A corresponding SPEC 5.6 amendment ratifying 'ecm:degraded' as a permitted value should be queued before or alongside sub-task B landing, to avoid the architect's ratification chain finding a SPEC/code mismatch.",
          "C3 async-path before-snippet anchors on `      return { ok: true, ontology, terms };\\n    })();\\n  }` (6-space indent + IIFE close). If the file uses CRLF line endings on Windows, the applier's before-match must normalize or match CRLF. Confirm the applier's line-ending handling for this file.",
          "The `makeLargeTtl(10_000)` test (LARGE-1) will invoke the N3 parser on ~10,000 triples synchronously. On slow CI this could add ~200\u00e2\u20ac\u201c500 ms to the unit test suite. If test suite runtime becomes an issue, LARGE-1/LARGE-2 can be gated behind a `--slow` flag or moved to a separate file; no change needed now."
        ],
        "summary": "Five minimal changes across two files implement IMPL section 3.3 sub-task A. C1 adds LARGE_IMPORT_THRESHOLD=10_000. C2 widens ImportedOntologyRecord.ecm:importStatus to the 'ecm:parsed'|'ecm:degraded' union and extends the ImportResult ok:true variant with warning? (optional), termCount (required), and thresholdExceeded (required). C3 and C4 update the async and synchronous return paths respectively to evaluate the threshold and populate the new fields. C5 adds three unit tests (boundary: 10000/no-warning, just-over: 10001/LARGE_IMPORT, small/no-warning) using programmatic Turtle generation. The importer signals LARGE_IMPORT only; ecm:degraded assignment and the two-stage dialog flow remain sub-task B's responsibility.",
        "self_assessment": "confident"
      },
