        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "Adds a new threshold constant, widens two type unions (ImportedOntologyRecord.ecm:importStatus and ImportResult ok:true variant fields), and introduces three new unit tests \u00e2\u20ac\u201d all behavioral/contract changes outside the editorial-correction scope (typos / formatting / terminology-sharpening-preserving-semantics).",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM (urn:fnsr:task:870-recon-p3-c6), satisfying the Spec 03 reconnaissance-required contract for substantive changes. The five proposed changes (C1\u00e2\u20ac\u201cC5) align precisely with the seven ratification criteria in INPUTS.purpose: (1) C1 introduces LARGE_IMPORT_THRESHOLD = 10_000 with a SPEC \u00c2\u00a714.2 reference comment, placed adjacent to MAX_SOURCE_BYTES for locality (recon F9 gap closed); (2) C2 extends the ImportResult ok:true variant with `warning?: \"LARGE_IMPORT\"`, `termCount: number`, and `thresholdExceeded: boolean`, giving the dialog a pre-computed signal rather than requiring it to re-count terms (recon F2 gap closed); (3) C2 widens ImportedOntologyRecord.ecm:importStatus to the union `\"ecm:parsed\" | \"ecm:degraded\"` (recon F3 + F18 gap closed at the code level); (4) C3 and C4 update both async (browser) and synchronous (Node) return paths to compute terms.length > threshold and populate the three new fields, while keeping ecm:importStatus hardcoded to \"ecm:parsed\" \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the importer signals but does not assign \"ecm:degraded\", preserving the separation of concerns explicitly required by INPUTS criterion (4) (the dialog sub-task B owns the degraded-mode write); (5) C5 covers the exact boundary semantics (LARGE-1 at exactly 10_000 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 thresholdExceeded=false, no warning; LARGE-2 at 10_001 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 thresholdExceeded=true, warning='LARGE_IMPORT'; LARGE-3 small \u00e2\u2020\u2019 no warning), establishing the strict-greater-than contract unambiguously per IMPL \u00c2\u00a73.3 AC5 wording (\"10,001 terms triggers\"); (6) layer purity is preserved \u00e2\u20ac\u201d changes confine to src/import/ and tests/; no new runtime dependencies; the programmatic Turtle generation in tests follows the established `a.repeat()` synthetic-fixture pattern from the existing SIZE_EXCEEDED test (recon F15); (7) regression risk on the existing 162-test suite is bounded \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the added required fields (termCount, thresholdExceeded) only affect ImportResult-construction sites, all of which are inside turtle-import.ts itself and are covered by C3/C4; existing consumers (App.tsx, tests) read `result.ok`, `result.ontology`, `result.terms` and are unaffected by additional fields. Anchor-snippet quality is high: C1 anchors on the unique MAX_SOURCE_BYTES + RDF_TYPE pair; C3 anchors on the unique `})();` IIFE close (async path only); C4 anchors on the 4-space-indent ecm:importStatus + sync-path tail. The developer's three open questions are non-blocking: (a) the SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.6 schema amendment for \"ecm:degraded\" is correctly forward-tracked to land before or alongside sub-task B (where the value is first written), not sub-task A (where only the type union widens) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d code-vs-SPEC mismatch surfaces at B's ratification, not A's; (b) CRLF/LF concern is an applier-layer property the substrate's applier already handles; (c) the 10_000-triple parse test runtime is acceptable and gating is a future optimization. Ratified for Pass 2b commit-finalize.",
