            "content": "Exact-boundary test triple (under-threshold / at-threshold / over-threshold) as a discipline for strict-inequality thresholds: C5 establishes LARGE-1 (10_000 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 no warning), LARGE-2 (10_001 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 warning), LARGE-3 (small \u00e2\u2020\u2019 no warning). This triple disambiguates the strict-greater-than vs. greater-or-equal semantics in a way that a single 10_001 test would not, and matches IMPL \u00c2\u00a73.3 AC5's wording ('10,001 terms triggers'). Future threshold-related changes should adopt this triple as a default test shape."
          }
