        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The proposal adds a new dialog phase, conditional rendering branch, new event handler that mutates project state with a previously-disallowed ecm:importStatus value, and new test-ids \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this is behavioral UI surface change, not typo/formatting/terminology tightening.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance (urn:fnsr:task:870-recon-p3-c6) is present in UPSTREAM, satisfying the Spec 03 reconnaissance-required contract for substantive changes. The proposed five-change diff to src/ui/ImportOntologyDialog.tsx satisfies all five INPUTS verification criteria: (1) C2 transitions to a new 'large_import_warning' phase when result.warning === 'LARGE_IMPORT' fires and C4 inserts the corresponding warning panel JSX scoped to that phase; (2) C5 conditionally renders a distinct two-button row (Continue-in-degraded / Cancel) in the warning phase, and C3's handleContinueDegraded spread-overrides ecm:importStatus to 'ecm:degraded' while the cancel path calls onClose with no project mutation; (3) the common case is preserved byte-for-byte \u00e2\u20ac\u201d C2 keeps the else-branch to phase 'preview', C4 leaves the error section verbatim, and C5's else-branch reproduces the existing button row with unchanged data-testid attributes (gw-btn-import-confirm, gw-btn-import-cancel) and unchanged disabled predicate (phase !== 'preview' || termCount === 0); (4) the four new test-ids (gw-import-large-warning, gw-import-large-term-count, gw-btn-import-cancel-large, gw-btn-import-continue-degraded) follow the gw-* convention and are textually distinct from the existing gw-btn-import-confirm/cancel pair \u00e2\u20ac\u201d no collision; (5) handleContinueDegraded is the only code path that constructs 'ecm:degraded'; handleConfirm uses pending.ontology unmodified, so the degraded status applies only on the Continue branch. The proposed structure correctly localizes degraded-mode status assignment in the dialog (the UI layer that owns the user decision), rather than in turtle-import.ts (the parse layer), consistent with reconnaissance F3 and the developer's own open-question #2. Minor structural observations recorded as bankings but not blocking. The proposal is conditionally dependent on sub-task A's widening of the ImportResult discriminator (to carry the optional warning field) and of ecm:importStatus to 'ecm:parsed' | 'ecm:degraded'; this is acknowledged in the developer's open-question #1 and is a sequencing constraint for Pass 2b dispatch, not a defect in this proposal.",
