            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "Sub-task B is structurally dependent on sub-task A landing first: the proposal references result.warning (a field sub-task A adds to the ImportResult ok:true variant) and assigns 'ecm:degraded' to ecm:importStatus (a literal sub-task A widens the type to permit). The chain must dispatch the Pass 2b applier for sub-task A before sub-task B's applier; otherwise npm run build fails on TS2353 (unknown property 'warning') and TS2322 ('ecm:degraded' not assignable to '\"ecm:parsed\"'). This is the chain-shape variation by sub-task ordering \u00e2\u20ac\u201d operator should sequence sub-task-A-applier \u00e2\u2020\u2019 sub-task-B-applier or schedule a single test-runner downstream of both."
          },
          {
            "id": "B2",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "C3 declares `const degradedOntology: ImportedOntologyRecord = {...}` but ImportedOntologyRecord is not visibly imported in ImportOntologyDialog.tsx per reconnaissance F5 (the existing handleConfirm uses untyped object literals and `Record<string, unknown>` for the updated project). If the type symbol is not already imported, the applier's `before`-match will succeed but `npm run build` will fail on TS2304 (cannot find name 'ImportedOntologyRecord'). A minimal fix at apply time is to either (a) add an import of ImportedOntologyRecord from '../import/turtle-import' or (b) rewrite the annotation as `typeof pending.ontology`. This is borderline-minor enough to ratify without revision but should be caught by test-runner; flagging as a forward observation for future developer-agent contract refinement around type-import discipline."
