      "outputs": {
        "ruling": "ratified",
        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "The change adds a new render branch (virtualized path), a new prop on TermSection (isDegraded), a new module-level helper (hasDegradedOntology), and changes runtime behavior when a degraded ontology is present \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this is behavioral specification content, not typo/formatting/citation tightening.",
        "rationale": "All seven verification criteria from INPUTS are satisfied by the proposed changes[] and reconnaissance evidence in UPSTREAM is present per Spec 03. (1) Virtualization gate `useVirt = isDegraded && filteredTerms.length > VIRT_THRESHOLD` in C3 is conjunctive over the degraded-ontology predicate and the 200-term threshold; VIRT_THRESHOLD is set to 200 in C1, matching IMPL \u00c2\u00a73.3 AC5. (2) Hand-rolled: no new imports; the windowing is a pure scroll-listener + slice + spacer-div construction (C3/C4), no react-window / react-virtualized. (3) Empty spacers \u00e2\u20ac\u201d top div height = virtStartIdx * VIRT_ITEM_HEIGHT and bottom div height = (virtTotal - virtEndIdx) * VIRT_ITEM_HEIGHT in C3/C4 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d preserve scrollbar total-height accuracy modulo the VIRT_ITEM_HEIGHT estimate (flagged in open_questions as known approximation). (4) Composition with Chain 5 search: the slice operates on `filteredTerms` (already-filtered array) in C4, so filter-first ordering is preserved; when search reduces filteredTerms.length \u00e2\u2030\u00a4 200, virtualization deactivates. (5) No behavior change when inactive: the renderTermItem helper extracted in C3 reproduces the prior inline <li> JSX faithfully (className, role, tabIndex, aria-disabled, onClick, onKeyDown branches identical); the full-list branch in C4 keeps `gw-term-list gw-term-section-list` classes on <ul> matching the original. (6) `data-testid=\"gw-term-section-virtualized\"` is present on the virtualized scroll container in C4 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Playwright AC5 handle satisfied. (7) No package.json mutation appears in changes[]; CLAUDE.md \u00c2\u00a76 no-runtime-deps constraint upheld. The change is single-file (src/ui/TermSidebar.tsx) and backward-compatible (isDegraded defaults to false), so non-import callsites remain valid. The hard-coded VIRT_ITEM_HEIGHT=28 and virtContainerH=192 constants introduce minor scrollbar-accuracy approximation but do not threaten the AC5 DOM-count assertion, which is gated by the conservative overscan + slice arithmetic. The hasDegradedOntology helper in C1 correctly implements the recon's F22 inference (scan `ecm:ontologies` for `ecm:importStatus === \"ecm:degraded\"`) without requiring per-term counting at validation time. Sub-task C's scope is virtualization in isolation; SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.6 amendment, validate() makeWarning, ImportOntologyDialog phase wiring, and Playwright fixture generation belong to sibling sub-tasks A/B/D \u00e2\u20ac\u201d recon F19 (\u00c2\u00a73.4 global-search interaction) is correctly deferred. Recommend ratification; operator queues commit-finalize (applier) downstream.",
