        "bankings": [
          {
            "id": "B1",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "Hand-rolled virtualization with fixed row-height + container-height constants (VIRT_ITEM_HEIGHT=28, virtContainerH=192) is sufficient for satisfying a bounded-DOM-node acceptance criterion (AC5: \u00e2\u2030\u00a4200 <li>) even when the constants are approximations, because overscan + Math.min/Math.max clamping keep slice arithmetic conservative. Scrollbar-position accuracy degrades proportionally to row-height estimation error, but the functional contract (degraded-mode performance, navigation via search) holds. A measure-then-virtualize variant using ResizeObserver to read actual rendered row height would eliminate the approximation but adds a first-render reflow cycle \u00e2\u20ac\u201d worth deferring until a concrete UX defect appears."
          },
          {
            "id": "B2",
            "category": "pattern-observation",
            "content": "When introducing a conditional render branch that must remain functionally identical on the inactive path, extracting the inner element renderer to a named helper (renderTermItem) before the conditional cleans up both the diff and the long-term maintenance surface. The proposed C3/C4 split \u00e2\u20ac\u201d helper extraction in C3, three-branch conditional in C4 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d converts what would have been a ~60-line nested JSX replacement into two small surgical patches that each carry a clear semantic claim. This is a reusable pattern for adding optional rendering modes (virtualization, lazy-loading, grouped-by-category) to a component without inflating the structural-change blast radius."
          },
          {
