        "editorial_verdict": "substantive",
        "editorial_verdict_reason": "Creating a new Playwright spec file with four end-to-end acceptance tests that gate behavioral conformance for IMPL section 3.3 AC2-AC5 is behavioral/spec content, well outside the editorial-correction scope of typo/formatting/citation-format updates.",
        "rationale": "Reconnaissance is present in UPSTREAM (urn:fnsr:task:870-recon-p3-c6), satisfying the Spec 03 refusal contract for substantive changes. Coverage of IMPL section 3.3 AC2-AC5 is verbatim and complete: AC2 (warning UI + term count visibility) is tested via gw-import-large-warning + gw-import-large-term-count with toHaveText('10001'); AC3 (Cancel leaves project unchanged) is tested via gw-btn-import-cancel-large click + dialog-closed assertion + 'No classes yet' empty-state check against gw-term-section-classes; AC4 (Continue degraded sets ecm:importStatus=ecm:degraded) is tested with a full save-and-reparse round-trip via Playwright download event, the strongest possible AC observation; AC5 (DOM node count <= 200 in degraded mode) is tested via locator('[data-testid=\"gw-term-item\"]').count() after the AC4 setup, with the fixture deliberately containing only owl:Class terms so the page-scoped count is equivalent to a class-scoped count. AC1 (validate() output) is correctly out of scope for sub-task D and belongs in sub-task C's unit-test layer. Programmatic fixture generation requirement is satisfied: generateLargeTurtle(10001) builds Turtle content in memory at module load (~450 KB; the recon's open question 3 trade resolved by passing a {name, mimeType, buffer} payload to setInputFiles rather than committing a file or adding a globalSetup hook); no static .ttl is written. Test-ids match sub-tasks B + C as applied: gw-import-large-warning (ImportOntologyDialog.tsx:288), gw-import-large-term-count (line 302), gw-btn-import-cancel-large (line 347), gw-btn-import-continue-degraded (line 355), gw-term-item (TermSidebar.tsx:224), and the VIRT_THRESHOLD=200 + hasDegradedOntology() activation conditions are accurately described in the inline comment. The developer's flagged 'gw-term-item-class testid mismatch' is mis-attributed in the open_questions: IMPL section 3.3 AC5 text reads 'DOM node count for term list <= 200 regardless of term count (virtualization). Playwright DOM assertion.' with no per-type testid prescription; the actual implementation using the shared gw-term-item testid is conformant. No SPEC amendment dependency for AC2-AC5 (the ecm:degraded value question affects sub-task A/C, not the Playwright surface). Two minor advisories that do not block ratification: (a) the 20s parse-timeout on slow CI may flake \u00e2\u20ac\u201d operator can bump to 30s if observed; (b) the AC5 assertion is page-scoped rather than per-section, acceptable here because the fixture imports only classes but a per-section assertion would be more robust for future fixtures mixing term types.",
