        "rationale": "Refused under CLAUDE.md section 7.11 architect refusal contract. Verification-ritual task 906 returned overall_status: needs_llm_judgment (Cat 9 'Cited-Content Consistency' deferred via evidence.llm_dispatcher_agent=verification-ritual-llm, evidence.llm_mode=cat-9-judge), but UPSTREAM contains no verification-ritual-llm task. CLAUDE.md section 7.11 states the architect 'refuses ratification on overall_status: veto (and refuses on needs_llm_judgment without the LLM-side chain in UPSTREAM).' The task INPUTS verification clause (1) asserts 'verification-ritual overall_status is pass' \u00e2\u20ac\u201d that precondition is unmet (status is needs_llm_judgment, not pass). Substance review (advisory, not the ground of refusal): the developer's single change to project/SPEC.md section 5.6 is well-formed (preserves the existing JSON example showing ecm:parsed; appends a normative prose block after the existing ecm:content sentence; cites SPEC section 14.2, IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN section 3.3 AC4, and src/import/turtle-import.ts ImportedOntologyRecord; all three citations are validated by recon F3, F5, F6). The amendment introduces zero ADR-NNN citations so the section 7.5 ADR-citation CPS check carries no risk (recon F9 confirms section 5.6 has no existing ADR citations either). The recon summary's editorial-vs-substantive judgment is sound: this is documentation alignment with already-shipped Chain 6 code, not a new design decision; the union widening occurred upstream and no ADR-010 is required. Cat 1 and Cat 2 returned pass; Cat 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 10 returned miss/missing_canonical_source. The seven category misses are vacuously satisfied for this artifact (the proposed text contains no Q-rulings, reason-codes, FOL/OWL @type discriminators, manifest mirrors, cross-phase cycle artifacts, or IRI registries on which those categories would adjudicate) and do not contribute to the refusal \u00e2\u20ac\u201d only the Cat 9 LLM chain gap does. Operator remediation: queue verification-ritual-llm (mode: cat-9-judge) downstream of task 906 and upstream of a re-issued ratification task; then re-dispatch ratification with both verification-ritual and verification-ritual-llm in UPSTREAM. If Cat 9 LLM verdict is pass, ratification can proceed to ratified with editorial_verdict: editorial; if Cat 9 vetoes, the adversarial-critic cat-9-second-pass chain extension applies per section 7.11.",
